{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HifrWoC33aTt2CqGQc8ENf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# User Stories — PRD-00 Project Foundation, App Shell & Design System\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-1 · Phase: intake\n4\t\n5\t## Project scaffold & tooling\n6\t\n7\t- As a developer, I want the project scaffolded with Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, ESLint and Prettier, so that the codebase has a consistent, enforced baseline. (FR-1)\n8\t- As a developer, I want standard npm scripts (dev/build/start/lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e/db:migrate/db:deploy/db:seed/db:reset/format), so that every later PRD can build, test and manage the database the same way. (FR-2)\n9\t- As a developer, I want the `@/*` path alias mapped to `src/*`, so that imports stay short and consistent. (FR-3)\n10\t- As a developer, I want a `docker-compose.yml` that starts Postgres 16 with a named volume and the `schoolhub` database/user, so that I can run the full stack locally with one command. (FR-4)\n11\t- As a developer, I want a documented `.env.example`, so that I know every environment variable the app needs before I start it. (FR-5)\n12\t- As a developer, I want startup-time Zod validation of `process.env`, so that a missing or invalid variable fails fast with a readable error instead of a cryptic runtime crash. (FR-6)\n13\t\n14\t## Database\n15\t\n16\t- As a developer, I want a Prisma schema with the singleton `SchoolSettings` model, so that school-wide settings have one source of truth. (FR-7)\n17\t- As a developer, I want a single cached Prisma client instance, so that hot reload in development doesn't exhaust database connections. (FR-8)\n18\t- As a developer, I want an idempotent seed script that creates the `SchoolSettings` row, so that re-running the seed never duplicates data. (FR-9)\n19\t\n20\t## API helpers\n21\t\n22\t- As a developer, I want a shared `ok()` helper, so that every successful API response has the same `{ data }` shape. (FR-10)\n23\t- As a developer, I want a shared `paginated()` helper, so that every list endpoint returns the same `{ data, page, pageSize, total }` shape. (FR-11)\n24\t- As a developer, I want a shared `apiError()` helper, so that every error response has the same shape and the correct HTTP status. (FR-12)\n25\t- As a developer, I want a `withHandler()` wrapper that maps Zod, AppError and Prisma errors to the right error codes, so that route handlers stay thin and error handling stays consistent. (FR-13)\n26\t- As a developer, I want a `parsePagination()` helper that clamps page/pageSize to safe bounds, so that no endpoint can be asked to return an unbounded page. (FR-14)\n27\t- As a developer, I want `parseBody()`/`parseQuery()` helpers, so that every handler validates input the same way. (FR-15)\n28\t\n29\t## Health & observability\n30\t\n31\t- As an operator, I want a `GET /api/health` endpoint that checks the database, so that I can monitor whether the app and its database connection are healthy. (FR-16)\n32\t- As a developer, I want a shared `logger` with info/warn/error levels, so that logging is structured and consistent instead of scattered `console.log` calls. (FR-40)\n33\t\n34\t## Design system\n35\t\n36\t- As a developer, I want the exact MUI v9 package set installed at the versions reported by the MUI MCP server, so that every later PRD builds against a known-good, documented version. (FR-17)\n37\t- As any user, I want a theme with light/dark colour schemes and a toggle that persists my preference, so that I can use SchoolHub comfortably without a flash of the wrong mode. (FR-18)\n38\t- As a developer, I want an ESLint rule that fails the build on any banned UI/styling library, so that the \"Material UI only\" rule is enforced automatically, not just by convention. (FR-19)\n39\t- As a developer, I want a shared `PageHeader` component, so that every page has a consistent title/description/actions layout. (FR-20)\n40\t- As a developer, I want a shared `DataTable` component wrapping MUI X DataGrid with server-side paging/sorting/search, so that every list screen in later PRDs behaves the same way. (FR-21)\n41\t- As any user, I want a shared `EmptyState` component, so that empty lists and unfinished pages look intentional instead of blank. (FR-22)\n42\t- As any user, I want a shared `ConfirmDialog`, so that destructive actions always ask for confirmation the same way. (FR-23)\n43\t- As any user, I want a shared toast notification system, so that I get consistent feedback after actions across the app. (FR-24)\n44\t- As a developer, I want shared `FormField` helpers wiring React Hook Form to MUI inputs, so that every form in later PRDs has consistent labels, errors and helper text. (FR-25)\n45\t- As any user, I want a shared `StatCard` component, so that future dashboards can present metrics consistently. (FR-26)\n46\t- As any user, I want a shared `UserAvatar` component with deterministic initials/colour, so that I can recognise people consistently across the app. (FR-27)\n47\t- As any user, I want dates displayed in the school's timezone via a shared `DateDisplay` component, so that I never have to mentally convert UTC timestamps. (FR-28)\n48\t- As any user, I want a shared `LoadingSkeleton`, so that loading states look consistent across tables, cards and forms. (FR-29)\n49\t\n50\t## App shell\n51\t\n52\t- As any authenticated user, I want a persistent sidebar and top bar, so that I can navigate SchoolHub consistently from any screen. (FR-30)\n53\t- As a mobile user, I want the sidebar to become a temporary drawer opened from a hamburger button on narrow screens, so that navigation doesn't crowd out content on my phone. (FR-31)\n54\t- As any authenticated user, I want the sidebar to show only the navigation items relevant to my role, with the current page highlighted, so that I'm not shown options I can't use. (FR-32)\n55\t- As any authenticated user, I want the top bar to show the school's name/logo, a theme toggle, a notification bell and a user menu, so that I have consistent, at-a-glance context and account actions. (FR-33)\n56\t- As any authenticated user, I want a welcoming `/dashboard` page, so that I land somewhere meaningful even before dashboards are built. (FR-34)\n57\t- As a developer, I want an empty, typed `student-tabs.ts` config, so that later PRDs can register student-detail tabs without creating new pages. (FR-35)\n58\t\n59\t## Public site\n60\t\n61\t- As a visitor, I want a public header/footer with the school's branding and contact details, so that I know whose site I'm on and how to reach the school. (FR-36)\n62\t- As a visitor, I want a simple home page with a hero section and a sign-in button, so that I can quickly understand the site and log in. (FR-37)\n63\t\n64\t## Error handling\n65\t\n66\t- As any user, I want clear 404 and error pages with a way to retry, so that something going wrong doesn't leave me stuck on a blank screen. (FR-38)\n67\t- As any user, I want a `/forbidden` page, so that later PRDs can tell me clearly when I lack permission instead of showing a broken page. (FR-39)\n68\t\n69\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n70\t\n71\t- **UI library discipline (NFR-1):** Material UI is the only UI/styling library. Every MUI component must be looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; a fixed list of alternative UI and styling libraries is banned and enforced by ESLint.\n72\t- **Performance (NFR-2):** `/dashboard` must reach Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5s on a production build.\n73\t- **Accessibility (NFR-3):** All shared components meet WCAG 2.1 AA; Playwright + axe must report zero serious/critical violations on `/` and `/dashboard`.\n74\t- **Responsiveness (NFR-4):** Layouts must work with no horizontal scroll from 360px to 1920px wide.\n75\t- **Security (NFR-5):** Security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, CSP) must be set in `next.config.js`.\n76\t- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest/Testing Library unit and component tests, plus Playwright e2e (including axe scans), must cover the behaviours listed in the PRD's Test Requirements.\n77\t- **Fast local bootstrap (NFR-7):** A fresh clone must be runnable end-to-end in under 5 minutes via the documented command sequence.\n78\t- **Green pipeline (NFR-8):** `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` and `test:e2e` must all pass on a fresh clone.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e178deb2-f3fc-4074-b26a-6dc2b835ef23","uuid":"ede8fd67-aaba-4574-a8f4-5d84253d4b8f","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:29:15.716Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories — PRD-00 Project Foundation, App Shell & Design System\n\nTicket: abcd-1 · Phase: intake\n\n## Project scaffold & tooling\n\n- As a developer, I want the project scaffolded with Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, ESLint and Prettier, so that the codebase has a consistent, enforced baseline. (FR-1)\n- As a developer, I want standard npm scripts (dev/build/start/lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e/db:migrate/db:deploy/db:seed/db:reset/format), so that every later PRD can build, test and manage the database the same way. (FR-2)\n- As a developer, I want the `@/*` path alias mapped to `src/*`, so that imports stay short and consistent. (FR-3)\n- As a developer, I want a `docker-compose.yml` that starts Postgres 16 with a named volume and the `schoolhub` database/user, so that I can run the full stack locally with one command. (FR-4)\n- As a developer, I want a documented `.env.example`, so that I know every environment variable the app needs before I start it. (FR-5)\n- As a developer, I want startup-time Zod validation of `process.env`, so that a missing or invalid variable fails fast with a readable error instead of a cryptic runtime crash. (FR-6)\n\n## Database\n\n- As a developer, I want a Prisma schema with the singleton `SchoolSettings` model, so that school-wide settings have one source of truth. (FR-7)\n- As a developer, I want a single cached Prisma client instance, so that hot reload in development doesn't exhaust database connections. (FR-8)\n- As a developer, I want an idempotent seed script that creates the `SchoolSettings` row, so that re-running the seed never duplicates data. (FR-9)\n\n## API helpers\n\n- As a developer, I want a shared `ok()` helper, so that every successful API response has the same `{ data }` shape. (FR-10)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `paginated()` helper, so that every list endpoint returns the same `{ data, page, pageSize, total }` shape. (FR-11)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `apiError()` helper, so that every error response has the same shape and the correct HTTP status. (FR-12)\n- As a developer, I want a `withHandler()` wrapper that maps Zod, AppError and Prisma errors to the right error codes, so that route handlers stay thin and error handling stays consistent. (FR-13)\n- As a developer, I want a `parsePagination()` helper that clamps page/pageSize to safe bounds, so that no endpoint can be asked to return an unbounded page. (FR-14)\n- As a developer, I want `parseBody()`/`parseQuery()` helpers, so that every handler validates input the same way. (FR-15)\n\n## Health & observability\n\n- As an operator, I want a `GET /api/health` endpoint that checks the database, so that I can monitor whether the app and its database connection are healthy. (FR-16)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `logger` with info/warn/error levels, so that logging is structured and consistent instead of scattered `console.log` calls. (FR-40)\n\n## Design system\n\n- As a developer, I want the exact MUI v9 package set installed at the versions reported by the MUI MCP server, so that every later PRD builds against a known-good, documented version. (FR-17)\n- As any user, I want a theme with light/dark colour schemes and a toggle that persists my preference, so that I can use SchoolHub comfortably without a flash of the wrong mode. (FR-18)\n- As a developer, I want an ESLint rule that fails the build on any banned UI/styling library, so that the \"Material UI only\" rule is enforced automatically, not just by convention. (FR-19)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `PageHeader` component, so that every page has a consistent title/description/actions layout. (FR-20)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `DataTable` component wrapping MUI X DataGrid with server-side paging/sorting/search, so that every list screen in later PRDs behaves the same way. (FR-21)\n- As any user, I want a shared `EmptyState` component, so that empty lists and unfinished pages look intentional instead of blank. (FR-22)\n- As any user, I want a shared `ConfirmDialog`, so that destructive actions always ask for confirmation the same way. (FR-23)\n- As any user, I want a shared toast notification system, so that I get consistent feedback after actions across the app. (FR-24)\n- As a developer, I want shared `FormField` helpers wiring React Hook Form to MUI inputs, so that every form in later PRDs has consistent labels, errors and helper text. (FR-25)\n- As any user, I want a shared `StatCard` component, so that future dashboards can present metrics consistently. (FR-26)\n- As any user, I want a shared `UserAvatar` component with deterministic initials/colour, so that I can recognise people consistently across the app. (FR-27)\n- As any user, I want dates displayed in the school's timezone via a shared `DateDisplay` component, so that I never have to mentally convert UTC timestamps. (FR-28)\n- As any user, I want a shared `LoadingSkeleton`, so that loading states look consistent across tables, cards and forms. (FR-29)\n\n## App shell\n\n- As any authenticated user, I want a persistent sidebar and top bar, so that I can navigate SchoolHub consistently from any screen. (FR-30)\n- As a mobile user, I want the sidebar to become a temporary drawer opened from a hamburger button on narrow screens, so that navigation doesn't crowd out content on my phone. (FR-31)\n- As any authenticated user, I want the sidebar to show only the navigation items relevant to my role, with the current page highlighted, so that I'm not shown options I can't use. (FR-32)\n- As any authenticated user, I want the top bar to show the school's name/logo, a theme toggle, a notification bell and a user menu, so that I have consistent, at-a-glance context and account actions. (FR-33)\n- As any authenticated user, I want a welcoming `/dashboard` page, so that I land somewhere meaningful even before dashboards are built. (FR-34)\n- As a developer, I want an empty, typed `student-tabs.ts` config, so that later PRDs can register student-detail tabs without creating new pages. (FR-35)\n\n## Public site\n\n- As a visitor, I want a public header/footer with the school's branding and contact details, so that I know whose site I'm on and how to reach the school. (FR-36)\n- As a visitor, I want a simple home page with a hero section and a sign-in button, so that I can quickly understand the site and log in. (FR-37)\n\n## Error handling\n\n- As any user, I want clear 404 and error pages with a way to retry, so that something going wrong doesn't leave me stuck on a blank screen. (FR-38)\n- As any user, I want a `/forbidden` page, so that later PRDs can tell me clearly when I lack permission instead of showing a broken page. (FR-39)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **UI library discipline (NFR-1):** Material UI is the only UI/styling library. Every MUI component must be looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; a fixed list of alternative UI and styling libraries is banned and enforced by ESLint.\n- **Performance (NFR-2):** `/dashboard` must reach Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5s on a production build.\n- **Accessibility (NFR-3):** All shared components meet WCAG 2.1 AA; Playwright + axe must report zero serious/critical violations on `/` and `/dashboard`.\n- **Responsiveness (NFR-4):** Layouts must work with no horizontal scroll from 360px to 1920px wide.\n- **Security (NFR-5):** Security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, CSP) must be set in `next.config.js`.\n- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest/Testing Library unit and component tests, plus Playwright e2e (including axe scans), must cover the behaviours listed in the PRD's Test Requirements.\n- **Fast local bootstrap (NFR-7):** A fresh clone must be runnable end-to-end in under 5 minutes via the documented command sequence.\n- **Green pipeline (NFR-8):** `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` and `test:e2e` must all pass on a fresh clone.\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"totalLines":79}}}
