{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XqcaApJ6RcD5C8ddNvjAa9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (SchoolHub scaffold PRD)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t## Overview\n6\t\n7\tThis PRD is a greenfield scaffold: Next.js 14 App Router monolith, Postgres\n8\t16 via Prisma, MUI v9 as the sole UI library, centralized API helpers, and a\n9\trole-aware (but auth-unwired) app shell. Intake reported **100% confidence\n10\tand zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is nothing to flag\n11\there beyond that figure. All 48 requirements are HIGH confidence with no\n12\tclarification log entries.\n13\t\n14\tArchitecturally this is one deployable Next.js app with two route-group\n15\ttrees — `(app)` for the authenticated shell and `(public)` for the marketing\n16\tpage — sharing one design-system layer, one API-helper chokepoint\n17\t(`src/server/http.ts`), and one data model (`SchoolSettings`, a singleton\n18\trow later PRDs will extend). Auth does not exist yet: every place a later\n19\tPRD will wire sign-in (user menu, `/forbidden`, nav role-filtering) is built\n20\tas a placeholder/slot only, per the explicit \"for later PRDs\" language in\n21\tFR-33/FR-39 and the cross-cutting note in `requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n22\tNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n23\t(ADR-1 through ADR-9) already fixed — this document arranges those choices\n24\tinto components and data flow.\n25\t\n26\t## Component Breakdown\n27\t\n28\t| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files |\n29\t|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|\n30\t| 1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline, npm script surface, path alias | `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.eslintrc*` |\n31\t| 2 | Server Infra | Env validation, Prisma client singleton, structured logger, local Postgres | `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/server/db.ts`, `src/lib/logger.ts`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` |\n32\t| 3 | Data Model | Singleton `SchoolSettings` schema + idempotent seed | `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts` |\n33\t| 4 | API Layer | Response envelopes, error mapping, pagination/body parsing, the one concrete endpoint | `src/server/http.ts`, `src/app/api/health/route.ts` |\n34\t| 5 | Design System | Theme + provider tree + 10 shared MUI-composed components | `src/theme/theme.ts`, `src/components/*` |\n35\t| 6 | App Shell (authenticated) | Sidebar/top-bar layout, role-filtered nav config, student-tab extension point, dashboard page | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` |\n36\t| 7 | Public Layout & Pages | Public header/footer, landing page, error/forbidden pages | `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/global-error.tsx`, `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` |\n37\t| 8 | Lint/CI Gate | Banned-import ESLint rule, security headers | `.eslintrc*` (`no-restricted-imports`), `next.config.js` |\n38\t| 9 | Test Harness | Unit/component + e2e/axe coverage of the above | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` |\n39\t\n40\tDependency order between components: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, and 1+2 → 5 → 6/7 (the\n41\tshell and public layout both consume the design system and, for branding,\n42\t`SchoolSettings` from component 3). Component 8 wraps all of 5–7. Component\n43\t9 observes all of 2–7.\n44\t\n45\t## Data Flow\n46\t\n47\t**Page render (authenticated), e.g. `GET /dashboard`:**\n48\t1. `(app)/layout.tsx` (server component) fetches the `SchoolSettings`\n49\t   singleton once (FR-7) for top-bar branding (FR-33) — not re-queried by\n50\t   child components.\n51\t2. Root layout's provider tree (`AppRouterCacheProvider` → `ThemeProvider`\n52\t   (`cssVariables`, light/dark) → `CssBaseline` → `LocalizationProvider`,\n53\t   plus `InitColorSchemeScript`) wraps the shell so every page below inherits\n54\t   theme/mode without a client-side flash (NFR-2's LCP budget depends on\n55\t   this being server-rendered, not client-hydrated).\n56\t3. Sidebar renders from `src/config/navigation.ts`, filtered by current\n57\t   user role (role source is a stub today — no auth yet — filtering logic\n58\t   exists so later PRDs plug a real role in without touching the shell).\n59\t4. `/dashboard` page renders `PageHeader` + `EmptyState` (FR-34) — no data\n60\t   fetch beyond step 1.\n61\t\n62\t**API call, e.g. a future list endpoint or `GET /api/health`:**\n63\t1. Route handler is wrapped in `withHandler(fn)` (ADR-4) — the single\n64\t   chokepoint every route (including `/api/health`) must go through.\n65\t2. Input parsing: `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (Zod) for request shape,\n66\t   `parsePagination` for list endpoints (clamps `pageSize` ≤ 100, `page` ≥ 1).\n67\t3. Handler body runs (for `/api/health`: `SELECT 1` against Prisma with a\n68\t   2000ms budget).\n69\t4. Success → `ok(data)` or `paginated(data, meta)`; failure inside\n70\t   `withHandler` maps `ZodError` → `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `AppError` → its\n71\t   status, Prisma `P2002`/`P2025` → `CONFLICT`/`NOT_FOUND`, anything else →\n72\t   `INTERNAL` (stack logged via `src/lib/logger.ts`, never returned to the\n73\t   client).\n74\t5. Client-side, `DataTable` (for list endpoints) reads `rowCount`/`total`\n75\t   straight from the `paginated()` envelope and syncs page/sort state to URL\n76\t   query params — no separate client-side pagination state machine.\n77\t\n78\t**Env/startup flow:** `src/lib/env.ts` validates `process.env` via Zod\n79\tbefore `src/server/db.ts` or any server entrypoint runs, throwing a\n80\treadable per-variable error on failure — this is a fail-fast boundary, not"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e178deb2-f3fc-4074-b26a-6dc2b835ef23","uuid":"5aae7b44-f81b-46de-a8b4-3c6e36aa671f","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:29:16.318Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (SchoolHub scaffold PRD)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nThis PRD is a greenfield scaffold: Next.js 14 App Router monolith, Postgres\n16 via Prisma, MUI v9 as the sole UI library, centralized API helpers, and a\nrole-aware (but auth-unwired) app shell. Intake reported **100% confidence\nand zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is nothing to flag\nhere beyond that figure. All 48 requirements are HIGH confidence with no\nclarification log entries.\n\nArchitecturally this is one deployable Next.js app with two route-group\ntrees — `(app)` for the authenticated shell and `(public)` for the marketing\npage — sharing one design-system layer, one API-helper chokepoint\n(`src/server/http.ts`), and one data model (`SchoolSettings`, a singleton\nrow later PRDs will extend). Auth does not exist yet: every place a later\nPRD will wire sign-in (user menu, `/forbidden`, nav role-filtering) is built\nas a placeholder/slot only, per the explicit \"for later PRDs\" language in\nFR-33/FR-39 and the cross-cutting note in `requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\nNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9) already fixed — this document arranges those choices\ninto components and data flow.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|\n| 1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline, npm script surface, path alias | `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.eslintrc*` |\n| 2 | Server Infra | Env validation, Prisma client singleton, structured logger, local Postgres | `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/server/db.ts`, `src/lib/logger.ts`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` |\n| 3 | Data Model | Singleton `SchoolSettings` schema + idempotent seed | `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| 4 | API Layer | Response envelopes, error mapping, pagination/body parsing, the one concrete endpoint | `src/server/http.ts`, `src/app/api/health/route.ts` |\n| 5 | Design System | Theme + provider tree + 10 shared MUI-composed components | `src/theme/theme.ts`, `src/components/*` |\n| 6 | App Shell (authenticated) | Sidebar/top-bar layout, role-filtered nav config, student-tab extension point, dashboard page | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` |\n| 7 | Public Layout & Pages | Public header/footer, landing page, error/forbidden pages | `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/global-error.tsx`, `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` |\n| 8 | Lint/CI Gate | Banned-import ESLint rule, security headers | `.eslintrc*` (`no-restricted-imports`), `next.config.js` |\n| 9 | Test Harness | Unit/component + e2e/axe coverage of the above | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` |\n\nDependency order between components: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, and 1+2 → 5 → 6/7 (the\nshell and public layout both consume the design system and, for branding,\n`SchoolSettings` from component 3). Component 8 wraps all of 5–7. Component\n9 observes all of 2–7.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Page render (authenticated), e.g. `GET /dashboard`:**\n1. `(app)/layout.tsx` (server component) fetches the `SchoolSettings`\n   singleton once (FR-7) for top-bar branding (FR-33) — not re-queried by\n   child components.\n2. Root layout's provider tree (`AppRouterCacheProvider` → `ThemeProvider`\n   (`cssVariables`, light/dark) → `CssBaseline` → `LocalizationProvider`,\n   plus `InitColorSchemeScript`) wraps the shell so every page below inherits\n   theme/mode without a client-side flash (NFR-2's LCP budget depends on\n   this being server-rendered, not client-hydrated).\n3. Sidebar renders from `src/config/navigation.ts`, filtered by current\n   user role (role source is a stub today — no auth yet — filtering logic\n   exists so later PRDs plug a real role in without touching the shell).\n4. `/dashboard` page renders `PageHeader` + `EmptyState` (FR-34) — no data\n   fetch beyond step 1.\n\n**API call, e.g. a future list endpoint or `GET /api/health`:**\n1. Route handler is wrapped in `withHandler(fn)` (ADR-4) — the single\n   chokepoint every route (including `/api/health`) must go through.\n2. Input parsing: `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (Zod) for request shape,\n   `parsePagination` for list endpoints (clamps `pageSize` ≤ 100, `page` ≥ 1).\n3. Handler body runs (for `/api/health`: `SELECT 1` against Prisma with a\n   2000ms budget).\n4. Success → `ok(data)` or `paginated(data, meta)`; failure inside\n   `withHandler` maps `ZodError` → `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `AppError` → its\n   status, Prisma `P2002`/`P2025` → `CONFLICT`/`NOT_FOUND`, anything else →\n   `INTERNAL` (stack logged via `src/lib/logger.ts`, never returned to the\n   client).\n5. Client-side, `DataTable` (for list endpoints) reads `rowCount`/`total`\n   straight from the `paginated()` envelope and syncs page/sort state to URL\n   query params — no separate client-side pagination state machine.\n\n**Env/startup flow:** `src/lib/env.ts` validates `process.env` via Zod\nbefore `src/server/db.ts` or any server entrypoint runs, throwing a\nreadable per-variable error on failure — this is a fail-fast boundary, not","numLines":80,"startLine":1,"totalLines":142}}}
