s, item 2 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":64,"newStart":1,"newLines":52,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T15:09:02Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Scaffold the project with Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict mode, ESLint (next/core-web-vitals + @typescript-eslint/recommended) and Prettier.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"package.json defines scripts: dev, build, start, lint, typecheck, test, test:e2e, db:migrate, db:deploy, db:seed, db:reset, format.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"Path alias @/* maps to src/*.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"docker-compose.yml starts PostgreSQL 16 on port 5432 with a named volume and database/user/password 'schoolhub'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \".env.example lists every env var with a comment, including DATABASE_URL, APP_URL, AUTH_SECRET, NODE_ENV.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"src/lib/env.ts validates process.env with Zod at startup and throws a readable error naming each missing/invalid variable.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"prisma/schema.prisma uses the postgresql provider and defines the singleton SchoolSettings model with the fields listed in the PRD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Database, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"src/server/db.ts exports a single globalThis-cached Prisma client instance that survives hot reload in development.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Database, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"prisma/seed.ts is idempotent (re-running never creates duplicates) and creates the SchoolSettings row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Database, item 3 + Seed Data\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports ok(data, init?) returning NextResponse.json({ data }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports paginated(data, { page, pageSize, total }) returning the list response shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports apiError(code, message, details?) returning the error shape with the HTTP status mapped from the code table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports withHandler(fn) that maps ZodError to VALIDATION_ERROR, AppError to its mapped status, Prisma P2002 to CONFLICT, P2025 to NOT_FOUND, and anything else to INTERNAL (stack logged, never returned to client).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports parsePagination(searchParams) returning { page, pageSize, skip, take }, clamping pageSize to max 100 and page to min 1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports parseBody(request, schema) and parseQuery(searchParams, schema) that run Zod validation and throw on failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"GET /api/health returns 200 { data: { status: 'ok', db: 'ok', time } } when SELECT 1 succeeds within 2000ms, else 503 with db: 'error'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Health endpoint\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Install @mui/material, @emotion/react, @emotion/styled, @mui/material-nextjs, @mui/icons-material, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers and @mui/x-charts at the MUI MCP-reported v9 versions, plus the react-is@18.3.1 override required for React 18.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"src/theme/theme.ts builds the MUI theme with cssVariables, light/dark colorSchemes, the specified palette/shape/font/component defaults; root layout wraps the app in AppRouterCacheProvider + ThemeProvider + CssBaseline + LocalizationProvider, renders InitColorSchemeScript, and the top-bar toggle uses useColorScheme().setMode.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"ESLint no-restricted-imports rule fails the build on any banned UI library (tailwindcss, @radix-ui/*, @headlessui/*, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, recharts, @fullcalendar/*, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack, antd, @chakra-ui/*, react-bootstrap); no Tailwind config/plugin may exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Shared PageHeader component: Typography title, optional description, optional Breadcrumbs, optional right-side actions slot.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (PageHeader)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Shared DataTable component wrapping MUI X DataGrid with server-side pagination/sorting, rowCount from API total, debounced search, empty/loading states and URL-synced query params.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (DataTable)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Shared EmptyState component: icon, title, description, optional action button, centred layout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (EmptyState)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Shared ConfirmDialog component using MUI Dialog, destructive variant, async onConfirm with pending spinner.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (ConfirmDialog)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Shared useToast() hook + ToastProvider using a single queued MUI Snackbar + Alert, auto-hide 5 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (useToast/ToastProvider)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Shared FormField helpers bind React Hook Form Controller to MUI TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Checkbox, Switch, RadioGroup and DatePicker/DateTimePicker, wiring label/helperText/error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (FormField)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Shared StatCard component: MUI Card with label, value, optional delta Chip and icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (StatCard)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Shared UserAvatar component: MUI Avatar showing initials on a deterministic background colour derived from the user id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (UserAvatar)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Shared DateDisplay component plus formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern) util in src/lib/dates.ts formatting a UTC date in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (DateDisplay)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Shared LoadingSkeleton component with MUI Skeleton variants for table, card and form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (LoadingSkeleton)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"src/app/(app)/layout.tsx renders a permanent left sidebar Drawer (256px, collapsible to 64px icon rail, state saved to localStorage) and a top bar built with AppBar + Toolbar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"On screens narrower than 1024px the sidebar becomes a temporary Drawer opened from a hamburger IconButton.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Sidebar items are sourced from src/config/navigation.ts, filtered by the current user's role, with the active item highlighted by current path prefix; initial entry is Dashboard (/dashboard, all roles).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Top bar shows school short name/logo from SchoolSettings, a theme toggle, a placeholder notification bell, and a user menu (avatar, name, role badge, Profile/Sign out items) for later wiring by PRD-01/PRD-03/PRD-04.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"/dashboard renders a PageHeader 'Welcome to SchoolHub' and an EmptyState noting dashboards arrive in a later release.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"src/config/student-tabs.ts exists, exporting an empty typed array of { key, label, href(studentId), roles } for later PRDs to register tabs into.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"src/app/(public)/layout.tsx renders a header (logo, school name, Sign in button to /login) and a footer with school address/phone/email from SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Public layout, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"/ renders a hero section with the school name, a one-sentence tagline, and the Sign in button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Public layout, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Custom not-found.tsx (404), error.tsx (with a Try again button calling reset()), and global-error.tsx are implemented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Error and status pages, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"/forbidden page shows a 403 message with a link back to /dashboard, for use by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Error and status pages, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"src/lib/logger.ts exports logger.info|warn|error(message, meta?) writing JSON lines in production and readable lines in development.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Logging\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }","   ],"," ","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI is the only permitted UI component/styling library; every component must be looked up via the MUI MCP server before use (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs), and a fixed list of alternative UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Chakra, Ant Design, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack, etc.) is banned and enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"/dashboard must reach Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5 seconds on a mid-range laptop running the production build.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Performance)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"All shared components meet WCAG 2.1 AA: visible focus rings, labelled controls, 4.5:1 colour contrast, full keyboard operability of sidebar/dialogs/menus; Playwright e2e runs @axe-core/playwright on / and /dashboard with zero serious/critical violations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Accessibility)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Layouts work from 360px to 1920px viewport width with no horizontal scroll.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Responsiveness)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"next.config.js sets security headers: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin, X-Frame-Options: DENY, and a Content-Security-Policy restricted to self plus inline styles required by Next.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Security)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test harness uses Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests and Playwright for e2e (tests/e2e), covering withHandler branches, parsePagination, formatInSchoolTz, env.ts validation, DataTable/ConfirmDialog/useToast component behaviour, the no-restricted-imports lint rule, and the Playwright/axe scenarios listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements section\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"A fresh clone must be runnable end-to-end (docker compose up -d && npm install && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed && npm run dev) and viewable at localhost:3000 in under 5 minutes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goals, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run test and npm run test:e2e must all pass on a fresh clone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goals, item 3\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }","   ],"," ","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 100,","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,","   \"clarificationLog\": [],","   \"status\": \"complete\""," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T15:09:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Scaffold the project with Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict mode, ESLint (next/core-web-vitals + @typescript-eslint/recommended) and Prettier.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"package.json defines scripts: dev, build, start, lint, typecheck, test, test:e2e, db:migrate, db:deploy, db:seed, db:reset, format.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"Path alias @/* maps to src/*.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"docker-compose.yml starts PostgreSQL 16 on port 5432 with a named volume and database/user/password 'schoolhub'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \".env.example lists every env var with a comment, including DATABASE_URL, APP_URL, AUTH_SECRET, NODE_ENV.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"src/lib/env.ts validates process.env with Zod at startup and throws a readable error naming each missing/invalid variable.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Project scaffold, item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"prisma/schema.prisma uses the postgresql provider and defines the singleton SchoolSettings model with the fields listed in the PRD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Database, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"src/server/db.ts exports a single globalThis-cached Prisma client instance that survives hot reload in development.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Database, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"prisma/seed.ts is idempotent (re-running never creates duplicates) and creates the SchoolSettings row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Database, item 3 + Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports ok(data, init?) returning NextResponse.json({ data }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports paginated(data, { page, pageSize, total }) returning the list response shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports apiError(code, message, details?) returning the error shape with the HTTP status mapped from the code table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports withHandler(fn) that maps ZodError to VALIDATION_ERROR, AppError to its mapped status, Prisma P2002 to CONFLICT, P2025 to NOT_FOUND, and anything else to INTERNAL (stack logged, never returned to client).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports parsePagination(searchParams) returning { page, pageSize, skip, take }, clamping pageSize to max 100 and page to min 1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"src/server/http.ts exports parseBody(request, schema) and parseQuery(searchParams, schema) that run Zod validation and throw on failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 API helpers, item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"GET /api/health returns 200 { data: { status: 'ok', db: 'ok', time } } when SELECT 1 succeeds within 2000ms, else 503 with db: 'error'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Health endpoint\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Install @mui/material, @emotion/react, @emotion/styled, @mui/material-nextjs, @mui/icons-material, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers and @mui/x-charts at the MUI MCP-reported v9 versions, plus the react-is@18.3.1 override required for React 18.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"src/theme/theme.ts builds the MUI theme with cssVariables, light/dark colorSchemes, the specified palette/shape/font/component defaults; root layout wraps the app in AppRouterCacheProvider + ThemeProvider + CssBaseline + LocalizationProvider, renders InitColorSchemeScript, and the top-bar toggle uses useColorScheme().setMode.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"ESLint no-restricted-imports rule fails the build on any banned UI library (tailwindcss, @radix-ui/*, @headlessui/*, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, recharts, @fullcalendar/*, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack, antd, @chakra-ui/*, react-bootstrap); no Tailwind config/plugin may exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Shared PageHeader component: Typography title, optional description, optional Breadcrumbs, optional right-side actions slot.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (PageHeader)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Shared DataTable component wrapping MUI X DataGrid with server-side pagination/sorting, rowCount from API total, debounced search, empty/loading states and URL-synced query params.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (DataTable)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Shared EmptyState component: icon, title, description, optional action button, centred layout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (EmptyState)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Shared ConfirmDialog component using MUI Dialog, destructive variant, async onConfirm with pending spinner.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (ConfirmDialog)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Shared useToast() hook + ToastProvider using a single queued MUI Snackbar + Alert, auto-hide 5 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (useToast/ToastProvider)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Shared FormField helpers bind React Hook Form Controller to MUI TextField, Select, Autocomplete, Checkbox, Switch, RadioGroup and DatePicker/DateTimePicker, wiring label/helperText/error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (FormField)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Shared StatCard component: MUI Card with label, value, optional delta Chip and icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (StatCard)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Shared UserAvatar component: MUI Avatar showing initials on a deterministic background colour derived from the user id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (UserAvatar)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Shared DateDisplay component plus formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern) util in src/lib/dates.ts formatting a UTC date in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (DateDisplay)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Shared LoadingSkeleton component with MUI Skeleton variants for table, card and form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Design system, item 4 (LoadingSkeleton)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"src/app/(app)/layout.tsx renders a permanent left sidebar Drawer (256px, collapsible to 64px icon rail, state saved to localStorage) and a top bar built with AppBar + Toolbar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"On screens narrower than 1024px the sidebar becomes a temporary Drawer opened from a hamburger IconButton.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Sidebar items are sourced from src/config/navigation.ts, filtered by the current user's role, with the active item highlighted by current path prefix; initial entry is Dashboard (/dashboard, all roles).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Top bar shows school short name/logo from SchoolSettings, a theme toggle, a placeholder notification bell, and a user menu (avatar, name, role badge, Profile/Sign out items) for later wiring by PRD-01/PRD-03/PRD-04.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"/dashboard renders a PageHeader 'Welcome to SchoolHub' and an EmptyState noting dashboards arrive in a later release.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"src/config/student-tabs.ts exists, exporting an empty typed array of { key, label, href(studentId), roles } for later PRDs to register tabs into.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 App shell, item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"src/app/(public)/layout.tsx renders a header (logo, school name, Sign in button to /login) and a footer with school address/phone/email from SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Public layout, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"/ renders a hero section with the school name, a one-sentence tagline, and the Sign in button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Public layout, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Custom not-found.tsx (404), error.tsx (with a Try again button calling reset()), and global-error.tsx are implemented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Error and status pages, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"/forbidden page shows a 403 message with a link back to /dashboard, for use by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Error and status pages, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"src/lib/logger.ts exports logger.info|warn|error(message, meta?) writing JSON lines in production and readable lines in development.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Logging\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI is the only permitted UI component/styling library; every component must be looked up via the MUI MCP server before use (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs), and a fixed list of alternative UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Chakra, Ant Design, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack, etc.) is banned and enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"/dashboard must reach Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5 seconds on a mid-range laptop running the production build.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"All shared components meet WCAG 2.1 AA: visible focus rings, labelled controls, 4.5:1 colour contrast, full keyboard operability of sidebar/dialogs/menus; Playwright e2e runs @axe-core/playwright on / and /dashboard with zero serious/critical violations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Accessibility)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Layouts work from 360px to 1920px viewport width with no horizontal scroll.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Responsiveness)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"next.config.js sets security headers: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin, X-Frame-Options: DENY, and a Content-Security-Policy restricted to self plus inline styles required by Next.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test harness uses Vitest + Testing Library for unit/component tests and Playwright for e2e (tests/e2e), covering withHandler branches, parsePagination, formatInSchoolTz, env.ts validation, DataTable/ConfirmDialog/useToast component behaviour, the no-restricted-imports lint rule, and the Playwright/axe scenarios listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements section\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"A fresh clone must be runnable end-to-end (docker compose up -d && npm install && npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed && npm run dev) and viewable at localhost:3000 in under 5 minutes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goals, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run test and npm run test:e2e must all pass on a fresh clone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goals, item 3\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 100,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false}}
