\n- As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active, so that I'm not logged out mid-task. (FR-9)\n- As a user, I want changing my password to sign out my other devices, so that a stolen session stops working once I secure my account. (FR-10)\n- As a user, I want unauthenticated page and API requests to be redirected or rejected automatically, so that protected data is never reachable without signing in. (FR-11)\n\n## Accept invitation\n\n- As an invited user, I want my invitation link checked for validity and expiry, so that I can't use a stale or reused link. (FR-12)\n- As an invited user, I want to see my name and email confirmed on the invite page, so that I know the invitation is really for me. (FR-13)\n- As an invited user, I want to set my own password from the invitation link, so that I can access SchoolHub for the first time. (FR-14)\n\n## Password policy\n\n- As an admin, I want new passwords to meet a minimum-strength policy, so that weak or common passwords can't be chosen. (FR-15)\n- As a user, I want to see a live checklist of password rules as I type, so that I know exactly what's still missing. (FR-16)\n\n## Forgot / reset password\n\n- As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link without revealing whether my email has an account, so that I can regain access without exposing other users' accounts. (FR-17)\n- As a user who forgot my password, I want a time-limited reset link emailed to me, so that only I can use it and only briefly. (FR-18)\n- As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link, so that I can get back into my account. (FR-19)\n\n## Change password (signed in)\n\n- As a user, I want to change my password while signed in, so that I can keep my account secure. (FR-20)\n- As a user, I want an \"Account security\" entry in my user menu, so that I can find the change-password page easily. (FR-21)\n\n## Services, permissions & auditing (for later PRDs)\n\n- As a developer, I want user-management service functions (createUser, invite, status, unlock), so that PRD-03's admin screens can be built on top without re-implementing auth logic. (FR-22)\n- As a developer, I want requireUser()/requireRole() permission helpers, so that restricting a handler or page to a role is a one-line call. (FR-23)\n- As a developer, I want a reusable audit() helper that never leaks secrets into audit metadata, so that every later PRD can record security-relevant actions consistently and safely. (FR-24)\n\n## App shell integration\n\n- As a user, I want the top-bar user menu to show my real name, role and initials and to actually sign me out, so that the placeholder from PRD-00 is replaced with my real session. (FR-25)\n- As a user, I want the sidebar to reflect my real role, so that I only see navigation I'm allowed to use. (FR-26)\n- As a developer, I want sendAuthEmail() to log emails to the console until PRD-04 lands, so that auth flows are testable before real email delivery exists. (FR-27)\n\n## Seed data\n\n- As a developer, I want seed accounts for every role plus one pending invitation, so that I can test and demo every sign-in/invite path immediately. (FR-28)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **Security (NFR-1):** Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and every auth form carries Auth.js CSRF protection.\n- **Security (NFR-2):** Sign-in timing for \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" must be similar, preventing user enumeration via response time.\n- **Performance (NFR-3):** Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **Accessibility (NFR-4):** Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"` and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\n- **UI library discipline (NFR-5):** Every visible element is built from Material UI only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned-library list is ESLint-enforced.\n- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest unit tests (policy, tokens, lockout, rate limiter, callbackUrl check), Vitest integration tests (authorize, invite, reset, change-password), and Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed login, forgot→reset).\n- **Brownfield discipline (NFR-7):** Reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.\n- **Delivery discipline (NFR-8):** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests listed in this PRD, and don't expand scope beyond it or touch behaviour owned by later PRDs.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":78,"newStart":1,"newLines":72,"lines":["-# User Stories — PRD-00 Project Foundation, App Shell & Design System","+# User Stories — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control"," ","-Ticket: abcd-1 · Phase: intake","+Ticket: abcd-2 · Phase: intake"," ","-## Project scaffold & tooling","+## Data model"," ","-- As a developer, I want the project scaffolded with Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, ESLint and Prettier, so that the codebase has a consistent, enforced baseline. (FR-1)","-- As a developer, I want standard npm scripts (dev/build/start/lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e/db:migrate/db:deploy/db:seed/db:reset/format), so that every later PRD can build, test and manage the database the same way. (FR-2)","-- As a developer, I want the `@/*` path alias mapped to `src/*`, so that imports stay short and consistent. (FR-3)","-- As a developer, I want a `docker-compose.yml` that starts Postgres 16 with a named volume and the `schoolhub` database/user, so that I can run the full stack locally with one command. (FR-4)","-- As a developer, I want a documented `.env.example`, so that I know every environment variable the app needs before I start it. (FR-5)","-- As a developer, I want startup-time Zod validation of `process.env`, so that a missing or invalid variable fails fast with a readable error instead of a cryptic runtime crash. (FR-6)","+- As the platform, I need User, AuthToken and AuditLog models with role/status/lockout fields, so that every later feature can authenticate, scope and audit users against one source of truth. (FR-1)"," ","-## Database","+## Sign-in"," ","-- As a developer, I want a Prisma schema with the singleton `SchoolSettings` model, so that school-wide settings have one source of truth. (FR-7)","-- As a developer, I want a single cached Prisma client instance, so that hot reload in development doesn't exhaust database connections. (FR-8)","-- As a developer, I want an idempotent seed script that creates the `SchoolSettings` row, so that re-running the seed never duplicates data. (FR-9)","+- As a user, I want to sign in with email and password on a Material UI /login form with a show-password toggle, so that I can see my information. (FR-2)","+- As a user, I want the system to reject sign-in for a non-existent, non-active, archived or locked account, so that only legitimate active accounts can get in. (FR-3)","+- As a user, I want wrong-password, locked and disabled sign-ins to show distinct, clear messages, so that I understand why I can't get in without leaking which emails exist. (FR-4)","+- As an admin, I want accounts to lock after 5 failed sign-ins for 15 minutes, so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. (FR-5)","+- As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP, so that a single source cannot hammer the login endpoint. (FR-6)","+- As a user, I want to land back on the page I was headed to after signing in, so that I don't lose my place. (FR-7)","+- As an admin, I want every sign-in success, failure and lockout audited, so that I can investigate security incidents. (FR-8)"," ","-## API helpers","+## Session"," ","-- As a developer, I want a shared `ok()` helper, so that every successful API response has the same `{ data }` shape. (FR-10)","-- As a developer, I want a shared `paginated()` helper, so that every list endpoint returns the same `{ data, page, pageSize, total }` shape. (FR-11)","-- As a developer, I want a shared `apiError()` helper, so that every error response has the same shape and the correct HTTP status. (FR-12)","-- As a developer, I want a `withHandler()` wrapper that maps Zod, AppError and Prisma errors to the right error codes, so that route handlers stay thin and error handling stays consistent. (FR-13)","-- As a developer, I want a `parsePagination()` helper that clamps page/pageSize to safe bounds, so that no endpoint can be asked to return an unbounded page. (FR-14)","-- As a developer, I want `parseBody()`/`parseQuery()` helpers, so that every handler validates input the same way. (FR-15)","+- As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active, so that I'm not logged out mid-task. (FR-9)","+- As a user, I want changing my password to sign out my other devices, so that a stolen session stops working once I secure my account. (FR-10)","+- As a user, I want unauthenticated page and API requests to be redirected or rejected automatically, so that protected data is never reachable without signing in. (FR-11)"," ","-## Health & observability","+## Accept invitation"," ","-- As an operator, I want a `GET /api/health` endpoint that checks the database, so that I can monitor whether the app and its database connection are healthy. (FR-16)","-- As a developer, I want a shared `logger` with info/warn/error levels, so that logging is structured and consistent instead of scattered `console.log` calls. (FR-40)","+- As an invited user, I want my invitation link checked for validity and expiry, so that I can't use a stale or reused link. (FR-12)","+- As an invited user, I want to see my name and email confirmed on the invite page, so that I know the invitation is really for me. (FR-13)","+- As an invited user, I want to set my own password from the invitation link, so that I can access SchoolHub for the first time. (FR-14)"," ","-## Design system","+## Password policy"," ","-- As a developer, I want the exact MUI v9 package set installed at the versions reported by the MUI MCP server, so that every later PRD builds against a known-good, documented version. (FR-17)","-- As any user, I want a theme with light/dark colour schemes and a toggle that persists my preference, so that I can use SchoolHub comfortably without a flash of the wrong mode. (FR-18)","-- As a developer, I want an ESLint rule that fails the build on any banned UI/styling library, so that the \"Material UI only\" rule is enforced automatically, not just by convention. (FR-19)","-- As a developer, I want a shared `PageHeader` component, so that every page has a consistent title/description/actions layout. (FR-20)","-- As a developer, I want a shared `DataTable` component wrapping MUI X DataGrid with server-side paging/sorting/search, so that every list screen in later PRDs behaves the same way. (FR-21)","-- As any user, I want a shared `EmptyState` component, so that empty lists and unfinished pages look intentional instead of blank. (FR-22)","-- As any user, I want a shared `ConfirmDialog`, so that destructive actions always ask for confirmation the same way. (FR-23)","-- As any user, I want a shared toast notification system, so that I get consistent feedback after actions across the app. (FR-24)","-- As a developer, I want shared `FormField` helpers wiring React Hook Form to MUI inputs, so that every form in later PRDs has consistent labels, errors and helper text. (FR-25)","-- As any user, I want a shared `StatCard` component, so that future dashboards can present metrics consistently. (FR-26)","-- As any user, I want a shared `UserAvatar` component with deterministic initials/colour, so that I can recognise people consistently across the app. (FR-27)","-- As any user, I want dates displayed in the school's timezone via a shared `DateDisplay` component, so that I never have to mentally convert UTC timestamps. (FR-28)","-- As any user, I want a shared `LoadingSkeleton`, so that loading states look consistent across tables, cards and forms. (FR-29)","+- As an admin, I want new passwords to meet a minimum-strength policy, so that weak or common passwords can't be chosen. (FR-15)","+- As a user, I want to see a live checklist of password rules as I type, so that I know exactly what's still missing. (FR-16)"," ","-## App shell","+## Forgot / reset password"," ","-- As any authenticated user, I want a persistent sidebar and top bar, so that I can navigate SchoolHub consistently from any screen. (FR-30)","-- As a mobile user, I want the sidebar to become a temporary drawer opened from a hamburger button on narrow screens, so that navigation doesn't crowd out content on my phone. (FR-31)","-- As any authenticated user, I want the sidebar to show only the navigation items relevant to my role, with the current page highlighted, so that I'm not shown options I can't use. (FR-32)","-- As any authenticated user, I want the top bar to show the school's name/logo, a theme toggle, a notification bell and a user menu, so that I have consistent, at-a-glance context and account actions. (FR-33)","-- As any authenticated user, I want a welcoming `/dashboard` page, so that I land somewhere meaningful even before dashboards are built. (FR-34)","-- As a developer, I want an empty, typed `student-tabs.ts` config, so that later PRDs can register student-detail tabs without creating new pages. (FR-35)","+- As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link without revealing whether my email has an account, so that I can regain access without exposing other users' accounts. (FR-17)","+- As a user who forgot my password, I want a time-limited reset link emailed to me, so that only I can use it and only briefly. (FR-18)","+- As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link, so that I can get back into my account. (FR-19)"," ","-## Public site","+## Change password (signed in)"," ","-- As a visitor, I want a public header/footer with the school's branding and contact details, so that I know whose site I'm on and how to reach the school. (FR-36)","-- As a visitor, I want a simple home page with a hero section and a sign-in button, so that I can quickly understand the site and log in. (FR-37)","+- As a user, I want to change my password while signed in, so that I can keep my account secure. (FR-20)","+- As a user, I want an \"Account security\" entry in my user menu, so that I can find the change-password page easily. (FR-21)"," ","-## Error handling","+## Services, permissions & auditing (for later PRDs)"," ","-- As any user, I want clear 404 and error pages with a way to retry, so that something going wrong doesn't leave me stuck on a blank screen. (FR-38)","-- As any user, I want a `/forbidden` page, so that later PRDs can tell me clearly when I lack permission instead of showing a broken page. (FR-39)","+- As a developer, I want user-management service functions (createUser, invite, status, unlock), so that PRD-03's admin screens can be built on top without re-implementing auth logic. (FR-22)","+- As a developer, I want requireUser()/requireRole() permission helpers, so that restricting a handler or page to a role is a one-line call. (FR-23)","+- As a developer, I want a reusable audit() helper that never leaks secrets into audit metadata, so that every later PRD can record security-relevant actions consistently and safely. (FR-24)"," ","+## App shell integration","+","+- As a user, I want the top-bar user menu to show my real name, role and initials and to actually sign me out, so that the placeholder from PRD-00 is replaced with my real session. (FR-25)","+- As a user, I want the sidebar to reflect my real role, so that I only see navigation I'm allowed to use. (FR-26)","+- As a developer, I want sendAuthEmail() to log emails to the console until PRD-04 lands, so that auth flows are testable before real email delivery exists. (FR-27)","+","+## Seed data","+","+- As a developer, I want seed accounts for every role plus one pending invitation, so that I can test and demo every sign-in/invite path immediately. (FR-28)","+"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **UI library discipline (NFR-1):** Material UI is the only UI/styling library. Every MUI component must be looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; a fixed list of alternative UI and styling libraries is banned and enforced by ESLint.","-- **Performance (NFR-2):** `/dashboard` must reach Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5s on a production build.","-- **Accessibility (NFR-3):** All shared components meet WCAG 2.1 AA; Playwright + axe must report zero serious/critical violations on `/` and `/dashboard`.","-- **Responsiveness (NFR-4):** Layouts must work with no horizontal scroll from 360px to 1920px wide.","-- **Security (NFR-5):** Security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, CSP) must be set in `next.config.js`.","-- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest/Testing Library unit and component tests, plus Playwright e2e (including axe scans), must cover the behaviours listed in the PRD's Test Requirements.","-- **Fast local bootstrap (NFR-7):** A fresh clone must be runnable end-to-end in under 5 minutes via the documented command sequence.","-- **Green pipeline (NFR-8):** `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` and `test:e2e` must all pass on a fresh clone.","+- **Security (NFR-1):** Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and every auth form carries Auth.js CSRF protection.","+- **Security (NFR-2):** Sign-in timing for \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" must be similar, preventing user enumeration via response time.","+- **Performance (NFR-3):** Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12).","+- **Accessibility (NFR-4):** Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"` and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.","+- **UI library discipline (NFR-5):** Every visible element is built from Material UI only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned-library list is ESLint-enforced.","+- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest unit tests (policy, tokens, lockout, rate limiter, callbackUrl check), Vitest integration tests (authorize, invite, reset, change-password), and Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed login, forgot→reset).","+- **Brownfield discipline (NFR-7):** Reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.","+- **Delivery discipline (NFR-8):** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests listed in this PRD, and don't expand scope beyond it or touch behaviour owned by later PRDs."]}],"originalFile":"# User Stories — PRD-00 Project Foundation, App Shell & Design System\n\nTicket: abcd-1 · Phase: intake\n\n## Project scaffold & tooling\n\n- As a developer, I want the project scaffolded with Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript strict, ESLint and Prettier, so that the codebase has a consistent, enforced baseline. (FR-1)\n- As a developer, I want standard npm scripts (dev/build/start/lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e/db:migrate/db:deploy/db:seed/db:reset/format), so that every later PRD can build, test and manage the database the same way. (FR-2)\n- As a developer, I want the `@/*` path alias mapped to `src/*`, so that imports stay short and consistent. (FR-3)\n- As a developer, I want a `docker-compose.yml` that starts Postgres 16 with a named volume and the `schoolhub` database/user, so that I can run the full stack locally with one command. (FR-4)\n- As a developer, I want a documented `.env.example`, so that I know every environment variable the app needs before I start it. (FR-5)\n- As a developer, I want startup-time Zod validation of `process.env`, so that a missing or invalid variable fails fast with a readable error instead of a cryptic runtime crash. (FR-6)\n\n## Database\n\n- As a developer, I want a Prisma schema with the singleton `SchoolSettings` model, so that school-wide settings have one source of truth. (FR-7)\n- As a developer, I want a single cached Prisma client instance, so that hot reload in development doesn't exhaust database connections. (FR-8)\n- As a developer, I want an idempotent seed script that creates the `SchoolSettings` row, so that re-running the seed never duplicates data. (FR-9)\n\n## API helpers\n\n- As a developer, I want a shared `ok()` helper, so that every successful API response has the same `{ data }` shape. (FR-10)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `paginated()` helper, so that every list endpoint returns the same `{ data, page, pageSize, total }` shape. (FR-11)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `apiError()` helper, so that every error response has the same shape and the correct HTTP status. (FR-12)\n- As a developer, I want a `withHandler()` wrapper that maps Zod, AppError and Prisma errors to the right error codes, so that route handlers stay thin and error handling stays consistent. (FR-13)\n- As a developer, I want a `parsePagination()` helper that clamps page/pageSize to safe bounds, so that no endpoint can be asked to return an unbounded page. (FR-14)\n- As a developer, I want `parseBody()`/`parseQuery()` helpers, so that every handler validates input the same way. (FR-15)\n\n## Health & observability\n\n- As an operator, I want a `GET /api/health` endpoint that checks the database, so that I can monitor whether the app and its database connection are healthy. (FR-16)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `logger` with info/warn/error levels, so that logging is structured and consistent instead of scattered `console.log` calls. (FR-40)\n\n## Design system\n\n- As a developer, I want the exact MUI v9 package set installed at the versions reported by the MUI MCP server, so that every later PRD builds against a known-good, documented version. (FR-17)\n- As any user, I want a theme with light/dark colour schemes and a toggle that persists my preference, so that I can use SchoolHub comfortably without a flash of the wrong mode. (FR-18)\n- As a developer, I want an ESLint rule that fails the build on any banned UI/styling library, so that the \"Material UI only\" rule is enforced automatically, not just by convention. (FR-19)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `PageHeader` component, so that every page has a consistent title/description/actions layout. (FR-20)\n- As a developer, I want a shared `DataTable` component wrapping MUI X DataGrid with server-side paging/sorting/search, so that every list screen in later PRDs behaves the same way. (FR-21)\n- As any user, I want a shared `EmptyState` component, so that empty lists and unfinished pages look intentional instead of blank. (FR-22)\n- As any user, I want a shared `ConfirmDialog`, so that destructive actions always ask for confirmation the same way. (FR-23)\n- As any user, I want a shared toast notification system, so that I get consistent feedback after actions across the app. (FR-24)\n- As a developer, I want shared `FormField` helpers wiring React Hook Form to MUI inputs, so that every form in later PRDs has consistent labels, errors and helper text. (FR-25)\n- As any user, I want a shared `StatCard` component, so that future dashboards can present metrics consistently. (FR-26)\n- As any user, I want a shared `UserAvatar` component with deterministic initials/colour, so that I can recognise people consistently across the app. (FR-27)\n- As any user, I want dates displayed in the school's timezone via a shared `DateDisplay` component, so that I never have to mentally convert UTC timestamps. (FR-28)\n- As any user, I want a shared `LoadingSkeleton`, so that loading states look consistent across tables, cards and forms. (FR-29)\n\n## App shell\n\n- As any authenticated user, I want a persistent sidebar and top bar, so that I can navigate SchoolHub consistently from any screen. (FR-30)\n- As a mobile user, I want the sidebar to become a temporary drawer opened from a hamburger button on narrow screens, so that navigation doesn't crowd out content on my phone. (FR-31)\n- As any authenticated user, I want the sidebar to show only the navigation items relevant to my role, with the current page highlighted, so that I'm not shown options I can't use. (FR-32)\n- As any authenticated user, I want the top bar to show the school's name/logo, a theme toggle, a notification bell and a user menu, so that I have consistent, at-a-glance context and account actions. (FR-33)\n- As any authenticated user, I want a welcoming `/dashboard` page, so that I land somewhere meaningful even before dashboards are built. (FR-34)\n- As a developer, I want an empty, typed `student-tabs.ts` config, so that later PRDs can register student-detail tabs without creating new pages. (FR-35)\n\n## Public site\n\n- As a visitor, I want a public header/footer with the school's branding and contact details, so that I know whose site I'm on and how to reach the school. (FR-36)\n- As a visitor, I want a simple home page with a hero section and a sign-in button, so that I can quickly understand the site and log in. (FR-37)\n\n## Error handling\n\n- As any user, I want clear 404 and error pages with a way to retry, so that something going wrong doesn't leave me stuck on a blank screen. (FR-38)\n- As any user, I want a `/forbidden` page, so that later PRDs can tell me clearly when I lack permission instead of showing a broken page. (FR-39)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **UI library discipline (NFR-1):** Material UI is the only UI/styling library. Every MUI component must be looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; a fixed list of alternative UI and styling libraries is banned and enforced by ESLint.\n- **Performance (NFR-2):** `/dashboard` must reach Largest Contentful Paint under 2.5s on a production build.\n- **Accessibility (NFR-3):** All shared components meet WCAG 2.1 AA; Playwright + axe must report zero serious/critical violations on `/` and `/dashboard`.\n- **Responsiveness (NFR-4):** Layouts must work with no horizontal scroll from 360px to 1920px wide.\n- **Security (NFR-5):** Security headers (`X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `X-Frame-Options`, CSP) must be set in `next.config.js`.\n- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest/Testing Library unit and component tests, plus Playwright e2e (including axe scans), must cover the behaviours listed in the PRD's Test Requirements.\n- **Fast local bootstrap (NFR-7):** A fresh clone must be runnable end-to-end in under 5 minutes via the documented command sequence.\n- **Green pipeline (NFR-8):** `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` and `test:e2e` must all pass on a fresh clone.\n","userModified":false}}
