FR-11** As an admin, I want a banner when no year is marked current, so that I immediately know to fix a broken default before other features misbehave.\n\n## Terms\n\n- **FR-12** As an admin, I want a detail page per academic year listing its terms in order, so that I can manage a year's terms in one place.\n- **FR-13** As an admin, I want term dates validated against their parent year and against sibling terms, so that terms never fall outside the year or overlap each other.\n- **FR-14** As an admin, I want a \"Generate terms\" shortcut for semesters/trimesters/quarters, so that I don't have to hand-compute equal date ranges for a new year.\n\n## Grade levels\n\n- **FR-15** As an admin, I want to create, edit, reorder and archive grade levels, so that classes can later be organized by grade.\n\n## Subjects\n\n- **FR-16** As an admin, I want to create, edit, search and colour-code subjects with a unique uppercase code, so that classes, timetables and calendars can reference a consistent subject list.\n\n## Rooms\n\n- **FR-17** As an admin, I want to create, edit and archive rooms with building and capacity, so that classes can later be scheduled into a real space.\n\n## Navigation\n\n- **FR-18** As an admin, I want an \"Administration\" sidebar group linking to all five screens above, so that I can find school configuration without hunting for URLs.\n\n## API\n\n- **FR-19** As a frontend or integration client, I want a consistent REST surface (settings, academic-years, terms, grade-levels, subjects, rooms) with role-gated writes and the shared response envelope, so that every screen above has a predictable backend to call.\n\n## Seed data\n\n- **FR-20** As a developer running the seed script, I want a ready-made academic year, terms, grade levels, subjects and rooms, so that every later PRD and local demo has realistic data to build against.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 (Integrity)** Overlap/range checks for years and terms run inside a database transaction, so concurrent requests can't both succeed and corrupt the schedule.\n- **NFR-2 (Performance)** Admin list pages render under 500ms at 50 records.\n- **NFR-3 (Usability)** Every table has an empty state with a \"Create …\" call to action.\n- **NFR-4 (UI discipline)** Every visible element is Material UI only, looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries are blocked by ESLint.\n- **NFR-5 (Timezones)** All timestamps are stored UTC and displayed in `SchoolSettings.timezone`; date-only fields use `@db.Date`.\n- **NFR-6 (AuthZ)** Every write is ADMIN-only, enforced server-side; a non-admin write returns 403.\n- **NFR-7 (Auditability & envelope)** Every write audits via the existing `audit()` helper and responses follow the shared `{ data }` / list / `{ error }` envelope.\n- **NFR-8 (Tests)** Vitest unit + integration coverage for overlap detection, term generation, code normalisation, set-current transaction and delete-in-use conflict; Playwright e2e for the core admin flows.\n- **NFR-9 (Brownfield discipline)** Reuse existing PRD-00/PRD-01 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.\n- **NFR-10 (Scope discipline)** Keep lint/typecheck/test green; don't expand into sections/courses, bell-schedule periods, grading scales or holidays (later PRDs).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
