01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":52,"newStart":1,"newLines":55,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-03\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T14:05:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: StudentProfile, TeacherProfile, ParentProfile and ParentStudentLink models (plus Gender and GuardianRelationship enums) with relations added from User to each profile and to ParentStudentLink as parent and as student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"User list (/admin/users) DataTable columns: avatar + full name, email, role chip, status chip (Invited=warning, Active=success, Disabled=default, Archived=outlined), grade level (students), last sign-in, actions menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"User list filters: role (multi-select), status, grade level (shown when role filter includes Student), search by name/email/admission number/employee number; archived users hidden unless 'Show archived' is checked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"User list row actions: View, Edit, Resend invitation (status Invited), Unlock (when lockedUntil > now), Disable/Enable, Archive/Restore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"User list bulk actions on selected rows: Resend invitations, Disable, Export CSV.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Create/edit user form is an MUI Stepper: step 1 selects role, step 2 shows common fields (first/last name, email, phone) plus role-specific fields for Student, Teacher and Parent (including inline linking/creation of family members).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Checkbox 'Send invitation email now' (default checked) calls sendInvite on user creation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Email changes on an existing user require a confirmation dialog and invalidate pending invite tokens.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Role cannot be changed after user creation; the edit form shows it read-only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Validation: student date of birth must make them between 3 and 21 years old; phone must match the pattern ^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"User detail page (/admin/users/[id]) shows profile data, status, last sign-in, linked family members (with links), and the 20 most recent audit entries where the user is actor or entity.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 User detail, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Disable sets status=DISABLED; the PRD-01 session check is extended so the user's sessions stop working within 5 minutes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Archive sets archivedAt=now and status=DISABLED; archived users are excluded from all pickers app-wide but their historical records remain visible.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"An admin cannot disable or archive their own account, and the last active admin cannot be disabled, erroring with 'At least one active admin is required.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Parent-student links are managed from either the student or parent form, and from a 'Family' card on the student detail page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A student can have at most 4 linked parents; exactly one link per student may be isPrimary (setting one clears the others).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/student-access.ts exports getAccessibleStudentIds(user) (role-based accessible student id resolution, returning [] for TEACHER until PRD-05) and assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId) (throws FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND for parents/students to avoid revealing existence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"CSV import page (/admin/users/import) provides downloadable students-template.csv and teachers-template.csv with the specified column headers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"CSV upload (max 2 MB, max 2,000 rows) is parsed in the browser with papaparse into a preview DataGrid marking each row Valid, Warning or Error with a per-cell reason.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"'Import N valid rows' sends rows to POST /api/users/import in batches of 200; the server re-validates every row, creates users and links in one transaction per batch, and returns per-row results.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Import option 'Send invitations after import' (default off); grade levels matched by name or shortName case-insensitively; dates accepted only as YYYY-MM-DD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"After import, show a summary (created students, created parents, linked existing parents, failed rows) and a 'Download error report' CSV listing failed rows with reasons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Re-importing the same file creates no duplicates: rows whose email already exists are reported as 'Skipped — already exists'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Student detail page (/students/[studentId]) header shows avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status; this PRD registers an 'Overview' tab (profile, family, emergency contact; medical notes only for ADMIN and TEACHER) in src/config/student-tabs.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Student detail page, item 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Student detail page access is gated through assertCanViewStudent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Student detail page, item 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Parent 'My children' page (/my-children, PARENT only) lists linked children as cards (name, grade level, admission number) linking to /students/[id], with an empty state when none are linked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Parent 'My children'\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Self-service profile page (/account/profile): any user sees their own name/email/role (read-only) and can edit phone, plus occupation and address for parents; a 'Profile' entry is added to the user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Profile\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"GET /api/users/search?role=&q= returns up to 20 {id, name, email, role} matches excluding archived users (ADMIN/TEACHER only), consumed by a reusable UserPicker component built on MUI Autocomplete (async options, multiple support, avatar+name+role renderOption).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 Directory pickers\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Audit log viewer (/admin/audit-log): read-only table of time, actor, action, entity type, entity id (linked when a user), IP, with filters for actor, action prefix and date range; a row click opens a right-anchored Drawer with pretty-printed metadata JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-12 Audit log viewer\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Navigation: Administration group gains Users, Import users and Audit log entries; Parents get 'My children'; all users get 'Profile' in the user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-13 Navigation\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"POST /api/users/:id/unlock clears the lockout fields (lockedUntil/failedLoginCount) set by the PRD-01 lockout mechanism, restoring sign-in access immediately.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table, 'POST /api/users/:id/unlock' row — behaviour inferred from the PRD-01 lockout fields this PRD's row action operates on\" }","   ],"," ","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Privacy: medicalNotes must never be returned to STUDENT or PARENT roles (enforced in the service layer, stripped from GET /api/students/:id for those roles) and must be excluded from exported CSVs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Privacy)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the user list must return a page in under 300 ms with 5,000 users, backed by an index on lastName, firstName, email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Performance)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an import batch either fully succeeds or fully rolls back; partial batches never persist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Reliability)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: CSV export must neutralise formula injection by prefixing cells starting with =, +, -, @ with a leading apostrophe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Security)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design, react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) is enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping and getAccessibleStudentIds per role; Vitest integration tests for import batch rollback, the last-admin guard and primary-link uniqueness; Playwright e2e for create-student-with-parent, CSV import happy path with an error row, and parent My-children → student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }","   ],"," ","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,","   \"clarificationLog\": [],","   \"status\": \"complete\""," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false}}
