FR-21** As an admin, I want to optionally send invitations after import and have grade levels matched case-insensitively so that onboarding a whole year is low-friction.","+- **FR-22** As an admin, I want an import summary and a downloadable error report so that I can see exactly what happened to each row.","+- **FR-23** As an admin, I want re-importing the same file to skip existing users instead of duplicating them so that imports are safe to retry.","+- **FR-24** As any authenticated user with access, I want a student detail page with an Overview tab (profile, family, emergency contact) so that I can see a student's core information.","+- **FR-25** As any user, I want the student detail page to enforce `assertCanViewStudent` so that I can't see students I'm not allowed to see.","+- **FR-26** As a parent, I want a \"My children\" page listing my linked students so that I can jump to each child's information.","+- **FR-27** As any user, I want a profile page where I can edit my phone (and occupation/address if I'm a parent) so that the school can reach me.","+- **FR-28** As an admin or teacher, I want a searchable user picker (`/api/users/search` + `UserPicker`) so that I can quickly find and select people in forms.","+- **FR-29** As an admin, I want a read-only audit log viewer with filters and a metadata drawer so that I can see who changed what.","+- **FR-30** As any user, I want the sidebar and user menu updated with the new pages (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) so that I can navigate to them.","+- **FR-31** As an admin, I want an \"unlock\" action that clears a locked-out account's lockout fields so that a legitimately locked user can sign in again without waiting out the timer."," ","-## Sign-in","-","-- As a user, I want to sign in with email and password on a Material UI /login form with a show-password toggle, so that I can see my information. (FR-2)","-- As a user, I want the system to reject sign-in for a non-existent, non-active, archived or locked account, so that only legitimate active accounts can get in. (FR-3)","-- As a user, I want wrong-password, locked and disabled sign-ins to show distinct, clear messages, so that I understand why I can't get in without leaking which emails exist. (FR-4)","-- As an admin, I want accounts to lock after 5 failed sign-ins for 15 minutes, so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. (FR-5)","-- As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP, so that a single source cannot hammer the login endpoint. (FR-6)","-- As a user, I want to land back on the page I was headed to after signing in, so that I don't lose my place. (FR-7)","-- As an admin, I want every sign-in success, failure and lockout audited, so that I can investigate security incidents. (FR-8)","-","-## Session","-","-- As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active, so that I'm not logged out mid-task. (FR-9)","-- As a user, I want changing my password to sign out my other devices, so that a stolen session stops working once I secure my account. (FR-10)","-- As a user, I want unauthenticated page and API requests to be redirected or rejected automatically, so that protected data is never reachable without signing in. (FR-11)","-","-## Accept invitation","-","-- As an invited user, I want my invitation link checked for validity and expiry, so that I can't use a stale or reused link. (FR-12)","-- As an invited user, I want to see my name and email confirmed on the invite page, so that I know the invitation is really for me. (FR-13)","-- As an invited user, I want to set my own password from the invitation link, so that I can access SchoolHub for the first time. (FR-14)","-","-## Password policy","-","-- As an admin, I want new passwords to meet a minimum-strength policy, so that weak or common passwords can't be chosen. (FR-15)","-- As a user, I want to see a live checklist of password rules as I type, so that I know exactly what's still missing. (FR-16)","-","-## Forgot / reset password","-","-- As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link without revealing whether my email has an account, so that I can regain access without exposing other users' accounts. (FR-17)","-- As a user who forgot my password, I want a time-limited reset link emailed to me, so that only I can use it and only briefly. (FR-18)","-- As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link, so that I can get back into my account. (FR-19)","-","-## Change password (signed in)","-","-- As a user, I want to change my password while signed in, so that I can keep my account secure. (FR-20)","-- As a user, I want an \"Account security\" entry in my user menu, so that I can find the change-password page easily. (FR-21)","-","-## Services, permissions & auditing (for later PRDs)","-","-- As a developer, I want user-management service functions (createUser, invite, status, unlock), so that PRD-03's admin screens can be built on top without re-implementing auth logic. (FR-22)","-- As a developer, I want requireUser()/requireRole() permission helpers, so that restricting a handler or page to a role is a one-line call. (FR-23)","-- As a developer, I want a reusable audit() helper that never leaks secrets into audit metadata, so that every later PRD can record security-relevant actions consistently and safely. (FR-24)","-","-## App shell integration","-","-- As a user, I want the top-bar user menu to show my real name, role and initials and to actually sign me out, so that the placeholder from PRD-00 is replaced with my real session. (FR-25)","-- As a user, I want the sidebar to reflect my real role, so that I only see navigation I'm allowed to use. (FR-26)","-- As a developer, I want sendAuthEmail() to log emails to the console until PRD-04 lands, so that auth flows are testable before real email delivery exists. (FR-27)","-","-## Seed data","-","-- As a developer, I want seed accounts for every role plus one pending invitation, so that I can test and demo every sign-in/invite path immediately. (FR-28)","-"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **Security (NFR-1):** Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and every auth form carries Auth.js CSRF protection.","-- **Security (NFR-2):** Sign-in timing for \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" must be similar, preventing user enumeration via response time.","-- **Performance (NFR-3):** Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12).","-- **Accessibility (NFR-4):** Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"` and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.","-- **UI library discipline (NFR-5):** Every visible element is built from Material UI only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned-library list is ESLint-enforced.","-- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest unit tests (policy, tokens, lockout, rate limiter, callbackUrl check), Vitest integration tests (authorize, invite, reset, change-password), and Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed login, forgot→reset).","-- **Brownfield discipline (NFR-7):** Reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.","-- **Delivery discipline (NFR-8):** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests listed in this PRD, and don't expand scope beyond it or touch behaviour owned by later PRDs.","+- **NFR-1 (Privacy)** Medical notes are never exposed to STUDENT or PARENT roles, in the API or in CSV exports.","+- **NFR-2 (Performance)** The user list returns a page in under 300 ms with 5,000 users.","+- **NFR-3 (Reliability)** CSV import batches are all-or-nothing — no partial persistence on failure.","+- **NFR-4 (Security)** CSV exports neutralise spreadsheet formula injection.","+- **NFR-5 (UI consistency)** Every visible element is built from Material UI, looked up via the MUI MCP server; banned UI/styling libraries are rejected by ESLint.","+- **NFR-6 (Test coverage)** Unit, integration and Playwright e2e tests as listed in the PRD's Test Requirements section.","+- **NFR-7 (Brownfield discipline)** Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename.","+- **NFR-8 (Delivery discipline)** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, stay within this PRD's scope, and don't touch later-PRD behaviour."]}],"originalFile":"# User Stories — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control\n\nTicket: abcd-2 · Phase: intake\n\n## Data model\n\n- As the platform, I need User, AuthToken and AuditLog models with role/status/lockout fields, so that every later feature can authenticate, scope and audit users against one source of truth. (FR-1)\n\n## Sign-in\n\n- As a user, I want to sign in with email and password on a Material UI /login form with a show-password toggle, so that I can see my information. (FR-2)\n- As a user, I want the system to reject sign-in for a non-existent, non-active, archived or locked account, so that only legitimate active accounts can get in. (FR-3)\n- As a user, I want wrong-password, locked and disabled sign-ins to show distinct, clear messages, so that I understand why I can't get in without leaking which emails exist. (FR-4)\n- As an admin, I want accounts to lock after 5 failed sign-ins for 15 minutes, so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. (FR-5)\n- As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP, so that a single source cannot hammer the login endpoint. (FR-6)\n- As a user, I want to land back on the page I was headed to after signing in, so that I don't lose my place. (FR-7)\n- As an admin, I want every sign-in success, failure and lockout audited, so that I can investigate security incidents. (FR-8)\n\n## Session\n\n- As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active, so that I'm not logged out mid-task. (FR-9)\n- As a user, I want changing my password to sign out my other devices, so that a stolen session stops working once I secure my account. (FR-10)\n- As a user, I want unauthenticated page and API requests to be redirected or rejected automatically, so that protected data is never reachable without signing in. (FR-11)\n\n## Accept invitation\n\n- As an invited user, I want my invitation link checked for validity and expiry, so that I can't use a stale or reused link. (FR-12)\n- As an invited user, I want to see my name and email confirmed on the invite page, so that I know the invitation is really for me. (FR-13)\n- As an invited user, I want to set my own password from the invitation link, so that I can access SchoolHub for the first time. (FR-14)\n\n## Password policy\n\n- As an admin, I want new passwords to meet a minimum-strength policy, so that weak or common passwords can't be chosen. (FR-15)\n- As a user, I want to see a live checklist of password rules as I type, so that I know exactly what's still missing. (FR-16)\n\n## Forgot / reset password\n\n- As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link without revealing whether my email has an account, so that I can regain access without exposing other users' accounts. (FR-17)\n- As a user who forgot my password, I want a time-limited reset link emailed to me, so that only I can use it and only briefly. (FR-18)\n- As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link, so that I can get back into my account. (FR-19)\n\n## Change password (signed in)\n\n- As a user, I want to change my password while signed in, so that I can keep my account secure. (FR-20)\n- As a user, I want an \"Account security\" entry in my user menu, so that I can find the change-password page easily. (FR-21)\n\n## Services, permissions & auditing (for later PRDs)\n\n- As a developer, I want user-management service functions (createUser, invite, status, unlock), so that PRD-03's admin screens can be built on top without re-implementing auth logic. (FR-22)\n- As a developer, I want requireUser()/requireRole() permission helpers, so that restricting a handler or page to a role is a one-line call. (FR-23)\n- As a developer, I want a reusable audit() helper that never leaks secrets into audit metadata, so that every later PRD can record security-relevant actions consistently and safely. (FR-24)\n\n## App shell integration\n\n- As a user, I want the top-bar user menu to show my real name, role and initials and to actually sign me out, so that the placeholder from PRD-00 is replaced with my real session. (FR-25)\n- As a user, I want the sidebar to reflect my real role, so that I only see navigation I'm allowed to use. (FR-26)\n- As a developer, I want sendAuthEmail() to log emails to the console until PRD-04 lands, so that auth flows are testable before real email delivery exists. (FR-27)\n\n## Seed data\n\n- As a developer, I want seed accounts for every role plus one pending invitation, so that I can test and demo every sign-in/invite path immediately. (FR-28)\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **Security (NFR-1):** Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and every auth form carries Auth.js CSRF protection.\n- **Security (NFR-2):** Sign-in timing for \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" must be similar, preventing user enumeration via response time.\n- **Performance (NFR-3):** Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **Accessibility (NFR-4):** Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"` and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\n- **UI library discipline (NFR-5):** Every visible element is built from Material UI only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned-library list is ESLint-enforced.\n- **Test coverage (NFR-6):** Vitest unit tests (policy, tokens, lockout, rate limiter, callbackUrl check), Vitest integration tests (authorize, invite, reset, change-password), and Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed login, forgot→reset).\n- **Brownfield discipline (NFR-7):** Reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model.\n- **Delivery discipline (NFR-8):** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests listed in this PRD, and don't expand scope beyond it or touch behaviour owned by later PRDs.\n","userModified":false}}
