{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBQXCD6QCt3uTc8T8voo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rzoi4hZWUBVwL393syXcFK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T15:05:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox, plus EmailStatus enum (PENDING/SENDING/SENT/FAILED), per the schema block given.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Create a typed notification type registry at src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES (key -> label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles) with categories ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM, seeded with account.invite, account.password_reset and system.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Notification type registry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"notify() must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TypeScript literal/union typing against the registry).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts that skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), creates a Notification row when in-app applies, and enqueues an EmailOutbox row when email applies and the user has an email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 notify() service\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"notify() must batch via createMany so notifying 1,000 users costs at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, and must never throw to the caller (log failures instead); callers invoke notify() after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3, FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }) that expands each student to the student plus all linked parents, deduplicated, for later PRDs (attendance, grades, assignments) to reuse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Build branded email templates with @react-email/components under src/server/email/templates/, rendered to both HTML and plain text, sharing a base layout (school logo/name header, content area, footer with school address, \\\"Manage email preferences\\\" link to /account/notifications, and the required disclosure sentence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Email templates\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Implement the invite, password-reset and generic-notification templates with the specified fields (name/school/accept-link/expiry; link/60-min expiry notice; title/body/CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Switch the existing PRD-01 auth email path onto the outbox: replace the current sendInvite() stub in src/server/services/users.ts (which only logs \\\"PRD-01 auth not landed yet\\\") with a sendAuthEmail() helper that enqueues the invite / password-reset templates via EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4; verified against src/server/services/users.ts:385-390 where sendInvite is currently a logging-only stub\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":43166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":291},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479","uuid":"030fba14-bb15-44c8-8f2a-65ef92f0a91b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:04:52.883Z","request_id":"req_011CgBQXBzBzXT1XLsNZLA8J"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rzoi4hZWUBVwL393syXcFK","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479","uuid":"b89e8671-f16a-48fc-8abd-d79452facd75","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:04:52.964Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T15:05:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox, plus EmailStatus enum (PENDING/SENDING/SENT/FAILED), per the schema block given.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Create a typed notification type registry at src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES (key -> label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles) with categories ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM, seeded with account.invite, account.password_reset and system.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Notification type registry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"notify() must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TypeScript literal/union typing against the registry).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts that skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), creates a Notification row when in-app applies, and enqueues an EmailOutbox row when email applies and the user has an email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 notify() service\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"notify() must batch via createMany so notifying 1,000 users costs at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, and must never throw to the caller (log failures instead); callers invoke notify() after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3, FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }) that expands each student to the student plus all linked parents, deduplicated, for later PRDs (attendance, grades, assignments) to reuse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Build branded email templates with @react-email/components under src/server/email/templates/, rendered to both HTML and plain text, sharing a base layout (school logo/name header, content area, footer with school address, \\\"Manage email preferences\\\" link to /account/notifications, and the required disclosure sentence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Email templates\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Implement the invite, password-reset and generic-notification templates with the specified fields (name/school/accept-link/expiry; link/60-min expiry notice; title/body/CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Switch the existing PRD-01 auth email path onto the outbox: replace the current sendInvite() stub in src/server/services/users.ts (which only logs \\\"PRD-01 auth not landed yet\\\") with a sendAuthEmail() helper that enqueues the invite / password-reset templates via EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4; verified against src/server/services/users.ts:385-390 where sendInvite is currently a logging-only stub\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":54,"newStart":1,"newLines":47,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-03\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T14:05:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T15:05:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: StudentProfile, TeacherProfile, ParentProfile and ParentStudentLink models (plus Gender and GuardianRelationship enums) with relations added from User to each profile and to ParentStudentLink as parent and as student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"User list (/admin/users) DataTable columns: avatar + full name, email, role chip, status chip (Invited=warning, Active=success, Disabled=default, Archived=outlined), grade level (students), last sign-in, actions menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"User list filters: role (multi-select), status, grade level (shown when role filter includes Student), search by name/email/admission number/employee number; archived users hidden unless 'Show archived' is checked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"User list row actions: View, Edit, Resend invitation (status Invited), Unlock (when lockedUntil > now), Disable/Enable, Archive/Restore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"User list bulk actions on selected rows: Resend invitations, Disable, Export CSV.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Create/edit user form is an MUI Stepper: step 1 selects role, step 2 shows common fields (first/last name, email, phone) plus role-specific fields for Student, Teacher and Parent (including inline linking/creation of family members).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Checkbox 'Send invitation email now' (default checked) calls sendInvite on user creation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Email changes on an existing user require a confirmation dialog and invalidate pending invite tokens.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Role cannot be changed after user creation; the edit form shows it read-only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Validation: student date of birth must make them between 3 and 21 years old; phone must match the pattern ^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"User detail page (/admin/users/[id]) shows profile data, status, last sign-in, linked family members (with links), and the 20 most recent audit entries where the user is actor or entity.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 User detail, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Disable sets status=DISABLED; the PRD-01 session check is extended so the user's sessions stop working within 5 minutes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Archive sets archivedAt=now and status=DISABLED; archived users are excluded from all pickers app-wide but their historical records remain visible.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"An admin cannot disable or archive their own account, and the last active admin cannot be disabled, erroring with 'At least one active admin is required.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Parent-student links are managed from either the student or parent form, and from a 'Family' card on the student detail page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A student can have at most 4 linked parents; exactly one link per student may be isPrimary (setting one clears the others).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/student-access.ts exports getAccessibleStudentIds(user) (role-based accessible student id resolution, returning [] for TEACHER until PRD-05) and assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId) (throws FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND for parents/students to avoid revealing existence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"CSV import page (/admin/users/import) provides downloadable students-template.csv and teachers-template.csv with the specified column headers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"CSV upload (max 2 MB, max 2,000 rows) is parsed in the browser with papaparse into a preview DataGrid marking each row Valid, Warning or Error with a per-cell reason.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"'Import N valid rows' sends rows to POST /api/users/import in batches of 200; the server re-validates every row, creates users and links in one transaction per batch, and returns per-row results.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Import option 'Send invitations after import' (default off); grade levels matched by name or shortName case-insensitively; dates accepted only as YYYY-MM-DD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"After import, show a summary (created students, created parents, linked existing parents, failed rows) and a 'Download error report' CSV listing failed rows with reasons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Re-importing the same file creates no duplicates: rows whose email already exists are reported as 'Skipped — already exists'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Student detail page (/students/[studentId]) header shows avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status; this PRD registers an 'Overview' tab (profile, family, emergency contact; medical notes only for ADMIN and TEACHER) in src/config/student-tabs.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Student detail page, item 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Student detail page access is gated through assertCanViewStudent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Student detail page, item 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Parent 'My children' page (/my-children, PARENT only) lists linked children as cards (name, grade level, admission number) linking to /students/[id], with an empty state when none are linked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Parent 'My children'\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Self-service profile page (/account/profile): any user sees their own name/email/role (read-only) and can edit phone, plus occupation and address for parents; a 'Profile' entry is added to the user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Profile\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"GET /api/users/search?role=&q= returns up to 20 {id, name, email, role} matches excluding archived users (ADMIN/TEACHER only), consumed by a reusable UserPicker component built on MUI Autocomplete (async options, multiple support, avatar+name+role renderOption).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 Directory pickers\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Audit log viewer (/admin/audit-log): read-only table of time, actor, action, entity type, entity id (linked when a user), IP, with filters for actor, action prefix and date range; a row click opens a right-anchored Drawer with pretty-printed metadata JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-12 Audit log viewer\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Navigation: Administration group gains Users, Import users and Audit log entries; Parents get 'My children'; all users get 'Profile' in the user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-13 Navigation\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"POST /api/users/:id/unlock clears the lockout fields (lockedUntil/failedLoginCount) set by the PRD-01 lockout mechanism, restoring sign-in access immediately.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table, 'POST /api/users/:id/unlock' row — behaviour inferred from the PRD-01 lockout fields this PRD's row action operates on\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox, plus EmailStatus enum (PENDING/SENDING/SENT/FAILED), per the schema block given.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Create a typed notification type registry at src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES (key -> label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles) with categories ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM, seeded with account.invite, account.password_reset and system.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Notification type registry\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"notify() must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TypeScript literal/union typing against the registry).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts that skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), creates a Notification row when in-app applies, and enqueues an EmailOutbox row when email applies and the user has an email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 notify() service\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"notify() must batch via createMany so notifying 1,000 users costs at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, and must never throw to the caller (log failures instead); callers invoke notify() after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3, FR-3.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }) that expands each student to the student plus all linked parents, deduplicated, for later PRDs (attendance, grades, assignments) to reuse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Build branded email templates with @react-email/components under src/server/email/templates/, rendered to both HTML and plain text, sharing a base layout (school logo/name header, content area, footer with school address, \\\"Manage email preferences\\\" link to /account/notifications, and the required disclosure sentence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Email templates\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Implement the invite, password-reset and generic-notification templates with the specified fields (name/school/accept-link/expiry; link/60-min expiry notice; title/body/CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Switch the existing PRD-01 auth email path onto the outbox: replace the current sendInvite() stub in src/server/services/users.ts (which only logs \\\"PRD-01 auth not landed yet\\\") with a sendAuthEmail() helper that enqueues the invite / password-reset templates via EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4; verified against src/server/services/users.ts:385-390 where sendInvite is currently a logging-only stub\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }","   ],","-","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Privacy: medicalNotes must never be returned to STUDENT or PARENT roles (enforced in the service layer, stripped from GET /api/students/:id for those roles) and must be excluded from exported CSVs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Privacy)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the user list must return a page in under 300 ms with 5,000 users, backed by an index on lastName, firstName, email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Performance)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an import batch either fully succeeds or fully rolls back; partial batches never persist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Reliability)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: CSV export must neutralise formula injection by prefixing cells starting with =, +, -, @ with a leading apostrophe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Security)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design, react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) is enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping and getAccessibleStudentIds per role; Vitest integration tests for import batch rollback, the last-admin guard and primary-link uniqueness; Playwright e2e for create-student-with-parent, CSV import happy path with an error row, and parent My-children → student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }","   ],","-","   \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,","   \"clarificationLog\": [],","   \"status\": \"complete\""]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-03\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T14:05:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: StudentProfile, TeacherProfile, ParentProfile and ParentStudentLink models (plus Gender and GuardianRelationship enums) with relations added from User to each profile and to ParentStudentLink as parent and as student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"User list (/admin/users) DataTable columns: avatar + full name, email, role chip, status chip (Invited=warning, Active=success, Disabled=default, Archived=outlined), grade level (students), last sign-in, actions menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"User list filters: role (multi-select), status, grade level (shown when role filter includes Student), search by name/email/admission number/employee number; archived users hidden unless 'Show archived' is checked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"User list row actions: View, Edit, Resend invitation (status Invited), Unlock (when lockedUntil > now), Disable/Enable, Archive/Restore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"User list bulk actions on selected rows: Resend invitations, Disable, Export CSV.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 User list, item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Create/edit user form is an MUI Stepper: step 1 selects role, step 2 shows common fields (first/last name, email, phone) plus role-specific fields for Student, Teacher and Parent (including inline linking/creation of family members).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Checkbox 'Send invitation email now' (default checked) calls sendInvite on user creation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Email changes on an existing user require a confirmation dialog and invalidate pending invite tokens.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Role cannot be changed after user creation; the edit form shows it read-only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Validation: student date of birth must make them between 3 and 21 years old; phone must match the pattern ^\\\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Create/edit user, item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"User detail page (/admin/users/[id]) shows profile data, status, last sign-in, linked family members (with links), and the 20 most recent audit entries where the user is actor or entity.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 User detail, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Disable sets status=DISABLED; the PRD-01 session check is extended so the user's sessions stop working within 5 minutes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Archive sets archivedAt=now and status=DISABLED; archived users are excluded from all pickers app-wide but their historical records remain visible.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"An admin cannot disable or archive their own account, and the last active admin cannot be disabled, erroring with 'At least one active admin is required.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Status changes, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Parent-student links are managed from either the student or parent form, and from a 'Family' card on the student detail page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A student can have at most 4 linked parents; exactly one link per student may be isPrimary (setting one clears the others).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/student-access.ts exports getAccessibleStudentIds(user) (role-based accessible student id resolution, returning [] for TEACHER until PRD-05) and assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId) (throws FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND for parents/students to avoid revealing existence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Parent-student links, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"CSV import page (/admin/users/import) provides downloadable students-template.csv and teachers-template.csv with the specified column headers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"CSV upload (max 2 MB, max 2,000 rows) is parsed in the browser with papaparse into a preview DataGrid marking each row Valid, Warning or Error with a per-cell reason.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"'Import N valid rows' sends rows to POST /api/users/import in batches of 200; the server re-validates every row, creates users and links in one transaction per batch, and returns per-row results.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Import option 'Send invitations after import' (default off); grade levels matched by name or shortName case-insensitively; dates accepted only as YYYY-MM-DD.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"After import, show a summary (created students, created parents, linked existing parents, failed rows) and a 'Download error report' CSV listing failed rows with reasons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Re-importing the same file creates no duplicates: rows whose email already exists are reported as 'Skipped — already exists'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 CSV import, item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Student detail page (/students/[studentId]) header shows avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status; this PRD registers an 'Overview' tab (profile, family, emergency contact; medical notes only for ADMIN and TEACHER) in src/config/student-tabs.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Student detail page, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Student detail page access is gated through assertCanViewStudent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Student detail page, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Parent 'My children' page (/my-children, PARENT only) lists linked children as cards (name, grade level, admission number) linking to /students/[id], with an empty state when none are linked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Parent 'My children'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Self-service profile page (/account/profile): any user sees their own name/email/role (read-only) and can edit phone, plus occupation and address for parents; a 'Profile' entry is added to the user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Profile\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"GET /api/users/search?role=&q= returns up to 20 {id, name, email, role} matches excluding archived users (ADMIN/TEACHER only), consumed by a reusable UserPicker component built on MUI Autocomplete (async options, multiple support, avatar+name+role renderOption).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 Directory pickers\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Audit log viewer (/admin/audit-log): read-only table of time, actor, action, entity type, entity id (linked when a user), IP, with filters for actor, action prefix and date range; a row click opens a right-anchored Drawer with pretty-printed metadata JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-12 Audit log viewer\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Navigation: Administration group gains Users, Import users and Audit log entries; Parents get 'My children'; all users get 'Profile' in the user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-13 Navigation\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"POST /api/users/:id/unlock clears the lockout fields (lockedUntil/failedLoginCount) set by the PRD-01 lockout mechanism, restoring sign-in access immediately.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table, 'POST /api/users/:id/unlock' row — behaviour inferred from the PRD-01 lockout fields this PRD's row action operates on\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Privacy: medicalNotes must never be returned to STUDENT or PARENT roles (enforced in the service layer, stripped from GET /api/students/:id for those roles) and must be excluded from exported CSVs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Privacy)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the user list must return a page in under 300 ms with 5,000 users, backed by an index on lastName, firstName, email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an import batch either fully succeeds or fully rolls back; partial batches never persist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: CSV export must neutralise formula injection by prefixing cells starting with =, +, -, @ with a leading apostrophe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design, react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) is enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping and getAccessibleStudentIds per role; Vitest integration tests for import batch rollback, the last-admin guard and primary-link uniqueness; Playwright e2e for create-student-with-parent, CSV import happy path with an error row, and parent My-children → student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false}}
