{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bvw1r1ao2","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LGxEFeEr1vfysZHKdMQLTQ","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub-prds/35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479/tasks/bvw1r1ao2.output","summary":"Background command \"echo \"=== requirements.json ticketId ===\"; head -c 300 artifacts/intake/requirements.json; echo; echo \"=== handoff ===\"; cat artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json; echo \"=== find intake.md ===\"; find / -iname \"intake.md\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== .forge and .pdlc ===\"; find .forge .pdlc -type f 2>/dev/null\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"c6ffa54e-5836-45cc-a120-be66e3e3d390","session_id":"35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBQaYS6djuqCVo8Bo32i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — no sass/less dependency. `\"css\"` stands. No Figma URL in this PRD, so `figma-readiness.json` is correctly skipped. Now the user stories file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":186,"cache_read_input_tokens":48622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":186},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479","uuid":"326d5ee0-5fb2-4756-a54f-95a28122ce54","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:05:02.217Z","request_id":"req_011CgBQaY9E6Qk5SVrSNoWXe"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBQaYS6djuqCVo8Bo32i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C3STsUmZ48hahBSw3kmaq9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (abcd-04)\n\n## Data & service layer\n\n- **FR-1 / FR-2 / FR-3** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` models plus a typed notification-type registry, so that I have a durable place to store notifications and emails and can't accidentally notify with an unregistered type.\n- **FR-4 / FR-5 / FR-6** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want a single `notify()` call (and a `notifyStudentAndParents()` helper) that handles preferences, batching and failure isolation for me, so that I never have to hand-roll notification or email delivery.\n\n## Email templates & delivery\n\n- **FR-7 / FR-8** — As a recipient of a SchoolHub email, I want a consistently branded email (school header, clear content, footer with an unsubscribe/preferences link) so that I trust and recognize messages from the school.\n- **FR-9** — As an admin resending an invite, I want the invite email to actually be queued and sent (not just logged), so that new users reliably receive their account invitation.\n- **FR-10 / FR-11 / FR-12 / FR-13** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry automatically and the system to dispatch them within a minute, so that important messages are not silently lost. *(Acceptance Criteria #3, #4)*\n\n## Notification bell & centre\n\n- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity. *(User Story 1)*\n- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it. *(User Story 2, Acceptance Criteria #5)*\n- **FR-16** — As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable. *(User Story 3)*\n- **FR-17** — As the platform, I want notifications older than 180 days purged automatically so that the list and database stay lean.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **FR-18 / FR-19 / FR-22** — As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded. *(User Story 4)*\n\n## Admin\n\n- **FR-20** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible in a log so that important messages are not silently lost, with a one-click retry and a test-send button. *(User Story 5)*\n\n## API surface\n\n- **FR-21** — As a frontend client, I want a consistent REST surface for notifications, preferences, dispatch and the admin log so that every screen above has a stable contract to call.\n- **FR-23** — As a user navigating the app, I want \"Notifications\" (and the admin email log, for admins) in the sidebar so that I can find these new pages.\n\n## Seed data\n\n- **FR-24** — As a developer testing locally, I want sample notifications pre-seeded for a student and parent account so that I can see the bell and list populated without manually triggering `notify()`.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** — Every screen in this PRD (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences page, admin email log) must be built only from MUI components looked up via the MUI MCP server; no banned UI libraries. Email templates are the one exception, using `@react-email/components`.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3** — `notify()` must handle 1,000 recipients in under 2 seconds; the unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50ms.\n- **NFR-4** — Concurrent dispatchers must never double-send an email; rows stuck in `SENDING` for 10+ minutes recover to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-5** — Notification links must be validated relative paths; email HTML must escape user-provided text.\n- **NFR-6** — Every email has HTML + plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header.\n- **NFR-7** — Every notification/email-log route enforces authorization server-side (`requireUser()`/`requireRole()`/`CRON_SECRET`), never relying on hidden UI alone.\n- **NFR-8** — Dispatch requests without a valid `CRON_SECRET` bearer token return `401`.\n- **NFR-9** — Existing lint/typecheck/test suites keep passing; new unit, integration and Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section are added.\n- **NFR-10** — No SMS/push, no websockets, no digest emails in this PRD.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":186,"cache_read_input_tokens":48622,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":186},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479","uuid":"1c79bf87-c8d3-4abf-872a-74b90fffe09f","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:05:17.105Z","request_id":"req_011CgBQaY9E6Qk5SVrSNoWXe"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C3STsUmZ48hahBSw3kmaq9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"35fc3024-b10f-4ae9-982f-2a29733c9479","uuid":"c9ffa78c-eead-4a4b-abb1-1e06620a2314","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:05:17.143Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (abcd-04)\n\n## Data & service layer\n\n- **FR-1 / FR-2 / FR-3** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` models plus a typed notification-type registry, so that I have a durable place to store notifications and emails and can't accidentally notify with an unregistered type.\n- **FR-4 / FR-5 / FR-6** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want a single `notify()` call (and a `notifyStudentAndParents()` helper) that handles preferences, batching and failure isolation for me, so that I never have to hand-roll notification or email delivery.\n\n## Email templates & delivery\n\n- **FR-7 / FR-8** — As a recipient of a SchoolHub email, I want a consistently branded email (school header, clear content, footer with an unsubscribe/preferences link) so that I trust and recognize messages from the school.\n- **FR-9** — As an admin resending an invite, I want the invite email to actually be queued and sent (not just logged), so that new users reliably receive their account invitation.\n- **FR-10 / FR-11 / FR-12 / FR-13** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry automatically and the system to dispatch them within a minute, so that important messages are not silently lost. *(Acceptance Criteria #3, #4)*\n\n## Notification bell & centre\n\n- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity. *(User Story 1)*\n- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it. *(User Story 2, Acceptance Criteria #5)*\n- **FR-16** — As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable. *(User Story 3)*\n- **FR-17** — As the platform, I want notifications older than 180 days purged automatically so that the list and database stay lean.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **FR-18 / FR-19 / FR-22** — As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded. *(User Story 4)*\n\n## Admin\n\n- **FR-20** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible in a log so that important messages are not silently lost, with a one-click retry and a test-send button. *(User Story 5)*\n\n## API surface\n\n- **FR-21** — As a frontend client, I want a consistent REST surface for notifications, preferences, dispatch and the admin log so that every screen above has a stable contract to call.\n- **FR-23** — As a user navigating the app, I want \"Notifications\" (and the admin email log, for admins) in the sidebar so that I can find these new pages.\n\n## Seed data\n\n- **FR-24** — As a developer testing locally, I want sample notifications pre-seeded for a student and parent account so that I can see the bell and list populated without manually triggering `notify()`.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** — Every screen in this PRD (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences page, admin email log) must be built only from MUI components looked up via the MUI MCP server; no banned UI libraries. Email templates are the one exception, using `@react-email/components`.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3** — `notify()` must handle 1,000 recipients in under 2 seconds; the unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50ms.\n- **NFR-4** — Concurrent dispatchers must never double-send an email; rows stuck in `SENDING` for 10+ minutes recover to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-5** — Notification links must be validated relative paths; email HTML must escape user-provided text.\n- **NFR-6** — Every email has HTML + plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header.\n- **NFR-7** — Every notification/email-log route enforces authorization server-side (`requireUser()`/`requireRole()`/`CRON_SECRET`), never relying on hidden UI alone.\n- **NFR-8** — Dispatch requests without a valid `CRON_SECRET` bearer token return `401`.\n- **NFR-9** — Existing lint/typecheck/test suites keep passing; new unit, integration and Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section are added.\n- **NFR-10** — No SMS/push, no websockets, no digest emails in this PRD.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":48,"newStart":1,"newLines":50,"lines":["-# User Stories — PRD-03 User Management, Profiles, Family Links & Audit Viewer","+# User Stories — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (abcd-04)"," ","-Ticket: abcd-03 · Phase: intake","+## Data & service layer"," ","-## Functional Requirements","+- **FR-1 / FR-2 / FR-3** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` models plus a typed notification-type registry, so that I have a durable place to store notifications and emails and can't accidentally notify with an unregistered type.","+- **FR-4 / FR-5 / FR-6** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want a single `notify()` call (and a `notifyStudentAndParents()` helper) that handles preferences, batching and failure isolation for me, so that I never have to hand-roll notification or email delivery."," ","-- **FR-1** As an admin, I want student/teacher/parent profile data and parent↔student link records to exist so that every user-management screen has somewhere to read and write role-specific data.","-- **FR-2** As an admin, I want a user list table with avatar, name, email, role, status and grade level columns so that I can scan everyone at a glance.","-- **FR-3** As an admin, I want to filter and search the user list by role, status, grade level and free text so that I can find people fast.","-- **FR-4** As an admin, I want per-row actions (view, edit, resend invite, unlock, disable/enable, archive/restore) so that I can manage one account at a time.","-- **FR-5** As an admin, I want bulk actions (resend invitations, disable, export CSV) on selected rows so that I can manage many accounts at once.","-- **FR-6** As an admin, I want a stepped create/edit form with role-specific fields so that I can create a user of any role with the right data.","-- **FR-7** As an admin, I want a \"send invitation email now\" option on user creation so that new users can sign in right away.","-- **FR-8** As an admin, I want a confirmation dialog when changing a user's email so that pending invite tokens are safely invalidated.","-- **FR-9** As an admin, I want a user's role locked after creation so that role changes can't silently break access rules.","-- **FR-10** As an admin, I want date-of-birth and phone fields validated so that bad data never enters a student or contact record.","-- **FR-11** As an admin, I want a user detail page showing profile, status, family links and recent audit entries so that I have full context on one screen.","-- **FR-12** As an admin, I want disabling a user to cut off their active sessions within 5 minutes so that access removal is prompt.","-- **FR-13** As an admin, I want archiving a user to hide them from pickers while keeping their historical records so that past data stays intact.","-- **FR-14** As an admin, I want to be blocked from disabling myself or the last active admin so that the school never loses admin access.","-- **FR-15** As an admin, I want to manage parent–student links from the student form, the parent form or a Family card so that I have flexible entry points.","-- **FR-16** As an admin, I want at most 4 parents per student and exactly one marked primary so that family data stays well-formed.","-- **FR-17** As a developer of a later PRD, I want `getAccessibleStudentIds` and `assertCanViewStudent` helpers so that every feature enforces student-level access the same way.","-- **FR-18** As an admin, I want downloadable CSV templates for students and teachers so that I know the exact columns to fill in.","-- **FR-19** As an admin, I want a client-side CSV preview marking each row Valid/Warning/Error so that I can fix problems before importing.","-- **FR-20** As an admin, I want the import to happen in server-validated batches of 200 inside one transaction per batch so that imports are safe and fast.","-- **FR-21** As an admin, I want to optionally send invitations after import and have grade levels matched case-insensitively so that onboarding a whole year is low-friction.","-- **FR-22** As an admin, I want an import summary and a downloadable error report so that I can see exactly what happened to each row.","-- **FR-23** As an admin, I want re-importing the same file to skip existing users instead of duplicating them so that imports are safe to retry.","-- **FR-24** As any authenticated user with access, I want a student detail page with an Overview tab (profile, family, emergency contact) so that I can see a student's core information.","-- **FR-25** As any user, I want the student detail page to enforce `assertCanViewStudent` so that I can't see students I'm not allowed to see.","-- **FR-26** As a parent, I want a \"My children\" page listing my linked students so that I can jump to each child's information.","-- **FR-27** As any user, I want a profile page where I can edit my phone (and occupation/address if I'm a parent) so that the school can reach me.","-- **FR-28** As an admin or teacher, I want a searchable user picker (`/api/users/search` + `UserPicker`) so that I can quickly find and select people in forms.","-- **FR-29** As an admin, I want a read-only audit log viewer with filters and a metadata drawer so that I can see who changed what.","-- **FR-30** As any user, I want the sidebar and user menu updated with the new pages (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) so that I can navigate to them.","-- **FR-31** As an admin, I want an \"unlock\" action that clears a locked-out account's lockout fields so that a legitimately locked user can sign in again without waiting out the timer.","+## Email templates & delivery"," ","+- **FR-7 / FR-8** — As a recipient of a SchoolHub email, I want a consistently branded email (school header, clear content, footer with an unsubscribe/preferences link) so that I trust and recognize messages from the school.","+- **FR-9** — As an admin resending an invite, I want the invite email to actually be queued and sent (not just logged), so that new users reliably receive their account invitation.","+- **FR-10 / FR-11 / FR-12 / FR-13** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry automatically and the system to dispatch them within a minute, so that important messages are not silently lost. *(Acceptance Criteria #3, #4)*","+","+## Notification bell & centre","+","+- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity. *(User Story 1)*","+- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it. *(User Story 2, Acceptance Criteria #5)*","+- **FR-16** — As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable. *(User Story 3)*","+- **FR-17** — As the platform, I want notifications older than 180 days purged automatically so that the list and database stay lean.","+","+## Preferences","+","+- **FR-18 / FR-19 / FR-22** — As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded. *(User Story 4)*","+","+## Admin","+","+- **FR-20** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible in a log so that important messages are not silently lost, with a one-click retry and a test-send button. *(User Story 5)*","+","+## API surface","+","+- **FR-21** — As a frontend client, I want a consistent REST surface for notifications, preferences, dispatch and the admin log so that every screen above has a stable contract to call.","+- **FR-23** — As a user navigating the app, I want \"Notifications\" (and the admin email log, for admins) in the sidebar so that I can find these new pages.","+","+## Seed data","+","+- **FR-24** — As a developer testing locally, I want sample notifications pre-seeded for a student and parent account so that I can see the bell and list populated without manually triggering `notify()`.","+","+---","+"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **NFR-1 (Privacy)** Medical notes are never exposed to STUDENT or PARENT roles, in the API or in CSV exports.","-- **NFR-2 (Performance)** The user list returns a page in under 300 ms with 5,000 users.","-- **NFR-3 (Reliability)** CSV import batches are all-or-nothing — no partial persistence on failure.","-- **NFR-4 (Security)** CSV exports neutralise spreadsheet formula injection.","-- **NFR-5 (UI consistency)** Every visible element is built from Material UI, looked up via the MUI MCP server; banned UI/styling libraries are rejected by ESLint.","-- **NFR-6 (Test coverage)** Unit, integration and Playwright e2e tests as listed in the PRD's Test Requirements section.","-- **NFR-7 (Brownfield discipline)** Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename.","-- **NFR-8 (Delivery discipline)** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, stay within this PRD's scope, and don't touch later-PRD behaviour.","+- **NFR-1** — Every screen in this PRD (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences page, admin email log) must be built only from MUI components looked up via the MUI MCP server; no banned UI libraries. Email templates are the one exception, using `@react-email/components`.","+- **NFR-2 / NFR-3** — `notify()` must handle 1,000 recipients in under 2 seconds; the unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50ms.","+- **NFR-4** — Concurrent dispatchers must never double-send an email; rows stuck in `SENDING` for 10+ minutes recover to `PENDING`.","+- **NFR-5** — Notification links must be validated relative paths; email HTML must escape user-provided text.","+- **NFR-6** — Every email has HTML + plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header.","+- **NFR-7** — Every notification/email-log route enforces authorization server-side (`requireUser()`/`requireRole()`/`CRON_SECRET`), never relying on hidden UI alone.","+- **NFR-8** — Dispatch requests without a valid `CRON_SECRET` bearer token return `401`.","+- **NFR-9** — Existing lint/typecheck/test suites keep passing; new unit, integration and Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section are added.","+- **NFR-10** — No SMS/push, no websockets, no digest emails in this PRD."]}],"originalFile":"# User Stories — PRD-03 User Management, Profiles, Family Links & Audit Viewer\n\nTicket: abcd-03 · Phase: intake\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-1** As an admin, I want student/teacher/parent profile data and parent↔student link records to exist so that every user-management screen has somewhere to read and write role-specific data.\n- **FR-2** As an admin, I want a user list table with avatar, name, email, role, status and grade level columns so that I can scan everyone at a glance.\n- **FR-3** As an admin, I want to filter and search the user list by role, status, grade level and free text so that I can find people fast.\n- **FR-4** As an admin, I want per-row actions (view, edit, resend invite, unlock, disable/enable, archive/restore) so that I can manage one account at a time.\n- **FR-5** As an admin, I want bulk actions (resend invitations, disable, export CSV) on selected rows so that I can manage many accounts at once.\n- **FR-6** As an admin, I want a stepped create/edit form with role-specific fields so that I can create a user of any role with the right data.\n- **FR-7** As an admin, I want a \"send invitation email now\" option on user creation so that new users can sign in right away.\n- **FR-8** As an admin, I want a confirmation dialog when changing a user's email so that pending invite tokens are safely invalidated.\n- **FR-9** As an admin, I want a user's role locked after creation so that role changes can't silently break access rules.\n- **FR-10** As an admin, I want date-of-birth and phone fields validated so that bad data never enters a student or contact record.\n- **FR-11** As an admin, I want a user detail page showing profile, status, family links and recent audit entries so that I have full context on one screen.\n- **FR-12** As an admin, I want disabling a user to cut off their active sessions within 5 minutes so that access removal is prompt.\n- **FR-13** As an admin, I want archiving a user to hide them from pickers while keeping their historical records so that past data stays intact.\n- **FR-14** As an admin, I want to be blocked from disabling myself or the last active admin so that the school never loses admin access.\n- **FR-15** As an admin, I want to manage parent–student links from the student form, the parent form or a Family card so that I have flexible entry points.\n- **FR-16** As an admin, I want at most 4 parents per student and exactly one marked primary so that family data stays well-formed.\n- **FR-17** As a developer of a later PRD, I want `getAccessibleStudentIds` and `assertCanViewStudent` helpers so that every feature enforces student-level access the same way.\n- **FR-18** As an admin, I want downloadable CSV templates for students and teachers so that I know the exact columns to fill in.\n- **FR-19** As an admin, I want a client-side CSV preview marking each row Valid/Warning/Error so that I can fix problems before importing.\n- **FR-20** As an admin, I want the import to happen in server-validated batches of 200 inside one transaction per batch so that imports are safe and fast.\n- **FR-21** As an admin, I want to optionally send invitations after import and have grade levels matched case-insensitively so that onboarding a whole year is low-friction.\n- **FR-22** As an admin, I want an import summary and a downloadable error report so that I can see exactly what happened to each row.\n- **FR-23** As an admin, I want re-importing the same file to skip existing users instead of duplicating them so that imports are safe to retry.\n- **FR-24** As any authenticated user with access, I want a student detail page with an Overview tab (profile, family, emergency contact) so that I can see a student's core information.\n- **FR-25** As any user, I want the student detail page to enforce `assertCanViewStudent` so that I can't see students I'm not allowed to see.\n- **FR-26** As a parent, I want a \"My children\" page listing my linked students so that I can jump to each child's information.\n- **FR-27** As any user, I want a profile page where I can edit my phone (and occupation/address if I'm a parent) so that the school can reach me.\n- **FR-28** As an admin or teacher, I want a searchable user picker (`/api/users/search` + `UserPicker`) so that I can quickly find and select people in forms.\n- **FR-29** As an admin, I want a read-only audit log viewer with filters and a metadata drawer so that I can see who changed what.\n- **FR-30** As any user, I want the sidebar and user menu updated with the new pages (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) so that I can navigate to them.\n- **FR-31** As an admin, I want an \"unlock\" action that clears a locked-out account's lockout fields so that a legitimately locked user can sign in again without waiting out the timer.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 (Privacy)** Medical notes are never exposed to STUDENT or PARENT roles, in the API or in CSV exports.\n- **NFR-2 (Performance)** The user list returns a page in under 300 ms with 5,000 users.\n- **NFR-3 (Reliability)** CSV import batches are all-or-nothing — no partial persistence on failure.\n- **NFR-4 (Security)** CSV exports neutralise spreadsheet formula injection.\n- **NFR-5 (UI consistency)** Every visible element is built from Material UI, looked up via the MUI MCP server; banned UI/styling libraries are rejected by ESLint.\n- **NFR-6 (Test coverage)** Unit, integration and Playwright e2e tests as listed in the PRD's Test Requirements section.\n- **NFR-7 (Brownfield discipline)** Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components and helpers; never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename.\n- **NFR-8 (Delivery discipline)** Keep lint/typecheck/test green, stay within this PRD's scope, and don't touch later-PRD behaviour.\n","userModified":false}}
