{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CaDKFA3ej9HKzyvTxWbR1z","type":"tool_result","content":"=== KNOWLEDGE.md head ===\n# Project Knowledge Base\n<!-- Generated by Forge Knowledge Builder -- vendor-agnostic, works with any AI tool -->\n<!-- Last updated: 2026-10-19T10:00:44.344Z -->\n\n## Overview\n- **Name**: schoolhub\n- **Type**: data-engineering (0.85% confidence)\n- **Language**: typescript\n- **Framework**: react\n\n## What This System Does\n\n### Page Routes\n- `/(app)/dashboard`\n- `/(public)`\n- `/forbidden`\n\n### Capabilities (from tests)\n- dashboard page (/dashboard)\n- landing page (/)\n- ConfirmDialog\n- DataTable\n- formatInSchoolTz\n- env.ts\n- no-restricted-imports (ADR-5: MUI-only)\n- ok/paginated/apiError envelopes\n- withHandler error mapping\n- parsePagination\n- parseBody / parseQuery\n- useToast / ToastProvider\n\n### NPM Scripts\n- `dev`: `next dev`\n- `build`: `next build`\n- `start`: `next start`\n- `lint`: `next lint`\n- `typecheck`: `tsc --noEmit`\n- `test`: `vitest run`\n- `test:e2e`: `playwright test`\n- `db:migrate`: `prisma migrate dev`\n- `db:deploy`: `prisma migrate deploy`\n- `db:seed`: `tsx prisma/seed.ts`\n- `db:reset`: `prisma migrate reset --force`\n- `format`: `prettier --write .`\n\n## Tech Stack\n| Component | Choice | Version |\n|-----------|--------|---------|\n| Runtime | node | 0.1.0 |\n| Framework | react | — |\n| Build Tool | npm | — |\n| Database | — | — |\n| ORM | prisma | — |\n| Testing | playwright | — |\n\n## Architecture\n### Directory Structure\n- `.pdlc/`\n- `artifacts/`\n  - `artifacts/architect/`\n  - `artifacts/dev/`\n  - `artifacts/dev-planning/`\n  - `artifacts/intake/`\n  - `artifacts/telemetry/`\n- `prisma/`\n  - `prisma/migrations/`\n    - `prisma/migrations/20261019000000_init/`\n    - `prisma/migrations/20261019151500_user_management_profiles/`\n- `public/`\n  - `public/templates/`\n- `src/`\n  - `src/app/`\n    - `src/app/(app)/`\n      - `src/app/(app)/dashboard/`\n    - `src/app/(public)/`\n    - `src/app/api/`\n      - `src/app/api/academic-years/`\n        - `src/app/api/academic-years/[id]/`\n      - `src/app/api/audit-logs/`\n      - `src/app/api/grade-levels/`\n=== .forge/knowledge.json ===\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://pdlc-forge.dev/knowledge/v1\",\n  \"version\": \"2.0.0\",\n  \"generatedAt\": \"2026-10-19T10:00:44.346Z\",\n  \"generatedBy\": \"pdlc-forge-knowledge-builder\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"workspacePath\": \"\",\n    \"checksums\": {\n      \"techStack\": \"sha256:dba99672339d781682eb2e9887c219f040ade2cfc73a0c88ed2e972fd84c8e33\",\n      \"structure\": \"sha256:1c1ce20ad4907da922eff8b88572e72540e698a0b389855382df7e627368304d\",\n      \"api\": \"sha256:empty\",\n      \"dataModels\": \"sha256:0e0144e8ae9ab45a0c8ee81380db4160a2e86fa2f2cbd68385551c764315227e\",\n      \"conventions\": \"sha256:4978d246d97ec2c37323f597b2d3c81881af743f4499c33bfc058990784b9e12\",\n      \"dependencies\": \"sha256:dba99672339d781682eb2e9887c219f040ade2cfc73a0c88ed2e972fd84c8e33\",\n      \"testing\": \"sha256:3e8c7b1a72848d08e11c53f4110cd5d0e29af7ca4e96408dee72667210308388\",\n      \"buildDeploy\": \"sha256:3f33e0773e0796d7b2212fb38cf84b43879c80cfffb2a1273ec207d203c2a2cb\",\n      \"intelligence\": \"always-stale\",\n      \"domain\": \"sha256:empty\",\n      \"segments\": \"sha256:742305e0a315e83b15291b85c6b3c6c6876cec52464f3ffd763fc73d06143791\",\n      \"functionalKnowledge\": \"sha256:empty\",\n      \"architecturalPatterns\": \"sha256:1c1ce20ad4907da922eff8b88572e72540e698a0b389855382df7e627368304d\",\n      \"brittleAreas\": \"sha256:1c1ce20ad4907da922eff8b88572e72540e698a0b389855382df7e627368304d\",\n      \"keyAreas\": \"sha256:1c1ce20ad4907da922eff8b88572e72540e698a0b389855382df7e627368304d\",\n      \"knownLimitations\": \"sha256:1c1ce20ad4907da922eff8b88572e72540e698a0b389855382df7e627368304d\",\n      \"coreConcepts\": \"sha256:1c1ce20ad4907da922eff8b88572e72540e698a0b389855382df7e627368304d\",\n      \"keyIdeas\": \"sha256:bbea87908d24d7610ffa55e29cc4d73f77cd4ba7fb0a3300e0987fad25062149\",\n      \"technicalKnowledge\": \"sha256:empty\",\n      \"regressions\": \"always-stale\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"name\": \"schoolhub\",\n    \"projectType\": \"data-engineering\",\n    \"language\": \"typescript\",\n    \"framework\": \"react\",\n    \"confidence\": 0.85\n  },\n  \"functionalKnowledge\": {\n\n=== existing requirements.json full (current, maybe stale) ===\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T15:05:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox, plus EmailStatus enum (PENDING/SENDING/SENT/FAILED), per the schema block given.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Create a typed notification type registry at src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES (key -> label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles) with categories ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM, seeded with account.invite, account.password_reset and system.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Notification type registry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"notify() must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TypeScript literal/union typing against the registry).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts that skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), creates a Notification row when in-app applies, and enqueues an EmailOutbox row when email applies and the user has an email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 notify() service\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"notify() must batch via createMany so notifying 1,000 users costs at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, and must never throw to the caller (log failures instead); callers invoke notify() after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3, FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }) that expands each student to the student plus all linked parents, deduplicated, for later PRDs (attendance, grades, assignments) to reuse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Build branded email templates with @react-email/components under src/server/email/templates/, rendered to both HTML and plain text, sharing a base layout (school logo/name header, content area, footer with school address, \\\"Manage email preferences\\\" link to /account/notifications, and the required disclosure sentence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Email templates\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Implement the invite, password-reset and generic-notification templates with the specified fields (name/school/accept-link/expiry; link/60-min expiry notice; title/body/CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Switch the existing PRD-01 auth email path onto the outbox: replace the current sendInvite() stub in src/server/services/users.ts (which only logs \\\"PRD-01 auth not landed yet\\\") with a sendAuthEmail() helper that enqueues the invite / password-reset templates via EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4; verified against src/server/services/users.ts:385-390 where sendInvite is currently a logging-only stub\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dac73de3-4f5e-494a-90ec-53320f756c7e","uuid":"06bac000-db20-4439-ba41-e83e3a221fd7","timestamp":"2026-10-20T05:54:12.215Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== KNOWLEDGE.md head ===\n# Project Knowledge Base\n<!-- Generated by Forge Knowledge Builder -- vendor-agnostic, works with any AI tool -->\n<!-- Last updated: 2026-10-19T10:00:44.344Z -->\n\n## Overview\n- **Name**: schoolhub\n- **Type**: data-engineering (0.85% confidence)\n- **Language**: typescript\n- **Framework**: react\n\n## What This System Does\n\n### Page Routes\n- `/(app)/dashboard`\n- `/(public)`\n- `/forbidden`\n\n### Capabilities (from tests)\n- dashboard page (/dashboard)\n- landing page (/)\n- ConfirmDialog\n- DataTable\n- formatInSchoolTz\n- env.ts\n- no-restricted-imports (ADR-5: MUI-only)\n- ok/paginated/apiError envelopes\n- withHandler error mapping\n- parsePagination\n- parseBody / parseQuery\n- useToast / ToastProvider\n\n### NPM Scripts\n- `dev`: `next dev`\n- `build`: `next build`\n- `start`: `next start`\n- `lint`: `next lint`\n- `typecheck`: `tsc --noEmit`\n- `test`: `vitest run`\n- `test:e2e`: `playwright test`\n- `db:migrate`: `prisma migrate dev`\n- `db:deploy`: `prisma migrate deploy`\n- `db:seed`: `tsx prisma/seed.ts`\n- `db:reset`: `prisma migrate reset --force`\n- `format`: `prettier --write .`\n\n## Tech Stack\n| Component | Choice | Version |\n|-----------|--------|---------|\n| Runtime | node | 0.1.0 |\n| Framework | react | — |\n| Build Tool | npm | — |\n| Database | — | — |\n| ORM | prisma | — |\n| Testing | playwright | — |\n\n## Architecture\n### Directory