"source\": \"FR-2.2; verified against existing src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx which already accepts a `role` prop\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections/[id]: members table with add (multi-select student picker filtered to the section's grade level and to students without a section this year) and remove; the section's course list; a 'Create core courses' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"'Create core courses' dialog: lists all active (non-archived) subjects with a checkbox and a teacher picker per subject; submitting creates one CORE course per checked subject with the default name/code pattern and enrolls all current section members in each created course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"'Copy sections to next year' action on /admin/sections, enabled only when a non-current, future academic year exists; copies section name, grade level advanced to the next GradeLevel by `order`, room and capacity, without members or teacher assignments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Auto-enroll on section add: adding a student to a section enrolls them ACTIVE in every non-archived CORE course of that section; a previously DROPPED enrollment in one of those courses is reactivated rather than duplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Auto-drop on section removal: removing a student from a section sets every ACTIVE enrollment in that section's CORE courses to DROPPED with droppedAt = now; elective enrollments are left untouched.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"'Move to section…' single action performs the FR-7 enroll and FR-8 drop steps for the destination/source sections in one database transaction, exposed via POST /api/students/:id/move-section.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; API table row POST /api/students/:id/move-section\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Creating a new CORE course on a section enrolls all of that section's current members (ACTIVE) in the new course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Capacity enforcement: adding a student beyond section or course capacity is refused with a CONFLICT error, message pattern 'Section 7A is full (30/30).', unless the admin explicitly ticks 'Override capacity'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criteria #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Dropped enrollments retain all historical data (attendance, grades) visible to admins and teachers, but dropped students disappear from active rosters and from add-student pickers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses: filters for academic year, grade level, subject, teacher, kind, and free-text search by name/code; table of code, name, subject colour chip (reusing Subject.color, already on the model), section, teacher, enrolled count, kind.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; verified Subject.color already exists on the Subject model in prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (optional, required when kind=CORE), teacher, up to 3 co-teachers, name, code (auto-filled from subject+section, editable, forced uppercase), kind, capacity, description.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses/[id]/enrollment: enrolled-students table with drop/reactivate row actions and an 'Add students' picker; for CORE courses show an info note that membership is managed via the section instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /courses/[courseId] header: subject colour band, course name, code, teacher(s) (including co-teachers), section, room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a course-tabs registry at src/config/course-tabs.ts (same shape as the existing src/config/student-tabs.ts, with a `roles` field) rendered as a scrollable MUI Tabs on the course home page; this PRD registers 'Overview' (description/teachers/counts, all roles that can view the course) and 'Roster' (TEACHER/ADMIN: full student list with avatar/name/admission number/link to student page/status; STUDENT: classmates' names only; PARENT: tab not shown).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; verified against the existing (empty) src/config/student-tabs.ts pattern this PRD is told to mirror\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add src/server/auth/course-access.ts exporting assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN: all; TEACHER: teacher or co-teacher; STUDENT: has an ACTIVE enrollment; PARENT: any linked child has an ACTIVE enrollment) and assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN, teacher, co-teacher) for later write operations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Build /my-courses: TEACHER sees MUI Cards in a responsive Grid for each non-archived course they teach/co-teach this year (name, section, enrolled count); STUDENT sees cards for their ACTIVE enrollments (name, teacher); PARENT sees the same cards grouped by child.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sidebar nav entries: 'My courses' for TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT, and 'Sections'/'Courses' grouped under an 'Administration' section for ADMIN. NavItem currently has no grouping field — src/config/navigation.ts (verified) is a flat array with only Dashboard/Notifications/Email log entries and no 'group' concept, and no admin-facing pages exist yet for the PRD-02/PRD-03 entities (academic years, subjects, rooms, grade levels, users) that would also belong in such a group. The Architect must decide whether to add a lightweight `group` field to NavItem now or ship Sections/Courses as flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav grouping PRD lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; cross-checked against the current flat src/config/navigation.ts and the absence of an 'Administration' grouping or admin pages anywhere under src/app/(app)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Register student tab 'Courses' in src/config/student-tabs.ts (visible to every role that can view the student): a table of the student's courses this year with teacher and enrollment status, plus their section and homeroom teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing getAccessibleStudentIds(user) in src/server/auth/student-access.ts so a TEACHER additionally gets students with ACTIVE enrollments in courses they teach or co-teach, plus members of the section they are homeroom teacher of.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1; verified getAccessibleStudentIds already exists and is exported from src/server/auth/student-access.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Expose the full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":46,"newStart":1,"newLines":43,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T05:55:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-05\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\","," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox, plus EmailStatus enum (PENDING/SENDING/SENT/FAILED), per the schema block given.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Create a typed notification type registry at src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES (key -> label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles) with categories ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM, seeded with account.invite, account.password_reset and system.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Notification type registry\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"notify() must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TypeScript literal/union typing against the registry).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts that skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), creates a Notification row when in-app applies, and enqueues an EmailOutbox row when email applies and the user has an email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 notify() service\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"notify() must batch via createMany so notifying 1,000 users costs at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, and must never throw to the caller (log failures instead); callers invoke notify() after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3, FR-3.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }) that expands each student to the student plus all linked parents, deduplicated, for later PRDs (attendance, grades, assignments) to reuse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Build branded email templates with @react-email/components under src/server/email/templates/, rendered to both HTML and plain text, sharing a base layout (school logo/name header, content area, footer with school address, \\\"Manage email preferences\\\" link to /account/notifications, and the required disclosure sentence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Email templates\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Implement the invite, password-reset and generic-notification templates with the specified fields (name/school/accept-link/expiry; link/60-min expiry notice; title/body/CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Switch the existing PRD-01 auth email path onto the outbox: replace the current sendInvite() stub in src/server/services/users.ts (which only logs \\\"PRD-01 auth not landed yet\\\") with a sendAuthEmail() helper that enqueues the invite / password-reset templates via EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4; verified against src/server/services/users.ts:385-390 where sendInvite is currently a logging-only stub\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Section, SectionMember, Course and Enrollment, plus enums CourseKind (CORE/ELECTIVE) and EnrollmentStatus (ACTIVE/DROPPED), exactly per the schema block given, including the @@unique([academicYearId, name]) on Section, @@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember, @@unique([academicYearId, code]) on Course and @@unique([courseId, studentId]) + @@index([studentId, status]) on Enrollment.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections: filtered by academic year (defaults to current, reusing the existing AcademicYear model), with a table of name, grade level, homeroom teacher, room, members/capacity (warning colour at >=90%), and course count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"Section create/edit dialog: grade level, name, homeroom teacher (UserPicker filtered to role=TEACHER — the existing src/components/UserPicker already supports a role filter), room, capacity; a teacher may be homeroom teacher of at most one section per academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; verified against existing src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx which already accepts a `role` prop\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Build /admin/sections/[id]: members table with add (multi-select student picker filtered to the section's grade level and to students without a section this year) and remove; the section's course list; a 'Create core courses' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"'Create core courses' dialog: lists all active (non-archived) subjects with a checkbox and a teacher picker per subject; submitting creates one CORE course per checked subject with the default name/code pattern and enrolls all current section members in each created course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"'Copy sections to next year' action on /admin/sections, enabled only when a non-current, future academic year exists; copies section name, grade level advanced to the next GradeLevel by `order`, room and capacity, without members or teacher assignments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Auto-enroll on section add: adding a student to a section enrolls them ACTIVE in every non-archived CORE course of that section; a previously DROPPED enrollment in one of those courses is reactivated rather than duplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Auto-drop on section removal: removing a student from a section sets every ACTIVE enrollment in that section's CORE courses to DROPPED with droppedAt = now; elective enrollments are left untouched.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"'Move to section…' single action performs the FR-7 enroll and FR-8 drop steps for the destination/source sections in one database transaction, exposed via POST /api/students/:id/move-section.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3; API table row POST /api/students/:id/move-section\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Creating a new CORE course on a section enrolls all of that section's current members (ACTIVE) in the new course.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Capacity enforcement: adding a student beyond section or course capacity is refused with a CONFLICT error, message pattern 'Section 7A is full (30/30).', unless the admin explicitly ticks 'Override capacity'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; Acceptance Criteria #4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Dropped enrollments retain all historical data (attendance, grades) visible to admins and teachers, but dropped students disappear from active rosters and from add-student pickers.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses: filters for academic year, grade level, subject, teacher, kind, and free-text search by name/code; table of code, name, subject colour chip (reusing Subject.color, already on the model), section, teacher, enrolled count, kind.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1; verified Subject.color already exists on the Subject model in prisma/schema.prisma\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (optional, required when kind=CORE), teacher, up to 3 co-teachers, name, code (auto-filled from subject+section, editable, forced uppercase), kind, capacity, description.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Build /admin/courses/[id]/enrollment: enrolled-students table with drop/reactivate row actions and an 'Add students' picker; for CORE courses show an info note that membership is managed via the section instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /courses/[courseId] header: subject colour band, course name, code, teacher(s) (including co-teachers), section, room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add a course-tabs registry at src/config/course-tabs.ts (same shape as the existing src/config/student-tabs.ts, with a `roles` field) rendered as a scrollable MUI Tabs on the course home page; this PRD registers 'Overview' (description/teachers/counts, all roles that can view the course) and 'Roster' (TEACHER/ADMIN: full student list with avatar/name/admission number/link to student page/status; STUDENT: classmates' names only; PARENT: tab not shown).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; verified against the existing (empty) src/config/student-tabs.ts pattern this PRD is told to mirror\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add src/server/auth/course-access.ts exporting assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN: all; TEACHER: teacher or co-teacher; STUDENT: has an ACTIVE enrollment; PARENT: any linked child has an ACTIVE enrollment) and assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId) (ADMIN, teacher, co-teacher) for later write operations.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Build /my-courses: TEACHER sees MUI Cards in a responsive Grid for each non-archived course they teach/co-teach this year (name, section, enrolled count); STUDENT sees cards for their ACTIVE enrollments (name, teacher); PARENT sees the same cards grouped by child.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sidebar nav entries: 'My courses' for TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT, and 'Sections'/'Courses' grouped under an 'Administration' section for ADMIN. NavItem currently has no grouping field — src/config/navigation.ts (verified) is a flat array with only Dashboard/Notifications/Email log entries and no 'group' concept, and no admin-facing pages exist yet for the PRD-02/PRD-03 entities (academic years, subjects, rooms, grade levels, users) that would also belong in such a group. The Architect must decide whether to add a lightweight `group` field to NavItem now or ship Sections/Courses as flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav grouping PRD lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; cross-checked against the current flat src/config/navigation.ts and the absence of an 'Administration' grouping or admin pages anywhere under src/app/(app)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Register student tab 'Courses' in src/config/student-tabs.ts (visible to every role that can view the student): a table of the student's courses this year with teacher and enrollment status, plus their section and homeroom teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing getAccessibleStudentIds(user) in src/server/auth/student-access.ts so a TEACHER additionally gets students with ACTIVE enrollments in courses they teach or co-teach, plus members of the section they are homeroom teacher of.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1; verified getAccessibleStudentIds already exists and is exported from src/server/auth/student-access.ts\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Expose the full REST surface from the API table: sections CRUD + members + move-section + core-courses + copy-to-year; courses CRUD + roster + enrollments + enrollment status PATCH; GET /api/me/courses — each with the role gating shown in the table and the existing success/list/error response envelope and pagination/sort/search query conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Every write (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*) records an AuditLog row via the existing audit() helper.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table footnote 'All writes audit (section.*, course.*, enrollment.*)'; verified audit() already exists and is exported from src/server/audit.ts\" }","   ],","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element in the section/course/enrollment screens is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the MUI X packages (DataGrid via the existing shared DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, Snackbar+Alert via useToast()); every component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, react-select, etc.) in this PRD's code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD); Compliance Rule 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Integrity: the one-section-per-student-per-year rule is enforced by the database unique constraint (@@unique([studentId, academicYearId]) on SectionMember), not only in application code.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: adding 30 students to a section with 8 core courses (240 resulting enrollments) completes in under 1 second.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Privacy: on the course Roster tab and GET /api/courses/:id/roster, students see classmates' names only — no emails, admission numbers or profile links in the response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3; Acceptance Criteria #7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Scope containment: no timetable slots (PRD-06), no course content (PRD-08), no prerequisite or course-request workflows, and no automatic year-to-year student promotion — only the manual 'Copy sections to next year' shortcut.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization gap carried forward from PRD-01/PRD-04: the Platform Context describes src/server/auth/permissions.ts exposing requireUser()/requireRole(...roles), but only src/server/auth/requireRole.ts and student-access.ts exist today (no permissions.ts, no requireUser()). New route handlers in this PRD must use the existing requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)-style stand-in (as PRD-04's handoff also flagged) rather than invent a new auth helper, until PRD-01 lands.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement), cross-checked against the current contents of src/server/auth/ (only requireRole.ts and student-access.ts present)\" }","   ],","   \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,","   \"clarificationLog\": [],"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-04\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T05:55:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Add Prisma models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox, plus EmailStatus enum (PENDING/SENDING/SENT/FAILED), per the schema block given.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"Create a typed notification type registry at src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES (key -> label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles) with categories ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM, seeded with account.invite, account.password_reset and system.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Notification type registry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"notify() must reject unknown type keys at compile time (TypeScript literal/union typing against the registry).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts that skips archived/disabled users, resolves preferences (falling back to registry defaults), creates a Notification row when in-app applies, and enqueues an EmailOutbox row when email applies and the user has an email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 notify() service\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"notify() must batch via createMany so notifying 1,000 users costs at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, and must never throw to the caller (log failures instead); callers invoke notify() after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3, FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }) that expands each student to the student plus all linked parents, deduplicated, for later PRDs (attendance, grades, assignments) to reuse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"Build branded email templates with @react-email/components under src/server/email/templates/, rendered to both HTML and plain text, sharing a base layout (school logo/name header, content area, footer with school address, \\\"Manage email preferences\\\" link to /account/notifications, and the required disclosure sentence).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Email templates\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Implement the invite, password-reset and generic-notification templates with the specified fields (name/school/accept-link/expiry; link/60-min expiry notice; title/body/CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"Switch the existing PRD-01 auth email path onto the outbox: replace the current sendInvite() stub in src/server/services/users.ts (which only logs \\\"PRD-01 auth not landed yet\\\") with a sendAuthEmail() helper that enqueues the invite / password-reset templates via EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4; verified against src/server/services/users.ts:385-390 where sendInvite is currently a logging-only stub\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }) that selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, and marks SENT or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Dispatcher, point 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Apply the retry schedule: attempts 1-5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; mark FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch protected by header Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET} for an external scheduler, and an npm run worker:email script that loops dispatchEmails every 15 seconds for local/simple deployments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add env vars SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, SMTP_SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET, EMAIL_TRANSPORT (smtp|console, default console in dev); console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Replace the existing placeholder bell icon (currently a static Badge badgeContent={0} in src/app/(app)/shell.tsx line ~141) with a live unread-count bell: MUI IconButton + Badge, polling GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30s while the tab is visible, paused on visibilitychange hidden, displaying \\\"9+\\\" above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; verified against src/app/(app)/shell.tsx:141 current static Badge\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications (unread bold with a dot, title, 2-line-clamped body, relative time); clicking an item marks it read and navigates to its link. Footer actions: \\\"Mark all as read\\\" and \\\"View all\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: paginated list (20/page), All/Unread filter tabs, category filter, bulk \\\"Mark all as read\\\", per-row mark read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days, invoked from the dispatcher endpoint once per day (in-memory last-run tracking; acceptable to re-run after a restart).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build /account/notifications preferences page: MUI Table grouped by category (ListSubheader-style group rows), each visible type shows label, description, an In-app switch and an Email switch; mandatory in-app types show a disabled Switch with tooltip \\\"Required by the school\\\".\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately via PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI and rollback on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Build the admin /admin/email-log page: table of created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/last-error, filterable by status, with a \\\"Retry now\\\" row action for FAILED rows (resets attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now) and a \\\"Send test notification to me\\\" button calling notify({ type: 'system.test', ... }).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Expose the REST surface: GET /api/notifications (?unread=&category=&page=), GET /api/notifications/unread-count, POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /unread, POST /api/notifications/read-all, GET and PUT /api/me/notification-preferences, POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, GET /api/admin/email-log, POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, POST /api/admin/notifications/test — with the roles/auth and response-envelope conventions from PRD-00 (success/list/error shapes, pagination, error codes).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/me/notification-preferences must refuse inApp=false for mandatory (mandatoryInApp) types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table row for PUT /api/me/notification-preferences\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a sidebar navigation entry for the notifications page (and any admin email-log entry) in src/config/navigation.ts, following the existing NavItem convention (currently only a Dashboard entry exists).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions, cross-referenced with current src/config/navigation.ts (only Dashboard registered); PRD does not explicitly list the nav entries to add\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 sample Notification rows (one read, two unread) of type system.test linking to /dashboard, for student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Material UI only: every visible element built from @mui/material / @mui/icons-material / MUI X packages; no hand-styled raw HTML where an MUI component exists; every MUI component looked up via the MUI MCP server before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, notistack, etc.) must not appear in notification/email UI code; email templates are exempt and use @react-email/components instead.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory, applies to every screen in this PRD)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"notify() for 1,000 recipients must complete in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"GET /api/notifications/unread-count must respond in under 50ms, backed by the (userId, readAt, createdAt) index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"An email must never be sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row-level locking via FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED); rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes must be recovered back to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Notification link values must be relative paths starting with \\\"/\\\" (validated) to prevent open redirects; email HTML must escape all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Every outbound email must include both HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at the preferences page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements #4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Server-side authorization: every notification/email-log route enforces access via requireUser()/requireRole() from src/server/auth (own-notifications-only for user-facing routes, ADMIN-only for /api/admin/email-log and related actions, CRON_SECRET bearer check for the internal dispatch route) — hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context > Code layout conventions (server-side access enforcement rule), applied to this PRD's API surface\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Dispatching without the correct CRON_SECRET bearer token returns 401 using the standard error envelope.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Acceptance Criteria #6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Keep all existing tests passing (npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test) and add the unit/integration/Playwright tests listed in Test Requirements.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints; Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Scope must not expand beyond this PRD's sections: no SMS/push, no real-time websockets (bell polls only), no digest emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false}}
