{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgT3sEVB87ATnxiaQ2fg2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SkmgfJMyWJ7WeZ8uEnpcT7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories — Ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05: Sections, Courses & Enrollment)\n\n## Sections\n\n- **[FR-1]** As the system, I need Section, SectionMember, Course and Enrollment data models so that homeroom groups, subject classes and student enrollment can be tracked and enforced at the database level.\n- **[FR-2]** As an admin, I want to see all sections for an academic year in one table (with roster size vs. capacity and course count at a glance) so that I can spot full or empty sections quickly.\n- **[FR-3]** As an admin, I want to create or edit a section with a homeroom teacher, room and capacity so that students have a home group, and so that a teacher is never accidentally double-booked as homeroom teacher for two sections in the same year.\n- **[FR-4]** As an admin, I want a section detail page where I can add or remove students and see the section's courses so that I can manage membership without leaving the section's context.\n- **[FR-5]** As an admin, I want a \"Create core courses\" shortcut that creates one course per subject (with a teacher assigned) and enrolls the whole section at once so that I can set up a section's whole course load in minutes instead of one course at a time.\n- **[FR-6]** As an admin, I want to copy a section's structure (name, grade level, room, capacity) into next year without copying its members so that I don't have to rebuild sections from scratch every year.\n\n## Enrollment rules\n\n- **[FR-7]** As an admin, I want adding a student to a section to automatically enroll them in that section's core courses so that I don't have to enroll them in each subject separately.\n- **[FR-8]** As an admin, I want removing a student from a section to automatically drop their core-course enrollments (leaving electives untouched) so that rosters stay accurate without manual cleanup.\n- **[FR-9]** As an admin, I want a single \"Move to section…\" action so that transferring a student between sections drops the old core enrollments and adds the new ones atomically, with no inconsistent in-between state.\n- **[FR-10]** As an admin, I want creating a new core course on a section to automatically enroll the section's current members so that a newly added subject doesn't require re-enrolling everyone by hand.\n- **[FR-11]** As an admin, I want to be blocked (with a clear message) from over-filling a section or course unless I explicitly override capacity so that class sizes stay intentional.\n- **[FR-12]** As an admin or teacher, I want dropped enrollments to keep their historical attendance and grade data so that past records are never lost even after a student leaves a class.\n\n## Courses\n\n- **[FR-13]** As an admin, I want to filter and search all courses by year, grade, subject, teacher and kind so that I can find any class quickly.\n- **[FR-14]** As an admin, I want to create or edit a course for a subject, section and teacher (with up to 3 co-teachers) so that teaching responsibility is clearly organised.\n- **[FR-15]** As an admin, I want a dedicated enrollment screen per course so that I can add, drop or reactivate students directly — understanding that core-course membership is actually driven by the section.\n- **[FR-16] [FR-17] [FR-18]** As a teacher, student or parent, I want a course home page with an Overview and a Roster tab (showing only what my role is allowed to see) so that I can see who's in the class without being shown information I'm not entitled to.\n\n## My courses\n\n- **[FR-19]** As a teacher, I want to see my courses and their rosters so that I know who I teach.\n- **[FR-19]** As a student, I want to see my courses and teachers so that I know my classes.\n- **[FR-19]** As a parent, I want my children's courses grouped by child so that I can tell at a glance what each of my kids is taking.\n- **[FR-20]** As any user, I want \"My courses\" (or \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" for admins) in the sidebar so that I can reach my classes in one click.\n\n## Student record integration\n\n- **[FR-21]** As anyone who can view a student's profile, I want a \"Courses\" tab on the student page listing their courses, teachers and section so that I don't have to cross-reference multiple screens.\n- **[FR-22]** As a teacher, I want the students I teach or am homeroom teacher for to count as \"my students\" everywhere access is checked, so that I can see their records consistent with my actual teaching load.\n\n## Platform / API\n\n- **[FR-23]** As a developer integrating with this feature, I want a consistent REST surface for sections, courses and enrollments (pagination, filters, role-gated) so that client code follows the same conventions as the rest of the app.\n- **[FR-24]** As an admin, I want every section/course/enrollment change audited so that there's a trail of who changed what.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **[NFR-1]** The system must build every section/course/enrollment screen from Material UI components only, looked up via the MUI MCP server — no banned styling/component libraries.\n- **[NFR-2]** The one-section-per-student-per-year rule must be enforced by a database constraint, not just application logic.\n- **[NFR-3]** Enrolling 30 students into an 8-core-course section (240 enrollments) must complete in under 1 second.\n- **[NFR-4]** Students viewing a course roster must see classmates' names only — never emails, admission numbers or profile links.\n- **[NFR-5]** All existing lint/typecheck/test commands must keep passing, and the new unit/integration/Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section must be added.\n- **[NFR-6]** This ticket must not expand into timetable slots, course content, prerequisites/course-requests, or automatic year-to-year promotion.\n- **[NFR-7]** (Flagged — MEDIUM confidence) Until PRD-01's `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()` lands, new routes in this PRD use the existing `requireRole()` stand-in pattern for server-side access control.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":63576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":619},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d389a295-cb2f-420f-b796-e4611e89acf2","uuid":"fe789d74-6253-4687-910d-a32f517e8eb2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:23:16.720Z","request_id":"req_011CgT3sEF3w3GC5DyxU5HEs"}
