ave to rebuild sections from scratch every year.\n\n## Enrollment rules\n\n- **[FR-7]** As an admin, I want adding a student to a section to automatically enroll them in that section's core courses so that I don't have to enroll them in each subject separately.\n- **[FR-8]** As an admin, I want removing a student from a section to automatically drop their core-course enrollments (leaving electives untouched) so that rosters stay accurate without manual cleanup.\n- **[FR-9]** As an admin, I want a single \"Move to section…\" action so that transferring a student between sections drops the old core enrollments and adds the new ones atomically, with no inconsistent in-between state.\n- **[FR-10]** As an admin, I want creating a new core course on a section to automatically enroll the section's current members so that a newly added subject doesn't require re-enrolling everyone by hand.\n- **[FR-11]** As an admin, I want to be blocked (with a clear message) from over-filling a section or course unless I explicitly override capacity so that class sizes stay intentional.\n- **[FR-12]** As an admin or teacher, I want dropped enrollments to keep their historical attendance and grade data so that past records are never lost even after a student leaves a class.\n\n## Courses\n\n- **[FR-13]** As an admin, I want to filter and search all courses by year, grade, subject, teacher and kind so that I can find any class quickly.\n- **[FR-14]** As an admin, I want to create or edit a course for a subject, section and teacher (with up to 3 co-teachers) so that teaching responsibility is clearly organised.\n- **[FR-15]** As an admin, I want a dedicated enrollment screen per course so that I can add, drop or reactivate students directly — understanding that core-course membership is actually driven by the section.\n- **[FR-16] [FR-17] [FR-18]** As a teacher, student or parent, I want a course home page with an Overview and a Roster tab (showing only what my role is allowed to see) so that I can see who's in the class without being shown information I'm not entitled to.\n\n## My courses\n\n- **[FR-19]** As a teacher, I want to see my courses and their rosters so that I know who I teach.\n- **[FR-19]** As a student, I want to see my courses and teachers so that I know my classes.\n- **[FR-19]** As a parent, I want my children's courses grouped by child so that I can tell at a glance what each of my kids is taking.\n- **[FR-20]** As any user, I want \"My courses\" (or \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" for admins) in the sidebar so that I can reach my classes in one click.\n\n## Student record integration\n\n- **[FR-21]** As anyone who can view a student's profile, I want a \"Courses\" tab on the student page listing their courses, teachers and section so that I don't have to cross-reference multiple screens.\n- **[FR-22]** As a teacher, I want the students I teach or am homeroom teacher for to count as \"my students\" everywhere access is checked, so that I can see their records consistent with my actual teaching load.\n\n## Platform / API\n\n- **[FR-23]** As a developer integrating with this feature, I want a consistent REST surface for sections, courses and enrollments (pagination, filters, role-gated) so that client code follows the same conventions as the rest of the app.\n- **[FR-24]** As an admin, I want every section/course/enrollment change audited so that there's a trail of who changed what.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **[NFR-1]** The system must build every section/course/enrollment screen from Material UI components only, looked up via the MUI MCP server — no banned styling/component libraries.\n- **[NFR-2]** The one-section-per-student-per-year rule must be enforced by a database constraint, not just application logic.\n- **[NFR-3]** Enrolling 30 students into an 8-core-course section (240 enrollments) must complete in under 1 second.\n- **[NFR-4]** Students viewing a course roster must see classmates' names only — never emails, admission numbers or profile links.\n- **[NFR-5]** All existing lint/typecheck/test commands must keep passing, and the new unit/integration/Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section must be added.\n- **[NFR-6]** This ticket must not expand into timetable slots, course content, prerequisites/course-requests, or automatic year-to-year promotion.\n- **[NFR-7]** (Flagged — MEDIUM confidence) Until PRD-01's `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()` lands, new routes in this PRD use the existing `requireRole()` stand-in pattern for server-side access control.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":50,"newStart":1,"newLines":53,"lines":["-# User Stories — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (abcd-04)","+# User Stories — Ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05: Sections, Courses & Enrollment)"," ","-## Data & service layer","+## Sections"," ","-- **FR-1 / FR-2 / FR-3** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` models plus a typed notification-type registry, so that I have a durable place to store notifications and emails and can't accidentally notify with an unregistered type.","-- **FR-4 / FR-5 / FR-6** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want a single `notify()` call (and a `notifyStudentAndParents()` helper) that handles preferences, batching and failure isolation for me, so that I never have to hand-roll notification or email delivery.","+- **[FR-1]** As the system, I need Section, SectionMember, Course and Enrollment data models so that homeroom groups, subject classes and student enrollment can be tracked and enforced at the database level.","+- **[FR-2]** As an admin, I want to see all sections for an academic year in one table (with roster size vs. capacity and course count at a glance) so that I can spot full or empty sections quickly.","+- **[FR-3]** As an admin, I want to create or edit a section with a homeroom teacher, room and capacity so that students have a home group, and so that a teacher is never accidentally double-booked as homeroom teacher for two sections in the same year.","+- **[FR-4]** As an admin, I want a section detail page where I can add or remove students and see the section's courses so that I can manage membership without leaving the section's context.","+- **[FR-5]** As an admin, I want a \"Create core courses\" shortcut that creates one course per subject (with a teacher assigned) and enrolls the whole section at once so that I can set up a section's whole course load in minutes instead of one course at a time.","+- **[FR-6]** As an admin, I want to copy a section's structure (name, grade level, room, capacity) into next year without copying its members so that I don't have to rebuild sections from scratch every year."," ","-## Email templates & delivery","+## Enrollment rules"," ","-- **FR-7 / FR-8** — As a recipient of a SchoolHub email, I want a consistently branded email (school header, clear content, footer with an unsubscribe/preferences link) so that I trust and recognize messages from the school.","-- **FR-9** — As an admin resending an invite, I want the invite email to actually be queued and sent (not just logged), so that new users reliably receive their account invitation.","-- **FR-10 / FR-11 / FR-12 / FR-13** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry automatically and the system to dispatch them within a minute, so that important messages are not silently lost. *(Acceptance Criteria #3, #4)*","+- **[FR-7]** As an admin, I want adding a student to a section to automatically enroll them in that section's core courses so that I don't have to enroll them in each subject separately.","+- **[FR-8]** As an admin, I want removing a student from a section to automatically drop their core-course enrollments (leaving electives untouched) so that rosters stay accurate without manual cleanup.","+- **[FR-9]** As an admin, I want a single \"Move to section…\" action so that transferring a student between sections drops the old core enrollments and adds the new ones atomically, with no inconsistent in-between state.","+- **[FR-10]** As an admin, I want creating a new core course on a section to automatically enroll the section's current members so that a newly added subject doesn't require re-enrolling everyone by hand.","+- **[FR-11]** As an admin, I want to be blocked (with a clear message) from over-filling a section or course unless I explicitly override capacity so that class sizes stay intentional.","+- **[FR-12]** As an admin or teacher, I want dropped enrollments to keep their historical attendance and grade data so that past records are never lost even after a student leaves a class."," ","-## Notification bell & centre","+## Courses"," ","-- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity. *(User Story 1)*","-- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it. *(User Story 2, Acceptance Criteria #5)*","-- **FR-16** — As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable. *(User Story 3)*","-- **FR-17** — As the platform, I want notifications older than 180 days purged automatically so that the list and database stay lean.","+- **[FR-13]** As an admin, I want to filter and search all courses by year, grade, subject, teacher and kind so that I can find any class quickly.","+- **[FR-14]** As an admin, I want to create or edit a course for a subject, section and teacher (with up to 3 co-teachers) so that teaching responsibility is clearly organised.","+- **[FR-15]** As an admin, I want a dedicated enrollment screen per course so that I can add, drop or reactivate students directly — understanding that core-course membership is actually driven by the section.","+- **[FR-16] [FR-17] [FR-18]** As a teacher, student or parent, I want a course home page with an Overview and a Roster tab (showing only what my role is allowed to see) so that I can see who's in the class without being shown information I'm not entitled to."," ","-## Preferences","+## My courses"," ","-- **FR-18 / FR-19 / FR-22** — As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded. *(User Story 4)*","+- **[FR-19]** As a teacher, I want to see my courses and their rosters so that I know who I teach.","+- **[FR-19]** As a student, I want to see my courses and teachers so that I know my classes.","+- **[FR-19]** As a parent, I want my children's courses grouped by child so that I can tell at a glance what each of my kids is taking.","+- **[FR-20]** As any user, I want \"My courses\" (or \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" for admins) in the sidebar so that I can reach my classes in one click."," ","-## Admin","+## Student record integration"," ","-- **FR-20** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible in a log so that important messages are not silently lost, with a one-click retry and a test-send button. *(User Story 5)*","+- **[FR-21]** As anyone who can view a student's profile, I want a \"Courses\" tab on the student page listing their courses, teachers and section so that I don't have to cross-reference multiple screens.","+- **[FR-22]** As a teacher, I want the students I teach or am homeroom teacher for to count as \"my students\" everywhere access is checked, so that I can see their records consistent with my actual teaching load."," ","-## API surface","+## Platform / API"," ","-- **FR-21** — As a frontend client, I want a consistent REST surface for notifications, preferences, dispatch and the admin log so that every screen above has a stable contract to call.","-- **FR-23** — As a user navigating the app, I want \"Notifications\" (and the admin email log, for admins) in the sidebar so that I can find these new pages.","+- **[FR-23]** As a developer integrating with this feature, I want a consistent REST surface for sections, courses and enrollments (pagination, filters, role-gated) so that client code follows the same conventions as the rest of the app.","+- **[FR-24]** As an admin, I want every section/course/enrollment change audited so that there's a trail of who changed what."," ","-## Seed data","-","-- **FR-24** — As a developer testing locally, I want sample notifications pre-seeded for a student and parent account so that I can see the bell and list populated without manually triggering `notify()`.","-","----","-"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **NFR-1** — Every screen in this PRD (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences page, admin email log) must be built only from MUI components looked up via the MUI MCP server; no banned UI libraries. Email templates are the one exception, using `@react-email/components`.","-- **NFR-2 / NFR-3** — `notify()` must handle 1,000 recipients in under 2 seconds; the unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50ms.","-- **NFR-4** — Concurrent dispatchers must never double-send an email; rows stuck in `SENDING` for 10+ minutes recover to `PENDING`.","-- **NFR-5** — Notification links must be validated relative paths; email HTML must escape user-provided text.","-- **NFR-6** — Every email has HTML + plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header.","-- **NFR-7** — Every notification/email-log route enforces authorization server-side (`requireUser()`/`requireRole()`/`CRON_SECRET`), never relying on hidden UI alone.","-- **NFR-8** — Dispatch requests without a valid `CRON_SECRET` bearer token return `401`.","-- **NFR-9** — Existing lint/typecheck/test suites keep passing; new unit, integration and Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section are added.","-- **NFR-10** — No SMS/push, no websockets, no digest emails in this PRD.","+- **[NFR-1]** The system must build every section/course/enrollment screen from Material UI components only, looked up via the MUI MCP server — no banned styling/component libraries.","+- **[NFR-2]** The one-section-per-student-per-year rule must be enforced by a database constraint, not just application logic.","+- **[NFR-3]** Enrolling 30 students into an 8-core-course section (240 enrollments) must complete in under 1 second.","+- **[NFR-4]** Students viewing a course roster must see classmates' names only — never emails, admission numbers or profile links.","+- **[NFR-5]** All existing lint/typecheck/test commands must keep passing, and the new unit/integration/Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section must be added.","+- **[NFR-6]** This ticket must not expand into timetable slots, course content, prerequisites/course-requests, or automatic year-to-year promotion.","+- **[NFR-7]** (Flagged — MEDIUM confidence) Until PRD-01's `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()` lands, new routes in this PRD use the existing `requireRole()` stand-in pattern for server-side access control."]}],"originalFile":"# User Stories — PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure (abcd-04)\n\n## Data & service layer\n\n- **FR-1 / FR-2 / FR-3** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` models plus a typed notification-type registry, so that I have a durable place to store notifications and emails and can't accidentally notify with an unregistered type.\n- **FR-4 / FR-5 / FR-6** — As a developer on a later feature PRD, I want a single `notify()` call (and a `notifyStudentAndParents()` helper) that handles preferences, batching and failure isolation for me, so that I never have to hand-roll notification or email delivery.\n\n## Email templates & delivery\n\n- **FR-7 / FR-8** — As a recipient of a SchoolHub email, I want a consistently branded email (school header, clear content, footer with an unsubscribe/preferences link) so that I trust and recognize messages from the school.\n- **FR-9** — As an admin resending an invite, I want the invite email to actually be queued and sent (not just logged), so that new users reliably receive their account invitation.\n- **FR-10 / FR-11 / FR-12 / FR-13** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry automatically and the system to dispatch them within a minute, so that important messages are not silently lost. *(Acceptance Criteria #3, #4)*\n\n## Notification bell & centre\n\n- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity. *(User Story 1)*\n- **FR-14 / FR-15** — As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it. *(User Story 2, Acceptance Criteria #5)*\n- **FR-16** — As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable. *(User Story 3)*\n- **FR-17** — As the platform, I want notifications older than 180 days purged automatically so that the list and database stay lean.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **FR-18 / FR-19 / FR-22** — As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded. *(User Story 4)*\n\n## Admin\n\n- **FR-20** — As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible in a log so that important messages are not silently lost, with a one-click retry and a test-send button. *(User Story 5)*\n\n## API surface\n\n- **FR-21** — As a frontend client, I want a consistent REST surface for notifications, preferences, dispatch and the admin log so that every screen above has a stable contract to call.\n- **FR-23** — As a user navigating the app, I want \"Notifications\" (and the admin email log, for admins) in the sidebar so that I can find these new pages.\n\n## Seed data\n\n- **FR-24** — As a developer testing locally, I want sample notifications pre-seeded for a student and parent account so that I can see the bell and list populated without manually triggering `notify()`.\n\n---\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** — Every screen in this PRD (bell, popover, notifications page, preferences page, admin email log) must be built only from MUI components looked up via the MUI MCP server; no banned UI libraries. Email templates are the one exception, using `@react-email/components`.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3** — `notify()` must handle 1,000 recipients in under 2 seconds; the unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50ms.\n- **NFR-4** — Concurrent dispatchers must never double-send an email; rows stuck in `SENDING` for 10+ minutes recover to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-5** — Notification links must be validated relative paths; email HTML must escape user-provided text.\n- **NFR-6** — Every email has HTML + plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header.\n- **NFR-7** — Every notification/email-log route enforces authorization server-side (`requireUser()`/`requireRole()`/`CRON_SECRET`), never relying on hidden UI alone.\n- **NFR-8** — Dispatch requests without a valid `CRON_SECRET` bearer token return `401`.\n- **NFR-9** — Existing lint/typecheck/test suites keep passing; new unit, integration and Playwright tests from the Test Requirements section are added.\n- **NFR-10** — No SMS/push, no websockets, no digest emails in this PRD.\n","userModified":false}}
