{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgT3uk4VBZ5qD4UbVBwdq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake phase for ticket **abcd-05** (PRD-05: Sections, Courses & Enrollment) is done. All four required artifacts are in `artifacts/intake/`, valid JSON, written in order with the handoff last; `figma-readiness.json` was correctly skipped (no Figma URL in the PRD).\n\nWhat I checked against the actual codebase before writing anything (not just the PRD text):\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`, `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/components/UserPicker`, `src/components/DataTable`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts` — confirming what PRD-05 can safely reuse (`AcademicYear`, `GradeLevel`, `Subject.color`, `Room`, `getAccessibleStudentIds`, `audit()`, `UserPicker`'s role filter).\n- Found two real brownfield gaps, flagged rather than silently assumed away:\n  - **FR-20 (MEDIUM):** PRD-05 assumes an \"Administration\" nav group; `navigation.ts` is flat today with no group concept and no admin pages for earlier PRDs' entities.\n  - **NFR-7 (MEDIUM):** PRD-05's Platform Context assumes `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` + `requireUser()`; only `requireRole.ts` exists — same gap PRD-04's architect handoff already flagged, so routes should keep using the `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` stand-in.\n\n31 requirements extracted (24 FR, 7 NFR), overall confidence 97% — above the 80% threshold, so no clarification round was needed; both gaps are carried forward as advisory blockers in `handoff-to-architect.json` instead of stalling the pipeline."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":606,"cache_read_input_tokens":67077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":606},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"dia