reateUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",\n    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",\n    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",\n        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",\n        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",\n        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",\n        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",\n        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",\n        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",\n        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",\n        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":75,"newStart":3,"newLines":92,"lines":["   \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","+  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",","+  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\","," ","+  \"brownfieldFindings\": [","+    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",","+    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",","+    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",","+    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",","+    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",","+    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",","+    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",","+    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"","+  ],","+","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog match the PRD's FR-1 schema block; these already exist in prisma/schema.prisma, so only add the gaps (e.g. User @@index([role, status]), AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) via a prisma migration without renaming existing fields or relations.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; brownfield check of prisma/schema.prisma\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"User.email is stored lower-cased and trimmed on every write and lookup.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build a public /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment + IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form-level errors) with email and password fields that submits via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1; §Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Configure Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a Credentials provider whose authorize function lower-cases/trims the email and rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, then verifies the password with bcrypt (cost 12); expose handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2; §Fixed technology decisions (Auth); §Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Sign-in failures show exactly 'Email or password is incorrect.' (including INVITED users), except a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; §Acceptance Criteria 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"On a wrong password increment failedLoginCount; at 5 set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the count to 0; on success reset failedLoginCount to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; §Acceptance Criteria 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Create a reusable in-memory sliding-window rate limiter in src/server/rate-limit.ts and limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes; exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; §Acceptance Criteria 1; §Test Requirements (callbackUrl same-origin check)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; §Acceptance Criteria 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use a JWT session strategy with an 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if the user's passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; §Acceptance Criteria 7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Add middleware.ts that redirects unauthenticated requests under the (app) group to /login?callbackUrl=<path> and returns 401 JSON (error.code UNAUTHENTICATED) for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in a new src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; §Goals 2; §Acceptance Criteria 8\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single producer/consumer of AuthToken rows, exposing createToken(userId, type, ttl) returning a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and storing only its SHA-256 hash, verifyToken(rawToken, type) returning the user/token or null when missing/used/expired, and consumeToken(tokenId) setting usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2; prisma/schema.prisma AuthToken doc comment\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Build public /invite/[token] page: verify the INVITE token (7-day expiry); if invalid/used/expired show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'; otherwise show read-only name and email with new password + confirm fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1–4.2; §Acceptance Criteria 4–5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"POST /api/auth/accept-invite ({ token, password }) validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; §Pages & Routes; §Acceptance Criteria 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy Zod schema in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-most-common list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; §Acceptance Criteria 10\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under every new-password field indicating each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build public /forgot-password page and POST /api/auth/forgot-password that always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' and rate-limits to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Pages & Routes; §Acceptance Criteria 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"When the forgot-password email belongs to an ACTIVE user, invalidate older unused PASSWORD_RESET tokens, create a new one with a 60-minute TTL via tokens.ts, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link); create no token row for unknown emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; §Acceptance Criteria 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sendAuthEmail(user, template, link) which, until PRD-04's outbox wiring is applied, logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail bullet); §FR-6.2; §FR-8.3 — EmailOutbox model already exists in the workspace, so whether to log or enqueue now needs architect confirmation\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Build public /reset-password/[token] page and POST /api/auth/reset-password ({ token, password }) that sets the new hash, passwordChangedAt = now, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a success toast via useToast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; §Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Build /account/security page (any signed-in role) and POST /api/account/password ({ currentPassword, newPassword }); wrong current password returns field error 'Current password is incorrect.'; success shows toast 'Password updated', sets passwordChangedAt to invalidate other sessions and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; §Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing createUser() in src/server/services/users.ts creating an INVITED user and throwing CONFLICT when the email exists (verify, do not re-implement).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; brownfield check: createUser already exported at users.ts\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts that invalidates older unused INVITE tokens and calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 }), returning the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite(userId) stub in users.ts so it calls createInviteToken() and sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), preserving its existing return shape used by /api/users/[id]/invite and userImport.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield check: stub at users.ts:388\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Keep setUserStatus and unlockUser available in users.ts; the existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status), which differs from the PRD's (userId, status) — keep the existing signature so current callers do not break.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.4; brownfield check: users.ts:344 and src/app/api/users/[id]/status/route.ts\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (session user or throws AppError('UNAUTHENTICATED'); server pages redirect to /login); do not create a separate permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1–9.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN when not listed (server pages redirect to /forbidden), keeping its call signature so its ~44 existing callers keep working.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4; §Acceptance Criteria 9; brownfield check: 44 files call requireRole\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Do not add a generic can(user, action, resource) helper and do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.5; §Out of Scope (per-entity RBAC bullet)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts to accept an optional request and capture the IP from x-forwarded-for (stored in the existing AuditLog.ip column), still never throwing.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield check: audit.ts exists without request param; AuditLog column is 'ip' not 'ipAddress'\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata must never contain password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the real session user; the top-bar user menu shows name, role badge and avatar initials, and 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1–11.2; §Acceptance Criteria 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Filter src/config/navigation.ts items by the session role instead of the placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can become ACTIVE.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Extend prisma/seed.ts (idempotently) with six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password 'SchoolHub123!') and one INVITED user invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Add tests: unit (password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check), integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and Playwright (sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot → reset).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }","   ],"," ","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (SHA-256 hashes only) and are compared in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in for a non-existent user runs a dummy bcrypt compare so its timing is similar to a wrong-password response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite' and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible UI element uses Material UI / MUI X only, each component looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use, no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, notistack, sonner, etc.); QA checks for no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented. Toasts use the existing useToast() hook (located at src/components/Toast/, not src/components/shared/).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule 1–6 (rule 6 mandates recording this as an NFR)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every protected handler and server page enforces access server-side via requireUser/requireRole; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); §Goals 2–3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (Zod parse → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and codes (UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, etc.).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers and response shape bullets)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code (use logger from src/lib/logger.ts) and no new UI/styling dependencies; reuse existing helpers and never re-scaffold or rename existing routes/models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Code layout and conventions (logger bullet)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Existing checks stay green: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test; scope must not expand beyond this PRD (no admin user-management screens, SSO, MFA, magic links or email infrastructure).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }","   ],"," ","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-1: AuditLog already exists with column 'ip' (PRD says 'ipAddress') and an actor relation, and indexes differ from the PRD block. Keep the existing column name and only add the missing indexes (assumed), or rename?\",","-        \"FR-20: EmailOutbox model already exists in the workspace (PRD-04 schema landed) but no src/server/notifications code was found. Should sendAuthEmail() log via logger.info as the PRD's Out of Scope bullet says (assumed), or enqueue into EmailOutbox now?\",","-        \"FR-27: Existing setUserStatus signature is (actorId, userId, status) vs the PRD's (userId, status). Keep existing signature (assumed) to avoid breaking /api/users/[id]/status?\",","-        \"FR-31: Extend existing audit() with an optional request param rather than replacing it (assumed)?\"","+        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",","+        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",","+        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",","+        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",","+        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",","+        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"FR-1 AuditLog field naming (ip vs ipAddress) — proceeding with existing 'ip' per 'never rename existing models' constraint.\",","-        \"FR-20 sendAuthEmail log-vs-enqueue — proceeding with logger.info per PRD Out of Scope.\",","-        \"FR-27 setUserStatus signature — proceeding with existing (actorId, userId, status).\",","-        \"FR-31 audit() request param — proceeding by extending the existing helper.\"","+        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",","+        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",","+        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",","+        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"","       ]","     }","   ],"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog match the PRD's FR-1 schema block; these already exist in prisma/schema.prisma, so only add the gaps (e.g. User @@index([role, status]), AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) via a prisma migration without renaming existing fields or relations.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; brownfield check of prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"User.email is stored lower-cased and trimmed on every write and lookup.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build a public /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment + IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form-level errors) with email and password fields that submits via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1; §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Configure Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a Credentials provider whose authorize function lower-cases/trims the email and rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, then verifies the password with bcrypt (cost 12); expose handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2; §Fixed technology decisions (Auth); §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Sign-in failures show exactly 'Email or password is incorrect.' (including INVITED users), except a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; §Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"On a wrong password increment failedLoginCount; at 5 set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the count to 0; on success reset failedLoginCount to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; §Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Create a reusable in-memory sliding-window rate limiter in src/server/rate-limit.ts and limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes; exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; §Acceptance Criteria 1; §Test Requirements (callbackUrl same-origin check)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; §Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use a JWT session strategy with an 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if the user's passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; §Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Add middleware.ts that redirects unauthenticated requests under the (app) group to /login?callbackUrl=<path> and returns 401 JSON (error.code UNAUTHENTICATED) for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in a new src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; §Goals 2; §Acceptance Criteria 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single producer/consumer of AuthToken rows, exposing createToken(userId, type, ttl) returning a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and storing only its SHA-256 hash, verifyToken(rawToken, type) returning the user/token or null when missing/used/expired, and consumeToken(tokenId) setting usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2; prisma/schema.prisma AuthToken doc comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Build public /invite/[token] page: verify the INVITE token (7-day expiry); if invalid/used/expired show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'; otherwise show read-only name and email with new password + confirm fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1–4.2; §Acceptance Criteria 4–5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"POST /api/auth/accept-invite ({ token, password }) validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; §Pages & Routes; §Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy Zod schema in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-most-common list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; §Acceptance Criteria 10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under every new-password field indicating each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Build public /forgot-password page and POST /api/auth/forgot-password that always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' and rate-limits to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Pages & Routes; §Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"When the forgot-password email belongs to an ACTIVE user, invalidate older unused PASSWORD_RESET tokens, create a new one with a 60-minute TTL via tokens.ts, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link); create no token row for unknown emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; §Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Add sendAuthEmail(user, template, link) which, until PRD-04's outbox wiring is applied, logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail bullet); §FR-6.2; §FR-8.3 — EmailOutbox model already exists in the workspace, so whether to log or enqueue now needs architect confirmation\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Build public /reset-password/[token] page and POST /api/auth/reset-password ({ token, password }) that sets the new hash, passwordChangedAt = now, clears failedLoginCount/lockedUntil, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a success toast via useToast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Build /account/security page (any signed-in role) and POST /api/account/password ({ currentPassword, newPassword }); wrong current password returns field error 'Current password is incorrect.'; success shows toast 'Password updated', sets passwordChangedAt to invalidate other sessions and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing createUser() in src/server/services/users.ts creating an INVITED user and throwing CONFLICT when the email exists (verify, do not re-implement).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; brownfield check: createUser already exported at users.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts that invalidates older unused INVITE tokens and calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 }), returning the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite(userId) stub in users.ts so it calls createInviteToken() and sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), preserving its existing return shape used by /api/users/[id]/invite and userImport.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield check: stub at users.ts:388\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Keep setUserStatus and unlockUser available in users.ts; the existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status), which differs from the PRD's (userId, status) — keep the existing signature so current callers do not break.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.4; brownfield check: users.ts:344 and src/app/api/users/[id]/status/route.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (session user or throws AppError('UNAUTHENTICATED'); server pages redirect to /login); do not create a separate permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1–9.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN when not listed (server pages redirect to /forbidden), keeping its call signature so its ~44 existing callers keep working.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4; §Acceptance Criteria 9; brownfield check: 44 files call requireRole\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Do not add a generic can(user, action, resource) helper and do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.5; §Out of Scope (per-entity RBAC bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts to accept an optional request and capture the IP from x-forwarded-for (stored in the existing AuditLog.ip column), still never throwing.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield check: audit.ts exists without request param; AuditLog column is 'ip' not 'ipAddress'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata must never contain password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the real session user; the top-bar user menu shows name, role badge and avatar initials, and 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1–11.2; §Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Filter src/config/navigation.ts items by the session role instead of the placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can become ACTIVE.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Extend prisma/seed.ts (idempotently) with six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password 'SchoolHub123!') and one INVITED user invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Add tests: unit (password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check), integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and Playwright (sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot → reset).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (SHA-256 hashes only) and are compared in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in for a non-existent user runs a dummy bcrypt compare so its timing is similar to a wrong-password response.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite' and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible UI element uses Material UI / MUI X only, each component looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use, no banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, notistack, sonner, etc.); QA checks for no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented. Toasts use the existing useToast() hook (located at src/components/Toast/, not src/components/shared/).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule 1–6 (rule 6 mandates recording this as an NFR)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every protected handler and server page enforces access server-side via requireUser/requireRole; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); §Goals 2–3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (Zod parse → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and codes (UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, etc.).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers and response shape bullets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code (use logger from src/lib/logger.ts) and no new UI/styling dependencies; reuse existing helpers and never re-scaffold or rename existing routes/models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Code layout and conventions (logger bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Existing checks stay green: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test; scope must not expand beyond this PRD (no admin user-management screens, SSO, MFA, magic links or email infrastructure).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-1: AuditLog already exists with column 'ip' (PRD says 'ipAddress') and an actor relation, and indexes differ from the PRD block. Keep the existing column name and only add the missing indexes (assumed), or rename?\",\n        \"FR-20: EmailOutbox model already exists in the workspace (PRD-04 schema landed) but no src/server/notifications code was found. Should sendAuthEmail() log via logger.info as the PRD's Out of Scope bullet says (assumed), or enqueue into EmailOutbox now?\",\n        \"FR-27: Existing setUserStatus signature is (actorId, userId, status) vs the PRD's (userId, status). Keep existing signature (assumed) to avoid breaking /api/users/[id]/status?\",\n        \"FR-31: Extend existing audit() with an optional request param rather than replacing it (assumed)?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-1 AuditLog field naming (ip vs ipAddress) — proceeding with existing 'ip' per 'never rename existing models' constraint.\",\n        \"FR-20 sendAuthEmail log-vs-enqueue — proceeding with logger.info per PRD Out of Scope.\",\n        \"FR-27 setUserStatus signature — proceeding with existing (actorId, userId, status).\",\n        \"FR-31 audit() request param — proceeding by extending the existing helper.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BDPBbbgkKcB2T3xKz2946p","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRQ35SrBLUAbdeVDbs1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kqd7evfccmDUMKJq1Rb8qi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories: abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n## Data & Infrastructure\n- **FR-1, FR-2**: As a developer, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog schema reconciled with PRD-01 so that auth features have the fields and indexes they need, without breaking the existing models.\n- **FR-13**: As a developer, I want one `tokens.ts` module for invite and reset tokens so that hashing, expiry and consumption are implemented once.\n- **FR-34**: As a developer, I want Auth.js mounted at `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` so that sign-in, sign-out and CSRF are handled by the framework.\n\n## Sign-in\n- **FR-3**: As a user, I want an MUI sign-in form with a show-password toggle so that I can sign in with my email and password.\n- **FR-4, FR-5**: As a user, I want clear but non-revealing error messages so that I know what to do without leaking whether an account exists.\n- **FR-6**: As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.\n- **FR-7**: As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated attacks are slowed.\n- **FR-8**: As a user, I want to land back on the page I asked for after signing in (same-origin only) so that I can continue my work safely.\n- **FR-9**: As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.\n- **FR-37**: As the school office, I want no public sign-up so that only invited users get accounts.\n\n## Session\n- **FR-10**: As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.\n- **FR-11**: As a user, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change so that a compromised session can't persist.\n- **FR-12**: As a user, I want protected pages to redirect me to sign-in (and protected APIs to return 401) so that no data is exposed when I'm signed out.\n\n## Invitations\n- **FR-14, FR-15, FR-16**: As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.\n- **FR-26, FR-27**: As the school office, I want `sendInvite()` to actually generate a 7-day link and send it so that new users can activate their accounts.\n\n## Password policy\n- **FR-17**: As an admin, I want strong password rules (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not the user's email, not a common password) so that minors' accounts are protected.\n- **FR-18**: As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules so that I know when my password is acceptable.\n\n## Forgot / reset password\n- **FR-19, FR-20, FR-22**: As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link (with a response that doesn't reveal whether an account exists) so that I can regain access.\n- **FR-21**: As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link so that I can sign in again with lockout cleared.\n\n## Change password\n- **FR-23**: As a signed-in user, I want to change my password on `/account/security` so that I can keep my account secure.\n- **FR-24**: As a signed-in user, I want an \"Account security\" item in my user menu so that I can find the page.\n\n## Permissions & audit\n- **FR-28, FR-29**: As a developer, I want `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole()` to read the real session so that every handler is protected with a one-line call.\n- **FR-25**: As a developer, I want the existing `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` reused so that there is one implementation of each.\n- **FR-30, FR-31**: As an admin, I want audit rows to capture the client IP and never contain secrets so that the trail is useful and safe.\n\n## App shell\n- **FR-32**: As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, plus a working Sign out, so that I know whose account I'm using.\n- **FR-33**: As a user, I want the sidebar to show only the pages my role can access so that the navigation is relevant to me.\n\n## Seed & tests\n- **FR-35**: As a developer, I want seeded users for every role, plus one invited user, so that I can test each flow locally.\n- **FR-36**: As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- **NFR-1**: Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and tokens are compared in constant time.\n- **NFR-2**: Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js provides CSRF protection.\n- **NFR-3**: A dummy bcrypt compare runs for unknown users, so sign-in timing doesn't reveal which accounts exist.\n- **NFR-4**: Sign-in p95 is under 1 s locally (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **NFR-5**: Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and focus moves to the first invalid field.\n- **NFR-6**: MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via the mui-mcp server and no banned libraries. QA verifies this.\n- **NFR-7**: Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page.\n- **NFR-8**: Standard response and error envelopes are used, and handlers stay thin.\n- **NFR-9**: Brownfield reuse: no renames, no duplicate helpers, and course-access.ts / student-access.ts are left untouched.\n- **NFR-10**: lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and there is no `console.log`.\n- **NFR-11**: Scope stays fixed: no PRD-03 admin screens, no SSO/MFA, no PRD-04 email infrastructure.\n- **NFR-12**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7354,"cache_read_input_tokens":47293,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7354},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcde22ab-6ed6-4b3a-aa2c-224b7672df14","uuid":"ddc8ecc7-57fb-45d7-afa4-68730d6226e8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:33:52.737Z","request_id":"req_011CghRQ2n6A8x7yUiC9wkTD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Kqd7evfccmDUMKJq1Rb8qi":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories: abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n## Data & Infrastructure\n- **FR-1, FR-2**: As a developer, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog schema reconciled with PRD-01 so that auth features have the fields and indexes they need, without breaking the existing models.\n- **FR-13**: As a developer, I want one `tokens.ts` module for invite and reset tokens so that hashing, expiry and consumption are implemented once.\n- **FR-34**: As a developer, I want Auth.js mounted at `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` so that sign-in, sign-out and CSRF are handled by the framework.\n\n## Sign-in\n- **FR-3**: As a user, I want an MUI sign-in form with a show-password toggle so that I can sign in with my email and password.\n- **FR-4, FR-5**: As a user, I want clear but non-revealing error messages so that I know what to do without leaking whether an account exists.\n- **FR-6**: As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.\n- **FR-7**: As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated attacks are slowed.\n- **FR-8**: As a user, I want to land back on the page I asked for after signing in (same-origin only) so that I can continue my work safely.\n- **FR-9**: As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.\n- **FR-37**: As the school office, I want no public sign-up so that only invited users get accounts.\n\n## Session\n- **FR-10**: As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.\n- **FR-11**: As a user, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change so that a compromised session can't persist.\n- **FR-12**: As a user, I want protected pages to redirect me to sign-in (and protected APIs to return 401) so that no data is exposed when I'm signed out.\n\n## Invitations\n- **FR-14, FR-15, FR-16**: As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.\n- **FR-26, FR-27**: As the school office, I want `sendInvite()` to actually generate a 7-day link and send it so that new users can activate their accounts.\n\n## Password policy\n- **FR-17**: As an admin, I want strong password rules (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not the user's email, not a common password) so that minors' accounts are protected.\n- **FR-18**: As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules so that I know when my password is acceptable.\n\n## Forgot / reset password\n- **FR-19, FR-20, FR-22**: As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link (with a response that doesn't reveal whether an account exists) so that I can regain access.\n- **FR-21**: As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link so that I can sign in again with lockout cleared.\n\n## Change password\n- **FR-23**: As a signed-in user, I want to change my password on `/account/security` so that I can keep my account secure.\n- **FR-24**: As a signed-in user, I want an \"Account security\" item in my user menu so that I can find the page.\n\n## Permissions & audit\n- **FR-28, FR-29**: As a developer, I want `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole()` to read the real session so that every handler is protected with a one-line call.\n- **FR-25**: As a developer, I want the existing `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` reused so that there is one implementation of each.\n- **FR-30, FR-31**: As an admin, I want audit rows to capture the client IP and never contain secrets so that the trail is useful and safe.\n\n## App shell\n- **FR-32**: As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, plus a working Sign out, so that I know whose account I'm using.\n- **FR-33**: As a user, I want the sidebar to show only the pages my role can access so that the navigation is relevant to me.\n\n## Seed & tests\n- **FR-35**: As a developer, I want seeded users for every role, plus one invited user, so that I can test each flow locally.\n- **FR-36**: As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- **NFR-1**: Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and tokens are compared in constant time.\n- **NFR-2**: Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js provides CSRF protection.\n- **NFR-3**: A dummy bcrypt compare runs for unknown users, so sign-in timing doesn't reveal which accounts exist.\n- **NFR-4**: Sign-in p95 is under 1 s locally (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **NFR-5**: Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and focus moves to the first invalid field.\n- **NFR-6**: MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via the mui-mcp server and no banned libraries. QA verifies this.\n- **NFR-7**: Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page.\n- **NFR-8**: Standard response and error envelopes are used, and handlers stay thin.\n- **NFR-9**: Brownfield reuse: no renames, no duplicate helpers, and course-access.ts / student-access.ts are left untouched.\n- **NFR-10**: lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and there is no `console.log`.\n- **NFR-11**: Scope stays fixed: no PRD-03 admin screens, no SSO/MFA, no PRD-04 email infrastructure.\n- **NFR-12**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kqd7evfccmDUMKJq1Rb8qi","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcde22ab-6ed6-4b3a-aa2c-224b7672df14","uuid":"39993af8-81e3-48d3-b6cd-bfb3961c405f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:33:52.791Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# User Stories: abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n## Data & Infrastructure\n- **FR-1, FR-2**: As a developer, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog schema reconciled with PRD-01 so that auth features have the fields and indexes they need, without breaking the existing models.\n- **FR-13**: As a developer, I want one `tokens.ts` module for invite and reset tokens so that hashing, expiry and consumption are implemented once.\n- **FR-34**: As a developer, I want Auth.js mounted at `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` so that sign-in, sign-out and CSRF are handled by the framework.\n\n## Sign-in\n- **FR-3**: As a user, I want an MUI sign-in form with a show-password toggle so that I can sign in with my email and password.\n- **FR-4, FR-5**: As a user, I want clear but non-revealing error messages so that I know what to do without leaking whether an account exists.\n- **FR-6**: As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.\n- **FR-7**: As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated attacks are slowed.\n- **FR-8**: As a user, I want to land back on the page I asked for after signing in (same-origin only) so that I can continue my work safely.\n- **FR-9**: As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.\n- **FR-37**: As the school office, I want no public sign-up so that only invited users get accounts.\n\n## Session\n- **FR-10**: As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.\n- **FR-11**: As a user, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change so that a compromised session can't persist.\n- **FR-12**: As a user, I want protected pages to redirect me to sign-in (and protected APIs to return 401) so that no data is exposed when I'm signed out.\n\n## Invitations\n- **FR-14, FR-15, FR-16**: As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.\n- **FR-26, FR-27**: As the school office, I want `sendInvite()` to actually generate a 7-day link and send it so that new users can activate their accounts.\n\n## Password policy\n- **FR-17**: As an admin, I want strong password rules (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not the user's email, not a common password) so that minors' accounts are protected.\n- **FR-18**: As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules so that I know when my password is acceptable.\n\n## Forgot / reset password\n- **FR-19, FR-20, FR-22**: As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link (with a response that doesn't reveal whether an account exists) so that I can regain access.\n- **FR-21**: As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link so that I can sign in again with lockout cleared.\n\n## Change password\n- **FR-23**: As a signed-in user, I want to change my password on `/account/security` so that I can keep my account secure.\n- **FR-24**: As a signed-in user, I want an \"Account security\" item in my user menu so that I can find the page.\n\n## Permissions & audit\n- **FR-28, FR-29**: As a developer, I want `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole()` to read the real session so that every handler is protected with a one-line call.\n- **FR-25**: As a developer, I want the existing `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` reused so that there is one implementation of each.\n- **FR-30, FR-31**: As an admin, I want audit rows to capture the client IP and never contain secrets so that the trail is useful and safe.\n\n## App shell\n- **FR-32**: As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, plus a working Sign out, so that I know whose account I'm using.\n- **FR-33**: As a user, I want the sidebar to show only the pages my role can access so that the navigation is relevant to me.\n\n## Seed & tests\n- **FR-35**: As a developer, I want seeded users for every role, plus one invited user, so that I can test each flow locally.\n- **FR-36**: As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- **NFR-1**: Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and tokens are compared in constant time.\n- **NFR-2**: Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js provides CSRF protection.\n- **NFR-3**: A dummy bcrypt compare runs for unknown users, so sign-in timing doesn't reveal which accounts exist.\n- **NFR-4**: Sign-in p95 is under 1 s locally (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **NFR-5**: Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and focus moves to the first invalid field.\n- **NFR-6**: MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via the mui-mcp server and no banned libraries. QA verifies this.\n- **NFR-7**: Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page.\n- **NFR-8**: Standard response and error envelopes are used, and handlers stay thin.\n- **NFR-9**: Brownfield reuse: no renames, no duplicate helpers, and course-access.ts / student-access.ts are left untouched.\n- **NFR-10**: lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and there is no `console.log`.\n- **NFR-11**: Scope stays fixed: no PRD-03 admin screens, no SSO/MFA, no PRD-04 email infrastructure.\n- **NFR-12**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":54,"newStart":1,"newLines":63,"lines":["-# User Stories — abcd-1 (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)","+# User Stories: abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)"," ","-Source: PRD-01 (SCH-001). Run mode `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+## Data & Infrastructure","+- **FR-1, FR-2**: As a developer, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog schema reconciled with PRD-01 so that auth features have the fields and indexes they need, without breaking the existing models.","+- **FR-13**: As a developer, I want one `tokens.ts` module for invite and reset tokens so that hashing, expiry and consumption are implemented once.","+- **FR-34**: As a developer, I want Auth.js mounted at `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` so that sign-in, sign-out and CSRF are handled by the framework."," ","-## Sign-in & session","+## Sign-in","+- **FR-3**: As a user, I want an MUI sign-in form with a show-password toggle so that I can sign in with my email and password.","+- **FR-4, FR-5**: As a user, I want clear but non-revealing error messages so that I know what to do without leaking whether an account exists.","+- **FR-6**: As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.","+- **FR-7**: As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated attacks are slowed.","+- **FR-8**: As a user, I want to land back on the page I asked for after signing in (same-origin only) so that I can continue my work safely.","+- **FR-9**: As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.","+- **FR-37**: As the school office, I want no public sign-up so that only invited users get accounts."," ","-- **FR-3, FR-4** — As a user, I want to sign in with my email and password on `/login` so that I can see my information.","-- **FR-2** — As a user, I want my email matched regardless of case or surrounding spaces so that sign-in is not tripped up by typing.","-- **FR-5** — As a user, I want one generic error for bad credentials, and a clear message when my account is locked or disabled, so that I know what to do next without revealing which accounts exist.","-- **FR-6** — As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.","-- **FR-7** — As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated guessing is throttled.","-- **FR-8** — As a user, I want to return to the page I originally requested after signing in (same-origin paths only) so that I don't lose my place, and no one can use the link to send me to another site.","-- **FR-9** — As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.","-- **FR-10** — As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.","-- **FR-11** — As a user, I want changing or resetting my password to sign out my other devices within 5 minutes so that a compromised session can't keep running.","-- **FR-12** — As the school, I want every protected page to redirect unauthenticated visitors to `/login`, and every protected API to return `401`, so that no data leaks without a session.","-- **FR-35** — As the school office, I want there to be no public sign-up so that only people we invite can get in.","+## Session","+- **FR-10**: As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.","+- **FR-11**: As a user, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change so that a compromised session can't persist.","+- **FR-12**: As a user, I want protected pages to redirect me to sign-in (and protected APIs to return 401) so that no data is exposed when I'm signed out."," "," ## Invitations","+- **FR-14, FR-15, FR-16**: As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.","+- **FR-26, FR-27**: As the school office, I want `sendInvite()` to actually generate a 7-day link and send it so that new users can activate their accounts."," ","-- **FR-13** — As a developer, I want one token module (`tokens.ts`) to create, verify and consume invite and reset tokens so that hashing and expiry rules live in one place.","-- **FR-14, FR-15** — As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.","-- **FR-25, FR-26** — As the school office (via later PRD-03 screens), I want sending an invite to issue a fresh 7-day link and cancel older ones so that only the latest link works.","+## Password policy","+- **FR-17**: As an admin, I want strong password rules (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not the user's email, not a common password) so that minors' accounts are protected.","+- **FR-18**: As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules so that I know when my password is acceptable."," ","-## Passwords","+## Forgot / reset password","+- **FR-19, FR-20, FR-22**: As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link (with a response that doesn't reveal whether an account exists) so that I can regain access.","+- **FR-21**: As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link so that I can sign in again with lockout cleared."," ","-- **FR-16, FR-17** — As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules as I type so that I pick a strong password the first time.","-- **FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21** — As a user who forgot my password, I want to reset it with an emailed link so that I can get back into my account.","-- **FR-22, FR-23** — As a user, I want to change my password from \"Account security\" while signed in so that I can keep my account secure.","+## Change password","+- **FR-23**: As a signed-in user, I want to change my password on `/account/security` so that I can keep my account secure.","+- **FR-24**: As a signed-in user, I want an \"Account security\" item in my user menu so that I can find the page."," ","-## Permissions, audit & shell","+## Permissions & audit","+- **FR-28, FR-29**: As a developer, I want `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole()` to read the real session so that every handler is protected with a one-line call.","+- **FR-25**: As a developer, I want the existing `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` reused so that there is one implementation of each.","+- **FR-30, FR-31**: As an admin, I want audit rows to capture the client IP and never contain secrets so that the trail is useful and safe."," ","-- **FR-28, FR-29, FR-30** — As a developer, I want `requireUser()` / `requireRole()` to check the real session so that restricting a handler to a role or entity takes one line.","-- **FR-31, FR-32** — As an admin, I want security-relevant actions recorded with the IP address, and never with secrets, so that I can investigate incidents safely.","-- **FR-33, FR-34** — As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, with a working \"Sign out\", and the sidebar to show only my role's pages.","-- **FR-1, FR-24, FR-27** — As a developer, I want the existing User/AuthToken/AuditLog models and user service functions reused, without renaming anything, so that already-built PRDs keep working.","+## App shell","+- **FR-32**: As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, plus a working Sign out, so that I know whose account I'm using.","+- **FR-33**: As a user, I want the sidebar to show only the pages my role can access so that the navigation is relevant to me."," "," ## Seed & tests","+- **FR-35**: As a developer, I want seeded users for every role, plus one invited user, so that I can test each flow locally.","+- **FR-36**: As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught."," ","-- **FR-36** — As a developer, I want seeded users for every role plus one invited user so that I can test each role locally.","-- **FR-37** — As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.","-"," ## Non-Functional Requirements","-","-- **NFR-1** — Raw tokens never stored; constant-time comparison.","-- **NFR-2** — HttpOnly / Secure (prod) / SameSite=Lax cookies; Auth.js CSRF on all auth forms.","-- **NFR-3** — Dummy bcrypt compare for unknown users, so response timing doesn't reveal whether an account exists.","-- **NFR-4** — Sign-in under 1 second at p95 locally (bcrypt cost 12).","-- **NFR-5** — `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements; focus moves to the first invalid field.","-- **NFR-6** — UI component rule: MUI / MUI X only, each component looked up through mui-mcp first, no banned libraries. QA verifies.","-- **NFR-7** — Access is enforced on the server for every handler and page.","-- **NFR-8** — Thin handlers and standard response/error shapes and codes.","-- **NFR-9** — Use `logger`, not `console.log`; reuse existing helpers; no renames or re-scaffolding.","-- **NFR-10** — lint, typecheck and test stay green; no scope creep beyond this PRD.","+- **NFR-1**: Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and tokens are compared in constant time.","+- **NFR-2**: Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js provides CSRF protection.","+- **NFR-3**: A dummy bcrypt compare runs for unknown users, so sign-in timing doesn't reveal which accounts exist.","+- **NFR-4**: Sign-in p95 is under 1 s locally (bcrypt cost 12).","+- **NFR-5**: Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and focus moves to the first invalid field.","+- **NFR-6**: MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via the mui-mcp server and no banned libraries. QA verifies this.","+- **NFR-7**: Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page.","+- **NFR-8**: Standard response and error envelopes are used, and handlers stay thin.","+- **NFR-9**: Brownfield reuse: no renames, no duplicate helpers, and course-access.ts / student-access.ts are left untouched.","+- **NFR-10**: lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and there is no `console.log`.","+- **NFR-11**: Scope stays fixed: no PRD-03 admin screens, no SSO/MFA, no PRD-04 email infrastructure.","+- **NFR-12**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone."]}],"originalFile":"# User Stories — abcd-1 (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\nSource: PRD-01 (SCH-001). Run mode `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **FR-3, FR-4** — As a user, I want to sign in with my email and password on `/login` so that I can see my information.\n- **FR-2** — As a user, I want my email matched regardless of case or surrounding spaces so that sign-in is not tripped up by typing.\n- **FR-5** — As a user, I want one generic error for bad credentials, and a clear message when my account is locked or disabled, so that I know what to do next without revealing which accounts exist.\n- **FR-6** — As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.\n- **FR-7** — As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated guessing is throttled.\n- **FR-8** — As a user, I want to return to the page I originally requested after signing in (same-origin paths only) so that I don't lose my place, and no one can use the link to send me to another site.\n- **FR-9** — As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.\n- **FR-10** — As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.\n- **FR-11** — As a user, I want changing or resetting my password to sign out my other devices within 5 minutes so that a compromised session can't keep running.\n- **FR-12** — As the school, I want every protected page to redirect unauthenticated visitors to `/login`, and every protected API to return `401`, so that no data leaks without a session.\n- **FR-35** — As the school office, I want there to be no public sign-up so that only people we invite can get in.\n\n## Invitations\n\n- **FR-13** — As a developer, I want one token module (`tokens.ts`) to create, verify and consume invite and reset tokens so that hashing and expiry rules live in one place.\n- **FR-14, FR-15** — As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.\n- **FR-25, FR-26** — As the school office (via later PRD-03 screens), I want sending an invite to issue a fresh 7-day link and cancel older ones so that only the latest link works.\n\n## Passwords\n\n- **FR-16, FR-17** — As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules as I type so that I pick a strong password the first time.\n- **FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21** — As a user who forgot my password, I want to reset it with an emailed link so that I can get back into my account.\n- **FR-22, FR-23** — As a user, I want to change my password from \"Account security\" while signed in so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## Permissions, audit & shell\n\n- **FR-28, FR-29, FR-30** — As a developer, I want `requireUser()` / `requireRole()` to check the real session so that restricting a handler to a role or entity takes one line.\n- **FR-31, FR-32** — As an admin, I want security-relevant actions recorded with the IP address, and never with secrets, so that I can investigate incidents safely.\n- **FR-33, FR-34** — As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, with a working \"Sign out\", and the sidebar to show only my role's pages.\n- **FR-1, FR-24, FR-27** — As a developer, I want the existing User/AuthToken/AuditLog models and user service functions reused, without renaming anything, so that already-built PRDs keep working.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **FR-36** — As a developer, I want seeded users for every role plus one invited user so that I can test each role locally.\n- **FR-37** — As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** — Raw tokens never stored; constant-time comparison.\n- **NFR-2** — HttpOnly / Secure (prod) / SameSite=Lax cookies; Auth.js CSRF on all auth forms.\n- **NFR-3** — Dummy bcrypt compare for unknown users, so response timing doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n- **NFR-4** — Sign-in under 1 second at p95 locally (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **NFR-5** — `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements; focus moves to the first invalid field.\n- **NFR-6** — UI component rule: MUI / MUI X only, each component looked up through mui-mcp first, no banned libraries. QA verifies.\n- **NFR-7** — Access is enforced on the server for every handler and page.\n- **NFR-8** — Thin handlers and standard response/error shapes and codes.\n- **NFR-9** — Use `logger`, not `console.log`; reuse existing helpers; no renames or re-scaffolding.\n- **NFR-10** — lint, typecheck and test stay green; no scope creep beyond this PRD.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kqd7evfccmDUMKJq1Rb8qi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
