{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRS5CVqtdpnW9uiavT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake for abcd-1 (PRD-01: Auth, Sessions & RBAC) is complete. I wrote four files to `artifacts/intake/`, and all three JSON files parse cleanly.\n\n- `requirements.json`: 37 functional and 12 non-functional requirements, each with a confidence level and a citation back to the PRD. Overall confidence is 94%. It also lists what already exists in the code.\n- `user-stories.md`: one story per requirement, grouped by flow.\n- `tech-stack.json`: React (Next.js 14, MUI v9) at 100% confidence. Auth.js and bcrypt are already in `package.json`, so no new libraries are needed.\n- `handoff-to-architect.json`: written last, with status `complete` and the open questions below.\n\nThere's no Figma link in the PRD, so I didn't create `figma-readiness.json`.\n\n**Overwrite:** these files replaced the intake artifacts from the previous ticket (abcd-05) in the same folder. If you still need those, they're in git history.\n\n**What's already built:** earlier PRDs already did part of this PRD's work:\n- The `User`, `AuthToken` and `AuditLog` database tables already exist.\n- `audit()` already exists, but doesn't yet record the client IP.\n- `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` already exist in the user service.\n- Two placeholder users remain, one in `requireRole.ts` and one in the app shell.\n\nSo many requirements mean \"extend or rewire what's there\" rather than \"build new\".\n\n**Questions for the Architect** (I recorded a default for each where I could):\n1. **Small schema differences from the PRD:** the code has an `ip` column where the PRD says `ipAddress`, an extra `ARCHIVED` user status, and different indexes on the audit table. Default: keep what exists and only add what's missing, since the PRD forbids renaming models.\n2. **Two user-service functions take different arguments than the PRD describes:** `createUser` and `setUserStatus`. Default: keep the existing versions rather than adding duplicates.\n3. **`requireRole()` is synchronous and called in about 94 places,** but reading a real Auth.js session is asynchronous. This is the biggest call left for the Architect, because the obvious fix means updating every caller.\n4. **UI work depends on the MUI docs server.** The PRD treats it being unreachable as a hard blocker for the Dev phase."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":57353,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1023},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcde22ab-6ed6-4b3a-aa2c-224b7672df14","uuid":"8d3f0564-ec6b-4b0c-b767-04a246b9bc3d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:34:10.958Z","request_id":"req_011CghRS4utCi3zmCedZnwLT"}
