{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTDGwJhdAcJFW6oHMN4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019B2EgU3Pjzx5s9hpBuCh6c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",\n    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",\n        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",\n        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",\n        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",\n        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":43569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82ff4961-f97f-45fc-820f-f6f30eb1c065","uuid":"f40bbd98-1075-4d0e-8437-6c1e7f66e787","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:58:25.561Z","request_id":"req_011CghTDGgSNcGktNWSWNbw3","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019B2EgU3Pjzx5s9hpBuCh6c":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",\n    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",\n        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",\n        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",\n        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",\n        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019B2EgU3Pjzx5s9hpBuCh6c","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82ff4961-f97f-45fc-820f-f6f30eb1c065","uuid":"1387ef9a-8459-444c-ab56-c0299b7c432c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:58:25.667Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",\n    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",\n        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",\n        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",\n        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",\n        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":94,"newStart":1,"newLines":117,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","-  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",","+  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",","   \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\","," ","   \"brownfieldFindings\": [","-    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",","-    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",","-    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",","-    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",","-    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",","-    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",","-    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",","-    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"","+    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",","+    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",","+    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",","+    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",","+    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",","+    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",","+    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",","+    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",","+    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",","+    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",","+    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",","+    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",","+    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"","   ],"," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }","   ],"," ","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }","   ],"," ","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,","+  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [","+    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },","+    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }","+  ],","+","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",","-        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",","-        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",","-        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",","-        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",","-        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"","+        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",","+        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",","+        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",","+        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",","-        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",","-        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",","-        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"","+        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",","+        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",","+        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",","+        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"","       ]","     }","   ],"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already contains Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog. Divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: UserStatus has an extra ARCHIVED value; AuditLog uses column `ip` (PRD says `ipAddress`) with indexes [actorId] and [action] (PRD says [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt]); AuthToken has an extra @@index([userId, type]); User has an extra @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) and many relations added by later PRDs. Platform rule 'never rename existing routes or models' applies, so these must be reconciled additively, not by renaming.\",\n    \"src/server/audit.ts already exists with audit({actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata}); it never throws but has no `request` param and does not capture IP.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exists with PLACEHOLDER_USER (ADMIN) and only requireRole(); about 94 call sites across src use requireRole().\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has its own PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 42, 81, 171-176).\",\n    \"src/server/services/users.ts already exports createUser (PRD-03 shape: profile + links + sendInvite flag), setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status), unlockUser(userId) and a no-op sendInvite stub. createInviteToken does not exist.\",\n    \"Missing today: middleware.ts, src/server/auth/tokens.ts, src/server/rate-limit.ts, src/config/public-routes.ts, src/lib/validators/auth.ts, src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt, Auth.js config, and every (auth) page. next-auth ^5.0.0-beta.25 and bcrypt ^6 are already in package.json.\",\n    \"The EmailOutbox model exists in the schema, but no email or notification service code exists (no src/server/notifications). Per Out of Scope, sendAuthEmail() should log via logger.info.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts seeds only office@schoolhub.test; the 6 PRD seed users plus invited@schoolhub.test are missing.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Ensure the Prisma schema has Role, UserStatus (INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED), AuthTokenType, User, AuthToken and AuditLog per the PRD block; the models already exist, so reconcile only the missing fields and indexes additively (AuditLog @@index([entityType, entityId]) and @@index([actorId, createdAt])) without renaming the existing `ip` column or dropping the ARCHIVED enum value.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 Data model; brownfield prisma/schema.prisma\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Store User.email lower-cased.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 (User.email comment); §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Build the /login page from MUI Sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email and password fields; submit calls Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"The Credentials authorize function trims and lower-cases the email, rejects a missing user, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt set, or lockedUntil > now, and compares the password with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.' except locked ('This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.') and disabled ('This account is disabled. Contact the school office.').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Each wrong password increments failedLoginCount; at 5, set lockedUntil = now + 15 min and reset the count to 0. On success, reset the count and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.4; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Rate-limit sign-in to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using an exported in-memory sliding window in src/server/rate-limit.ts. Over the limit, return RATE_LIMITED and show 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl only if it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.6; Test Requirements (callbackUrl unit test)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Write the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.7; AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Use JWT sessions with an 8-hour lifetime, refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"In the jwt callback, at most once every 5 minutes per token, invalidate the session if passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app) page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 UNAUTHENTICATED JSON for /api/* except /api/health, /api/auth/* and routes listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3; Goals 2; AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/auth/tokens.ts as the single AuthToken module: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns a raw token (32 random bytes, base64url) and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns the token and user, or null if the token is missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.0; §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] verifies an INVITE token (7-day expiry). If it is invalid, show 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1; AC-4, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The invite page shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite (POST /api/auth/accept-invite {token, password}) validates the policy, hashes the password, sets status ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3; Pages & Routes; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Define the password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled top-1,000 list at src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1; AC-10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Show a live strength checklist under the password field, marking each policy rule as met or unmet.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password (POST /api/auth/forgot-password) always responds 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.', and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user only: create a PASSWORD_RESET token (60 min) through tokens.ts, invalidate older unused reset tokens and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] (POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, password}) sets the hash and passwordChangedAt, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, audits auth.password.reset and redirects to /login with a useToast success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.3; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) logs recipient, subject and link via logger.info until PRD-04 replaces its body with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"/account/security (POST /api/account/password {currentPassword, newPassword}) changes the password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1; Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"users.ts: reuse the existing createUser (it already creates INVITED users; confirm a duplicate email maps to CONFLICT) instead of adding a second one, and reuse the existing setUserStatus/unlockUser signatures.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1, §FR-8.4; Platform Context 'never duplicate a helper'; brownfield users.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Add createInviteToken(userId) to users.ts. It calls createToken(userId, 'INVITE', {days: 7}), invalidates older unused invite tokens and returns the raw token.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Replace the no-op sendInvite stub with a real implementation that calls createInviteToken() then sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link), keeping its existing return shape for the current call sites.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.3; brownfield users.ts:388\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"In src/server/auth/requireRole.ts, delete PLACEHOLDER_USER and add getCurrentUser() (session user or null) and requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED, or redirects to /login in server pages). Do not create permissions.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1-9.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"requireRole(...roles) checks the real session role and throws FORBIDDEN (403), or redirects to /forbidden in server pages. Keep the signature compatible with the ~94 existing call sites. Do not add can().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.4-9.5; AC-9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Extend the existing audit() in src/server/audit.ts with an optional `request` param that captures the IP from x-forwarded-for into the existing `ip` column. It must still never throw.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.1; brownfield audit.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx so the shell reads the session user. The top-bar menu shows the real name, a role badge and avatar initials, and Sign out calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.1-11.2; AC-1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Filter the navigation.ts entries by the session role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Mount the Auth.js handlers at /api/auth/[...nextauth].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Pages & Routes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, teacher, teacher2, student, student2, parent @schoolhub.test, password SchoolHub123!) plus one INVITED invited@schoolhub.test whose invite link is logged during seeding. The existing office@schoolhub.test seed stays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; brownfield prisma/seed.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Add tests. Unit: password policy, token hashing and expiry, lockout logic, rate limiter, callbackUrl check. Integration: authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password. Playwright: sign-in/out, failed login message, forgot→reset.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"There is no public sign-up route; only invited users can activate an account.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Store only SHA-256 hashes of raw tokens and compare tokens in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; all auth forms use Auth.js CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Prevent timing-based user enumeration: run a dummy bcrypt compare when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 s at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live='polite', and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: MUI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, next-themes, lucide-react, notistack, sonner, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. If the MCP is unreachable, report it as a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Every handler and server page enforces access server-side; hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Use the standard response and error envelopes ({data} / {error:{code,message,details}}) with codes UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403 and RATE_LIMITED 429. Route handlers stay thin: Zod parse → service → JSON.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models and helpers (audit.ts, users.ts, requireRole.ts, useToast, AppError); never rename routes or models; do not modify course-access.ts or student-access.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. No console.log outside the dev email transport; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Scope is fixed to this PRD: no admin user-management screens (PRD-03), no SSO/MFA/magic links, and no email infrastructure (PRD-04).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC and display them in SchoolSettings.timezone (applies to the lockout 'N minutes' message and to lastLoginAt display).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps bullet)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-1: Should AuditLog.ip be renamed to ipAddress to match the PRD schema, or kept as `ip` under the 'never rename existing models' rule?\",\n        \"FR-1: Should UserStatus.ARCHIVED (added by an earlier PRD) be kept even though the PRD enum lists only INVITED/ACTIVE/DISABLED?\",\n        \"FR-25: The PRD's createUser({email, firstName, lastName, role, phone?}) differs from the existing PRD-03 createUser(CreateUserInput with profile/links/sendInvite). Reuse the existing one, or add an overload?\",\n        \"FR-25: The existing setUserStatus takes (actorId, userId, status) while the PRD says (userId, status). Keep the existing signature?\",\n        \"FR-28/29: Under middleware, should requireRole() keep returning {id, role} synchronously for its ~94 existing call sites, or become async (which would touch every caller)?\",\n        \"FR-12: How should /api/health and the existing public pages under src/app/(public) be represented in src/config/public-routes.ts?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"AuditLog.ip vs ipAddress. Default: keep `ip`, no rename; add the PRD's two indexes.\",\n        \"UserStatus.ARCHIVED. Default: keep it (removing it is a destructive migration).\",\n        \"createUser/setUserStatus signatures. Default: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures and do not duplicate them.\",\n        \"requireRole sync vs async. Auth.js auth() is async, so callers likely need `await`. The Architect must decide, and this may touch ~94 call sites.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019B2EgU3Pjzx5s9hpBuCh6c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTHxJXevbk921mhgi6m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LCGsRgH8hM2XJMt97DZDPF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## In-app notifications\n\n- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.\n- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.\n- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.\n- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.\n- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.\n- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.\n\n## Feature integration\n\n- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.\n- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.\n\n## Email delivery\n\n- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.\n- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.\n- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.\n- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-14 (FR-1, FR-40):** As a developer, I want the notification tables migrated and seeded with sample notifications so that the UI is testable locally.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 / NFR-2 Performance:** `notify()` handles 1,000 recipients in under 2 s; unread-count responds in under 50 ms.\n- **NFR-3 Latency:** no request waits on SMTP; emails go out within 60 s.\n- **NFR-4 / NFR-5 Reliability:** no email is sent twice (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`); rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 min return to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-6 / NFR-7 / NFR-8 Security:** links must be relative `/` paths (no `//`); email HTML is escaped; access is enforced server-side; dispatch requires `CRON_SECRET`.\n- **NFR-9 Deliverability:** every email has HTML and text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing to `/account/notifications`.\n- **NFR-10 UI component rule:** MUI only, every component looked up via `mui-mcp` before use, no banned libraries. QA verifies this. An unreachable `mui-mcp` is a blocker.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 Conventions:** thin handlers, standard response and pagination shapes, `logger` instead of `console.log`, and display in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-13 Brownfield:** reuse the existing schema models, env vars, nav entries, `requireUser`/`requireRole` and `useToast`. Keep lint, typecheck and tests green.\n- **NFR-14 / NFR-15 / NFR-16 Tests:** unit (preferences, backoff, link validation, expansion), integration (locking, stuck recovery), and Playwright (bell, mark all read, preference persistence).\n- **NFR-17 Scope:** no SMS, push, websockets or digests.\n- **NFR-18 Limits:** title at most 140 characters and body at most 500; truncated, never thrown.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8603,"cache_read_input_tokens":43732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8603},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82ff4961-f97f-45fc-820f-f6f30eb1c065","uuid":"0b5b42af-c1aa-45ff-a282-cccfd6e8ce45","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:58:39.150Z","request_id":"req_011CghTHwzRmEsSJQZc76nJ2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LCGsRgH8hM2XJMt97DZDPF":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## In-app notifications\n\n- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.\n- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.\n- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.\n- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.\n- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.\n- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.\n\n## Feature integration\n\n- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.\n- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.\n\n## Email delivery\n\n- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.\n- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.\n- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.\n- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-14 (FR-1, FR-40):** As a developer, I want the notification tables migrated and seeded with sample notifications so that the UI is testable locally.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 / NFR-2 Performance:** `notify()` handles 1,000 recipients in under 2 s; unread-count responds in under 50 ms.\n- **NFR-3 Latency:** no request waits on SMTP; emails go out within 60 s.\n- **NFR-4 / NFR-5 Reliability:** no email is sent twice (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`); rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 min return to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-6 / NFR-7 / NFR-8 Security:** links must be relative `/` paths (no `//`); email HTML is escaped; access is enforced server-side; dispatch requires `CRON_SECRET`.\n- **NFR-9 Deliverability:** every email has HTML and text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing to `/account/notifications`.\n- **NFR-10 UI component rule:** MUI only, every component looked up via `mui-mcp` before use, no banned libraries. QA verifies this. An unreachable `mui-mcp` is a blocker.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 Conventions:** thin handlers, standard response and pagination shapes, `logger` instead of `console.log`, and display in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-13 Brownfield:** reuse the existing schema models, env vars, nav entries, `requireUser`/`requireRole` and `useToast`. Keep lint, typecheck and tests green.\n- **NFR-14 / NFR-15 / NFR-16 Tests:** unit (preferences, backoff, link validation, expansion), integration (locking, stuck recovery), and Playwright (bell, mark all read, preference persistence).\n- **NFR-17 Scope:** no SMS, push, websockets or digests.\n- **NFR-18 Limits:** title at most 140 characters and body at most 500; truncated, never thrown.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LCGsRgH8hM2XJMt97DZDPF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82ff4961-f97f-45fc-820f-f6f30eb1c065","uuid":"a7a038df-ed7c-4cac-9c03-7795281ca24f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:58:39.214Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## In-app notifications\n\n- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.\n- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.\n- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.\n- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.\n- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.\n- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.\n\n## Feature integration\n\n- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.\n- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.\n\n## Email delivery\n\n- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.\n- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.\n- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.\n- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-14 (FR-1, FR-40):** As a developer, I want the notification tables migrated and seeded with sample notifications so that the UI is testable locally.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 / NFR-2 Performance:** `notify()` handles 1,000 recipients in under 2 s; unread-count responds in under 50 ms.\n- **NFR-3 Latency:** no request waits on SMTP; emails go out within 60 s.\n- **NFR-4 / NFR-5 Reliability:** no email is sent twice (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`); rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 min return to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-6 / NFR-7 / NFR-8 Security:** links must be relative `/` paths (no `//`); email HTML is escaped; access is enforced server-side; dispatch requires `CRON_SECRET`.\n- **NFR-9 Deliverability:** every email has HTML and text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing to `/account/notifications`.\n- **NFR-10 UI component rule:** MUI only, every component looked up via `mui-mcp` before use, no banned libraries. QA verifies this. An unreachable `mui-mcp` is a blocker.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 Conventions:** thin handlers, standard response and pagination shapes, `logger` instead of `console.log`, and display in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-13 Brownfield:** reuse the existing schema models, env vars, nav entries, `requireUser`/`requireRole` and `useToast`. Keep lint, typecheck and tests green.\n- **NFR-14 / NFR-15 / NFR-16 Tests:** unit (preferences, backoff, link validation, expansion), integration (locking, stuck recovery), and Playwright (bell, mark all read, preference persistence).\n- **NFR-17 Scope:** no SMS, push, websockets or digests.\n- **NFR-18 Limits:** title at most 140 characters and body at most 500; truncated, never thrown.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":63,"newStart":1,"newLines":46,"lines":["-# User Stories: abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)","+# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure"," ","-## Data & Infrastructure","-- **FR-1, FR-2**: As a developer, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog schema reconciled with PRD-01 so that auth features have the fields and indexes they need, without breaking the existing models.","-- **FR-13**: As a developer, I want one `tokens.ts` module for invite and reset tokens so that hashing, expiry and consumption are implemented once.","-- **FR-34**: As a developer, I want Auth.js mounted at `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` so that sign-in, sign-out and CSRF are handled by the framework.","+Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`."," ","-## Sign-in","-- **FR-3**: As a user, I want an MUI sign-in form with a show-password toggle so that I can sign in with my email and password.","-- **FR-4, FR-5**: As a user, I want clear but non-revealing error messages so that I know what to do without leaking whether an account exists.","-- **FR-6**: As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.","-- **FR-7**: As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated attacks are slowed.","-- **FR-8**: As a user, I want to land back on the page I asked for after signing in (same-origin only) so that I can continue my work safely.","-- **FR-9**: As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.","-- **FR-37**: As the school office, I want no public sign-up so that only invited users get accounts.","+## In-app notifications"," ","-## Session","-- **FR-10**: As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.","-- **FR-11**: As a user, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change so that a compromised session can't persist.","-- **FR-12**: As a user, I want protected pages to redirect me to sign-in (and protected APIs to return 401) so that no data is exposed when I'm signed out.","+- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.","+- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.","+- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.","+- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.","+- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small."," ","-## Invitations","-- **FR-14, FR-15, FR-16**: As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.","-- **FR-26, FR-27**: As the school office, I want `sendInvite()` to actually generate a 7-day link and send it so that new users can activate their accounts.","+## Preferences"," ","-## Password policy","-- **FR-17**: As an admin, I want strong password rules (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not the user's email, not a common password) so that minors' accounts are protected.","-- **FR-18**: As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules so that I know when my password is acceptable.","+- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.","+- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users."," ","-## Forgot / reset password","-- **FR-19, FR-20, FR-22**: As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link (with a response that doesn't reveal whether an account exists) so that I can regain access.","-- **FR-21**: As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link so that I can sign in again with lockout cleared.","+## Feature integration"," ","-## Change password","-- **FR-23**: As a signed-in user, I want to change my password on `/account/security` so that I can keep my account secure.","-- **FR-24**: As a signed-in user, I want an \"Account security\" item in my user menu so that I can find the page.","+- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.","+- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account."," ","-## Permissions & audit","-- **FR-28, FR-29**: As a developer, I want `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole()` to read the real session so that every handler is protected with a one-line call.","-- **FR-25**: As a developer, I want the existing `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` reused so that there is one implementation of each.","-- **FR-30, FR-31**: As an admin, I want audit rows to capture the client IP and never contain secrets so that the trail is useful and safe.","+## Email delivery"," ","-## App shell","-- **FR-32**: As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, plus a working Sign out, so that I know whose account I'm using.","-- **FR-33**: As a user, I want the sidebar to show only the pages my role can access so that the navigation is relevant to me.","+- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.","+- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.","+- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.","+- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end."," ","-## Seed & tests","-- **FR-35**: As a developer, I want seeded users for every role, plus one invited user, so that I can test each flow locally.","-- **FR-36**: As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.","+## Data"," ","+- **US-14 (FR-1, FR-40):** As a developer, I want the notification tables migrated and seeded with sample notifications so that the UI is testable locally.","+"," ## Non-Functional Requirements","-- **NFR-1**: Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and tokens are compared in constant time.","-- **NFR-2**: Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js provides CSRF protection.","-- **NFR-3**: A dummy bcrypt compare runs for unknown users, so sign-in timing doesn't reveal which accounts exist.","-- **NFR-4**: Sign-in p95 is under 1 s locally (bcrypt cost 12).","-- **NFR-5**: Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and focus moves to the first invalid field.","-- **NFR-6**: MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via the mui-mcp server and no banned libraries. QA verifies this.","-- **NFR-7**: Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page.","-- **NFR-8**: Standard response and error envelopes are used, and handlers stay thin.","-- **NFR-9**: Brownfield reuse: no renames, no duplicate helpers, and course-access.ts / student-access.ts are left untouched.","-- **NFR-10**: lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and there is no `console.log`.","-- **NFR-11**: Scope stays fixed: no PRD-03 admin screens, no SSO/MFA, no PRD-04 email infrastructure.","-- **NFR-12**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.","+","+- **NFR-1 / NFR-2 Performance:** `notify()` handles 1,000 recipients in under 2 s; unread-count responds in under 50 ms.","+- **NFR-3 Latency:** no request waits on SMTP; emails go out within 60 s.","+- **NFR-4 / NFR-5 Reliability:** no email is sent twice (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`); rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 min return to `PENDING`.","+- **NFR-6 / NFR-7 / NFR-8 Security:** links must be relative `/` paths (no `//`); email HTML is escaped; access is enforced server-side; dispatch requires `CRON_SECRET`.","+- **NFR-9 Deliverability:** every email has HTML and text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing to `/account/notifications`.","+- **NFR-10 UI component rule:** MUI only, every component looked up via `mui-mcp` before use, no banned libraries. QA verifies this. An unreachable `mui-mcp` is a blocker.","+- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 Conventions:** thin handlers, standard response and pagination shapes, `logger` instead of `console.log`, and display in the school timezone.","+- **NFR-13 Brownfield:** reuse the existing schema models, env vars, nav entries, `requireUser`/`requireRole` and `useToast`. Keep lint, typecheck and tests green.","+- **NFR-14 / NFR-15 / NFR-16 Tests:** unit (preferences, backoff, link validation, expansion), integration (locking, stuck recovery), and Playwright (bell, mark all read, preference persistence).","+- **NFR-17 Scope:** no SMS, push, websockets or digests.","+- **NFR-18 Limits:** title at most 140 characters and body at most 500; truncated, never thrown."]}],"originalFile":"# User Stories: abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n## Data & Infrastructure\n- **FR-1, FR-2**: As a developer, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog schema reconciled with PRD-01 so that auth features have the fields and indexes they need, without breaking the existing models.\n- **FR-13**: As a developer, I want one `tokens.ts` module for invite and reset tokens so that hashing, expiry and consumption are implemented once.\n- **FR-34**: As a developer, I want Auth.js mounted at `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` so that sign-in, sign-out and CSRF are handled by the framework.\n\n## Sign-in\n- **FR-3**: As a user, I want an MUI sign-in form with a show-password toggle so that I can sign in with my email and password.\n- **FR-4, FR-5**: As a user, I want clear but non-revealing error messages so that I know what to do without leaking whether an account exists.\n- **FR-6**: As an admin, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced.\n- **FR-7**: As an admin, I want sign-in attempts rate-limited per IP so that automated attacks are slowed.\n- **FR-8**: As a user, I want to land back on the page I asked for after signing in (same-origin only) so that I can continue my work safely.\n- **FR-9**: As an admin, I want sign-in successes, failures and lockouts audited so that I can investigate incidents.\n- **FR-37**: As the school office, I want no public sign-up so that only invited users get accounts.\n\n## Session\n- **FR-10**: As a user, I want my session to last 8 hours and refresh while I'm active so that I'm not signed out mid-task.\n- **FR-11**: As a user, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change so that a compromised session can't persist.\n- **FR-12**: As a user, I want protected pages to redirect me to sign-in (and protected APIs to return 401) so that no data is exposed when I'm signed out.\n\n## Invitations\n- **FR-14, FR-15, FR-16**: As an invited user, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub.\n- **FR-26, FR-27**: As the school office, I want `sendInvite()` to actually generate a 7-day link and send it so that new users can activate their accounts.\n\n## Password policy\n- **FR-17**: As an admin, I want strong password rules (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not the user's email, not a common password) so that minors' accounts are protected.\n- **FR-18**: As a user, I want a live checklist of the password rules so that I know when my password is acceptable.\n\n## Forgot / reset password\n- **FR-19, FR-20, FR-22**: As a user who forgot my password, I want to request a reset link (with a response that doesn't reveal whether an account exists) so that I can regain access.\n- **FR-21**: As a user, I want to set a new password from the reset link so that I can sign in again with lockout cleared.\n\n## Change password\n- **FR-23**: As a signed-in user, I want to change my password on `/account/security` so that I can keep my account secure.\n- **FR-24**: As a signed-in user, I want an \"Account security\" item in my user menu so that I can find the page.\n\n## Permissions & audit\n- **FR-28, FR-29**: As a developer, I want `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` and `requireRole()` to read the real session so that every handler is protected with a one-line call.\n- **FR-25**: As a developer, I want the existing `createUser`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` reused so that there is one implementation of each.\n- **FR-30, FR-31**: As an admin, I want audit rows to capture the client IP and never contain secrets so that the trail is useful and safe.\n\n## App shell\n- **FR-32**: As a user, I want the top bar to show my real name, role and initials, plus a working Sign out, so that I know whose account I'm using.\n- **FR-33**: As a user, I want the sidebar to show only the pages my role can access so that the navigation is relevant to me.\n\n## Seed & tests\n- **FR-35**: As a developer, I want seeded users for every role, plus one invited user, so that I can test each flow locally.\n- **FR-36**: As a developer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n- **NFR-1**: Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and tokens are compared in constant time.\n- **NFR-2**: Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js provides CSRF protection.\n- **NFR-3**: A dummy bcrypt compare runs for unknown users, so sign-in timing doesn't reveal which accounts exist.\n- **NFR-4**: Sign-in p95 is under 1 s locally (bcrypt cost 12).\n- **NFR-5**: Form errors use `aria-live=\"polite\"`, and focus moves to the first invalid field.\n- **NFR-6**: MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via the mui-mcp server and no banned libraries. QA verifies this.\n- **NFR-7**: Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page.\n- **NFR-8**: Standard response and error envelopes are used, and handlers stay thin.\n- **NFR-9**: Brownfield reuse: no renames, no duplicate helpers, and course-access.ts / student-access.ts are left untouched.\n- **NFR-10**: lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and there is no `console.log`.\n- **NFR-11**: Scope stays fixed: no PRD-03 admin screens, no SSO/MFA, no PRD-04 email infrastructure.\n- **NFR-12**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LCGsRgH8hM2XJMt97DZDPF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
