{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTKzYmTkKNmhnS3PRmi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The SH-4 intake phase is done: the requirements, user stories and tech-stack files are written, and the handoff to the Architect was written last. Status is `complete`, with 59 requirements (41 functional, 18 non-functional) and 93% confidence (55 rated HIGH, 4 MEDIUM). All JSON files load cleanly, and every requirement has a confidence label and a PRD citation.\n\n**Things already in the codebase that the Architect should know (logged in `brownfieldFindings`):**\n- **Database:** the three notification tables are defined in `schema.prisma`, but none of the four existing migrations creates them, so a new migration is needed.\n- **Schema vs. PRD:** the schema adds a few extra `updatedAt` columns the PRD doesn't list. I kept them, because the \"stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes\" recovery can use `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`.\n- **Already set up, don't redo:** the SMTP, email and cron settings, the email libraries in `package.json`, the `worker:email` script entry (its file doesn't exist yet), and the Notifications and Email log sidebar links.\n- **Auth emails:** `sendAuthEmail()` currently only logs the link. Its signature and its two callers (invite and password reset) stay the same; only the body changes to queue the email.\n- **Toasts:** `useToast()` is in `src/components/Toast/`, not `src/components/shared/` as the PRD says. The plan is to reuse it rather than create a second one.\n\n**Defaults I chose where the PRD was unclear (listed as open questions in the handoff):**\n- **Invite and password-reset emails** go straight into the email queue and create no in-app notification.\n- **Seed data:** 3 notifications for each of the two users, one read and two unread.\n- **Over-length titles and bodies** are cut short with a warning in the log, because `notify()` must never throw.\n- **Preferences table:** 