{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWmngqkYnovwVZ3QF3ZkQC","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:02:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 59,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-1: The Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models exist in schema.prisma, but no migration creates them, so a new migration is required. Keep the additive updatedAt columns, because EmailOutbox.updatedAt backs the NFR-5 stuck-row recovery.\",\n    \"FR-4/FR-16: Default decision: sendAuthEmail() enqueues the outbox directly and creates no Notification row. The account.* types are registered as email-only and hidden from preferences. The Architect should confirm.\",\n    \"FR-40: The seed count is ambiguous. The default is 3 notifications per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n    \"NFR-10: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode explicitly declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, and MUI v9 with emotion. Every dependency this PRD needs is already installed: nodemailer ^6.9.14 (+ @types/nodemailer), @react-email/components 0.0.25 and @react-email/render 1.0.1. tsx is used by the existing worker:email script. Styling uses only the MUI theme, sx and styled(); Tailwind and CSS modules are banned. Email templates are the only non-MUI rendering and are exempt per the PRD.\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/comp\n# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## In-app notifications\n\n- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.\n- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.\n- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.\n- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.\n- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.\n- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.\n\n## Feature integration\n\n- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.\n- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.\n\n## Email delivery\n\n- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.\n- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.\n- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.\n- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.\n\n## Data\n{\n  \"intake-main\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"82ff4961-f97f-45fc-820f-f6f30eb1c065\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T06:59:02.878Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"arch-research-stack\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"43ba1665-ff77-440a-aa0d-eea7f83f9b17\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:00:54.079Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"arch-research-reqs\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:01:13.187Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"arch-design-system\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:03:43.798Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"arch-api-contracts\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"346b8f8b-0fbc-4ed8-97c5-558f3d48dba1\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:05:18.738Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"dev-planning-main\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"01342abc-2768-44d6-a3f9-0083d13d7230\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:07:07.601Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"dev-planning\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d2232b-5b66-4c64-98a2-53d3d0b92b18","uuid":"81dc6590-7d1d-45d4-a7d8-b267c8f2cddf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:10:43.552Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:02:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 59,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"FR-1: The Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models exist in schema.prisma, but no migration creates them, so a new migration is required. Keep the additive updatedAt columns, because EmailOutbox.updatedAt backs the NFR-5 stuck-row recovery.\",\n    \"FR-4/FR-16: Default decision: sendAuthEmail() enqueues the outbox directly and creates no Notification row. The account.* types are registered as email-only and hidden from preferences. The Architect should confirm.\",\n    \"FR-40: The seed count is ambiguous. The default is 3 notifications per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n    \"NFR-10: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode explicitly declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, and MUI v9 with emotion. Every dependency this PRD needs is already installed: nodemailer ^6.9.14 (+ @types/nodemailer), @react-email/components 0.0.25 and @react-email/render 1.0.1. tsx is used by the existing worker:email script. Styling uses only the MUI theme, sx and styled(); Tailwind and CSS modules are banned. Email templates are the only non-MUI rendering and are exempt per the PRD.\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/comp\n# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## In-app notifications\n\n- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.\n- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.\n- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.\n- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.\n- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.\n- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.\n\n## Feature integration\n\n- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.\n- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.\n\n## Email delivery\n\n- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.\n- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.\n- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.\n- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.\n\n## Data\n{\n  \"intake-main\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"82ff4961-f97f-45fc-820f-f6f30eb1c065\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T06:59:02.878Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"arch-research-stack\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"43ba1665-ff77-440a-aa0d-eea7f83f9b17\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:00:54.079Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"arch-research-reqs\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"6976ca3f-645f-4a29-bf49-9d0601ccb133\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:01:13.187Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"arch-design-system\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:03:43.798Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"arch-api-contracts\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"346b8f8b-0fbc-4ed8-97c5-558f3d48dba1\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:05:18.738Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"architect\"\n  },\n  \"dev-planning-main\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"01342abc-2768-44d6-a3f9-0083d13d7230\",\n    \"ts\": \"2026-11-04T07:07:07.601Z\",\n    \"phase\": \"dev-planning\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KWmngqkYnovwVZ3QF3ZkQC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
