{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCw2UM7ZaQ3bqtxZSVf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ofGB8qvaWF7kVfMtLq22A","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",\n    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",\n    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",\n    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",\n    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",\n    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",\n    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",\n        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",\n        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",\n        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",\n        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",\n        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",\n        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",\n        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",\n        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",\n        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",\n        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",\n        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1392,"cache_read_input_tokens":47071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1392},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d2232b-5b66-4c64-98a2-53d3d0b92b18","uuid":"ebc173cb-56ce-490e-acca-3806b86c231f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:11.636Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCw2ECpvy6ySTVMeo8a","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015ofGB8qvaWF7kVfMtLq22A":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",\n    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",\n    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",\n    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",\n    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",\n    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",\n    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",\n        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",\n        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",\n        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",\n        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",\n        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",\n        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",\n        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",\n        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",\n        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",\n        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",\n        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ofGB8qvaWF7kVfMtLq22A","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d2232b-5b66-4c64-98a2-53d3d0b92b18","uuid":"e84073b5-e58d-417b-aad9-8c18e33c4a64","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:11.699Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",\n    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",\n    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",\n    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",\n    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",\n    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",\n    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",\n        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",\n        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",\n        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",\n        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",\n        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",\n        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",\n        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",\n        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",\n        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",\n        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",\n        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":119,"newStart":1,"newLines":121,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","-  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",","+  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",","   \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\","," ","   \"brownfieldFindings\": [","-    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",","-    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",","-    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",","-    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",","-    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",","-    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",","-    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",","-    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",","-    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",","-    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",","-    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",","-    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",","-    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"","+    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",","+    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",","+    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",","+    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",","+    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",","+    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",","+    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",","+    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",","+    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",","+    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",","+    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",","+    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"","   ],"," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }","   ],"," ","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }","   ],"," ","-  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [","-    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },","-    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }","-  ],","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,","+  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\","," ","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",","-        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",","-        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",","-        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"","+        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",","+        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",","+        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",","+        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",","+        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",","+        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",","+        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",","+        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",","-        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",","-        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",","-        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"","+        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",","+        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",","+        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",","+        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",","+        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",","+        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",","+        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",","+        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"","       ]","     }","   ],","+","   \"status\": \"complete\""," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-4\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-04T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-04: Notifications & Email Infrastructure (SCH-004)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma already declares enum EmailStatus and the models Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox. None of the 4 existing migrations (init, user_management_profiles, classes_enrollment, auth_reconcile) creates them, so this ticket needs a new migration.\",\n    \"The schema has additive divergences from the PRD FR-1 block: Notification.updatedAt and EmailOutbox.updatedAt (the EmailOutbox one is used as the 'flipped to SENDING' timestamp for stuck-row recovery), plus a NotificationPreference.user relation with onDelete Cascade. Keep them. They are consistent with the platform rule that every model has createdAt and updatedAt.\",\n    \"The env vars are already declared in src/lib/env.ts and .env.example: EMAIL_TRANSPORT (default console), SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE, EMAIL_FROM, CRON_SECRET and APP_URL. Do not redeclare them.\",\n    \"@react-email/components 0.0.25, @react-email/render 1.0.1, nodemailer ^6.9.14 and @types/nodemailer are already in package.json. No new dependencies are needed.\",\n    \"package.json already defines \\\"worker:email\\\": \\\"tsx scripts/worker-email.ts\\\". The scripts/ directory does not exist yet.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts already contains the 'Notifications' (/notifications, all roles) and 'Email log' (/admin/email-log, ADMIN) entries. Do not add them again.\",\n    \"src/app/(app)/shell.tsx has the PRD-00 placeholder bell (an IconButton with NotificationsNoneIcon inside a Tooltip). FR-6 replaces it.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/email.ts sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link) currently only logs the link. Its callers are src/server/services/users.ts:396 (invite) and src/server/services/auth.ts:54 (password-reset). Keep the signature and change only the body to enqueue to the outbox.\",\n    \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts already exports requireUser(), requireRole(), requirePageUser() and requirePageRole(). Reuse them.\",\n    \"UserStatus has ACTIVE, INVITED, DISABLED and ARCHIVED, and User also has archivedAt. For notify(), 'archived or disabled' means status in (DISABLED, ARCHIVED) or archivedAt set.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings already has name, shortName, logoUrl, addressLine1 and addressLine2, which the email base layout header and footer can use.\",\n    \"useToast() lives at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts, not under src/components/shared/. Reuse the existing hook and do not create a second one.\",\n    \"These directories do not exist yet: src/server/notifications/, src/server/email/, src/app/api/notifications/, src/app/api/internal/, src/app/api/admin/, src/app/(app)/notifications/, src/app/(app)/account/ and src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Persist the EmailStatus enum and the Notification, NotificationPreference and EmailOutbox models (with indexes [userId, readAt, createdAt] and [status, nextAttemptAt]) through a new Prisma migration, keeping the existing additive updatedAt columns.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model; brownfield: no existing migration creates these tables\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/notifications/types.ts exporting NOTIFICATION_TYPES as a typed record: key → { label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Restrict notification categories to ACCOUNT, ACADEMIC, ATTENDANCE, COMMUNICATION, FINANCE and SYSTEM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Register the types account.invite and account.password_reset (email only, hidden from preferences) and system.test (admin test message).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Type notify()'s `type` parameter as keyof NOTIFICATION_TYPES so TypeScript rejects unknown keys, and let later PRDs extend the registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-2.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Implement notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } }) in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.1; Goals #1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"For each recipient, notify() skips archived or disabled users and resolves preferences from NotificationPreference rows, falling back to registry defaults.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"notify() creates a Notification row when in-app is enabled or the type is mandatoryInApp.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"notify() enqueues an EmailOutbox row (rendered HTML and text) when email is enabled for the type and the user has an email address.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"notify() uses createMany so that 1,000 recipients take at most 3 DB round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"notify() never throws to the caller. Failures are logged via logger, and callers invoke it after their own transaction commits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Provide notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest }), which expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (via ParentStudentLink), deduplicated.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-3.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Build email templates in src/server/email/templates/ with @react-email/components, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Create a base email layout with a school logo and name header (from SchoolSettings), a content area, and a footer containing the school address, a 'Manage email preferences' link to /account/notifications, and the sentence 'You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Create templates invite (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), password-reset (link, 60-minute expiry notice) and generic-notification (title, body, CTA button to APP_URL + link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Change the body of the existing sendAuthEmail() in src/server/auth/email.ts to enqueue the invite / password-reset template to EmailOutbox instead of only logging, keeping its signature and callers unchanged.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-4.4; §Summary; AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Implement dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 }). It selects PENDING rows with nextAttemptAt <= now using FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, marks them SENDING, sends via Nodemailer, then marks them SENT (with sentAt) or schedules a retry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"On send failure, increment attempts, record lastError and back off 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes for attempts 1–5. Set FAILED after the 5th failure.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.2; AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/internal/email/dispatch, protected by 'Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}'. It returns { sent, failed, retried } and returns 401 when the token is missing or wrong.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3; §API; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Create scripts/worker-email.ts (already wired to `npm run worker:email`), a Node loop that calls dispatchEmails every 15 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Provide an email transport selected by EMAIL_TRANSPORT. 'smtp' uses Nodemailer with SMTP_* and EMAIL_FROM. 'console' (the dev default) logs subject, recipient and text body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell in shell.tsx with an MUI IconButton + Badge showing the unread count, displayed as '9+' above 9.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"The bell polls GET /api/notifications/unread-count every 30 seconds while the tab is visible and pauses when visibilitychange reports hidden.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.1; §Out of Scope (no websockets)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Clicking the bell opens an MUI Popover with a List of the 10 most recent notifications. Unread items are bold with a dot, and each item shows its title, the body clamped to 2 lines, and a relative time such as '5 min ago'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Clicking a bell item marks it read and navigates to its link. The popover footer has 'Mark all as read' and 'View all' (/notifications).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-6.2; AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Build the /notifications page: a paginated list (20 per page), All / Unread filter tabs, a category filter, bulk 'Mark all as read', and a per-row read/unread toggle.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Implement purgeOldNotifications() to delete notifications older than 180 days. The dispatcher endpoint calls it at most about once per day, tracking the last run in memory (re-running after a restart is acceptable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Build the /account/notifications preferences page: an MUI Table grouped by category, listing each type visible to the user's role with its label, description, an 'In app' Switch and an 'Email' Switch. Types marked email-only or hidden (account.*) are excluded.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; §FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"On the preferences page, mandatoryInApp types show a disabled 'In app' Switch with the tooltip 'Required by the school'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.1; Goals #3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Preference changes save immediately through PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with optimistic UI, and roll back with a toast on error.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Build the /admin/email-log page: a table of created, recipient, subject, status, attempts and last error, with a status filter.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Retry now' row action for FAILED email-log rows that resets attempts = 0, status = PENDING and nextAttemptAt = now.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.1; §API POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a 'Send test notification to me' admin button that calls notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [currentAdmin] }) via POST /api/admin/notifications/test.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-9.2; §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications (?unread=true&category=&page=&pageSize=), returning only the caller's own notifications in the standard list shape.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/notifications/unread-count, returning { data: { count } } for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Expose POST /api/notifications/:id/read and /:id/unread, restricted to the owner (a non-owner gets 404 or 403), and POST /api/notifications/read-all for the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/me/notification-preferences, which returns the caller's preferences merged with registry defaults and filtered to the caller's role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Expose PUT /api/me/notification-preferences with body { type, inApp, email }, validated by Zod. It upserts the row and refuses inApp=false for mandatoryInApp types with VALIDATION_ERROR.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; §FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Expose GET /api/admin/email-log (paginated, ?status= filter) and POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry, both ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Seed 3 system.test notifications linking to /dashboard for each of student@schoolhub.test and parent@schoolhub.test (one read, two unread), idempotently.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data (wording '3 sample notifications for student… and parent…' is read as 3 per user; idempotency inferred from existing seed.ts convention)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Zod validators for the notification and preference payloads live in src/lib/validators/notifications.ts and are shared by client and API.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (Validation row; validators/<feature>.ts)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Performance: notify() for 1,000 recipients completes in under 2 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the unread-count endpoint responds in under 50 ms, backed by the [userId, readAt, createdAt] index.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Latency: no user request waits on SMTP. Emails are only enqueued in-request and are dispatched within 60 seconds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals #2; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Reliability: an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers, enforced with row locking (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Reliability: rows stuck in SENDING for more than 10 minutes (judged by updatedAt) are returned to PENDING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Security: notification link values must be relative paths starting with '/' and are validated to prevent open redirects. Protocol-relative '//' and backslash forms must be rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3 (the '//' rejection is MEDIUM, inferred from the open-redirect intent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Security: every route enforces access server-side through requireUser/requireRole. Admin routes are ADMIN only, and the dispatch route checks CRON_SECRET (a missing CRON_SECRET env means always 401).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole); §API Role column; AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Deliverability: every email has HTML and plain-text parts and a List-Unsubscribe header pointing at APP_URL/account/notifications.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: all UI uses MUI only (@mui/material v9, @mui/icons-material, MUI X). Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs, then fetchDocs) before use. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, notistack, sonner, etc.) must not be imported, and email templates are exempt via @react-email/components. QA must verify this. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §UI component rule (mandatory) items 1–6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Conventions: route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON) and use the standard response/error shapes and pagination (?page, ?pageSize default 20, max 100). New services go under src/server/notifications/ and src/server/email/. Use logger instead of console.log, except in the console email transport.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC, and relative and absolute times are displayed in the SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (timestamps); applied to bell/list/email-log display\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: reuse existing models, helpers and navigation entries. Never rename existing routes or models, never re-scaffold, and keep `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context; §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Tests (unit): preference resolution, retry backoff calculation, link validation, and notifyStudentAndParents expansion and dedupe.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Tests (integration, test DB): dispatcher locking with two concurrent calls, and stuck-SENDING recovery.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements; AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"Tests (Playwright): the bell count updates after a test notification, mark all as read works, and a preference toggle persists.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-17\", \"description\": \"Scope: SMS, mobile push, websockets and digest emails are out of scope and must not be built.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-18\", \"description\": \"Field limits: title is at most 140 characters, body at most 500 characters of plain text. notify() truncates or validates against these.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §FR-1 schema comments (enforcement point inferred)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    { \"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Default preferences + notify(system.test) → 1 Notification row + 1 EmailOutbox row; bell count +1 within 30 s.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-8\", \"FR-9\", \"FR-23\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Parent turned email off for a type → only the in-app row is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-7\", \"FR-9\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"SMTP failure → attempts=1, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt ≈ now+1 min; after 5 failures FAILED and visible in the admin email log.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-18\", \"FR-31\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"Two concurrent dispatchers over 10 pending emails → each sent exactly once.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"NFR-4\", \"NFR-15\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"Clicking a bell notification marks it read and navigates to its link.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-25\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"Dispatch without the correct bearer token → 401.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-19\", \"NFR-8\"] },\n    { \"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"Admin resends an invite → an EmailOutbox row with the invite template is created.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\"] }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-40: Should the seed create 3 notifications per user (6 total) or 3 total across both users?\",\n        \"FR-28: The PRD calls the preferences view an MUI Table with 'ListSubheader-style' group rows. Is a full-width TableRow header per category acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-4: account.invite and account.password_reset are 'email only'. Should notify() skip in-app rows for them (sendAuthEmail enqueues directly rather than via notify())?\",\n        \"NFR-18: Should an over-length title/body be truncated silently or rejected? notify() must never throw.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-40: no interactive answer available. Defaulting to 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread each).\",\n        \"FR-28: defaulting to a full-width TableRow category header inside an MUI Table.\",\n        \"FR-4: defaulting to sendAuthEmail enqueuing the outbox directly with no Notification row (the types are registered with an email-only flag so preferences hide them).\",\n        \"NFR-18: defaulting to truncation with a logger.warn, since notify() must not throw.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015ofGB8qvaWF7kVfMtLq22A","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
