{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCw2UM7ZaQ3bqtxZSVf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PBnAMTpA8W7bMuPnSNKbii","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-6 — User Stories: PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Bell schedule\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-5, FR-6, FR-33, FR-41):** As an admin, I want to define the periods of the school day (name, start, end, kind, order) so that the timetable has a consistent grid.\n- **US-2 (FR-8):** As an admin, I want to be stopped from deleting a period that still has lessons, and told how many, so that I don't silently break the timetable.\n- **US-3 (FR-2, FR-7, FR-34, FR-42):** As an admin, I want to toggle which weekdays are teaching days, and confirm before the lessons on a removed day are deleted, so that the grid matches the school week.\n\n## Timetable editor\n\n- **US-4 (FR-15, FR-16):** As an admin, I want to view the timetable by section, teacher or room for an academic year so that I can check it from any angle.\n- **US-5 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-23, FR-37):** As an admin, I want to drag courses onto a section's weekly grid, move them and remove them, so that I can build the timetable visually.\n- **US-6 (FR-9–FR-14, FR-19, FR-20, FR-36):** As an admin, I want clashes shown while I drag and blocked on save with every reason listed, so that no teacher, room, section or student is double-booked.\n- **US-7 (FR-21):** As an admin, I want to change a lesson's room from a list of free rooms so that room changes never create a clash.\n- **US-8 (FR-22):** As an admin using a keyboard, I want to place a course on a focused cell with Enter so that I can build the timetable without a mouse.\n- **US-9 (FR-29):** As an admin, I want to print any timetable on an A4 landscape page so that I can post it on a noticeboard.\n\n## Personal timetables\n\n- **US-10 (FR-24, FR-35):** As a teacher, I want my weekly timetable with rooms, including co-taught courses, so that I know where to be.\n- **US-11 (FR-24, FR-25, FR-38):** As a student or parent, I want the student's timetable (with a child selector when I have several children) so that we can plan the week.\n- **US-12 (FR-26, FR-31, FR-45):** As any user, I want a \"Today\" view with \"Now\" and \"Next\" badges so that I know what I have now and next.\n- **US-13 (FR-27):** As staff viewing a student, I want a \"Timetable\" tab on the student page so that I can see the student's week.\n- **US-14 (FR-28):** As a course member, I want a \"Schedule\" tab on the course page listing its weekly meeting times.\n- **US-15 (FR-32):** As any user, I want timetable entries in the sidebar so that the timetable is one click away.\n\n## Integration for later PRDs\n\n- **US-16 (FR-30, FR-31):** As the developer of Attendance (PRD-07), I want `getScheduleForDate()` and `getCurrentSlot()` so that I can look up which course a section has at a given day and period.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-17 (FR-4, FR-39, FR-40):** As the school, I want an additive migration, shared validation and audit history of timetable changes.\n- **US-18 (FR-41–FR-44):** As a developer or tester, I want seeded periods, teaching days, a clash-free 7A/7B week, Robotics Club, and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) so that the acceptance criteria can be demonstrated.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1:** Clash check and write run in one serializable transaction, so concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3:** The section week loads in under 400 ms, and the availability map returns in under 300 ms.\n- **NFR-4:** Keyboard alternative to drag-and-drop, and colour is never the only signal.\n- **NFR-5 / NFR-6:** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first (unreachable means blocker). No banned libraries. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added.\n- **NFR-7 / NFR-8:** Server-side access checks on every handler and page, plus the standard response and error shape.\n- **NFR-9 / NFR-10 / NFR-14:** Brownfield reuse, lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and the logger is used instead of console.log.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 / NFR-13:** Unit tests (clash rules, period overlap, now/next across timezones), an integration test (concurrent inserts) and Playwright tests (drag, clash snackbar, Today view).\n- **NFR-15:** Out of scope: a solver, A/B weeks, substitutes and holidays (PRD-14).\n- **NFR-16:** English-only, single school, evergreen browsers.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1392,"cache_read_input_tokens":47071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1392},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d2232b-5b66-4c64-98a2-53d3d0b92b18","uuid":"3dbe148b-9b61-496e-a35e-c277962d3362","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:28.934Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCw2ECpvy6ySTVMeo8a","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PBnAMTpA8W7bMuPnSNKbii":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-6 — User Stories: PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Bell schedule\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-5, FR-6, FR-33, FR-41):** As an admin, I want to define the periods of the school day (name, start, end, kind, order) so that the timetable has a consistent grid.\n- **US-2 (FR-8):** As an admin, I want to be stopped from deleting a period that still has lessons, and told how many, so that I don't silently break the timetable.\n- **US-3 (FR-2, FR-7, FR-34, FR-42):** As an admin, I want to toggle which weekdays are teaching days, and confirm before the lessons on a removed day are deleted, so that the grid matches the school week.\n\n## Timetable editor\n\n- **US-4 (FR-15, FR-16):** As an admin, I want to view the timetable by section, teacher or room for an academic year so that I can check it from any angle.\n- **US-5 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-23, FR-37):** As an admin, I want to drag courses onto a section's weekly grid, move them and remove them, so that I can build the timetable visually.\n- **US-6 (FR-9–FR-14, FR-19, FR-20, FR-36):** As an admin, I want clashes shown while I drag and blocked on save with every reason listed, so that no teacher, room, section or student is double-booked.\n- **US-7 (FR-21):** As an admin, I want to change a lesson's room from a list of free rooms so that room changes never create a clash.\n- **US-8 (FR-22):** As an admin using a keyboard, I want to place a course on a focused cell with Enter so that I can build the timetable without a mouse.\n- **US-9 (FR-29):** As an admin, I want to print any timetable on an A4 landscape page so that I can post it on a noticeboard.\n\n## Personal timetables\n\n- **US-10 (FR-24, FR-35):** As a teacher, I want my weekly timetable with rooms, including co-taught courses, so that I know where to be.\n- **US-11 (FR-24, FR-25, FR-38):** As a student or parent, I want the student's timetable (with a child selector when I have several children) so that we can plan the week.\n- **US-12 (FR-26, FR-31, FR-45):** As any user, I want a \"Today\" view with \"Now\" and \"Next\" badges so that I know what I have now and next.\n- **US-13 (FR-27):** As staff viewing a student, I want a \"Timetable\" tab on the student page so that I can see the student's week.\n- **US-14 (FR-28):** As a course member, I want a \"Schedule\" tab on the course page listing its weekly meeting times.\n- **US-15 (FR-32):** As any user, I want timetable entries in the sidebar so that the timetable is one click away.\n\n## Integration for later PRDs\n\n- **US-16 (FR-30, FR-31):** As the developer of Attendance (PRD-07), I want `getScheduleForDate()` and `getCurrentSlot()` so that I can look up which course a section has at a given day and period.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-17 (FR-4, FR-39, FR-40):** As the school, I want an additive migration, shared validation and audit history of timetable changes.\n- **US-18 (FR-41–FR-44):** As a developer or tester, I want seeded periods, teaching days, a clash-free 7A/7B week, Robotics Club, and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) so that the acceptance criteria can be demonstrated.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1:** Clash check and write run in one serializable transaction, so concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3:** The section week loads in under 400 ms, and the availability map returns in under 300 ms.\n- **NFR-4:** Keyboard alternative to drag-and-drop, and colour is never the only signal.\n- **NFR-5 / NFR-6:** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first (unreachable means blocker). No banned libraries. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added.\n- **NFR-7 / NFR-8:** Server-side access checks on every handler and page, plus the standard response and error shape.\n- **NFR-9 / NFR-10 / NFR-14:** Brownfield reuse, lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and the logger is used instead of console.log.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 / NFR-13:** Unit tests (clash rules, period overlap, now/next across timezones), an integration test (concurrent inserts) and Playwright tests (drag, clash snackbar, Today view).\n- **NFR-15:** Out of scope: a solver, A/B weeks, substitutes and holidays (PRD-14).\n- **NFR-16:** English-only, single school, evergreen browsers.\n"}}}
