cess.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3:** The section week loads in under 400 ms, and the availability map returns in under 300 ms.\n- **NFR-4:** Keyboard alternative to drag-and-drop, and colour is never the only signal.\n- **NFR-5 / NFR-6:** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first (unreachable means blocker). No banned libraries. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added.\n- **NFR-7 / NFR-8:** Server-side access checks on every handler and page, plus the standard response and error shape.\n- **NFR-9 / NFR-10 / NFR-14:** Brownfield reuse, lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and the logger is used instead of console.log.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 / NFR-13:** Unit tests (clash rules, period overlap, now/next across timezones), an integration test (concurrent inserts) and Playwright tests (drag, clash snackbar, Today view).\n- **NFR-15:** Out of scope: a solver, A/B weeks, substitutes and holidays (PRD-14).\n- **NFR-16:** English-only, single school, evergreen browsers.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":46,"newStart":1,"newLines":48,"lines":["-# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure","+# SH-6 — User Stories: PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable"," "," Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`."," ","-## In-app notifications","+## Bell schedule"," ","-- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.","-- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.","-- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.","-- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.","-- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.","+- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-5, FR-6, FR-33, FR-41):** As an admin, I want to define the periods of the school day (name, start, end, kind, order) so that the timetable has a consistent grid.","+- **US-2 (FR-8):** As an admin, I want to be stopped from deleting a period that still has lessons, and told how many, so that I don't silently break the timetable.","+- **US-3 (FR-2, FR-7, FR-34, FR-42):** As an admin, I want to toggle which weekdays are teaching days, and confirm before the lessons on a removed day are deleted, so that the grid matches the school week."," ","-## Preferences","+## Timetable editor"," ","-- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.","-- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.","+- **US-4 (FR-15, FR-16):** As an admin, I want to view the timetable by section, teacher or room for an academic year so that I can check it from any angle.","+- **US-5 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-23, FR-37):** As an admin, I want to drag courses onto a section's weekly grid, move them and remove them, so that I can build the timetable visually.","+- **US-6 (FR-9–FR-14, FR-19, FR-20, FR-36):** As an admin, I want clashes shown while I drag and blocked on save with every reason listed, so that no teacher, room, section or student is double-booked.","+- **US-7 (FR-21):** As an admin, I want to change a lesson's room from a list of free rooms so that room changes never create a clash.","+- **US-8 (FR-22):** As an admin using a keyboard, I want to place a course on a focused cell with Enter so that I can build the timetable without a mouse.","+- **US-9 (FR-29):** As an admin, I want to print any timetable on an A4 landscape page so that I can post it on a noticeboard."," ","-## Feature integration","+## Personal timetables"," ","-- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.","-- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.","+- **US-10 (FR-24, FR-35):** As a teacher, I want my weekly timetable with rooms, including co-taught courses, so that I know where to be.","+- **US-11 (FR-24, FR-25, FR-38):** As a student or parent, I want the student's timetable (with a child selector when I have several children) so that we can plan the week.","+- **US-12 (FR-26, FR-31, FR-45):** As any user, I want a \"Today\" view with \"Now\" and \"Next\" badges so that I know what I have now and next.","+- **US-13 (FR-27):** As staff viewing a student, I want a \"Timetable\" tab on the student page so that I can see the student's week.","+- **US-14 (FR-28):** As a course member, I want a \"Schedule\" tab on the course page listing its weekly meeting times.","+- **US-15 (FR-32):** As any user, I want timetable entries in the sidebar so that the timetable is one click away."," ","-## Email delivery","+## Integration for later PRDs"," ","-- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.","-- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.","-- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.","-- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.","+- **US-16 (FR-30, FR-31):** As the developer of Attendance (PRD-07), I want `getScheduleForDate()` and `getCurrentSlot()` so that I can look up which course a section has at a given day and period."," "," ## Data"," ","-- **US-14 (FR-1, FR-40):** As a developer, I want the notification tables migrated and seeded with sample notifications so that the UI is testable locally.","+- **US-17 (FR-4, FR-39, FR-40):** As the school, I want an additive migration, shared validation and audit history of timetable changes.","+- **US-18 (FR-41–FR-44):** As a developer or tester, I want seeded periods, teaching days, a clash-free 7A/7B week, Robotics Club, and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) so that the acceptance criteria can be demonstrated."," "," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **NFR-1 / NFR-2 Performance:** `notify()` handles 1,000 recipients in under 2 s; unread-count responds in under 50 ms.","-- **NFR-3 Latency:** no request waits on SMTP; emails go out within 60 s.","-- **NFR-4 / NFR-5 Reliability:** no email is sent twice (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`); rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 min return to `PENDING`.","-- **NFR-6 / NFR-7 / NFR-8 Security:** links must be relative `/` paths (no `//`); email HTML is escaped; access is enforced server-side; dispatch requires `CRON_SECRET`.","-- **NFR-9 Deliverability:** every email has HTML and text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing to `/account/notifications`.","-- **NFR-10 UI component rule:** MUI only, every component looked up via `mui-mcp` before use, no banned libraries. QA verifies this. An unreachable `mui-mcp` is a blocker.","-- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 Conventions:** thin handlers, standard response and pagination shapes, `logger` instead of `console.log`, and display in the school timezone.","-- **NFR-13 Brownfield:** reuse the existing schema models, env vars, nav entries, `requireUser`/`requireRole` and `useToast`. Keep lint, typecheck and tests green.","-- **NFR-14 / NFR-15 / NFR-16 Tests:** unit (preferences, backoff, link validation, expansion), integration (locking, stuck recovery), and Playwright (bell, mark all read, preference persistence).","-- **NFR-17 Scope:** no SMS, push, websockets or digests.","-- **NFR-18 Limits:** title at most 140 characters and body at most 500; truncated, never thrown.","+- **NFR-1:** Clash check and write run in one serializable transaction, so concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.","+- **NFR-2 / NFR-3:** The section week loads in under 400 ms, and the availability map returns in under 300 ms.","+- **NFR-4:** Keyboard alternative to drag-and-drop, and colour is never the only signal.","+- **NFR-5 / NFR-6:** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first (unreachable means blocker). No banned libraries. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added.","+- **NFR-7 / NFR-8:** Server-side access checks on every handler and page, plus the standard response and error shape.","+- **NFR-9 / NFR-10 / NFR-14:** Brownfield reuse, lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and the logger is used instead of console.log.","+- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 / NFR-13:** Unit tests (clash rules, period overlap, now/next across timezones), an integration test (concurrent inserts) and Playwright tests (drag, clash snackbar, Today view).","+- **NFR-15:** Out of scope: a solver, A/B weeks, substitutes and holidays (PRD-14).","+- **NFR-16:** English-only, single school, evergreen browsers."]}],"originalFile":"# SH-4 — User Stories: PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## In-app notifications\n\n- **US-1 (FR-22, FR-23, FR-35):** As a user, I want a bell with an unread count so that I notice new activity.\n- **US-2 (FR-24, FR-25):** As a user, I want to click a notification and go straight to the related page so that I can act on it.\n- **US-3 (FR-25, FR-26, FR-36):** As a user, I want to mark one or all notifications as read so that the list stays manageable.\n- **US-4 (FR-26, FR-34):** As a user, I want a full notifications page with All/Unread tabs and a category filter so that I can review older activity.\n- **US-5 (FR-27):** As the school, I want notifications older than 180 days purged so that the table stays small.\n\n## Preferences\n\n- **US-6 (FR-28, FR-30, FR-37, FR-38):** As a parent, I want to choose which events email me so that my inbox is not flooded.\n- **US-7 (FR-29, FR-8):** As the school, I want safety-critical in-app notifications to be impossible to turn off so that important events always reach users.\n\n## Feature integration\n\n- **US-8 (FR-2–FR-12):** As a developer of a later feature, I want one typed `notify()` call (and `notifyStudentAndParents()`) so that I never build my own delivery.\n- **US-9 (FR-16):** As an invited user or a user who forgot their password, I want to receive a real, branded email so that I can activate or reset my account.\n\n## Email delivery\n\n- **US-10 (FR-13–FR-15):** As a recipient, I want branded HTML emails with a plain-text fallback and a link to manage preferences so that emails look trustworthy and are easy to opt out of.\n- **US-11 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21):** As the school, I want emails queued and dispatched in the background with retries so that a slow SMTP server never blocks users.\n- **US-12 (FR-31, FR-32, FR-39):** As an admin, I want failed emails to retry and be visible so that important messages are not silently lost.\n- **US-13 (FR-33):** As an admin, I want to send myself a test notification so that I can verify delivery end to end.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-14 (FR-1, FR-40):** As a developer, I want the notification tables migrated and seeded with sample notifications so that the UI is testable locally.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1 / NFR-2 Performance:** `notify()` handles 1,000 recipients in under 2 s; unread-count responds in under 50 ms.\n- **NFR-3 Latency:** no request waits on SMTP; emails go out within 60 s.\n- **NFR-4 / NFR-5 Reliability:** no email is sent twice (`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`); rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 min return to `PENDING`.\n- **NFR-6 / NFR-7 / NFR-8 Security:** links must be relative `/` paths (no `//`); email HTML is escaped; access is enforced server-side; dispatch requires `CRON_SECRET`.\n- **NFR-9 Deliverability:** every email has HTML and text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing to `/account/notifications`.\n- **NFR-10 UI component rule:** MUI only, every component looked up via `mui-mcp` before use, no banned libraries. QA verifies this. An unreachable `mui-mcp` is a blocker.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 Conventions:** thin handlers, standard response and pagination shapes, `logger` instead of `console.log`, and display in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-13 Brownfield:** reuse the existing schema models, env vars, nav entries, `requireUser`/`requireRole` and `useToast`. Keep lint, typecheck and tests green.\n- **NFR-14 / NFR-15 / NFR-16 Tests:** unit (preferences, backoff, link validation, expansion), integration (locking, stuck recovery), and Playwright (bell, mark all read, preference persistence).\n- **NFR-17 Scope:** no SMS, push, websockets or digests.\n- **NFR-18 Limits:** title at most 140 characters and body at most 500; truncated, never thrown.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PBnAMTpA8W7bMuPnSNKbii","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
