{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD7ZZefyyHmsE6XPS7s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake for SH-6 is finished and the handoff status is `complete`. I found 61 requirements (45 functional, 16 non-functional) with 96% overall confidence. All four JSON files load as valid JSON and carry ticket ID SH-6.\n\n**Files written** to `artifacts/intake/`: `requirements.json`, `user-stories.md`, `tech-stack.json` and `handoff-to-architect.json` (written last). These replace the SH-4 files that were in the same folder. There's no `figma-readiness.json` because the PRD has no Figma link.\n\n**Problems in the existing workspace that the Architect needs to settle** (listed as blockers in the handoff, each with a default I've picked):\n1. **The seed data has nothing to build on.** `prisma/seed.ts` creates no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD's 7A/7B week, Robotics Club and the test people (Tom, Sam, Pat) all depend on them. Default: the seed also creates a minimal set of these. This is LOW confidence.\n2. **Subject names don't match.** The PRD uses ENG and HIST, but the seed has ELA and SOC. Default: reuse ELA and SOC, with course codes like ENG-7A and HIST-7A.\n3. **No API returns free rooms**, but the room picker needs one (FR-21). I recommended adding one small admin-only endpoint.\n4. **No API gives the slot count** that the \"turn off a teaching day\" confirmation shows. Default: `GET /api/school-days` returns a slot count for each day.\n5. **Schema and dependency work:**\n   - The new tables need a new migration that only adds things.\n   - Prisma needs matching relation fields added to Course, Room and Period.\n   - `@dnd-kit/core` isn't installed and needs adding at a fixed version.\n6. **The MUI docs server (`mui-mcp`) must be reachable before any UI is written.** The PRD says to stop if it's down.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- Shared components live in `src/components/<Name>/`, not `src/components/shared/` as the PRD says.\n- The student page route is `/students/[id]`, not `[studentId]`.\n\nThere was nobody to answer clarifying questions, so I logged 8 of them as one unresolved round in `requirements.json`, each with its default."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1127,"cache_read_input_tokens":64710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1127},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2d2232b-5b66-4c64-98a2-53d3d0b92b18","uuid":"15270d90-afcb-4b50-b6d2-d549acabdcc4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:51.050Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD7ZJGcPBgV9WygcVds"}
