{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BaybQfB5o5f7GxiDGuNEhR","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ca0c89-dbfd-4c24-b1d8-a82da51658f9","uuid":"e5f220e4-7b49-4900-b773-9bb4add43aff","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:35:40.872Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T06:34:34Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. Artifacts use SH-1.\",\n    \"The workspace is already further along than the PRD describes. PRD-02 to PRD-06 are already present (migrations up to 20261105000000_timetable), and most of the PRD-01 backend already exists, including a 20261104000000_auth_reconcile migration.\",\n    \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED: the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (prisma/schema.prisma); src/server/auth/tokens.ts (createToken/verifyToken/consumeToken, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual); credentials.ts (authorizeCredentials, a DUMMY_HASH bcrypt cost-12 compare, MAX_FAILED_LOGINS=5, LOCKOUT_MS=15min); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT maxAge 8h, updateAge 15min, passwordChangedAt recheck every 5 min); src/middleware.ts plus src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, schemas); common-passwords.txt (1,000 lines); services/auth.ts (acceptInvite, requestPasswordReset, resetPassword, changePassword); services/users.ts sendInvite/createInviteToken (a real implementation, not a stub); and every API route in the Pages & Routes table (/api/auth/[...nextauth], forgot-password, reset-password, accept-invite, /api/account/password).\",\n    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser, requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is already satisfied, so do not re-scaffold it.\",\n    \"MISSING: no UI pages exist under src/app/(auth)/ (only layout.tsx): /login, /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] are all absent. /account/security is absent (only /account/notifications exists).\",\n    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and there is no 'Account security' user-menu item.\",\n    \"MISSING: prisma/seed.ts creates no users. The six ACTIVE seed users and the INVITED invited@schoolhub.test user are not seeded.\",\n    \"MISSING TESTS: unit tests already exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators incl. safeCallbackUrl). The integration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and the Playwright auth specs are not there.\",\n    \"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`. User has @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) but not @@index([role, status]). Email lower-casing happens in the validator (emailField), not in the schema.\",\n    \"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() already enqueues into EmailOutbox and never logs the raw link. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.0\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: page MISSING (POST /api/auth/accept-invite present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: UI MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: page MISSING (API and service present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: page MISSING (API present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: page MISSING (API present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1–FR-8.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1–FR-9.5; Goals 3; Acceptance Criterion 9\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data, final sentence\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data + §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery) + §Platform Context 'reuse existing… never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from a test-only DB helper or the EmailOutbox (MISSING).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, that is a blocker; do not guess. Toasts use useToast() (Snackbar+Alert).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 1, 2, 5, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 3, 6; Fixed technology decisions 'Theming'\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers, response shape)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope; §Platform Context intro\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Only invited users can sign in. There is no public sign-up route or UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Browser support: the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. English-only UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (45 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column, or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet? A rename breaks existing callers and the no-rename rule.\",\n        \"FR-30/FR-31: PRD-04 already makes sendAuthEmail() enqueue to EmailOutbox. Confirm that the seed should log the invited user's link directly through logger.\",\n        \"FR-33: Add the missing @@index([role, status]) on User through a new additive migration?\",\n        \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the canonical id for SCH-001 (PRD)?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-32: no interactive answer is available. Default: keep `ip` (no rename).\",\n        \"FR-30/FR-31: no answer. Default: keep PRD-04 enqueue behaviour; the seed logs the link through logger.info.\",\n        \"FR-33: no answer. Default: add the index in an additive migration.\",\n        \"Ticket id: no answer. Default: SH-1 in all artifacts.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":118,"newStart":1,"newLines":96,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T06:34:34Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","-  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",","+  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",","   \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\","," ","   \"brownfieldFindings\": [","-    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",","-    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",","-    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",","-    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",","-    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",","-    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",","-    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",","-    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",","-    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",","-    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",","-    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",","-    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"","+    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. Artifacts use SH-1.\",","+    \"The workspace is already further along than the PRD describes. PRD-02 to PRD-06 are already present (migrations up to 20261105000000_timetable), and most of the PRD-01 backend already exists, including a 20261104000000_auth_reconcile migration.\",","+    \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED: the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (prisma/schema.prisma); src/server/auth/tokens.ts (createToken/verifyToken/consumeToken, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual); credentials.ts (authorizeCredentials, a DUMMY_HASH bcrypt cost-12 compare, MAX_FAILED_LOGINS=5, LOCKOUT_MS=15min); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT maxAge 8h, updateAge 15min, passwordChangedAt recheck every 5 min); src/middleware.ts plus src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, schemas); common-passwords.txt (1,000 lines); services/auth.ts (acceptInvite, requestPasswordReset, resetPassword, changePassword); services/users.ts sendInvite/createInviteToken (a real implementation, not a stub); and every API route in the Pages & Routes table (/api/auth/[...nextauth], forgot-password, reset-password, accept-invite, /api/account/password).\",","+    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser, requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is already satisfied, so do not re-scaffold it.\",","+    \"MISSING: no UI pages exist under src/app/(auth)/ (only layout.tsx): /login, /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] are all absent. /account/security is absent (only /account/notifications exists).\",","+    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and there is no 'Account security' user-menu item.\",","+    \"MISSING: prisma/seed.ts creates no users. The six ACTIVE seed users and the INVITED invited@schoolhub.test user are not seeded.\",","+    \"MISSING TESTS: unit tests already exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators incl. safeCallbackUrl). The integration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and the Playwright auth specs are not there.\",","+    \"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`. User has @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) but not @@index([role, status]). Email lower-casing happens in the validator (emailField), not in the schema.\",","+    \"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() already enqueues into EmailOutbox and never logs the raw link. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"","   ],"," ","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.0\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: page MISSING (POST /api/auth/accept-invite present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: UI MISSING.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: page MISSING (API and service present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: page MISSING (API present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: page MISSING (API present).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1–FR-8.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1–FR-9.5; Goals 3; Acceptance Criterion 9\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data, final sentence\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data + §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery) + §Platform Context 'reuse existing… never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from a test-only DB helper or the EmailOutbox (MISSING).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" }","   ],"," ","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, that is a blocker; do not guess. Toasts use useToast() (Snackbar+Alert).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 1, 2, 5, 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 3, 6; Fixed technology decisions 'Theming'\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers, response shape)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope; §Platform Context intro\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"Only invited users can sign in. There is no public sign-up route or UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Browser support: the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. English-only UI.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\" }","   ],"," ","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,","-  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,","+  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (45 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\","," ","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",","-        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",","-        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",","-        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",","-        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",","-        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",","-        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",","-        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"","+        \"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column, or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet? A rename breaks existing callers and the no-rename rule.\",","+        \"FR-30/FR-31: PRD-04 already makes sendAuthEmail() enqueue to EmailOutbox. Confirm that the seed should log the invited user's link directly through logger.\",","+        \"FR-33: Add the missing @@index([role, status]) on User through a new additive migration?\",","+        \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the canonical id for SCH-001 (PRD)?\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",","-        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",","-        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",","-        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",","-        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",","-        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",","-        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",","-        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"","+        \"FR-32: no interactive answer is available. Default: keep `ip` (no rename).\",","+        \"FR-30/FR-31: no answer. Default: keep PRD-04 enqueue behaviour; the seed logs the link through logger.info.\",","+        \"FR-33: no answer. Default: add the index in an additive migration.\",","+        \"Ticket id: no answer. Default: SH-1 in all artifacts.\"","       ]","     }","   ],"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-6\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T05:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-06: Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind yet. 5 migrations exist (latest 20261104120000_notifications_email), so this ticket needs a new additive migration.\",\n    \"Prisma requires back-relations for the FR-1 relations: Course.timetableSlots, Period.slots and Room.timetableSlots. They are additive and rename nothing.\",\n    \"Course has teacherId, coTeacherIds String[] (query with `has`), sectionId (null for cross-section electives), kind CORE|ELECTIVE, archivedAt and academicYearId. Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED with @@index([studentId, status]). Section has roomId (the homeroom room) and homeroomTeacherId.\",\n    \"Room has name @unique and archivedAt. Seeded rooms: Room 101, Room 102, Science Lab A, Gymnasium, Art Studio.\",\n    \"SchoolSettings.timezone exists (default 'UTC'). date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and @mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0 (TimeField) are installed. @dnd-kit/core is NOT installed and must be added.\",\n    \"prisma/seed.ts only seeds settings, academic year 2026-2027, terms, grade levels, subjects (MATH, ELA, SCI, SOC, PE, ART), and rooms. It seeds no users, sections, courses or enrollments. The PRD seed (7A/7B week, Robotics Club) and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) have nothing to attach to yet.\",\n    \"The seeded subject codes are ELA and SOC, not the ENG and HIST the PRD seed section names.\",\n    \"The shared UI components live in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, DataTable, PageHeader, EmptyState, UserPicker, Toast/useToast...), not in src/components/shared/. useToast() is at src/components/Toast/useToast.ts and exposes showToast({ message, severity }).\",\n    \"Feature services follow the PRD-05 subdirectory precedent (src/server/sections/sections-service.ts, src/server/courses/courses-service.ts). The PRD mandates src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"These access helpers exist: requireUser/requireRole/requirePageUser/requirePageRole (src/server/auth/requireRole.ts), assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse (course-access.ts), and getAccessibleStudentIds/assertCanViewStudent (student-access.ts). The HTTP helpers in src/server/http.ts are ok, paginated, apiError, AppError, withHandler, parseBody and parseQuery. audit() is in src/server/audit.ts.\",\n    \"The student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]). student-tabs.ts currently has 'courses'. course-tabs.ts exists with 'overview' and 'roster', and the Course 'Schedule' tab goes there.\",\n    \"src/config/navigation.ts entries support an optional `group: 'Administration'`. There is no Timetable entry yet.\"\n  ],\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY } and model Period (name, startTime/endTime 'HH:MM' strings in school timezone, kind default CLASS, order Int @unique, createdAt/updatedAt) exactly as specified.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add model SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id (ISO 1=Mon…7=Sun), isTeaching Boolean @default(true) }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add model TimetableSlot (academicYearId, courseId → Course onDelete Cascade, dayOfWeek 1–7, periodId → Period, roomId? → Room, timestamps) with @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId]) and @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId]).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Create one new additive Prisma migration for FR-1–FR-3, including the back-relation fields Prisma requires on Course, Period and Room. Do not rename or alter any existing model.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 + Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'; inferred from Prisma relation rules\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Bell schedule page /admin/timetable/periods (ADMIN): an ordered MUI Table of periods (name, start, end, kind) with add / edit / delete / reorder. Times are edited with MUI X TimeField.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Period validation (shared Zod + service): times are 'HH:MM' 24-hour, endTime is after startTime, and periods must not overlap any other period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Teaching days editor: seven MUI ToggleButtons (Mon–Sun). Turning off a day that has slots shows a confirmation with the number of slots to be removed, and confirming deletes those slots and marks the day non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Deleting a period that still has slots is refused with 409 CONFLICT, and the message/details give the count of affected slots.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: teacher. Reject when any other slot in the same academic year at (day, period) belongs to a course whose teacher or any co-teacher equals the new course's teacher or any co-teacher. Message: 'Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: room. When roomId is set, reject if another slot at (day, period) in the same academic year uses the same room. Message: 'Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: section. Reject if another slot at (day, period) belongs to a course with the same non-null sectionId. Message: 'Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Clash rule: student overlap. Reject if any student has ACTIVE enrollment in both the new course and a course in another slot at (day, period). The message includes the student count: 'Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4; Acceptance Criteria 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Reject slots on a non-CLASS period ('Period '<name>' is not a class period.') or on a non-teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5; FR-1 TimetableSlot.dayOfWeek comment; Acceptance Criteria 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"validateSlot(input) in src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts returns ALL clashes (not just the first). When moving a slot (PATCH), the slot itself is excluded from comparison.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3 (closing sentence); FR-4.3 move\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Timetable editor /admin/timetable: a view selector (Section default, Teacher, Room), an entity picker (Autocomplete) and an academic year selector.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Editor grid: columns are teaching days and rows are periods in order. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and non-droppable. A filled cell shows the subject colour, course code, teacher surname and room.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Section view sidebar lists the section's courses, each with a 'placed N' counter. Dropping a course on a cell calls POST /api/timetable/slots with the section's homeroom room (Section.roomId) as the default roomId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Dragging an existing slot to another cell moves it (PATCH). Dragging a slot out of the grid, or pressing Delete on a focused slot, removes it after a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"While dragging, cells that would clash are tinted red and also show an icon and a Tooltip with the messages. These come from a clash map preloaded via GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId=.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.4; NFR-3 Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"If the server rejects a drop or move, the card snaps back and an error toast (useToast) lists every clash returned in details.clashes[].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a slot opens an MUI Popover with an Autocomplete to change the room. The picker lists only rooms free at that day/period.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Keyboard alternative: every grid cell is focusable, and Enter on an empty cell opens a 'Place course' Dialog listing the section's courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Drag behaviour uses @dnd-kit/core only. The grid is an MUI Table or CSS-grid Box, and every course card and cell is an MUI Paper/Card with Chips and Tooltips.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.8; UI component rule 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criteria 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2; Acceptance Criteria 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.4; registry file inferred from the brownfield course-tabs.ts\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.5; Acceptance Criteria 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Goals 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Acceptance Criteria 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §API; Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Fixed technology decisions (Validation) and §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout ('Mutations that change records owned by someone else write an AuditLog row'). Whether school-wide admin config counts as 'owned by someone else' is assumed.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data; FR-1 SchoolDay comment\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data. The prerequisite sections, courses and subjects are not in the brownfield seed (see FR-44).\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"Inferred from PRD §Seed Data and Acceptance Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5. The brownfield prisma/seed.ts has no users, sections or courses.\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Period.startTime comment; Test Requirements ('across timezones'); Platform Context timestamps rule\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1; Test Requirements (integration)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 1, 2, 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §UI component rule 3, 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout (requireRole) and §Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context intro; FR-3 service path\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-14\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-15\", \"description\": \"Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope; FR-6.1; Constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-16\", \"description\": \"English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context §Assumptions\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 96,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"Weighted mean over 61 requirements (HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40): 54 HIGH, 5 MEDIUM, 2 LOW.\",\n\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-44: The brownfield seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments. May intake assume the timetable seed also creates minimal fixtures (Tom, Sam, Pat + 2 children, 7A/7B, the courses, Robotics Club)?\",\n        \"FR-43: The seed subjects are ELA and SOC, but the PRD says ENG and HIST. Should courses reuse ELA/SOC (with course codes ENG-7A/HIST-7A), or should new subjects be added?\",\n        \"FR-21: No API listed returns free rooms for a day/period. Should we add a small ADMIN endpoint (e.g. GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek=&periodId=&academicYearId=) or extend the availability response?\",\n        \"FR-7: How does the client learn the slot count before confirming a teaching-day switch-off? Option A: GET /api/school-days returns slotCount per day. Option B: PUT without confirm returns 409 with details.slotCount.\",\n        \"FR-5/FR-33: Must Period.order match chronological startTime order, or is reorder purely presentational? Also, Period.order @unique means the reorder needs a two-phase update in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40: Should timetable and bell-schedule mutations be audited, given they are school-wide admin configuration?\",\n        \"FR-35: Does 'own sections' for TEACHER mean homeroom sections only, or also sections whose courses they teach?\",\n        \"Archived courses and rooms (archivedAt set): exclude them from the editor sidebar, the room picker and the clash checks?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-44 default: seed minimal idempotent fixtures needed by the PRD seed and acceptance criteria.\",\n        \"FR-43 default: reuse the existing ELA and SOC subjects. Course codes follow the PRD names (MATH-7A, ENG-7A, SCI-7A, HIST-7A, PE-7A, ART-7A, likewise for 7B, and ROBOTICS).\",\n        \"FR-21 default: Architect decides. The recommendation is one ADMIN-only GET /api/timetable/free-rooms endpoint, the smallest addition.\",\n        \"FR-7 default: GET /api/school-days includes slotCount per day for the current academic year. PUT deletes the slots of switched-off days in one transaction.\",\n        \"FR-5 default: order is the display order and is not forced to be chronological. Reorder uses up/down buttons (no @dnd-kit/sortable) and a two-phase update in a transaction.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: audit slot, period and school-day mutations (LOW, Architect to confirm).\",\n        \"FR-35 default: TEACHER can view their own teacher view, sections they are homeroom teacher of (per the §Roles wording), and sections of courses they teach.\",\n        \"Archived default: archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BaybQfB5o5f7GxiDGuNEhR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
