{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKNHAmqUGQ7mYPf7XDF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8684,"cache_read_input_tokens":53847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8684},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ca0c89-dbfd-4c24-b1d8-a82da51658f9","uuid":"aa3183eb-d787-4050-8e86-78e27617aa59","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:35:44.949Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKNGhk81o2LzTvmiqJf","thinking_duration_ms":1014,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKNHAmqUGQ7mYPf7XDF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JMRjBcsGp8nnNgozuMbhSN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note: most of the backend (models, tokens.ts, credentials, session, middleware, services, API routes,\n> requireRole.ts, audit.ts) already exists. The remaining work is mainly the auth UI pages, the shell/user-menu\n> integration, the seed users, and the integration/e2e tests. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## App shell & permissions\n\n- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.\n- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.\n- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.\n\n## Audit\n\n- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.\n- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Data model\n\n- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (plus the missing `@@index([role, status])`) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |\n| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |\n| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |\n| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |\n| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |\n| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |\n| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |\n| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |\n| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |\n| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |\n| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |\n| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |\n| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8684,"cache_read_input_tokens":53847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8684},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ca0c89-dbfd-4c24-b1d8-a82da51658f9","uuid":"f504411a-c770-4866-93ec-db41c3d30c0d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:36:01.712Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKNGhk81o2LzTvmiqJf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JMRjBcsGp8nnNgozuMbhSN":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note: most of the backend (models, tokens.ts, credentials, session, middleware, services, API routes,\n> requireRole.ts, audit.ts) already exists. The remaining work is mainly the auth UI pages, the shell/user-menu\n> integration, the seed users, and the integration/e2e tests. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## App shell & permissions\n\n- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.\n- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.\n- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.\n\n## Audit\n\n- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.\n- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Data model\n\n- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (plus the missing `@@index([role, status])`) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |\n| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |\n| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |\n| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |\n| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |\n| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |\n| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |\n| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |\n| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |\n| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |\n| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |\n| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |\n| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JMRjBcsGp8nnNgozuMbhSN","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ca0c89-dbfd-4c24-b1d8-a82da51658f9","uuid":"015566ea-291e-48b9-9a3a-2164e997b192","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:36:01.788Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note: most of the backend (models, tokens.ts, credentials, session, middleware, services, API routes,\n> requireRole.ts, audit.ts) already exists. The remaining work is mainly the auth UI pages, the shell/user-menu\n> integration, the seed users, and the integration/e2e tests. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## App shell & permissions\n\n- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.\n- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.\n- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.\n\n## Audit\n\n- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.\n- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Data model\n\n- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (plus the missing `@@index([role, status])`) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |\n| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |\n| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |\n| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |\n| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |\n| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |\n| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |\n| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |\n| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |\n| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |\n| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |\n| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |\n| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":48,"newStart":1,"newLines":62,"lines":["-# SH-6 — User Stories: PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable","+# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)"," ","-Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.","+> Brownfield note: most of the backend (models, tokens.ts, credentials, session, middleware, services, API routes,","+> requireRole.ts, audit.ts) already exists. The remaining work is mainly the auth UI pages, the shell/user-menu","+> integration, the seed users, and the integration/e2e tests. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`."," ","-## Bell schedule","+## Sign-in & session"," ","-- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-5, FR-6, FR-33, FR-41):** As an admin, I want to define the periods of the school day (name, start, end, kind, order) so that the timetable has a consistent grid.","-- **US-2 (FR-8):** As an admin, I want to be stopped from deleting a period that still has lessons, and told how many, so that I don't silently break the timetable.","-- **US-3 (FR-2, FR-7, FR-34, FR-42):** As an admin, I want to toggle which weekdays are teaching days, and confirm before the lessons on a removed day are deleted, so that the grid matches the school week.","+- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.","+- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"","+- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.","+- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"","+- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure."," ","-## Timetable editor","+## Invitation"," ","-- **US-4 (FR-15, FR-16):** As an admin, I want to view the timetable by section, teacher or room for an academic year so that I can check it from any angle.","-- **US-5 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-23, FR-37):** As an admin, I want to drag courses onto a section's weekly grid, move them and remove them, so that I can build the timetable visually.","-- **US-6 (FR-9–FR-14, FR-19, FR-20, FR-36):** As an admin, I want clashes shown while I drag and blocked on save with every reason listed, so that no teacher, room, section or student is double-booked.","-- **US-7 (FR-21):** As an admin, I want to change a lesson's room from a list of free rooms so that room changes never create a clash.","-- **US-8 (FR-22):** As an admin using a keyboard, I want to place a course on a focused cell with Enter so that I can build the timetable without a mouse.","-- **US-9 (FR-29):** As an admin, I want to print any timetable on an A4 landscape page so that I can post it on a noticeboard.","+- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working."," ","-## Personal timetables","+## Password reset & change"," ","-- **US-10 (FR-24, FR-35):** As a teacher, I want my weekly timetable with rooms, including co-taught courses, so that I know where to be.","-- **US-11 (FR-24, FR-25, FR-38):** As a student or parent, I want the student's timetable (with a child selector when I have several children) so that we can plan the week.","-- **US-12 (FR-26, FR-31, FR-45):** As any user, I want a \"Today\" view with \"Now\" and \"Next\" badges so that I know what I have now and next.","-- **US-13 (FR-27):** As staff viewing a student, I want a \"Timetable\" tab on the student page so that I can see the student's week.","-- **US-14 (FR-28):** As a course member, I want a \"Schedule\" tab on the course page listing its weekly meeting times.","-- **US-15 (FR-32):** As any user, I want timetable entries in the sidebar so that the timetable is one click away.","+- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.","+- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.","+- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure."," ","-## Integration for later PRDs","+## App shell & permissions"," ","-- **US-16 (FR-30, FR-31):** As the developer of Attendance (PRD-07), I want `getScheduleForDate()` and `getCurrentSlot()` so that I can look up which course a section has at a given day and period.","+- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.","+- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.","+- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them."," ","-## Data","+## Audit"," ","-- **US-17 (FR-4, FR-39, FR-40):** As the school, I want an additive migration, shared validation and audit history of timetable changes.","-- **US-18 (FR-41–FR-44):** As a developer or tester, I want seeded periods, teaching days, a clash-free 7A/7B week, Robotics Club, and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) so that the acceptance criteria can be demonstrated.","+- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents."," ","+## Seed & tests","+","+- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.","+- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.","+","+## Data model","+","+- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (plus the missing `@@index([role, status])`) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.","+"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **NFR-1:** Clash check and write run in one serializable transaction, so concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.","-- **NFR-2 / NFR-3:** The section week loads in under 400 ms, and the availability map returns in under 300 ms.","-- **NFR-4:** Keyboard alternative to drag-and-drop, and colour is never the only signal.","-- **NFR-5 / NFR-6:** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first (unreachable means blocker). No banned libraries. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added.","-- **NFR-7 / NFR-8:** Server-side access checks on every handler and page, plus the standard response and error shape.","-- **NFR-9 / NFR-10 / NFR-14:** Brownfield reuse, lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and the logger is used instead of console.log.","-- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 / NFR-13:** Unit tests (clash rules, period overlap, now/next across timezones), an integration test (concurrent inserts) and Playwright tests (drag, clash snackbar, Today view).","-- **NFR-15:** Out of scope: a solver, A/B weeks, substitutes and holidays (PRD-14).","-- **NFR-16:** English-only, single school, evergreen browsers.","+| ID | Requirement |","+|---|---|","+| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |","+| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |","+| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |","+| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |","+| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |","+| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |","+| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |","+| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |","+| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |","+| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |","+| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |","+| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |","+| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |","+| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |","+| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |"]}],"originalFile":"# SH-6 — User Stories: PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. All requirement IDs are listed in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Bell schedule\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-5, FR-6, FR-33, FR-41):** As an admin, I want to define the periods of the school day (name, start, end, kind, order) so that the timetable has a consistent grid.\n- **US-2 (FR-8):** As an admin, I want to be stopped from deleting a period that still has lessons, and told how many, so that I don't silently break the timetable.\n- **US-3 (FR-2, FR-7, FR-34, FR-42):** As an admin, I want to toggle which weekdays are teaching days, and confirm before the lessons on a removed day are deleted, so that the grid matches the school week.\n\n## Timetable editor\n\n- **US-4 (FR-15, FR-16):** As an admin, I want to view the timetable by section, teacher or room for an academic year so that I can check it from any angle.\n- **US-5 (FR-17, FR-18, FR-23, FR-37):** As an admin, I want to drag courses onto a section's weekly grid, move them and remove them, so that I can build the timetable visually.\n- **US-6 (FR-9–FR-14, FR-19, FR-20, FR-36):** As an admin, I want clashes shown while I drag and blocked on save with every reason listed, so that no teacher, room, section or student is double-booked.\n- **US-7 (FR-21):** As an admin, I want to change a lesson's room from a list of free rooms so that room changes never create a clash.\n- **US-8 (FR-22):** As an admin using a keyboard, I want to place a course on a focused cell with Enter so that I can build the timetable without a mouse.\n- **US-9 (FR-29):** As an admin, I want to print any timetable on an A4 landscape page so that I can post it on a noticeboard.\n\n## Personal timetables\n\n- **US-10 (FR-24, FR-35):** As a teacher, I want my weekly timetable with rooms, including co-taught courses, so that I know where to be.\n- **US-11 (FR-24, FR-25, FR-38):** As a student or parent, I want the student's timetable (with a child selector when I have several children) so that we can plan the week.\n- **US-12 (FR-26, FR-31, FR-45):** As any user, I want a \"Today\" view with \"Now\" and \"Next\" badges so that I know what I have now and next.\n- **US-13 (FR-27):** As staff viewing a student, I want a \"Timetable\" tab on the student page so that I can see the student's week.\n- **US-14 (FR-28):** As a course member, I want a \"Schedule\" tab on the course page listing its weekly meeting times.\n- **US-15 (FR-32):** As any user, I want timetable entries in the sidebar so that the timetable is one click away.\n\n## Integration for later PRDs\n\n- **US-16 (FR-30, FR-31):** As the developer of Attendance (PRD-07), I want `getScheduleForDate()` and `getCurrentSlot()` so that I can look up which course a section has at a given day and period.\n\n## Data\n\n- **US-17 (FR-4, FR-39, FR-40):** As the school, I want an additive migration, shared validation and audit history of timetable changes.\n- **US-18 (FR-41–FR-44):** As a developer or tester, I want seeded periods, teaching days, a clash-free 7A/7B week, Robotics Club, and the acceptance-criteria personas (Tom, Sam, Pat) so that the acceptance criteria can be demonstrated.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1:** Clash check and write run in one serializable transaction, so concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\n- **NFR-2 / NFR-3:** The section week loads in under 400 ms, and the availability map returns in under 300 ms.\n- **NFR-4:** Keyboard alternative to drag-and-drop, and colour is never the only signal.\n- **NFR-5 / NFR-6:** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first (unreachable means blocker). No banned libraries. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added.\n- **NFR-7 / NFR-8:** Server-side access checks on every handler and page, plus the standard response and error shape.\n- **NFR-9 / NFR-10 / NFR-14:** Brownfield reuse, lint, typecheck and tests stay green, and the logger is used instead of console.log.\n- **NFR-11 / NFR-12 / NFR-13:** Unit tests (clash rules, period overlap, now/next across timezones), an integration test (concurrent inserts) and Playwright tests (drag, clash snackbar, Today view).\n- **NFR-15:** Out of scope: a solver, A/B weeks, substitutes and holidays (PRD-14).\n- **NFR-16:** English-only, single school, evergreen browsers.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JMRjBcsGp8nnNgozuMbhSN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
