{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKREZb7eH7YCNtL65bG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake for SH-1 is done and the handoff to the architect is written. I pulled out 49 requirements (34 functional, 15 non-functional) with an overall confidence of 97%. The intake folder held old files from ticket SH-6; I replaced all four.\n\n**Most of PRD-01 is already built.** The PRD describes a starting point that's behind what the workspace actually contains:\n- **Already in place:**\n  - the user, token and audit-log database models, including a migration that already lines them up with this PRD\n  - the token module, sign-in checks and lockout\n  - the 8-hour session that signs other devices out after a password change\n  - the redirect/401 gate (`middleware.ts`) and the rate limiter\n  - the audit helper and the password rules\n  - the auth and user service functions, and every auth API route\n- **`requireRole.ts` is already finished.** The placeholder user the PRD says to remove is gone, so its FR-9 needs no work.\n- **`sendInvite` is a real implementation, not a stub.**\n- **Email (PRD-04) is already wired up.** `sendAuthEmail()` already queues mail, so the PRD's interim \"just log the email\" version must not be brought back.\n\n**What's actually left to build:**\n- The sign-in, forgot-password, reset-password and invite pages; the `(auth)` folder only has a layout.\n- The `/account/security` page.\n- The app shell: remove its placeholder user and show the real one (name, role badge, initials, Sign out, an \"Account security\" menu item), and filter the sidebar by the real role.\n- Seed users: the seed currently creates none. That means the six test accounts and the invited user, with its invite link logged.\n- Integration tests (sign-in branches, accept invite, reset password, change password) and the Playwright browser tests. The unit tests mostly exist.\n\n**Open questions.** No one was available to answer these, so I used defaults:\n- **Audit-log IP column:** the existing column is `ip`, not the PRD's `ipAddress`. I kept `ip` (low confidence) because the PRD forbids renaming existing models.\n- **Role/status index:** the `User` model is missing the PRD's `@@index([role, status])`. I planned a new migration that only adds it.\n- **Invite link in the seed:** the email function deliberately never logs raw links, so the seed should log the invited user's link itself.\n- **Ticket id:** the PRD header says SCH-001; all files use SH-1, as in your task.\n\nThe PRD has no Figma link, so there's no `figma-readiness.json`. One hard rule carries forward: the dev phase must reach the MUI docs server before writing any UI, and the PRD says to stop and report it if that server is unreachable.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/intake/`:\n- requirements.json\n- user-stories.md\n- tech-stack.json\n- handoff-to-architect.json"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":840,"cache_read_input_tokens":65849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":840},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ca0c89-dbfd-4c24-b1d8-a82da51658f9","uuid":"8c598ec6-3006-4105-80b9-831bc8c36d80","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:36:32.112Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKREKD2qEP66P4p5itT"}
