{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJcNQNZ1LLYA4BKM2b1XN7","type":"tool_result","content":"dict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'brownfieldFindings', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'confidenceMethod', 'clarificationLog', 'status'])\nTicket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. Artifacts use SH-1.\nThe workspace is already further along than the PRD describes. PRD-02 to PRD-06 are already present (migrations up to 20261105000000_timetable), and most of the PRD-01 backend already exists, including a 20261104000000_auth_reconcile migration.\nALREADY IMPLEMENTED: the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (prisma/schema.prisma); src/server/auth/tokens.ts (createToken/verifyToken/consumeToken, SHA-256, timingSafeEqual); credentials.ts (authorizeCredentials, a DUMMY_HASH bcrypt cost-12 compare, MAX_FAILED_LOGINS=5, LOCKOUT_MS=15min); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT maxAge 8h, updateAge 15min, passwordChangedAt recheck every 5 min); src/middleware.ts plus src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, schemas); common-passwords.txt (1,000 lines); services/auth.ts (acceptInvite, requestPasswordReset, resetPassword, changePassword); services/users.ts sendInvite/createInviteToken (a real implementation, not a stub); and every API route in the Pages & Routes table (/api/auth/[...nextauth], forgot-password, reset-password, accept-invite, /api/account/password).\nrequireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser, requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is already satisfied, so do not re-scaffold it.\nMISSING: no UI pages exist under src/app/(auth)/ (only layout.tsx): /login, /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] are all absent. /account/security is absent (only /account/notifications exists).\nMISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and there is no 'Account security' user-menu item.\nMISSING: prisma/seed.ts creates no users. The six ACTIVE seed users and the INVITED invited@schoolhub.test user are not seeded.\nMISSING TESTS: unit tests already exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators incl. safeCallbackUrl). The integration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) and the Playwright auth specs are not there.\nSCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`. User has @@index([lastName, firstName, email]) but not @@index([role, status]). Email lower-casing happens in the validator (emailField), not in the schema.\nPRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() already enqueues into EmailOutbox and never logs the raw link. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\nFR-1 HIGH Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLogi\nFR-2 HIGH A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form\nFR-3 HIGH The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or l\nFR-4 HIGH Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try ag\nFR-5 HIGH A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets f\nFR-6 HIGH Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over retu\nFR-7 HIGH After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() fro\nFR-8 HIGH Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\nFR-9 HIGH The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\nFR-10 HIGH A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, s\nFR-11 HIGH middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with erro\nFR-12 HIGH All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores\nFR-13 HIGH A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or ha\nFR-14 HIGH Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the us\nFR-15 HIGH Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bun\nFR-16 HIGH A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PA\nFR-17 HIGH A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" (no user enumeratio\nFR-18 HIGH When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 ra\nFR-19 HIGH A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the \nFR-20 HIGH An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current pass\nFR-21 HIGH Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu.\nFR-22 HIGH src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, i\nFR-23 HIGH src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /log\nFR-24 HIGH src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-\nFR-25 HIGH Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source \nFR-26 HIGH The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\nFR-27 HIGH Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role.\nFR-28 HIGH The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina T\nFR-29 HIGH The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding.\nFR-30 MEDIUM The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues\nFR-31 MEDIUM Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub de\nFR-32 LOW The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields i\nFR-33 MEDIUM An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks.\nFR-34 HIGH Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration\nNFR-1 HIGH Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\nNFR-2 HIGH Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\nNFR-3 HIGH 'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\nNFR-4 HIGH Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\nNFR-5 HIGH Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\"polite\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\nNFR-6 HIGH UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the th\nNFR-7 HIGH No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/rea\nNFR-8 HIGH Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\nNFR-9 HIGH Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\nNFR-10 HIGH API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the stan\nNFR-11 HIGH Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\nNFR-12 HIGH No console.