ndAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n]\nstatus = {\n 'FR-2': ' Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.',\n 'FR-13': ' Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.',\n 'FR-14': ' Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.',\n 'FR-16': ' Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.',\n 'FR-17': ' Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.',\n 'FR-19': ' Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.',\n 'FR-20': ' Status: the API exists; the /account/security UI page is MISSING.',\n 'FR-21': ' Status: MISSING.',\n 'FR-25': ' Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).',\n 'FR-26': ' Status: MISSING.',\n 'FR-27': ' Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).',\n 'FR-28': ' Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).',\n 'FR-29': ' Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).',\n 'FR-33': ' Status: PRESENT (migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index).',\n 'FR-34': ' Status: the unit tests exist. The integration tests and Playwright auth specs are MISSING.',\n}\nfor r in d['functionalRequirements']:\n    s = status.get(r['id'])\n    if s:\n        r['description'] = r['description'].split(' Status:')[0].rstrip() + s\nd['clarificationLog'] = [{\n \"round\": 1,\n \"questions\": [\n  \"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column (and its existing indexes), or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet?\",\n  \"FR-30/FR-31: Since PRD-04 already enqueues auth emails into EmailOutbox, is it correct that the seed logs the invite link directly via logger and the PRD's interim logger stub is not restored?\",\n  \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the canonical id for SCH-001 (PRD)?\"\n ],\n \"unresolved\": [\n  \"FR-32: no interactive answer is available. Default: keep `ip` and the existing indexes (no-rename rule).\",\n  \"FR-30/FR-31: no answer. Default: keep the PRD-04 enqueue behaviour; the seed logs the link (already implemented).\",\n  \"Ticket id: no answer. Default: SH-1.\"\n ]\n}]\nd['status'] = 'complete'\njson.dump(d, open('requirements.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nt = json.load(open('tech-stack.json')); t['timestamp'] = ts\njson.dump(t, open('tech-stack.json','w'), indent=2)\nprint(ts, len(d['functionalRequirements'])+len(d['nonFunctionalRequirements']), d['overallConfidencePct'],\n      all(r.get('confidence') and r.get('source') for r in d['functionalRequirements']+d['nonFunctionalRequirements']))\nEOF\ncat user-stories.md | head -62","description":"Update requirements.json and tech-stack.json"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnK8C8ZrLzuqz1zKkjqJiH","type":"tool_result","content":"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z 49 97 True\n# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note: most of the backend (models, tokens.ts, credentials, session, middleware, services, API routes,\n> requireRole.ts, audit.ts) already exists. The remaining work is mainly the auth UI pages, the shell/user-menu\n> integration, the seed users, and the integration/e2e tests. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## App shell & permissions\n\n- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.\n- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.\n- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.\n\n## Audit\n\n- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.\n- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Data model\n\n- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (plus the missing `@@index([role, status])`) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |\n| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |\n| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |\n| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |\n| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |\n| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |\n| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |\n| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |\n| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |\n| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |\n| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |\n| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |\n| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef677fc-a5ec-4701-b31e-b39b1716460a","uuid":"03e918f3-95f4-488c-bf58-6e8695769677","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:26:10.088Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z 49 97 True\n# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note: most of the backend (models, tokens.ts, credentials, session, middleware, services, API routes,\n> requireRole.ts, audit.ts) already exists. The remaining work is mainly the auth UI pages, the shell/user-menu\n> integration, the seed users, and the integration/e2e tests. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account