kenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, signInSchema); common-passwords.txt; services/auth.ts; services/users.ts (createUser, createInviteToken, real sendInvite → sendAuthEmail); every API route in the Pages & Routes table.\",\n    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\",\n    \"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index (@@index([role, status])).\",\n    \"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\",\n    \"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\",\n    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\",\n    \"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-v\n# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note (re-checked 2026-11-05): the backend, the `/login` page, the seed users and the `@@index([role, status])` migration already exist.\n> Remaining: the `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]` and `/account/security` pages; removing PLACEHOLDER_USER from\n> `shell.tsx` (session user, role badge, initials, Sign out, \"Account security\" item); and the integration and Playwright auth tests.\n> Reuse `TextFormField`, `PasswordChecklist`/`passwordInputSlot` and `useToast`. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## App shell & permissions\n\n- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.\n- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.\n- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.\n../src/server/audit.ts\n../src/server/csv.ts\n../src/server/db.ts\n../src/server/http.ts\n../src/server/rate-limit.ts\n\n../src/config:\ncourse-tabs.ts\nnavigation.ts\npublic-routes.ts\nstudent-tabs.ts\n\n../src/server:\naudit.ts\nauth\ncourses\ncsv.ts\ndb.ts\nemail\nenrollment\nhttp.ts\nnotifications\nrate-limit.ts\nsections\nservices\ntimetable\n\n../src/server/auth:\nauth.config.ts\nauth.ts\ncommon-passwords.txt\ncourse-access.ts\ncredentials.ts\nemail.ts\npassword-policy.ts\nrequireRole.ts\nstudent-access.ts\ntokens.ts\n\n../src/server/courses:\ncourses-service.ts\n\n../src/server/email:\nadmin.ts\nbackoff.ts\ndispatch.ts\noutbox.ts\nrender.ts\ntemplates\ntransport.ts\n\n../src/server/enrollment:\nr