{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm86XEu7xAhjWBajYiZx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GGxkwKGcd2cQ9dqSbuJTVA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",\n    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",\n    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",\n    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",\n    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",\n    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",\n        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",\n        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",\n        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",\n        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",\n        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148,"cache_read_input_tokens":48174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":148},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57a4dc66-5d3c-4bfa-a9bb-908be3700630","uuid":"b131493d-343d-46c7-a146-ff9b0d9741d0","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:30:07.756Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm86X2kECpwQmavw6diL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GGxkwKGcd2cQ9dqSbuJTVA":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",\n    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",\n    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",\n    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",\n    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",\n    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",\n        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",\n        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",\n        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",\n        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",\n        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GGxkwKGcd2cQ9dqSbuJTVA","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57a4dc66-5d3c-4bfa-a9bb-908be3700630","uuid":"d8b0e805-ae6b-49e4-8094-08d16827d105","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:30:07.874Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",\n    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",\n    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",\n    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",\n    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",\n    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",\n        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",\n        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",\n        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",\n        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",\n        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":337,"newStart":1,"newLines":96,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","-  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",","+  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",","   \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",","   \"brownfieldFindings\": [","-    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. All artifacts use SH-1.\",","-    \"Re-run of intake on 2026-11-05. The workspace was re-checked, and some gaps reported by the earlier SH-1 intake have since been closed.\",","-    \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED (do not rebuild): the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, signInSchema); common-passwords.txt; services/auth.ts; services/users.ts (createUser, createInviteToken, real sendInvite → sendAuthEmail); every API route in the Pages & Routes table.\",","-    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\",","-    \"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index (@@index([role, status])).\",","-    \"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\",","-    \"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\",","-    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\",","-    \"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators, login-error-message). No integration tests exist for the authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password or change-password (tests/integration has only email-dispatch and timetable). No Playwright auth specs exist (tests/e2e has only dashboard, landing and notifications).\",","-    \"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`, and has @@index([actorId]) and @@index([action]) rather than the PRD's [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt] indexes. Under the no-rename rule, keep `ip`.\",","-    \"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"","+    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",","+    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",","+    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",","+    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",","+    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",","+    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",","+    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",","+    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",","+    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",","+    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",","+    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",","+    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"","   ],","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-1\",","-      \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-2\",","-      \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-3\",","-      \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-4\",","-      \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-5\",","-      \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-6\",","-      \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-7\",","-      \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-8\",","-      \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-9\",","-      \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-10\",","-      \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-11\",","-      \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-12\",","-      \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.0\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-13\",","-      \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-14\",","-      \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message. Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3; Acceptance Criterion 4\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-15\",","-      \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-16\",","-      \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-17\",","-      \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-18\",","-      \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 6\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-19\",","-      \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-20\",","-      \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; the /account/security UI page is MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-21\",","-      \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-22\",","-      \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1–FR-8.4\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-23\",","-      \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1–FR-9.5; Goals 3; Acceptance Criterion 9\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-24\",","-      \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-25\",","-      \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-26\",","-      \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-27\",","-      \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-28\",","-      \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data table\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-29\",","-      \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data, final sentence\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-30\",","-      \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data + §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-31\",","-      \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery) + §Platform Context 'reuse existing… never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-32\",","-      \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-33\",","-      \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks. Status: PRESENT (migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"FR-34\",","-      \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from a test-only DB helper or the EmailOutbox (MISSING). Status: the unit tests exist. The integration tests and Playwright auth specs are MISSING.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\"","-    }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }","   ],","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",","-      \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",","-      \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",","-      \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",","-      \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",","-      \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",","-      \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, that is a blocker; do not guess. Toasts use useToast() (Snackbar+Alert).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 1, 2, 5, 6\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",","-      \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 3, 6; Fixed technology decisions 'Theming'\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",","-      \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",","-      \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",","-      \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers, response shape)\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",","-      \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",","-      \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-13\",","-      \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope; §Platform Context intro\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-14\",","-      \"description\": \"Only invited users can sign in. There is no public sign-up route or UI.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\"","-    },","-    {","-      \"id\": \"NFR-15\",","-      \"description\": \"Browser support: the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. English-only UI.\",","-      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",","-      \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\"","-    }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }","   ],","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,","-  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (45 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\",","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column (and its existing indexes), or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet?\",","-        \"FR-30/FR-31: Since PRD-04 already enqueues auth emails into EmailOutbox, is it correct that the seed logs the invite link directly via logger and the PRD's interim logger stub is not restored?\",","-        \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the canonical id for SCH-001 (PRD)?\"","+        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",","+        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",","+        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",","+        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",","+        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"FR-32: no interactive answer is available. Default: keep `ip` and the existing indexes (no-rename rule).\",","-        \"FR-30/FR-31: no answer. Default: keep the PRD-04 enqueue behaviour; the seed logs the link (already implemented).\",","-        \"Ticket id: no answer. Default: SH-1.\"","+        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",","+        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",","+        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"","       ]","     }","   ],","   \"status\": \"complete\"","-}","\\ No newline at end of file","+}"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. All artifacts use SH-1.\",\n    \"Re-run of intake on 2026-11-05. The workspace was re-checked, and some gaps reported by the earlier SH-1 intake have since been closed.\",\n    \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED (do not rebuild): the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, signInSchema); common-passwords.txt; services/auth.ts; services/users.ts (createUser, createInviteToken, real sendInvite → sendAuthEmail); every API route in the Pages & Routes table.\",\n    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\",\n    \"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index (@@index([role, status])).\",\n    \"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\",\n    \"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\",\n    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\",\n    \"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators, login-error-message). No integration tests exist for the authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password or change-password (tests/integration has only email-dispatch and timetable). No Playwright auth specs exist (tests/e2e has only dashboard, landing and notifications).\",\n    \"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`, and has @@index([actorId]) and @@index([action]) rather than the PRD's [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt] indexes. Under the no-rename rule, keep `ip`.\",\n    \"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message. Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3; Acceptance Criterion 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n      \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; the /account/security UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n      \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1–FR-8.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n      \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1–FR-9.5; Goals 3; Acceptance Criterion 9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n      \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data, final sentence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data + §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery) + §Platform Context 'reuse existing… never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks. Status: PRESENT (migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from a test-only DB helper or the EmailOutbox (MISSING). Status: the unit tests exist. The integration tests and Playwright auth specs are MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, that is a blocker; do not guess. Toasts use useToast() (Snackbar+Alert).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 1, 2, 5, 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 3, 6; Fixed technology decisions 'Theming'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers, response shape)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope; §Platform Context intro\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Only invited users can sign in. There is no public sign-up route or UI.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Goals 1; §Background\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Browser support: the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari. English-only UI.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints (Assumptions)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 97,\n  \"confidenceMethod\": \"HIGH=100, MEDIUM=70, LOW=40, averaged over 49 requirements (45 HIGH, 3 MEDIUM, 1 LOW).\",\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-32: Should AuditLog keep its existing `ip` column (and its existing indexes), or be renamed to `ipAddress` as in the PRD FR-1 snippet?\",\n        \"FR-30/FR-31: Since PRD-04 already enqueues auth emails into EmailOutbox, is it correct that the seed logs the invite link directly via logger and the PRD's interim logger stub is not restored?\",\n        \"Ticket id: is SH-1 (pipeline) the canonical id for SCH-001 (PRD)?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-32: no interactive answer is available. Default: keep `ip` and the existing indexes (no-rename rule).\",\n        \"FR-30/FR-31: no answer. Default: keep the PRD-04 enqueue behaviour; the seed logs the link (already implemented).\",\n        \"Ticket id: no answer. Default: SH-1.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GGxkwKGcd2cQ9dqSbuJTVA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm86XEu7xAhjWBajYiZx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WCAa7ueusfEjgvQkku1hxi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-7 — User Stories (PRD-07: Attendance Tracking)\n\n> Brownfield note: the workspace has no attendance code yet. Reuse `getScheduleForDate`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `assertCanManageCourse`,\n> `assertCanViewStudent`, `audit()`, `toCsv()`, `getSchoolSettings`/`updateSchoolSettings` and the shared components in `src/components/<Name>/`.\n> No school settings page exists yet (see FR-5). See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Teacher register\n\n- **US-1** (FR-6, FR-7, FR-34): As a **teacher**, I want my current class's register to open in one tap from `/attendance/take` so that I can take attendance at the start of the lesson.\n- **US-2** (FR-9, FR-11, FR-13, FR-17): As a **teacher**, I want to mark everyone present at once on my phone and then change the exceptions so that a 30-student class takes under 30 seconds.\n- **US-3** (FR-12): As a **teacher**, I want to record minutes late (default 5) and an optional note per student so that the record is precise.\n- **US-4** (FR-14, FR-1–FR-3): As a **teacher**, I want saving to be all-or-nothing and to show who last changed the register so that the record is trustworthy.\n- **US-5** (FR-8): As a **teacher**, I want to open registers from the last 14 days (admins: any past date) so that I can catch up on a missed register. Future dates are refused.\n- **US-6** (FR-15, FR-16, FR-7): As a **homeroom teacher**, I want a daily register for my section when the school uses daily mode so that I can take whole-day attendance.\n\n## Corrections & audit\n\n- **US-7** (FR-18, FR-19): As a **teacher**, I want to correct a mark later with a note, within 14 days of the date, so that the record stays accurate. Every change is audited with the old and new status.\n- **US-8** (FR-10, FR-19): As an **admin**, I want to edit any register at any time and to mark students EXCUSED so that the office can fix older records.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21, FR-22): As a **parent**, I want to be notified when my child is marked absent or late, and when an absence is corrected to present, so that I can react immediately. I never get duplicate notifications for the same register.\n- **US-10** (FR-31, FR-23): As a **teacher**, I want a reminder when an admin sees my register is missing so that I can take it.\n\n## History & reports\n\n- **US-11** (FR-24–FR-28): As a **student or parent**, I want to see attendance history (term and year rates, a coloured calendar and a records table) so that we can track punctuality. Teacher notes stay hidden from me.\n- **US-12** (FR-29): As a **teacher**, I want a course attendance matrix of the last 20 sessions with per-student rates so that I can spot patterns and jump into any register.\n- **US-13** (FR-30, FR-31): As an **admin**, I want a today overview of registers taken vs expected and a list of missing ones so that I can follow up the same day.\n- **US-14** (FR-32): As an **admin**, I want to filter attendance by date range, grade, section, course and status and export it as CSV so that I can report externally.\n- **US-15** (FR-33, FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want a list of students below a configurable threshold (default 90%) so that I can act on chronic absence.\n- **US-16** (FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want to choose the attendance mode (per period, daily homeroom or both) so that the system matches how my school works.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-17** (FR-38): As a **developer/demo user**, I want deterministic seeded attendance for 7A/7B over the last 15 teaching days, including two students below 85%, so that every screen has realistic data.\n- **US-18** (FR-39–FR-41): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and mobile Playwright tests for the rules above so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** Performance: a 35-student save takes under 500 ms; the yearly tab with 1,200 records loads in under 400 ms.\n- **NFR-2** Reliability: unsaved marks are kept in `localStorage` and the next open offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\".\n- **NFR-3** Integrity: only students with an ACTIVE enrollment on the date (or section members) can be saved; anything else returns `VALIDATION_ERROR`.\n- **NFR-4** Speed goal: a 30-student register takes under 30 s on a phone.\n- **NFR-5** Absence notifications arrive within 5 minutes (in-app immediately, email queued).\n- **NFR-6** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via `mui-mcp` first; banned libraries are forbidden. An unreachable MCP server is a blocker.\n- **NFR-7** Server-side access checks everywhere, matching the role visibility rules.\n- **NFR-8** Platform conventions: response/error shapes, pagination, cuid, `@db.Date`, school timezone, `logger`, `audit()`.\n- **NFR-9** Accessibility: screen-reader labels on the toggles and 44×44 px touch targets.\n- **NFR-10** Brownfield safety: reuse what exists, no renames, keep tests green, and stay out of PRD-14/PRD-15 scope.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148,"cache_read_input_tokens":48174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":148},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57a4dc66-5d3c-4bfa-a9bb-908be3700630","uuid":"07577378-2db9-4874-afcf-abe1ebe4d2cc","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:30:23.198Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm86X2kECpwQmavw6diL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WCAa7ueusfEjgvQkku1hxi":{"file_path":"/Users/ikra