m teacher**, I want a daily register for my section when the school uses daily mode so that I can take whole-day attendance.\n\n## Corrections & audit\n\n- **US-7** (FR-18, FR-19): As a **teacher**, I want to correct a mark later with a note, within 14 days of the date, so that the record stays accurate. Every change is audited with the old and new status.\n- **US-8** (FR-10, FR-19): As an **admin**, I want to edit any register at any time and to mark students EXCUSED so that the office can fix older records.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21, FR-22): As a **parent**, I want to be notified when my child is marked absent or late, and when an absence is corrected to present, so that I can react immediately. I never get duplicate notifications for the same register.\n- **US-10** (FR-31, FR-23): As a **teacher**, I want a reminder when an admin sees my register is missing so that I can take it.\n\n## History & reports\n\n- **US-11** (FR-24–FR-28): As a **student or parent**, I want to see attendance history (term and year rates, a coloured calendar and a records table) so that we can track punctuality. Teacher notes stay hidden from me.\n- **US-12** (FR-29): As a **teacher**, I want a course attendance matrix of the last 20 sessions with per-student rates so that I can spot patterns and jump into any register.\n- **US-13** (FR-30, FR-31): As an **admin**, I want a today overview of registers taken vs expected and a list of missing ones so that I can follow up the same day.\n- **US-14** (FR-32): As an **admin**, I want to filter attendance by date range, grade, section, course and status and export it as CSV so that I can report externally.\n- **US-15** (FR-33, FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want a list of students below a configurable threshold (default 90%) so that I can act on chronic absence.\n- **US-16** (FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want to choose the attendance mode (per period, daily homeroom or both) so that the system matches how my school works.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-17** (FR-38): As a **developer/demo user**, I want deterministic seeded attendance for 7A/7B over the last 15 teaching days, including two students below 85%, so that every screen has realistic data.\n- **US-18** (FR-39–FR-41): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and mobile Playwright tests for the rules above so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** Performance: a 35-student save takes under 500 ms; the yearly tab with 1,200 records loads in under 400 ms.\n- **NFR-2** Reliability: unsaved marks are kept in `localStorage` and the next open offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\".\n- **NFR-3** Integrity: only students with an ACTIVE enrollment on the date (or section members) can be saved; anything else returns `VALIDATION_ERROR`.\n- **NFR-4** Speed goal: a 30-student register takes under 30 s on a phone.\n- **NFR-5** Absence notifications arrive within 5 minutes (in-app immediately, email queued).\n- **NFR-6** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via `mui-mcp` first; banned libraries are forbidden. An unreachable MCP server is a blocker.\n- **NFR-7** Server-side access checks everywhere, matching the role visibility rules.\n- **NFR-8** Platform conventions: response/error shapes, pagination, cuid, `@db.Date`, school timezone, `logger`, `audit()`.\n- **NFR-9** Accessibility: screen-reader labels on the toggles and 44×44 px touch targets.\n- **NFR-10** Brownfield safety: reuse what exists, no renames, keep tests green, and stay out of PRD-14/PRD-15 scope.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":63,"newStart":1,"newLines":51,"lines":["-# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)","+# SH-7 — User Stories (PRD-07: Attendance Tracking)"," ","-> Brownfield note (re-checked 2026-11-05): the backend, the `/login` page, the seed users and the `@@index([role, status])` migration already exist.","-> Remaining: the `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]` and `/account/security` pages; removing PLACEHOLDER_USER from","-> `shell.tsx` (session user, role badge, initials, Sign out, \"Account security\" item); and the integration and Playwright auth tests.","-> Reuse `TextFormField`, `PasswordChecklist`/`passwordInputSlot` and `useToast`. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.","+> Brownfield note: the workspace has no attendance code yet. Reuse `getScheduleForDate`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `assertCanManageCourse`,","+> `assertCanViewStudent`, `audit()`, `toCsv()`, `getSchoolSettings`/`updateSchoolSettings` and the shared components in `src/components/<Name>/`.","+> No school settings page exists yet (see FR-5). See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`."," ","-## Sign-in & session","+## Teacher register"," ","-- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.","-- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"","-- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.","-- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"","-- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.","+- **US-1** (FR-6, FR-7, FR-34): As a **teacher**, I want my current class's register to open in one tap from `/attendance/take` so that I can take attendance at the start of the lesson.","+- **US-2** (FR-9, FR-11, FR-13, FR-17): As a **teacher**, I want to mark everyone present at once on my phone and then change the exceptions so that a 30-student class takes under 30 seconds.","+- **US-3** (FR-12): As a **teacher**, I want to record minutes late (default 5) and an optional note per student so that the record is precise.","+- **US-4** (FR-14, FR-1–FR-3): As a **teacher**, I want saving to be all-or-nothing and to show who last changed the register so that the record is trustworthy.","+- **US-5** (FR-8): As a **teacher**, I want to open registers from the last 14 days (admins: any past date) so that I can catch up on a missed register. Future dates are refused.","+- **US-6** (FR-15, FR-16, FR-7): As a **homeroom teacher**, I want a daily register for my section when the school uses daily mode so that I can take whole-day attendance."," ","-## Invitation","+## Corrections & audit"," ","-- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.","+- **US-7** (FR-18, FR-19): As a **teacher**, I want to correct a mark later with a note, within 14 days of the date, so that the record stays accurate. Every change is audited with the old and new status.","+- **US-8** (FR-10, FR-19): As an **admin**, I want to edit any register at any time and to mark students EXCUSED so that the office can fix older records."," ","-## Password reset & change","+## Notifications"," ","-- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.","-- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.","-- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.","+- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21, FR-22): As a **parent**, I want to be notified when my child is marked absent or late, and when an absence is corrected to present, so that I can react immediately. I never get duplicate notifications for the same register.","+- **US-10** (FR-31, FR-23): As a **teacher**, I want a reminder when an admin sees my register is missing so that I can take it."," ","-## App shell & permissions","+## History & reports"," ","-- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.","-- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.","-- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.","+- **US-11** (FR-24–FR-28): As a **student or parent**, I want to see attendance history (term and year rates, a coloured calendar and a records table) so that we can track punctuality. Teacher notes stay hidden from me.","+- **US-12** (FR-29): As a **teacher**, I want a course attendance matrix of the last 20 sessions with per-student rates so that I can spot patterns and jump into any register.","+- **US-13** (FR-30, FR-31): As an **admin**, I want a today overview of registers taken vs expected and a list of missing ones so that I can follow up the same day.","+- **US-14** (FR-32): As an **admin**, I want to filter attendance by date range, grade, section, course and status and export it as CSV so that I can report externally.","+- **US-15** (FR-33, FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want a list of students below a configurable threshold (default 90%) so that I can act on chronic absence.","+- **US-16** (FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want to choose the attendance mode (per period, daily homeroom or both) so that the system matches how my school works."," ","-## Audit","-","-- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents.","-"," ## Seed & tests"," ","-- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.","-- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.","+- **US-17** (FR-38): As a **developer/demo user**, I want deterministic seeded attendance for 7A/7B over the last 15 teaching days, including two students below 85%, so that every screen has realistic data.","+- **US-18** (FR-39–FR-41): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and mobile Playwright tests for the rules above so that regressions are caught."," ","-## Data model","-","-- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (including `@@index([role, status])`, now migrated) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.","-"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-| ID | Requirement |","-|---|---|","-| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |","-| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |","-| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |","-| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |","-| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |","-| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |","-| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |","-| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |","-| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |","-| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |","-| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |","-| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |","-| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |","-| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |","-| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |","+- **NFR-1** Performance: a 35-student save takes under 500 ms; the yearly tab with 1,200 records loads in under 400 ms.","+- **NFR-2** Reliability: unsaved marks are kept in `localStorage` and the next open offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\".","+- **NFR-3** Integrity: only students with an ACTIVE enrollment on the date (or section members) can be saved; anything else returns `VALIDATION_ERROR`.","+- **NFR-4** Speed goal: a 30-student register takes under 30 s on a phone.","+- **NFR-5** Absence notifications arrive within 5 minutes (in-app immediately, email queued).","+- **NFR-6** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via `mui-mcp` first; banned libraries are forbidden. An unreachable MCP server is a blocker.","+- **NFR-7** Server-side access checks everywhere, matching the role visibility rules.","+- **NFR-8** Platform conventions: response/error shapes, pagination, cuid, `@db.Date`, school timezone, `logger`, `audit()`.","+- **NFR-9** Accessibility: screen-reader labels on the toggles and 44×44 px touch targets.","+- **NFR-10** Brownfield safety: reuse what exists, no renames, keep tests green, and stay out of PRD-14/PRD-15 scope."]}],"originalFile":"# SH-1 — User Stories (PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n> Brownfield note (re-checked 2026-11-05): the backend, the `/login` page, the seed users and the `@@index([role, status])` migration already exist.\n> Remaining: the `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]` and `/account/security` pages; removing PLACEHOLDER_USER from\n> `shell.tsx` (session user, role badge, initials, Sign out, \"Account security\" item); and the integration and Playwright auth tests.\n> Reuse `TextFormField`, `PasswordChecklist`/`passwordInputSlot` and `useToast`. See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Sign-in & session\n\n- **US-1** (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-7, FR-9): As a **user**, I want to sign in with my email and password so that I can see my information. If my callbackUrl is safe I go there, otherwise I land on `/dashboard`.\n- **US-2** (FR-4): As an **invited or disabled user**, I want a clear, non-revealing message when sign-in is refused so that I know what to do. The message is \"Email or password is incorrect.\" or \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\"\n- **US-3** (FR-5, FR-8): As an **admin**, I want accounts to lock for 15 minutes after 5 failed sign-ins so that passwords cannot be brute-forced. Lockouts are audited as `auth.lockout`.\n- **US-4** (FR-6): As an **admin**, I want sign-in limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes so that automated attacks are throttled. The user sees \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"\n- **US-5** (FR-10, FR-11): As a **user**, I want my other devices signed out within 5 minutes of a password change, and unauthenticated access redirected to `/login` (pages) or answered with `401` (API), so that my account stays secure.\n\n## Invitation\n\n- **US-6** (FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16): As an **invited user**, I want to set my own password from an invitation link so that I can access SchoolHub. The page shows my name and email read-only and a live password checklist. Afterwards I am signed in and the link stops working.\n\n## Password reset & change\n\n- **US-7** (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-16): As a **user who forgot my password**, I want to reset it with an emailed link (valid 60 minutes) so that I can regain access. The request page never reveals whether an account exists.\n- **US-8** (FR-15): As a **user**, I want weak and common passwords rejected (10–128 characters, a letter and a digit, not my email, not in the common-password list) so that my account is hard to guess.\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21): As a **signed-in user**, I want to change my password at `/account/security`, reached from \"Account security\" in the user menu, so that I can keep my account secure.\n\n## App shell & permissions\n\n- **US-10** (FR-25, FR-26, FR-27): As a **signed-in user**, I want the top bar to show my real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar to show only my role's items, and \"Sign out\" to return me to `/login`.\n- **US-11** (FR-23): As a **developer of later PRDs**, I want one-line `requireUser()` / `requireRole(...roles)` checks so that handlers and pages are restricted on the server.\n- **US-12** (FR-22): As a **developer of PRD-03**, I want `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus` and `unlockUser` service functions so that the admin user screens can be built on them.\n\n## Audit\n\n- **US-13** (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19, FR-24, FR-32): As an **admin**, I want a record of security-relevant actions (login success/failure, lockout, invite accepted, password reset), including actor and IP, so that I can investigate incidents.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-14** (FR-28, FR-29, FR-30): As a **developer/tester**, I want seeded ACTIVE users for each role (password `SchoolHub123!`) and one INVITED user whose invite link is logged, so that I can exercise every flow locally.\n- **US-15** (FR-34): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and Playwright tests for the auth flows so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Data model\n\n- **US-16** (FR-1, FR-33, FR-31): As a **developer**, I want the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models (including `@@index([role, status])`, now migrated) and PRD-04's EmailOutbox-backed `sendAuthEmail()` kept intact.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Only SHA-256 token hashes are stored, and they are compared in constant time |\n| NFR-2 | Cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production and SameSite=Lax; Auth.js CSRF protection on every auth form |\n| NFR-3 | A dummy bcrypt compare keeps \"no such user\" and \"wrong password\" response times similar |\n| NFR-4 | Sign-in p95 under 1 second on local hardware (bcrypt cost 12) |\n| NFR-5 | Form errors announced with `aria-live=\"polite\"`; focus moves to the first invalid field |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs`) before use; MCP unreachable = blocker |\n| NFR-7 | No banned UI or styling libraries; QA verifies imports |\n| NFR-8 | No password hashes, raw tokens or passwords in audit metadata |\n| NFR-9 | Server-side enforcement on every handler and page |\n| NFR-10 | Thin Zod handlers, standard response envelope and error codes |\n| NFR-11 | React Hook Form + zodResolver with the shared `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas |\n| NFR-12 | No `console.log`; use `logger` |\n| NFR-13 | No scope creep; don't touch course-access.ts or student-access.ts; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | No public sign-up |\n| NFR-15 | Evergreen browsers (last 2 versions); English-only UI |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WCAa7ueusfEjgvQkku1hxi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
