{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8DL2QRwVb7QwikNzT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake for SH-7 is done and the hand-off to the Architect is written. I pulled out 51 requirements (41 functional, 10 non-functional) at 94% overall confidence. All four JSON files load and carry ticket id SH-7. The old files in `artifacts/intake/` belonged to SH-1 and have been overwritten.\n\n**What I found in the codebase:**\n- **No attendance code exists yet.** There are no attendance models, routes, pages or tests, so this is all new work inside an existing project.\n- **The helpers it needs are already there:** `getScheduleForDate`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `audit()`, `toCsv()`, `getSchoolSettings` and `updateSchoolSettings`.\n- **The shared components are in a different folder than the PRD says.** They live in `src/components/<Name>/`, not `src/components/shared/`. I noted this so they get reused, not moved or copied.\n- **No new packages are needed.** Everything is installed: MUI X DataGrid, the date pickers and charts at 9.5.0, plus date-fns and papaparse.\n\n**Three gaps I filled with defaults and flagged for the Architect:**\n- **School settings page (medium confidence):** the PRD says admins pick the attendance mode on the school settings page, but no such page exists and `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty. Default: a small attendance-settings card plus an update route that uses `updateSchoolSettings()`.\n- **Daily register page address (low confidence):** the PRD doesn't give one for homeroom registers. Default: `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=`, reusing the course register screen.\n- **Settings for two notification types (low confidence):** the PRD doesn't say who gets `attendance.corrected` and `attendance.register_missing`, or whether they send email. Default: both under the Attendance category with email off. Corrections go to students and parents, missing-register reminders to the teacher.\n\nDev must reach the MUI docs server (`mui-mcp`) before building any screens; the PRD makes that a hard blocker. There's no Figma link in the PRD, so I didn't create a `figma-readiness.json`.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/intake/`:\n- `requirements.json`\n- `user-stories.md`\n- `tech-stack.json`\n- `handoff-to-architect.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":60208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":344},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"57a4dc66-5d3c-4bfa-a9bb-908be3700630","uuid":"cff51d6c-005a-4ed4-8ebd-4a870f5ecfec","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:30:44.063Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8DKp12qhtvUJzp7yAa"}
