{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnArmnDmHEYSmRwTo2CS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0124cH1vLk1hxAnTcd17XhhJ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-08: File Storage & Course Content (Modules and Lessons) (SCH-008)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-8 and the PRD header says SCH-008. All artifacts use SH-8. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-7 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no file storage or course content code yet. There are no FileObject/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress models, no ContentStatus enum, no src/server/storage.ts, no src/server/files/, no content routes or pages, and no UPLOAD_DIR/MAX_UPLOAD_MB entries in .env.example.\",\n    \"MISSING DEPENDENCIES: the PRD needs file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable, and none of them are in package.json. @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 is installed. All of these are on the PRD's allowed list of non-visual libraries.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse()/assertCanManageCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts, assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts, and requireUser()/requireRole() in src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) in src/server/rate-limit.ts (a per-process sliding window) for the 60 uploads/hour limit. audit() comes from src/server/audit.ts, notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts, and the type keys live in NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: the course tab registry src/config/course-tabs.ts (currently overview, roster and attendance) and the student tab registry src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently courses and attendance). The 'Content' and 'Learning' tabs are added there.\",\n    \"DAILY MAINTENANCE HOOK: PRD-04's 'daily maintenance run' is the once-per-day purgeOldNotifications() call inside src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, which is gated by an in-memory lastPurgeAt. purgeOrphanFiles() should be called next to it.\",\n    \"LOGO: SchoolSettings.logoUrl (String?) is in prisma/schema.prisma:195 and in UpdateSchoolSettingsInput (src/server/services/settings.ts), the email BaseLayout and render.ts use it, and PATCH /api/settings/school exists. However, there is NO /admin/settings/school page in src/app/(app)/admin/, so FR-9's 'replace the logo URL field' has no field to replace.\",\n    \"SHARED COMPONENTS: they live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, FormField, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker...), not in src/components/shared/. New shared components (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView) should follow the existing src/components/<Name>/ layout.\",\n    \"No .gitignore was found at the workspace root. UPLOAD_DIR (./uploads) must be git-ignored, so either create one or add the entry if a .gitignore exists elsewhere.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when one of their linked students is enrolled in it. This relies on the existing assertCanViewCourse behaviour, and the tab is extended to PARENT if the current course-access rule excludes parents.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-46\", \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-47\", \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-48\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Security); FR-1.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 requires intake to record it)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (timestamps); FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions; Fixed technology decisions (.env.example)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-42: /admin/settings/school (said to come from PRD-02) does not exist in the workspace. Should intake create a minimal school settings page to host the logo upload?\",\n        \"FR-6: How should txt/csv (no magic number) and docx/xlsx/pptx (sniff as zip) pass magic-number validation?\",\n        \"FR-40: Should SchoolSettings.logoUrl store '/api/files/<id>', or should a new logoFileId column be added?\",\n        \"FR-37: Does the existing assertCanViewCourse allow PARENT for courses of linked students?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-42 default: create a minimal ADMIN /admin/settings/school page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school.\",\n        \"FR-6 default: accept text types when no signature is detected, accept OOXML when the sniffed type is zip or the matching OOXML mime, and reject everything else that mismatches.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: store '/api/files/<id>' in the existing logoUrl column, with no schema change. Email templates then need an absolute URL (APP_URL prefix).\",\n        \"FR-37 default: the architect verifies course-access.ts and extends the view check to linked parents if it is missing.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":44673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":623},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c329f7d-691a-4a75-afbf-a9bd625b840d","uuid":"68ca4dea-0442-49ce-89d5-59880e11091f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:47:04.407Z","request_id":"req_011CgnArmb4gCB5c24ygen4y","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0124cH1vLk1hxAnTcd17XhhJ":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-08: File Storage & Course Content (Modules and Lessons) (SCH-008)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-8 and the PRD header says SCH-008. All artifacts use SH-8. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-7 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no file storage or course content code yet. There are no FileObject/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress models, no ContentStatus enum, no src/server/storage.ts, no src/server/files/, no content routes or pages, and no UPLOAD_DIR/MAX_UPLOAD_MB entries in .env.example.\",\n    \"MISSING DEPENDENCIES: the PRD needs file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable, and none of them are in package.json. @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 is installed. All of these are on the PRD's allowed list of non-visual libraries.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse()/assertCanManageCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts, assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts, and requireUser()/requireRole() in src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) in src/server/rate-limit.ts (a per-process sliding window) for the 60 uploads/hour limit. audit() comes from src/server/audit.ts, notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts, and the type keys live in NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: the course tab registry src/config/course-tabs.ts (currently overview, roster and attendance) and the student tab registry src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently courses and attendance). The 'Content' and 'Learning' tabs are added there.\",\n    \"DAILY MAINTENANCE HOOK: PRD-04's 'daily maintenance run' is the once-per-day purgeOldNotifications() call inside src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, which is gated by an in-memory lastPurgeAt. purgeOrphanFiles() should be called next to it.\",\n    \"LOGO: SchoolSettings.logoUrl (String?) is in prisma/schema.prisma:195 and in UpdateSchoolSettingsInput (src/server/services/settings.ts), the email BaseLayout and render.ts use it, and PATCH /api/settings/school exists. However, there is NO /admin/settings/school page in src/app/(app)/admin/, so FR-9's 'replace the logo URL field' has no field to replace.\",\n    \"SHARED COMPONENTS: they live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, FormField, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker...), not in src/components/shared/. New shared components (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView) should follow the existing src/components/<Name>/ layout.\",\n    \"No .gitignore was found at the workspace root. UPLOAD_DIR (./uploads) must be git-ignored, so either create one or add the entry if a .gitignore exists elsewhere.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when one of their linked students is enrolled in it. This relies on the existing assertCanViewCourse behaviour, and the tab is extended to PARENT if the current course-access rule excludes parents.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-46\", \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-47\", \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-48\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Security); FR-1.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 requires intake to record it)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (timestamps); FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions; Fixed technology decisions (.env.example)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-42: /admin/settings/school (said to come from PRD-02) does not exist in the workspace. Should intake create a minimal school settings page to host the logo upload?\",\n        \"FR-6: How should txt/csv (no magic number) and docx/xlsx/pptx (sniff as zip) pass magic-number validation?\",\n        \"FR-40: Should SchoolSettings.logoUrl store '/api/files/<id>', or should a new logoFileId column be added?\",\n        \"FR-37: Does the existing assertCanViewCourse allow PARENT for courses of linked students?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-42 default: create a minimal ADMIN /admin/settings/school page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school.\",\n        \"FR-6 default: accept text types when no signature is detected, accept OOXML when the sniffed type is zip or the matching OOXML mime, and reject everything else that mismatches.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: store '/api/files/<id>' in the existing logoUrl column, with no schema change. Email templates then need an absolute URL (APP_URL prefix).\",\n        \"FR-37 default: the architect verifies course-access.ts and extends the view check to linked parents if it is missing.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0124cH1vLk1hxAnTcd17XhhJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c329f7d-691a-4a75-afbf-a9bd625b840d","uuid":"5d572530-c7e9-4439-b719-c0aa2510b3d5","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:47:04.688Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-08: File Storage & Course Content (Modules and Lessons) (SCH-008)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-8 and the PRD header says SCH-008. All artifacts use SH-8. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-7 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no file storage or course content code yet. There are no FileObject/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress models, no ContentStatus enum, no src/server/storage.ts, no src/server/files/, no content routes or pages, and no UPLOAD_DIR/MAX_UPLOAD_MB entries in .env.example.\",\n    \"MISSING DEPENDENCIES: the PRD needs file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable, and none of them are in package.json. @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 is installed. All of these are on the PRD's allowed list of non-visual libraries.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse()/assertCanManageCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts, assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts, and requireUser()/requireRole() in src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) in src/server/rate-limit.ts (a per-process sliding window) for the 60 uploads/hour limit. audit() comes from src/server/audit.ts, notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts, and the type keys live in NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: the course tab registry src/config/course-tabs.ts (currently overview, roster and attendance) and the student tab registry src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently courses and attendance). The 'Content' and 'Learning' tabs are added there.\",\n    \"DAILY MAINTENANCE HOOK: PRD-04's 'daily maintenance run' is the once-per-day purgeOldNotifications() call inside src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, which is gated by an in-memory lastPurgeAt. purgeOrphanFiles() should be called next to it.\",\n    \"LOGO: SchoolSettings.logoUrl (String?) is in prisma/schema.prisma:195 and in UpdateSchoolSettingsInput (src/server/services/settings.ts), the email BaseLayout and render.ts use it, and PATCH /api/settings/school exists. However, there is NO /admin/settings/school page in src/app/(app)/admin/, so FR-9's 'replace the logo URL field' has no field to replace.\",\n    \"SHARED COMPONENTS: they live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, FormField, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker...), not in src/components/shared/. New shared components (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView) should follow the existing src/components/<Name>/ layout.\",\n    \"No .gitignore was found at the workspace root. UPLOAD_DIR (./uploads) must be git-ignored, so either create one or add the entry if a .gitignore exists elsewhere.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when one of their linked students is enrolled in it. This relies on the existing assertCanViewCourse behaviour, and the tab is extended to PARENT if the current course-access rule excludes parents.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-46\", \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-47\", \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-48\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Security); FR-1.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 requires intake to record it)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Assumptions and constraints\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (timestamps); FR-5.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions; Fixed technology decisions (.env.example)\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-42: /admin/settings/school (said to come from PRD-02) does not exist in the workspace. Should intake create a minimal school settings page to host the logo upload?\",\n        \"FR-6: How should txt/csv (no magic number) and docx/xlsx/pptx (sniff as zip) pass magic-number validation?\",\n        \"FR-40: Should SchoolSettings.logoUrl store '/api/files/<id>', or should a new logoFileId column be added?\",\n        \"FR-37: Does the existing assertCanViewCourse allow PARENT for courses of linked students?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-42 default: create a minimal ADMIN /admin/settings/school page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school.\",\n        \"FR-6 default: accept text types when no signature is detected, accept OOXML when the sniffed type is zip or the matching OOXML mime, and reject everything else that mismatches.\",\n        \"FR-40 default: store '/api/files/<id>' in the existing logoUrl column, with no schema change. Email templates then need an absolute URL (APP_URL prefix).\",\n        \"FR-37 default: the architect verifies course-access.ts and extends the view check to linked parents if it is missing.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":94,"newStart":1,"newLines":101,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","-  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",","+  \"prd\": \"PRD-08: File Storage & Course Content (Modules and Lessons) (SCH-008)\",","   \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",","   \"brownfieldFindings\": [","-    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",","-    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",","-    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",","-    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",","-    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",","-    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",","-    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",","-    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",","-    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",","-    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",","-    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",","-    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"","+    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-8 and the PRD header says SCH-008. All artifacts use SH-8. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-7 and are overwritten.\",","+    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no file storage or course content code yet. There are no FileObject/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress models, no ContentStatus enum, no src/server/storage.ts, no src/server/files/, no content routes or pages, and no UPLOAD_DIR/MAX_UPLOAD_MB entries in .env.example.\",","+    \"MISSING DEPENDENCIES: the PRD needs file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable, and none of them are in package.json. @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 is installed. All of these are on the PRD's allowed list of non-visual libraries.\",","+    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse()/assertCanManageCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts, assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts, and requireUser()/requireRole() in src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",","+    \"REUSE: rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) in src/server/rate-limit.ts (a per-process sliding window) for the 60 uploads/hour limit. audit() comes from src/server/audit.ts, notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts, and the type keys live in NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",","+    \"REUSE: the course tab registry src/config/course-tabs.ts (currently overview, roster and attendance) and the student tab registry src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently courses and attendance). The 'Content' and 'Learning' tabs are added there.\",","+    \"DAILY MAINTENANCE HOOK: PRD-04's 'daily maintenance run' is the once-per-day purgeOldNotifications() call inside src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, which is gated by an in-memory lastPurgeAt. purgeOrphanFiles() should be called next to it.\",","+    \"LOGO: SchoolSettings.logoUrl (String?) is in prisma/schema.prisma:195 and in UpdateSchoolSettingsInput (src/server/services/settings.ts), the email BaseLayout and render.ts use it, and PATCH /api/settings/school exists. However, there is NO /admin/settings/school page in src/app/(app)/admin/, so FR-9's 'replace the logo URL field' has no field to replace.\",","+    \"SHARED COMPONENTS: they live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, FormField, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker...), not in src/components/shared/. New shared components (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView) should follow the existing src/components/<Name>/ layout.\",","+    \"No .gitignore was found at the workspace root. UPLOAD_DIR (./uploads) must be git-ignored, so either create one or add the entry if a .gitignore exists elsewhere.\"","   ],","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },","-    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }","+    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1.6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when one of their linked students is enrolled in it. This relies on the existing assertCanViewCourse behaviour, and the tab is extended to PARENT if the current course-access rule excludes parents.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-43\", \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-44\", \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-45\", \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON).\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-46\", \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-47\", \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" },","+    { \"id\": \"FR-48\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" }","   ],","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },","-    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Security); FR-1.1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1; Acceptance Criterion 6\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Performance)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 requires intake to record it)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts)\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Assumptions and constraints\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (timestamps); FR-5.3\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope\" },","+    { \"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions; Fixed technology decisions (.env.example)\" }","   ],","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",","-        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",","-        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",","-        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",","-        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"","+        \"FR-42: /admin/settings/school (said to come from PRD-02) does not exist in the workspace. Should intake create a minimal school settings page to host the logo upload?\",","+        \"FR-6: How should txt/csv (no magic number) and docx/xlsx/pptx (sniff as zip) pass magic-number validation?\",","+        \"FR-40: Should SchoolSettings.logoUrl store '/api/files/<id>', or should a new logoFileId column be added?\",","+        \"FR-37: Does the existing assertCanViewCourse allow PARENT for courses of linked students?\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",","-        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",","-        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"","+        \"FR-42 default: create a minimal ADMIN /admin/settings/school page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school.\",","+        \"FR-6 default: accept text types when no signature is detected, accept OOXML when the sniffed type is zip or the matching OOXML mime, and reject everything else that mismatches.\",","+        \"FR-40 default: store '/api/files/<id>' in the existing logoUrl column, with no schema change. Email templates then need an absolute URL (APP_URL prefix).\",","+        \"FR-37 default: the architect verifies course-access.ts and extends the view check to linked parents if it is missing.\"","       ]","     }","   ],"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T05:29:02Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-07: Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-7 and the PRD header says SCH-007. All artifacts use SH-7. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-1 and are overwritten.\",\n    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no attendance code yet. There are no AttendanceSession/AttendanceRecord models, no AttendanceStatus enum, no attendance routes, pages, services, validators or tests, and no attendance.* notification types. The only mentions are the ATTENDANCE notification category in src/server/notifications/types.ts and a comment in timetable-service.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE (already exported): getScheduleForDate(target, date) and the ScheduleTarget/ScheduleEntry types from src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts (PRD-06 FR-30/31). It returns [] on non-teaching days and has a PRD-14 holiday hook comment.\",\n    \"REUSE: notifyStudentAndParents() and notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts. Both never throw. Register new type keys in the NOTIFICATION_TYPES map in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanManageCourse()/assertCanViewCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts and assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts. requireUser()/requireRole() come from src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE: audit() from src/server/audit.ts, toCsv()/escapeCsvCell() from src/server/csv.ts, the HTTP response helpers in src/server/http.ts, and getSchoolSettings()/updateSchoolSettings() from src/server/services/settings.ts.\",\n    \"REUSE UI: shared components live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast). They are NOT in src/components/shared/ as the PRD says. Reuse them where they are and do not move or duplicate them.\",\n    \"EXTENSION POINTS: src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently only 'courses'), src/config/course-tabs.ts (overview and roster) and src/config/navigation.ts.\",\n    \"DATA MODEL FACTS: Section has homeroomTeacherId and members (SectionMember with studentId, sectionId, academicYearId and joinedAt, unique on [studentId, academicYearId]). Enrollment has status ACTIVE|DROPPED plus enrolledAt and droppedAt, and DROPPED rows are kept. Period has startTime/endTime as strings and an order field. Term has startDate/endDate per academicYear. SchoolSettings is a singleton with a timezone field and no attendanceMode or attendanceAlertThreshold yet.\",\n    \"GAP: there is no school settings page under src/app/(app)/admin, and src/app/api/settings/school/ is an empty directory, although the service has updateSchoolSettings(). FR-2 assumes an existing 'school settings page'. See FR-5 below (MEDIUM).\",\n    \"The latest migration is 20261106000000_user_role_status_index. The new attendance migration must come after it and must include the raw SQL CHECK and the two partial unique indexes.\",\n    \"Installed packages already cover this PRD. @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/material and @mui/icons-material are all 9.5.0, along with date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0 and papaparse. No new dependencies are needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (paragraph after schema)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1, FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1 ('Admin edits it on the school settings page'), FR-8.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"/attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, Out of Scope (PRD-15 EXCUSED workflow)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.5, FR-1 field comments\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.6, AC-5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table (register ?sectionId=), FR-3.1, NFR-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=).\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1 ('Daily register – 7A'), API table — route not specified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.2, AC-4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, AC-3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false.\", \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.3, FR-8.1 — type metadata unspecified\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1, API table, AC-8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2, FR-2.1, AC-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"/admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1, API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.2, Goal 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.3, AC-7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD API table\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Fixed technology decisions (Validation), Code layout\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions (services path)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Seed Data\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Test Requirements\" }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Reliability)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Non-Functional Requirements 3 (Integrity)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Goals 2, AC-2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › UI component rule (items 1–6)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout (requireRole), Roles\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Code layout and conventions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3, FR-3.8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"PRD Platform Context › Assumptions and constraints, Out of Scope\" }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Should a minimal /admin/settings page (or an attendance section on it) be built, given that no school settings page or API route exists? Default: add a small 'Attendance settings' card editing attendanceMode and attendanceAlertThreshold, plus PATCH /api/settings/school built on updateSchoolSettings().\",\n        \"FR-16: Which route should the daily homeroom register use? Default: /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=, reusing the course register component.\",\n        \"FR-23: What metadata should attendance.corrected and attendance.register_missing have? Default: category ATTENDANCE, email false; corrected goes to PARENT+STUDENT, register_missing to TEACHER.\",\n        \"FR-21: The PRD's sample body is 'Mathematics – 7A, Period 1, ...'. For daily registers (no course or period), is '<Section> daily register, <date>' acceptable? Default: yes.\",\n        \"FR-28: Does 'current term' mean the Term whose startDate–endDate contains today in the current AcademicYear? Default: yes. If today falls between terms, use the most recent ended term.\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 school settings page does not exist; proceeding with the default above (MEDIUM).\",\n        \"FR-16 daily register route not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\",\n        \"FR-23 notification metadata for attendance.corrected / attendance.register_missing not specified; proceeding with the default (LOW).\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0124cH1vLk1hxAnTcd17XhhJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
