** As a developer or demo user, I want realistic seed content for MATH-7A and ENG-7A, with Sam having completed 4 lessons, so that the feature is demonstrable.\n- **FR-48:** As a maintainer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the risky logic so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1:** Files are never served statically, and every download is access-checked.\n- **NFR-2:** Markdown is sanitised and `javascript:` URLs are stripped.\n- **NFR-3:** Uploads are limited to 60 per user per hour (reuse `rateLimit()`).\n- **NFR-4:** The Content tab for 20 × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms, with no N+1 queries.\n- **NFR-5:** Uploads stream to disk without whole-file buffering.\n- **NFR-6:** Video iframes have titles, the editor warns on missing alt text, and keyboard reorder alternatives exist.\n- **NFR-7:** The MUI-only UI rule applies: every component is looked up via mui-mcp, banned libraries are never imported, and QA verifies both.\n- **NFR-8:** Access is enforced server-side on every handler and page.\n- **NFR-9:** Brownfield work only: no re-scaffolding, renames or duplicate helpers, existing tests stay green, and new dependencies are limited to the allowed set.\n- **NFR-10:** Times are stored in UTC and displayed and picked in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-11:** Out of scope: S3, SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\n- **NFR-12:** No `console.log` (use `logger`), and `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":51,"newStart":1,"newLines":43,"lines":["-# SH-7 — User Stories (PRD-07: Attendance Tracking)","+# SH-8 — User Stories: File Storage & Course Content (PRD-08 / SCH-008)"," ","-> Brownfield note: the workspace has no attendance code yet. Reuse `getScheduleForDate`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `assertCanManageCourse`,","-> `assertCanViewStudent`, `audit()`, `toCsv()`, `getSchoolSettings`/`updateSchoolSettings` and the shared components in `src/components/<Name>/`.","-> No school settings page exists yet (see FR-5). See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.","+## File storage"," ","-## Teacher register","+- **FR-1, FR-2:** As a platform developer, I want a FileObject record and a local-disk storage module outside `public/` so that every feature stores files the same way.","+- **FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7:** As any signed-in user, I want to upload a file with a context so that I can attach it to content. I want oversize, disallowed or disguised files (e.g. an `.exe` renamed `.pdf`) rejected with a clear message.","+- **FR-8, FR-9, FR-10:** As a user, I want to download a file only if I can see the content it belongs to so that private materials stay private. Logos are public, and unknown contexts are limited to the owner and admins.","+- **FR-11:** As an uploader or admin, I want to delete an unattached file so that mistakes don't linger.","+- **FR-12:** As an operator, I want unattached files older than 24 h purged daily so that disk use stays bounded.","+- **FR-13, FR-14:** As a teacher, I want a drag-and-drop upload widget with per-file progress and a list of attached files so that adding materials is quick."," ","-- **US-1** (FR-6, FR-7, FR-34): As a **teacher**, I want my current class's register to open in one tap from `/attendance/take` so that I can take attendance at the start of the lesson.","-- **US-2** (FR-9, FR-11, FR-13, FR-17): As a **teacher**, I want to mark everyone present at once on my phone and then change the exceptions so that a 30-student class takes under 30 seconds.","-- **US-3** (FR-12): As a **teacher**, I want to record minutes late (default 5) and an optional note per student so that the record is precise.","-- **US-4** (FR-14, FR-1–FR-3): As a **teacher**, I want saving to be all-or-nothing and to show who last changed the register so that the record is trustworthy.","-- **US-5** (FR-8): As a **teacher**, I want to open registers from the last 14 days (admins: any past date) so that I can catch up on a missed register. Future dates are refused.","-- **US-6** (FR-15, FR-16, FR-7): As a **homeroom teacher**, I want a daily register for my section when the school uses daily mode so that I can take whole-day attendance.","+## Course content"," ","-## Corrections & audit","+- **FR-15, FR-16, FR-45:** As a teacher, I want modules containing ordered lessons (Markdown, video, attachments, links) so that content follows my teaching plan.","+- **FR-22, FR-23, FR-24:** As a teacher, I want to create modules, order lessons and drag them within and across modules (with keyboard up/down) so that content follows my teaching plan. I want deleting a non-empty module to require typing its title.","+- **FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-29, FR-30:** As a teacher, I want to write lessons in Markdown with images, attach files, add links and embed a YouTube or Vimeo video, with autosave, so that materials are rich and never lost.","+- **FR-28, FR-39:** As a teacher, I want to save a draft, publish now or schedule a lesson for a future date so that I can prepare ahead.","+- **FR-18, FR-19:** As a teacher or admin, I want to see every module and lesson with a Draft/Scheduled/Published badge. As a student or parent, I want to see only what is published or past its schedule.","+- **FR-20, FR-21:** As a student, I want a Content tab with module and course progress bars and a Continue button so that I always know what is next.","+- **FR-31, FR-32, FR-33:** As a student, I want to read lessons safely rendered, watch videos, download materials, move to the previous or next lesson, and mark lessons complete so that I can track my progress.","+- **FR-34:** As a teacher, I want a Progress panel showing which students viewed or completed each lesson so that I can follow up.","+- **FR-35:** As a student, parent, teacher or admin, I want a Learning tab on the student page showing per-course progress so that learning is visible.","+- **FR-36, FR-37:** As a parent, I want to read my child's course content read-only so that I can support learning at home.","+- **FR-38:** As a student, I want a notification when a teacher publishes a lesson now so that I don't miss new content.","+- **FR-40, FR-41, FR-42:** As an admin, I want to upload the school logo (PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG ≤ 2 MB) instead of typing a URL so that branding is easy, with SVGs served safely.","+- **FR-43, FR-44, FR-46:** As a client developer, I want REST endpoints with consistent access checks, envelopes and audit logging so that the UI and later PRDs can build on them.","+- **FR-47:** As a developer or demo user, I want realistic seed content for MATH-7A and ENG-7A, with Sam having completed 4 lessons, so that the feature is demonstrable.","+- **FR-48:** As a maintainer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the risky logic so that regressions are caught."," ","-- **US-7** (FR-18, FR-19): As a **teacher**, I want to correct a mark later with a note, within 14 days of the date, so that the record stays accurate. Every change is audited with the old and new status.","-- **US-8** (FR-10, FR-19): As an **admin**, I want to edit any register at any time and to mark students EXCUSED so that the office can fix older records.","-","-## Notifications","-","-- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21, FR-22): As a **parent**, I want to be notified when my child is marked absent or late, and when an absence is corrected to present, so that I can react immediately. I never get duplicate notifications for the same register.","-- **US-10** (FR-31, FR-23): As a **teacher**, I want a reminder when an admin sees my register is missing so that I can take it.","-","-## History & reports","-","-- **US-11** (FR-24–FR-28): As a **student or parent**, I want to see attendance history (term and year rates, a coloured calendar and a records table) so that we can track punctuality. Teacher notes stay hidden from me.","-- **US-12** (FR-29): As a **teacher**, I want a course attendance matrix of the last 20 sessions with per-student rates so that I can spot patterns and jump into any register.","-- **US-13** (FR-30, FR-31): As an **admin**, I want a today overview of registers taken vs expected and a list of missing ones so that I can follow up the same day.","-- **US-14** (FR-32): As an **admin**, I want to filter attendance by date range, grade, section, course and status and export it as CSV so that I can report externally.","-- **US-15** (FR-33, FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want a list of students below a configurable threshold (default 90%) so that I can act on chronic absence.","-- **US-16** (FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want to choose the attendance mode (per period, daily homeroom or both) so that the system matches how my school works.","-","-## Seed & tests","-","-- **US-17** (FR-38): As a **developer/demo user**, I want deterministic seeded attendance for 7A/7B over the last 15 teaching days, including two students below 85%, so that every screen has realistic data.","-- **US-18** (FR-39–FR-41): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and mobile Playwright tests for the rules above so that regressions are caught.","-"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **NFR-1** Performance: a 35-student save takes under 500 ms; the yearly tab with 1,200 records loads in under 400 ms.","-- **NFR-2** Reliability: unsaved marks are kept in `localStorage` and the next open offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\".","-- **NFR-3** Integrity: only students with an ACTIVE enrollment on the date (or section members) can be saved; anything else returns `VALIDATION_ERROR`.","-- **NFR-4** Speed goal: a 30-student register takes under 30 s on a phone.","-- **NFR-5** Absence notifications arrive within 5 minutes (in-app immediately, email queued).","-- **NFR-6** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via `mui-mcp` first; banned libraries are forbidden. An unreachable MCP server is a blocker.","-- **NFR-7** Server-side access checks everywhere, matching the role visibility rules.","-- **NFR-8** Platform conventions: response/error shapes, pagination, cuid, `@db.Date`, school timezone, `logger`, `audit()`.","-- **NFR-9** Accessibility: screen-reader labels on the toggles and 44×44 px touch targets.","-- **NFR-10** Brownfield safety: reuse what exists, no renames, keep tests green, and stay out of PRD-14/PRD-15 scope.","+- **NFR-1:** Files are never served statically, and every download is access-checked.","+- **NFR-2:** Markdown is sanitised and `javascript:` URLs are stripped.","+- **NFR-3:** Uploads are limited to 60 per user per hour (reuse `rateLimit()`).","+- **NFR-4:** The Content tab for 20 × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms, with no N+1 queries.","+- **NFR-5:** Uploads stream to disk without whole-file buffering.","+- **NFR-6:** Video iframes have titles, the editor warns on missing alt text, and keyboard reorder alternatives exist.","+- **NFR-7:** The MUI-only UI rule applies: every component is looked up via mui-mcp, banned libraries are never imported, and QA verifies both.","+- **NFR-8:** Access is enforced server-side on every handler and page.","+- **NFR-9:** Brownfield work only: no re-scaffolding, renames or duplicate helpers, existing tests stay green, and new dependencies are limited to the allowed set.","+- **NFR-10:** Times are stored in UTC and displayed and picked in the school timezone.","+- **NFR-11:** Out of scope: S3, SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.","+- **NFR-12:** No `console.log` (use `logger`), and `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`."]}],"originalFile":"# SH-7 — User Stories (PRD-07: Attendance Tracking)\n\n> Brownfield note: the workspace has no attendance code yet. Reuse `getScheduleForDate`, `notifyStudentAndParents`, `assertCanManageCourse`,\n> `assertCanViewStudent`, `audit()`, `toCsv()`, `getSchoolSettings`/`updateSchoolSettings` and the shared components in `src/components/<Name>/`.\n> No school settings page exists yet (see FR-5). See `requirements.json › brownfieldFindings`.\n\n## Teacher register\n\n- **US-1** (FR-6, FR-7, FR-34): As a **teacher**, I want my current class's register to open in one tap from `/attendance/take` so that I can take attendance at the start of the lesson.\n- **US-2** (FR-9, FR-11, FR-13, FR-17): As a **teacher**, I want to mark everyone present at once on my phone and then change the exceptions so that a 30-student class takes under 30 seconds.\n- **US-3** (FR-12): As a **teacher**, I want to record minutes late (default 5) and an optional note per student so that the record is precise.\n- **US-4** (FR-14, FR-1–FR-3): As a **teacher**, I want saving to be all-or-nothing and to show who last changed the register so that the record is trustworthy.\n- **US-5** (FR-8): As a **teacher**, I want to open registers from the last 14 days (admins: any past date) so that I can catch up on a missed register. Future dates are refused.\n- **US-6** (FR-15, FR-16, FR-7): As a **homeroom teacher**, I want a daily register for my section when the school uses daily mode so that I can take whole-day attendance.\n\n## Corrections & audit\n\n- **US-7** (FR-18, FR-19): As a **teacher**, I want to correct a mark later with a note, within 14 days of the date, so that the record stays accurate. Every change is audited with the old and new status.\n- **US-8** (FR-10, FR-19): As an **admin**, I want to edit any register at any time and to mark students EXCUSED so that the office can fix older records.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **US-9** (FR-20, FR-21, FR-22): As a **parent**, I want to be notified when my child is marked absent or late, and when an absence is corrected to present, so that I can react immediately. I never get duplicate notifications for the same register.\n- **US-10** (FR-31, FR-23): As a **teacher**, I want a reminder when an admin sees my register is missing so that I can take it.\n\n## History & reports\n\n- **US-11** (FR-24–FR-28): As a **student or parent**, I want to see attendance history (term and year rates, a coloured calendar and a records table) so that we can track punctuality. Teacher notes stay hidden from me.\n- **US-12** (FR-29): As a **teacher**, I want a course attendance matrix of the last 20 sessions with per-student rates so that I can spot patterns and jump into any register.\n- **US-13** (FR-30, FR-31): As an **admin**, I want a today overview of registers taken vs expected and a list of missing ones so that I can follow up the same day.\n- **US-14** (FR-32): As an **admin**, I want to filter attendance by date range, grade, section, course and status and export it as CSV so that I can report externally.\n- **US-15** (FR-33, FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want a list of students below a configurable threshold (default 90%) so that I can act on chronic absence.\n- **US-16** (FR-4, FR-5): As an **admin**, I want to choose the attendance mode (per period, daily homeroom or both) so that the system matches how my school works.\n\n## Seed & tests\n\n- **US-17** (FR-38): As a **developer/demo user**, I want deterministic seeded attendance for 7A/7B over the last 15 teaching days, including two students below 85%, so that every screen has realistic data.\n- **US-18** (FR-39–FR-41): As a **maintainer**, I want unit, integration and mobile Playwright tests for the rules above so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1** Performance: a 35-student save takes under 500 ms; the yearly tab with 1,200 records loads in under 400 ms.\n- **NFR-2** Reliability: unsaved marks are kept in `localStorage` and the next open offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\".\n- **NFR-3** Integrity: only students with an ACTIVE enrollment on the date (or section members) can be saved; anything else returns `VALIDATION_ERROR`.\n- **NFR-4** Speed goal: a 30-student register takes under 30 s on a phone.\n- **NFR-5** Absence notifications arrive within 5 minutes (in-app immediately, email queued).\n- **NFR-6** MUI-only UI, with every component looked up via `mui-mcp` first; banned libraries are forbidden. An unreachable MCP server is a blocker.\n- **NFR-7** Server-side access checks everywhere, matching the role visibility rules.\n- **NFR-8** Platform conventions: response/error shapes, pagination, cuid, `@db.Date`, school timezone, `logger`, `audit()`.\n- **NFR-9** Accessibility: screen-reader labels on the toggles and 44×44 px touch targets.\n- **NFR-10** Brownfield safety: reuse what exists, no renames, keep tests green, and stay out of PRD-14/PRD-15 scope.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0189hDnMQmQfk6j3cerT1Gzx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnAxtVTJg1khZy7k3BD6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SWyRjExzASS1tLQLDinU5i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -f figma-readiness.json && cat > handoff-to-architect.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 60,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"GREENFIELD within brownfield: there is no file storage or content code yet. Design the FileObject/ContentStatus/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress migration, src/server/storage.ts, src/server/files/ (access registry, purge), src/server/content/content-service.ts, src/lib/validators/content.ts, the 13 API routes, the Content course tab, the lesson editor and viewer pages, the Learning student tab, the FileUpload/FileList/MarkdownView components, seed data plus prisma/seed-assets PDF, and the tests.\",\n    \"NEW DEPS required (all PRD-allowed): file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable.\",\n    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse (already handles PARENT via linked ACTIVE enrollment), assertCanManageCourse, assertCanViewStudent, rateLimit(), audit(), notify() + NOTIFICATION_TYPES, the courseTabs/studentTabs registries, updateSchoolSettings(), and the components in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, PageHeader, Toast/useToast).\",\n    \"FR-12: hook purgeOrphanFiles() into the once-daily purge block in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, next to purgeOldNotifications().\",\n    \"FR-42 (LOW): /admin/settings/school does not exist. Default: create a minimal ADMIN page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school. FR-40 stores '/api/files/<id>' in the existing SchoolSettings.logoUrl, and email templates need an APP_URL-absolute URL.\",\n    \"FR-6 (MEDIUM): define sni