{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QwRUxqSswPaJA6r4U6cpd6","type":"tool_result","content":"# QA Report — SH-8 (PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-8\n- timestamp: 2026-11-07T03:45:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 60\n- requirementsPassed: 21\n- requirementsFailed: 39\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 QA report. Of the 39 failed requirements, 2 are FAIL and 37 are NOT-IMPLEMENTED.\n\n## Headline findings\n\n### 1. BLOCKER: the Dev phase for SH-8 is incomplete, and it left no report\n\n- `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `artifacts/dev/task-completion-markers.json` are still the **SH-7** files. Dev never wrote SH-8 versions.\n- `dev-rerun-count.json` shows `count: 3, firstPassAccepted: false`.\n- `security-scan-report.json` (SH-8) scanned **0 files**.\n- QA therefore checked reality against `file-ownership-matrix.json` (SH-8) directly. **33 of the 66 owned paths are missing on disk.**\n\n### 2. What was built: the file storage backend (TASK-1 to TASK-8, roughly)\n\n- Built:\n  - dependencies, env vars and `.gitignore`\n  - the Prisma models and migration\n  - `storage.ts`\n  - upload validation\n  - the visibility rule and video parser\n  - the access registry and built-in contexts\n  - the files service\n  - the `/api/files` routes\n  - the orphan purge and its maintenance hook\n  - the content Zod validators\n- This code is real (no stubs or TODOs). It typechecks and lints clean, and it passes 40/40 tests, including the 14 QA added.\n\n### 3. What is missing: TASK-10 to TASK-21\n\n- **Server:** the content service, every content/lesson/module/progress/learning API route, and the settings validator.\n- **UI:** every UI component (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, StatusChip, VideoEmbed) and every page (Content tab, lesson viewer and editor, Learning tab, `/admin/settings/school`).\n- **Seed:** the seed content and the seed PDF asset.\n- **Tests:** the Dev-owned integration, Markdown and e2e tests.\n- **Effect:** no course-content feature is usable by any role.\n\n### 4. Pre-existing: `npm test` does not start\n\n- `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js` (MODULE_NOT_FOUND). This was carried over from SH-7 and is not caused by SH-8.\n- All runs used `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.\n\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.\n   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.\n3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.\n4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.\n5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.\n6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T11:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    