{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LS8sjSHVQQNaCfRzi2SEop","type":"tool_result","content":"\"complete\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df495bd9-17af-4404-ad8d-134253d4d6e0","uuid":"3fa5800a-ec10-459c-acf9-d3302b9dda2c","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:22:35.157Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"complete\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LS8sjSHVQQNaCfRzi2SEop","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgro2f5dSkrbiTyHMe3we","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VTwC1Es94eDKB1nut3pL3c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-9 — PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions: User Stories\n\nTicket: SH-9 (PRD header ref SCH-009) · Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react` · Generated by intake on 2026-11-09.\nRequirement ids refer to `requirements.json`. Confidence is shown as [H]/[M]/[L].\n\n## Data & platform\n\n- **FR-1 to FR-6 [H]** — As the platform, I want the Assignment, AssignmentAttachment, Rubric, RubricCriterion, Submission, SubmissionFile, SubmissionHistory, GradeExemption and AssignmentReminder models (plus `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt` and `archivedAt` on Assignment), so that assignment work is stored with full history.\n- **FR-7 [H]** — As a developer, I want shared Zod limits (title ≤150, instructions ≤50k, maxPoints 0–1000, cutoff > due, penalties 0–100, maxFileCount 1–10, text ≤50k, feedback ≤10k), so that the client and server validate the same way.\n- **FR-8 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to record a grade for a student who did not submit (stored as attempt 0), so that offline work is scored.\n\n## Teacher — create & manage\n\n- **FR-9 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to create an assignment with instructions, files, submission type, due date, max points, late policy, file limit, extra-credit flag and optional rubric, so that students know what to do.\n- **FR-10 [M]** — As a teacher, I want the due date to default to the next teaching day at 23:59 (school timezone), so that the common case needs no editing.\n- **FR-11 [H]** — As a teacher, I want an optional rubric builder that warns \"Rubric totals 18 points but the assignment is worth 20.\", so that grading is consistent and transparent.\n- **FR-12, FR-13 [H/M]** — As a teacher, I want to save a draft, publish now, or schedule for a future available-from, so that students see the work only when I intend.\n- **FR-14 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a warning when I change the due date or points after students have submitted, plus a \"review grades\" banner, so that I don't silently invalidate scores.\n- **FR-15 [L]** — As a teacher, I want to duplicate an assignment as a draft into other courses I manage, keeping the same due date, so that parallel classes get the same work.\n- **FR-51, FR-52 [H/L]** — As a teacher, I want deleting an assignment that already has submissions to archive it instead, so that student work is never lost.\n- **FR-16, FR-17 [H]** — As a teacher, I want an Assignments course tab showing title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a Grade button, so that I can see progress at a glance.\n\n## Student — submit\n\n- **FR-18 [H]** — As a student, I want my course's assignments grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned, so that I know what to do next.\n- **FR-19 [H]** — As a student, I want to see the instructions, attachments, rubric, late policy and a countdown when less than 48 h remain (\"Due in 5 h 12 min\"), so that I don't miss the deadline.\n- **FR-20, FR-21 [H]** — As a student, I want to submit text and/or files (within the file limit) after a confirmation, with my draft text autosaved locally, so that I don't lose work.\n- **FR-22, FR-23 [H]** — As a student, I want late work accepted only under my teacher's policy, and I want lateness measured in started 24 h periods, so that the rules are fair and predictable.\n- **FR-24 [H]** — As a student, I want to resubmit before the deadline until my work is returned, so that I can hand in my best work.\n- **FR-25 [H]** — As a student, I want a receipt such as \"Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)\" showing what I sent, so that I have proof of submission.\n- **FR-26, FR-27 [H]** — As a student, I want to see \"Submitted — awaiting grading\" until my work is returned, and then my final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and late penalty, so that I can improve.\n\n## Teacher — grade\n\n- **FR-28 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a student list with status chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter and sorting, so that I can work through the class.\n- **FR-29 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to read the submission as sanitised Markdown, preview images and PDFs inline, and open previous attempts, so that I never leave the grading screen.\n- **FR-30, FR-31, FR-36 [H]** — As a teacher, I want rubric level clicks to auto-sum into the raw score, the late penalty pre-filled (and overridable), and the final score computed live (raw × (1 − penalty%), 2 dp half-up), within 0–max or 120 % with extra credit, so that my late policy is applied automatically.\n- **FR-32 [H]** — As a teacher, I want \"Save\", \"Save & return\" and \"Return all graded\", so that I control when students see grades.\n- **FR-33 [M]** — As a teacher, I want J/K for next/previous and Ctrl+Enter to save and go to the next student, so that I can grade 30 submissions quickly.\n- **FR-34 [H]** — As a teacher, I want \"Grade without submission\", so that offline and no-submission work gets a score.\n- **FR-35 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to exempt a student, so that they drop out of missing counts, reminders and future gradebook calculation.\n\n## Cross-course views\n\n- **FR-37 [H]** — As a student, I want a \"My assignments\" page with Upcoming, Missing, Submitted and Returned tabs and a course filter, so that I see every deadline across all my courses on one page.\n- **FR-38 [H]** — As a parent, I want to pick my child and see their upcoming and missing assignments (read-only), so that I can help them stay on track.\n- **FR-39 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a \"To grade\" list of ungraded submissions across my courses, oldest first, so that nothing waits too long.\n- **FR-40 [M]** — As any user, I want an \"Assignments\" sidebar entry, so that I can find the page.\n- **FR-41 [H]** — As a teacher or admin viewing a student, I want an Assignments student tab, so that I can see that student's work in one place.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **FR-42 [H]** — As a student, I want to be notified once when an assignment is published or a scheduled one becomes visible.\n- **FR-43 [H]** — As a student who hasn't submitted, I want exactly one reminder 24 h before the due time.\n- **FR-44 [H]** — As a student or parent, I want a notification when work is returned, including the score (\"Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20\").\n- **FR-45 [H]** — As a parent, I want one notification (email on by default) when my child is still missing work 24 h after the due time.\n- **FR-46 [M]** — As a user, I want these notification types listed in my preferences under Academic.\n\n## Files, API, audit, seed\n\n- **FR-47 [H]** — As a student, I want my submission files visible only to me, my parents, my teachers and admins, so that my work stays private.\n- **FR-48 to FR-58 [H]** — As a client, I want the REST endpoints from the PRD API table, with role-shaped responses, so that every screen gets only the data its role may see.\n- **FR-59 [M]** — As an admin, I want grading, returning and exemptions written to the audit log, so that changes to student records are traceable.\n- **FR-60 [L]** — As a teacher, I want NO_SUBMISSION assignments excluded from Missing and from reminders, so that offline tasks don't nag students.\n- **FR-61 [H]** — As a developer, I want seed assignments in MATH-7A, ENG-7A and SCI-7A, so that every state is demoable.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| Id | Requirement | Conf. |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Decimal arithmetic end to end; final scores round half-up to 2 dp | H |\n| NFR-2 | Server time only for deadlines, lateness, visibility and reminders | H |\n| NFR-3 | Grading screen switches students in under 300 ms (prefetch next and previous) | H |\n| NFR-4 | Students never see other students' submissions, scores or files | H |\n| NFR-5 | Server-side access checks on every handler and page | H |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up via mui-mcp first; banned-import check by QA | H |\n| NFR-7 | Standard response envelope, error codes and pagination | H |\n| NFR-8 | Feature layout: `src/server/assignments/`, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | H |\n| NFR-9 | UTC storage, school-timezone display; correct at the DST change and the exact 24 h boundary | H |\n| NFR-10 | Sanitised Markdown rendered through MUI components | H |\n| NFR-11 | Brownfield reuse of existing helpers, components and registries | H |\n| NFR-12 | No console.log; use the logger | H |\n| NFR-13 | lint, typecheck and test stay green | H |\n| NFR-14 | Unit, integration and Playwright tests as listed in the PRD | H |\n| NFR-15 | Out of scope: plagiarism, peer review, groups, annotation, gradebook weighting | H |\n| NFR-16 | Create and publish in under 2 min; keyboard grading of 30 submissions | H |\n| NFR-17 | English, evergreen browsers, basic accessibility | M |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":69346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df495bd9-17af-4404-ad8d-134253d4d6e0","uuid":"bd247104-97c3-463c-853b-1821161bc1a8","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:23:04.980Z","request_id":"req_011Cgro2etTmCci36J1m9Y79","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VTwC1Es94eDKB1nut3pL3c":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-9 — PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions: User Stories\n\nTicket: SH-9 (PRD header ref SCH-009) · Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react` · Generated by intake on 2026-11-09.\nRequirement ids refer to `requirements.json`. Confidence is shown as [H]/[M]/[L].\n\n## Data & platform\n\n- **FR-1 to FR-6 [H]** — As the platform, I want the Assignment, AssignmentAttachment, Rubric, RubricCriterion, Submission, SubmissionFile, SubmissionHistory, GradeExemption and AssignmentReminder models (plus `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt` and `archivedAt` on Assignment), so that assignment work is stored with full history.\n- **FR-7 [H]** — As a developer, I want shared Zod limits (title ≤150, instructions ≤50k, maxPoints 0–1000, cutoff > due, penalties 0–100, maxFileCount 1–10, text ≤50k, feedback ≤10k), so that the client and server validate the same way.\n- **FR-8 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to record a grade for a student who did not submit (stored as attempt 0), so that offline work is scored.\n\n## Teacher — create & manage\n\n- **FR-9 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to create an assignment with instructions, files, submission type, due date, max points, late policy, file limit, extra-credit flag and optional rubric, so that students know what to do.\n- **FR-10 [M]** — As a teacher, I want the due date to default to the next teaching day at 23:59 (school timezone), so that the common case needs no editing.\n- **FR-11 [H]** — As a teacher, I want an optional rubric builder that warns \"Rubric totals 18 points but the assignment is worth 20.\", so that grading is consistent and transparent.\n- **FR-12, FR-13 [H/M]** — As a teacher, I want to save a draft, publish now, or schedule for a future available-from, so that students see the work only when I intend.\n- **FR-14 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a warning when I change the due date or points after students have submitted, plus a \"review grades\" banner, so that I don't silently invalidate scores.\n- **FR-15 [L]** — As a teacher, I want to duplicate an assignment as a draft into other courses I manage, keeping the same due date, so that parallel classes get the same work.\n- **FR-51, FR-52 [H/L]** — As a teacher, I want deleting an assignment that already has submissions to archive it instead, so that student work is never lost.\n- **FR-16, FR-17 [H]** — As a teacher, I want an Assignments course tab showing title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a Grade button, so that I can see progress at a glance.\n\n## Student — submit\n\n- **FR-18 [H]** — As a student, I want my course's assignments grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned, so that I know what to do next.\n- **FR-19 [H]** — As a student, I want to see the instructions, attachments, rubric, late policy and a countdown when less than 48 h remain (\"Due in 5 h 12 min\"), so that I don't miss the deadline.\n- **FR-20, FR-21 [H]** — As a student, I want to submit text and/or files (within the file limit) after a confirmation, with my draft text autosaved locally, so that I don't lose work.\n- **FR-22, FR-23 [H]** — As a student, I want late work accepted only under my teacher's policy, and I want lateness measured in started 24 h periods, so that the rules are fair and predictable.\n- **FR-24 [H]** — As a student, I want to resubmit before the deadline until my work is returned, so that I can hand in my best work.\n- **FR-25 [H]** — As a student, I want a receipt such as \"Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)\" showing what I sent, so that I have proof of submission.\n- **FR-26, FR-27 [H]** — As a student, I want to see \"Submitted — awaiting grading\" until my work is returned, and then my final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and late penalty, so that I can improve.\n\n## Teacher — grade\n\n- **FR-28 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a student list with status chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter and sorting, so that I can work through the class.\n- **FR-29 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to read the submission as sanitised Markdown, preview images and PDFs inline, and open previous attempts, so that I never leave the grading screen.\n- **FR-30, FR-31, FR-36 [H]** — As a teacher, I want rubric level clicks to auto-sum into the raw score, the late penalty pre-filled (and overridable), and the final score computed live (raw × (1 − penalty%), 2 dp half-up), within 0–max or 120 % with extra credit, so that my late policy is applied automatically.\n- **FR-32 [H]** — As a teacher, I want \"Save\", \"Save & return\" and \"Return all graded\", so that I control when students see grades.\n- **FR-33 [M]** — As a teacher, I want J/K for next/previous and Ctrl+Enter to save and go to the next student, so that I can grade 30 submissions quickly.\n- **FR-34 [H]** — As a teacher, I want \"Grade without submission\", so that offline and no-submission work gets a score.\n- **FR-35 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to exempt a student, so that they drop out of missing counts, reminders and future gradebook calculation.\n\n## Cross-course views\n\n- **FR-37 [H]** — As a student, I want a \"My assignments\" page with Upcoming, Missing, Submitted and Returned tabs and a course filter, so that I see every deadline across all my courses on one page.\n- **FR-38 [H]** — As a parent, I want to pick my child and see their upcoming and missing assignments (read-only), so that I can help them stay on track.\n- **FR-39 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a \"To grade\" list of ungraded submissions across my courses, oldest first, so that nothing waits too long.\n- **FR-40 [M]** — As any user, I want an \"Assignments\" sidebar entry, so that I can find the page.\n- **FR-41 [H]** — As a teacher or admin viewing a student, I want an Assignments student tab, so that I can see that student's work in one place.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **FR-42 [H]** — As a student, I want to be notified once when an assignment is published or a scheduled one becomes visible.\n- **FR-43 [H]** — As a student who hasn't submitted, I want exactly one reminder 24 h before the due time.\n- **FR-44 [H]** — As a student or parent, I want a notification when work is returned, including the score (\"Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20\").\n- **FR-45 [H]** — As a parent, I want one notification (email on by default) when my child is still missing work 24 h after the due time.\n- **FR-46 [M]** — As a user, I want these notification types listed in my preferences under Academic.\n\n## Files, API, audit, seed\n\n- **FR-47 [H]** — As a student, I want my submission files visible only to me, my parents, my teachers and admins, so that my work stays private.\n- **FR-48 to FR-58 [H]** — As a client, I want the REST endpoints from the PRD API table, with role-shaped responses, so that every screen gets only the data its role may see.\n- **FR-59 [M]** — As an admin, I want grading, returning and exemptions written to the audit log, so that changes to student records are traceable.\n- **FR-60 [L]** — As a teacher, I want NO_SUBMISSION assignments excluded from Missing and from reminders, so that offline tasks don't nag students.\n- **FR-61 [H]** — As a developer, I want seed assignments in MATH-7A, ENG-7A and SCI-7A, so that every state is demoable.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| Id | Requirement | Conf. |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | Decimal arithmetic end to end; final scores round half-up to 2 dp | H |\n| NFR-2 | Server time only for deadlines, lateness, visibility and reminders | H |\n| NFR-3 | Grading screen switches students in under 300 ms (prefetch next and previous) | H |\n| NFR-4 | Students never see other students' submissions, scores or files | H |\n| NFR-5 | Server-side access checks on every handler and page | H |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up via mui-mcp first; banned-import check by QA | H |\n| NFR-7 | Standard response envelope, error codes and pagination | H |\n| NFR-8 | Feature layout: `src/server/assignments/`, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | H |\n| NFR-9 | UTC storage, school-timezone display; correct at the DST change and the exact 24 h boundary | H |\n| NFR-10 | Sanitised Markdown rendered through MUI components | H |\n| NFR-11 | Brownfield reuse of existing helpers, components and registries | H |\n| NFR-12 | No console.log; use the logger | H |\n| NFR-13 | lint, typecheck and test stay green | H |\n| NFR-14 | Unit, integration and Playwright tests as listed in the PRD | H |\n| NFR-15 | Out of scope: plagiarism, peer review, groups, annotation, gradebook weighting | H |\n| NFR-16 | Create and publish in under 2 min; keyboard grading of 30 submissions | H |\n| NFR-17 | English, evergreen browsers, basic accessibility | M |\n"}}}
