R-1 | Decimal arithmetic end to end; final scores round half-up to 2 dp | H |\n| NFR-2 | Server time only for deadlines, lateness, visibility and reminders | H |\n| NFR-3 | Grading screen switches students in under 300 ms (prefetch next and previous) | H |\n| NFR-4 | Students never see other students' submissions, scores or files | H |\n| NFR-5 | Server-side access checks on every handler and page | H |\n| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up via mui-mcp first; banned-import check by QA | H |\n| NFR-7 | Standard response envelope, error codes and pagination | H |\n| NFR-8 | Feature layout: `src/server/assignments/`, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | H |\n| NFR-9 | UTC storage, school-timezone display; correct at the DST change and the exact 24 h boundary | H |\n| NFR-10 | Sanitised Markdown rendered through MUI components | H |\n| NFR-11 | Brownfield reuse of existing helpers, components and registries | H |\n| NFR-12 | No console.log; use the logger | H |\n| NFR-13 | lint, typecheck and test stay green | H |\n| NFR-14 | Unit, integration and Playwright tests as listed in the PRD | H |\n| NFR-15 | Out of scope: plagiarism, peer review, groups, annotation, gradebook weighting | H |\n| NFR-16 | Create and publish in under 2 min; keyboard grading of 30 submissions | H |\n| NFR-17 | English, evergreen browsers, basic accessibility | M |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":43,"newStart":1,"newLines":87,"lines":["-# SH-8 — User Stories: File Storage & Course Content (PRD-08 / SCH-008)","+# SH-9 — PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions: User Stories"," ","-## File storage","+Ticket: SH-9 (PRD header ref SCH-009) · Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react` · Generated by intake on 2026-11-09.","+Requirement ids refer to `requirements.json`. Confidence is shown as [H]/[M]/[L]."," ","-- **FR-1, FR-2:** As a platform developer, I want a FileObject record and a local-disk storage module outside `public/` so that every feature stores files the same way.","-- **FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7:** As any signed-in user, I want to upload a file with a context so that I can attach it to content. I want oversize, disallowed or disguised files (e.g. an `.exe` renamed `.pdf`) rejected with a clear message.","-- **FR-8, FR-9, FR-10:** As a user, I want to download a file only if I can see the content it belongs to so that private materials stay private. Logos are public, and unknown contexts are limited to the owner and admins.","-- **FR-11:** As an uploader or admin, I want to delete an unattached file so that mistakes don't linger.","-- **FR-12:** As an operator, I want unattached files older than 24 h purged daily so that disk use stays bounded.","-- **FR-13, FR-14:** As a teacher, I want a drag-and-drop upload widget with per-file progress and a list of attached files so that adding materials is quick.","+## Data & platform"," ","-## Course content","+- **FR-1 to FR-6 [H]** — As the platform, I want the Assignment, AssignmentAttachment, Rubric, RubricCriterion, Submission, SubmissionFile, SubmissionHistory, GradeExemption and AssignmentReminder models (plus `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt` and `archivedAt` on Assignment), so that assignment work is stored with full history.","+- **FR-7 [H]** — As a developer, I want shared Zod limits (title ≤150, instructions ≤50k, maxPoints 0–1000, cutoff > due, penalties 0–100, maxFileCount 1–10, text ≤50k, feedback ≤10k), so that the client and server validate the same way.","+- **FR-8 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to record a grade for a student who did not submit (stored as attempt 0), so that offline work is scored."," ","-- **FR-15, FR-16, FR-45:** As a teacher, I want modules containing ordered lessons (Markdown, video, attachments, links) so that content follows my teaching plan.","-- **FR-22, FR-23, FR-24:** As a teacher, I want to create modules, order lessons and drag them within and across modules (with keyboard up/down) so that content follows my teaching plan. I want deleting a non-empty module to require typing its title.","-- **FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-29, FR-30:** As a teacher, I want to write lessons in Markdown with images, attach files, add links and embed a YouTube or Vimeo video, with autosave, so that materials are rich and never lost.","-- **FR-28, FR-39:** As a teacher, I want to save a draft, publish now or schedule a lesson for a future date so that I can prepare ahead.","-- **FR-18, FR-19:** As a teacher or admin, I want to see every module and lesson with a Draft/Scheduled/Published badge. As a student or parent, I want to see only what is published or past its schedule.","-- **FR-20, FR-21:** As a student, I want a Content tab with module and course progress bars and a Continue button so that I always know what is next.","-- **FR-31, FR-32, FR-33:** As a student, I want to read lessons safely rendered, watch videos, download materials, move to the previous or next lesson, and mark lessons complete so that I can track my progress.","-- **FR-34:** As a teacher, I want a Progress panel showing which students viewed or completed each lesson so that I can follow up.","-- **FR-35:** As a student, parent, teacher or admin, I want a Learning tab on the student page showing per-course progress so that learning is visible.","-- **FR-36, FR-37:** As a parent, I want to read my child's course content read-only so that I can support learning at home.","-- **FR-38:** As a student, I want a notification when a teacher publishes a lesson now so that I don't miss new content.","-- **FR-40, FR-41, FR-42:** As an admin, I want to upload the school logo (PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG ≤ 2 MB) instead of typing a URL so that branding is easy, with SVGs served safely.","-- **FR-43, FR-44, FR-46:** As a client developer, I want REST endpoints with consistent access checks, envelopes and audit logging so that the UI and later PRDs can build on them.","-- **FR-47:** As a developer or demo user, I want realistic seed content for MATH-7A and ENG-7A, with Sam having completed 4 lessons, so that the feature is demonstrable.","-- **FR-48:** As a maintainer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the risky logic so that regressions are caught.","+## Teacher — create & manage"," ","+- **FR-9 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to create an assignment with instructions, files, submission type, due date, max points, late policy, file limit, extra-credit flag and optional rubric, so that students know what to do.","+- **FR-10 [M]** — As a teacher, I want the due date to default to the next teaching day at 23:59 (school timezone), so that the common case needs no editing.","+- **FR-11 [H]** — As a teacher, I want an optional rubric builder that warns \"Rubric totals 18 points but the assignment is worth 20.\", so that grading is consistent and transparent.","+- **FR-12, FR-13 [H/M]** — As a teacher, I want to save a draft, publish now, or schedule for a future available-from, so that students see the work only when I intend.","+- **FR-14 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a warning when I change the due date or points after students have submitted, plus a \"review grades\" banner, so that I don't silently invalidate scores.","+- **FR-15 [L]** — As a teacher, I want to duplicate an assignment as a draft into other courses I manage, keeping the same due date, so that parallel classes get the same work.","+- **FR-51, FR-52 [H/L]** — As a teacher, I want deleting an assignment that already has submissions to archive it instead, so that student work is never lost.","+- **FR-16, FR-17 [H]** — As a teacher, I want an Assignments course tab showing title, due date, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted and a Grade button, so that I can see progress at a glance.","+","+## Student — submit","+","+- **FR-18 [H]** — As a student, I want my course's assignments grouped as Upcoming, Past due (missing), Submitted and Returned, so that I know what to do next.","+- **FR-19 [H]** — As a student, I want to see the instructions, attachments, rubric, late policy and a countdown when less than 48 h remain (\"Due in 5 h 12 min\"), so that I don't miss the deadline.","+- **FR-20, FR-21 [H]** — As a student, I want to submit text and/or files (within the file limit) after a confirmation, with my draft text autosaved locally, so that I don't lose work.","+- **FR-22, FR-23 [H]** — As a student, I want late work accepted only under my teacher's policy, and I want lateness measured in started 24 h periods, so that the rules are fair and predictable.","+- **FR-24 [H]** — As a student, I want to resubmit before the deadline until my work is returned, so that I can hand in my best work.","+- **FR-25 [H]** — As a student, I want a receipt such as \"Submitted Mon 14 Sep 2026, 21:04 (attempt 2)\" showing what I sent, so that I have proof of submission.","+- **FR-26, FR-27 [H]** — As a student, I want to see \"Submitted — awaiting grading\" until my work is returned, and then my final score, rubric breakdown, feedback and late penalty, so that I can improve.","+","+## Teacher — grade","+","+- **FR-28 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a student list with status chips (Not submitted, Submitted, Late, Graded, Returned, Exempt), a status filter and sorting, so that I can work through the class.","+- **FR-29 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to read the submission as sanitised Markdown, preview images and PDFs inline, and open previous attempts, so that I never leave the grading screen.","+- **FR-30, FR-31, FR-36 [H]** — As a teacher, I want rubric level clicks to auto-sum into the raw score, the late penalty pre-filled (and overridable), and the final score computed live (raw × (1 − penalty%), 2 dp half-up), within 0–max or 120 % with extra credit, so that my late policy is applied automatically.","+- **FR-32 [H]** — As a teacher, I want \"Save\", \"Save & return\" and \"Return all graded\", so that I control when students see grades.","+- **FR-33 [M]** — As a teacher, I want J/K for next/previous and Ctrl+Enter to save and go to the next student, so that I can grade 30 submissions quickly.","+- **FR-34 [H]** — As a teacher, I want \"Grade without submission\", so that offline and no-submission work gets a score.","+- **FR-35 [H]** — As a teacher, I want to exempt a student, so that they drop out of missing counts, reminders and future gradebook calculation.","+","+## Cross-course views","+","+- **FR-37 [H]** — As a student, I want a \"My assignments\" page with Upcoming, Missing, Submitted and Returned tabs and a course filter, so that I see every deadline across all my courses on one page.","+- **FR-38 [H]** — As a parent, I want to pick my child and see their upcoming and missing assignments (read-only), so that I can help them stay on track.","+- **FR-39 [H]** — As a teacher, I want a \"To grade\" list of ungraded submissions across my courses, oldest first, so that nothing waits too long.","+- **FR-40 [M]** — As any user, I want an \"Assignments\" sidebar entry, so that I can find the page.","+- **FR-41 [H]** — As a teacher or admin viewing a student, I want an Assignments student tab, so that I can see that student's work in one place.","+","+## Notifications","+","+- **FR-42 [H]** — As a student, I want to be notified once when an assignment is published or a scheduled one becomes visible.","+- **FR-43 [H]** — As a student who hasn't submitted, I want exactly one reminder 24 h before the due time.","+- **FR-44 [H]** — As a student or parent, I want a notification when work is returned, including the score (\"Mathematics: Fractions worksheet — 18/20\").","+- **FR-45 [H]** — As a parent, I want one notification (email on by default) when my child is still missing work 24 h after the due time.","+- **FR-46 [M]** — As a user, I want these notification types listed in my preferences under Academic.","+","+## Files, API, audit, seed","+","+- **FR-47 [H]** — As a student, I want my submission files visible only to me, my parents, my teachers and admins, so that my work stays private.","+- **FR-48 to FR-58 [H]** — As a client, I want the REST endpoints from the PRD API table, with role-shaped responses, so that every screen gets only the data its role may see.","+- **FR-59 [M]** — As an admin, I want grading, returning and exemptions written to the audit log, so that changes to student records are traceable.","+- **FR-60 [L]** — As a teacher, I want NO_SUBMISSION assignments excluded from Missing and from reminders, so that offline tasks don't nag students.","+- **FR-61 [H]** — As a developer, I want seed assignments in MATH-7A, ENG-7A and SCI-7A, so that every state is demoable.","+"," ## Non-Functional Requirements"," ","-- **NFR-1:** Files are never served statically, and every download is access-checked.","-- **NFR-2:** Markdown is sanitised and `javascript:` URLs are stripped.","-- **NFR-3:** Uploads are limited to 60 per user per hour (reuse `rateLimit()`).","-- **NFR-4:** The Content tab for 20 × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms, with no N+1 queries.","-- **NFR-5:** Uploads stream to disk without whole-file buffering.","-- **NFR-6:** Video iframes have titles, the editor warns on missing alt text, and keyboard reorder alternatives exist.","-- **NFR-7:** The MUI-only UI rule applies: every component is looked up via mui-mcp, banned libraries are never imported, and QA verifies both.","-- **NFR-8:** Access is enforced server-side on every handler and page.","-- **NFR-9:** Brownfield work only: no re-scaffolding, renames or duplicate helpers, existing tests stay green, and new dependencies are limited to the allowed set.","-- **NFR-10:** Times are stored in UTC and displayed and picked in the school timezone.","-- **NFR-11:** Out of scope: S3, SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.","-- **NFR-12:** No `console.log` (use `logger`), and `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`.","+| Id | Requirement | Conf. |","+|---|---|---|","+| NFR-1 | Decimal arithmetic end to end; final scores round half-up to 2 dp | H |","+| NFR-2 | Server time only for deadlines, lateness, visibility and reminders | H |","+| NFR-3 | Grading screen switches students in under 300 ms (prefetch next and previous) | H |","+| NFR-4 | Students never see other students' submissions, scores or files | H |","+| NFR-5 | Server-side access checks on every handler and page | H |","+| NFR-6 | MUI-only UI; every component looked up via mui-mcp first; banned-import check by QA | H |","+| NFR-7 | Standard response envelope, error codes and pagination | H |","+| NFR-8 | Feature layout: `src/server/assignments/`, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | H |","+| NFR-9 | UTC storage, school-timezone display; correct at the DST change and the exact 24 h boundary | H |","+| NFR-10 | Sanitised Markdown rendered through MUI components | H |","+| NFR-11 | Brownfield reuse of existing helpers, components and registries | H |","+| NFR-12 | No console.log; use the logger | H |","+| NFR-13 | lint, typecheck and test stay green | H |","+| NFR-14 | Unit, integration and Playwright tests as listed in the PRD | H |","+| NFR-15 | Out of scope: plagiarism, peer review, groups, annotation, gradebook weighting | H |","+| NFR-16 | Create and publish in under 2 min; keyboard grading of 30 submissions | H |","+| NFR-17 | English, evergreen browsers, basic accessibility | M |"]}],"originalFile":"# SH-8 — User Stories: File Storage & Course Content (PRD-08 / SCH-008)\n\n## File storage\n\n- **FR-1, FR-2:** As a platform developer, I want a FileObject record and a local-disk storage module outside `public/` so that every feature stores files the same way.\n- **FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7:** As any signed-in user, I want to upload a file with a context so that I can attach it to content. I want oversize, disallowed or disguised files (e.g. an `.exe` renamed `.pdf`) rejected with a clear message.\n- **FR-8, FR-9, FR-10:** As a user, I want to download a file only if I can see the content it belongs to so that private materials stay private. Logos are public, and unknown contexts are limited to the owner and admins.\n- **FR-11:** As an uploader or admin, I want to delete an unattached file so that mistakes don't linger.\n- **FR-12:** As an operator, I want unattached files older than 24 h purged daily so that disk use stays bounded.\n- **FR-13, FR-14:** As a teacher, I want a drag-and-drop upload widget with per-file progress and a list of attached files so that adding materials is quick.\n\n## Course content\n\n- **FR-15, FR-16, FR-45:** As a teacher, I want modules containing ordered lessons (Markdown, video, attachments, links) so that content follows my teaching plan.\n- **FR-22, FR-23, FR-24:** As a teacher, I want to create modules, order lessons and drag them within and across modules (with keyboard up/down) so that content follows my teaching plan. I want deleting a non-empty module to require typing its title.\n- **FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-29, FR-30:** As a teacher, I want to write lessons in Markdown with images, attach files, add links and embed a YouTube or Vimeo video, with autosave, so that materials are rich and never lost.\n- **FR-28, FR-39:** As a teacher, I want to save a draft, publish now or schedule a lesson for a future date so that I can prepare ahead.\n- **FR-18, FR-19:** As a teacher or admin, I want to see every module and lesson with a Draft/Scheduled/Published badge. As a student or parent, I want to see only what is published or past its schedule.\n- **FR-20, FR-21:** As a student, I want a Content tab with module and course progress bars and a Continue button so that I always know what is next.\n- **FR-31, FR-32, FR-33:** As a student, I want to read lessons safely rendered, watch videos, download materials, move to the previous or next lesson, and mark lessons complete so that I can track my progress.\n- **FR-34:** As a teacher, I want a Progress panel showing which students viewed or completed each lesson so that I can follow up.\n- **FR-35:** As a student, parent, teacher or admin, I want a Learning tab on the student page showing per-course progress so that learning is visible.\n- **FR-36, FR-37:** As a parent, I want to read my child's course content read-only so that I can support learning at home.\n- **FR-38:** As a student, I want a notification when a teacher publishes a lesson now so that I don't miss new content.\n- **FR-40, FR-41, FR-42:** As an admin, I want to upload the school logo (PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG ≤ 2 MB) instead of typing a URL so that branding is easy, with SVGs served safely.\n- **FR-43, FR-44, FR-46:** As a client developer, I want REST endpoints with consistent access checks, envelopes and audit logging so that the UI and later PRDs can build on them.\n- **FR-47:** As a developer or demo user, I want realistic seed content for MATH-7A and ENG-7A, with Sam having completed 4 lessons, so that the feature is demonstrable.\n- **FR-48:** As a maintainer, I want unit, integration and e2e tests for the risky logic so that regressions are caught.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1:** Files are never served statically, and every download is access-checked.\n- **NFR-2:** Markdown is sanitised and `javascript:` URLs are stripped.\n- **NFR-3:** Uploads are limited to 60 per user per hour (reuse `rateLimit()`).\n- **NFR-4:** The Content tab for 20 × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms, with no N+1 queries.\n- **NFR-5:** Uploads stream to disk without whole-file buffering.\n- **NFR-6:** Video iframes have titles, the editor warns on missing alt text, and keyboard reorder alternatives exist.\n- **NFR-7:** The MUI-only UI rule applies: every component is looked up via mui-mcp, banned libraries are never imported, and QA verifies both.\n- **NFR-8:** Access is enforced server-side on every handler and page.\n- **NFR-9:** Brownfield work only: no re-scaffolding, renames or duplicate helpers, existing tests stay green, and new dependencies are limited to the allowed set.\n- **NFR-10:** Times are stored in UTC and displayed and picked in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-11:** Out of scope: S3, SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\n- **NFR-12:** No `console.log` (use `logger`), and `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VTwC1Es94eDKB1nut3pL3c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgro2f5dSkrbiTyHMe3we","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LdyWCJAGppJDYPwwbakW3F","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-9\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20 on PostgreSQL 16, and Auth.js v5 beta.25. The MUI packages (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/material-nextjs, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts) are all 9.5.0. Everything PRD-09 needs is already installed: react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, and decimal.js (shipped with Prisma; use Prisma.Decimal for score maths). No new dependencies are required. Known environment breaks: (1) @mui/x-internals 9.15.0 is mismatched with @mui/x-data-grid 9.5.0, so DataGrid pages fail to compile; (2) vitest.config.ts imports 'vitest/config.js', which does not resolve; (3) the CSP script-src 'self' blocks hydration. Styling goes only through the MUI theme, sx and styled().\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":69346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":384},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df495bd9-17af-4404-ad8d-134253d4d6e0","uuid":"