{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgro6FMV44ACDUQrFrjKZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake for SH-9 is complete, and the handoff marks it ready for the Architect phase. The bigger problem is underneath: PRD-08 (SH-8) never finished, so some of what PRD-09 builds on doesn't exist.\n\n**What I wrote** (in `artifacts/intake/`, replacing the SH-8 versions):\n- `requirements.json`: 78 requirements (61 functional, 17 non-functional), each with a confidence label and a PRD citation. 68 are explicitly stated, 7 inferred and 3 are guesses that need your check. Overall confidence is 95%, above the 80% threshold.\n- `user-stories.md`, `tech-stack.json` (React/Next.js, confirmed from the workspace), and `handoff-to-architect.json`, written last.\n- There's no Figma file because the PRD has no Figma link.\n- Everything PRD-09 needs is already installed, so no new dependencies.\n\n**Blockers passed to the Architect:**\n1. **PRD-08 is only half built.** Its QA failed on 39 of 60 requirements. The file storage backend exists and can be reused, but there is no file-upload component and no Markdown editor or viewer. PRD-09 needs those for creating assignments, submitting work and grading. The Architect has to decide whether to build them as part of this ticket.\n2. **Data table pages don't compile.** Two MUI X package versions don't match. The teacher's assignments table needs this component, so either the versions get aligned or the table is built differently.\n3. **`npm test` doesn't start.** `vitest.config.ts` has a broken import; the workaround copy `vitest.tmp.config.ts` works.\n4. **The app's content security policy stops pages from loading their scripts in a real browser.** The end-to-end tests need to bypass it, as earlier runs did.\n5. **The student \"Assignments\" tab will be registered but invisible.** No page displays the student tabs yet.\n\n**Defaults I chose where the PRD is unclear** (recorded in the requirements):\n- **Copying to other courses:** the copy keeps the same due date and time. I wasn't sure what \"same relative due date\" means.\n- **Archived assignments:** hidden from students and parents, closed to new submissions, excluded from reminders, still visible to teachers.\n- **\"No submission\" assignments:** never count as missing and send no reminders.\n- **Scheduled assignments:** they appear once the start time passes, but their status isn't changed to Published.\n- **Default due date:** \"next teaching day\" uses the existing weekday settings and ignores holidays.\n- **Extra credit:** applies to the raw score only.\n- **Admin's \"My assignments\" page:** shows the teacher's \"To grade\" list across all courses.\n\nThe PRD calls this ticket SCH-009; I used SH-9, as the task said."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":285,"cache_read_input_tokens":75266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":285},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df495bd9-17af-4404-ad8d-134253d4d6e0","uuid":"f75f7b3d-3d7f-4033-9b3f-78940700d331","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:23:35.078Z","request_id":"req_011Cgro6F9pScjPZ9Wm3N81C"}
