{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKYkGzaVQg32VHAtRBS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Intake for SH-11 is finished. I wrote all four required files to `artifacts/intake/`, and all three JSON files parse correctly. They replace the SH-10 versions that were in that folder.\n\n- **`requirements.json`**: 42 functional and 13 non-functional requirements (55 total). Each has a confidence label and a citation back to the PRD. Overall confidence is 95%, so the 80% threshold was met in one round of clarifying questions. The questions with no answer available are recorded with the assumption I used.\n- **`user-stories.md`**: 24 user stories, each linked to its requirement IDs, plus a summary of the non-functional requirements.\n- **`tech-stack.json`**: React (Next.js 14, MUI 9.5.0), at 100% confidence. The PRD needs no new packages.\n- **`handoff-to-architect.json`**: written last, with status complete and no blockers.\n- **`figma-readiness.json`**: not created, because the PRD has no Figma link.\n\nThings I found in the codebase that the architect needs to know:\n1. **`getStudentQuizScore` doesn't exist.** The PRD names it, but nothing in the code has that name. I flagged that it should be built from the existing quiz helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` rather than written from scratch.\n2. **The PRD's rounding example gives a different letter than it says.** In the seed scale, 89.95 rounds to 90.0, which is an A− (A starts at 93). The PRD's test says \"A\". I noted that the test should check for A−.\n3. **Some pieces already exist.** The exemption table (`GradeExemption`), practice-quiz flag, submission final score and return date, homeroom access checks, and CSV and score-maths helpers are all in place to reuse. None of the new gradebook tables, the category fields on assignments and quizzes, or the course grading-scale field exist yet.\n\nThese assumptions are marked lower-confidence for someone to confirm:\n- Removing an exemption un-excuses the grade and re-syncs the score.\n- `/grades` and `/report-cards` get sidebar menu entries.\n- \"Past due\" means after the exact due time.\n- An item whose due date falls in no term is skipped and a warning is logged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3827,"cache_read_input_tokens":54530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3827},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4e8afab1-1108-4d52-897c-dc8864dd952a","uuid":"344d82cc-9bae-4e01-91d7-d6e6512230f6","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:02:56.419Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKYjzd7Uzto9bc53m1t"}
