{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Eg6xP1J2JVctvCpwHsPeVe","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 55,\n  \"functionalCount\": 42,\n  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 13,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"figmaPresent\": false,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"assumptionsFlagged\": [\n    \"FR-6 (MEDIUM): removing a GradeExemption clears excused and re-syncs the score.\",\n    \"FR-7: getStudentQuizScore does not exist. Build it on src/server/quiz/grading.ts applyScoringPolicy + resultsVisible.\",\n    \"FR-13: in the seed scale 89.95 → 90.0 lands in A− (90), not A (93). The test should assert 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\",\n    \"FR-27/FR-33 (MEDIUM): add nav entries for /grades (STUDENT, PARENT) and /report-cards (TEACHER).\",\n    \"NFR-10 (MEDIUM): 'past due' = now > dueAt. Items with no term to place them in are skipped and a warning is logged.\"\n  ],\n  \"keyRisks\": [\n    \"NFR-5 privacy: student and parent serializers must exclude hidden items, unreturned submissions and not-yet-visible quiz results. Sync only on return or visibility, so Grade rows never hold unreleased scores.\",\n    \"FR-31 snapshot immutability: regeneration must filter status = DRAFT, and grade edits must never touch ReportCard.\",\n    \"NFR-3: 600×8 generation must batch-load items, grades, overrides and attendance per course or term, then run the pure calc in memory.\",\n    \"FR-20: keyboard editing (E/M/Delete) within MIT DataGrid processRowUpdate and custom edit cells must be checked against the mui-mcp docs for v9.5.0.\",\n    \"FR-2: adding categoryId to the Assignment and Quiz editors touches PRD-09/10 code. Only add the field; don't change existing behaviour.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The PRD declares '--brownfield --tech-stack react', and package.json confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright. The MUI packages are pinned at 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), with @mui/x-internals overridden to 9.1.0. PRD-11 needs no new dependencies. The MIT x-data-grid covers the gradebook grid (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation); papaparse and src/server/csv.ts cover CSV export; Prisma.Decimal and src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts cover the arithmetic; and src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) covers quiz scores. Printing uses @media print and window.print(), so no PDF library is needed. The mui-mcp server is available for component lookup. Styling goes only through the MUI theme, sx and styled().\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-011 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-11.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Assignment.categoryId, Quiz.categoryId, Course.gradingScaleId and every PRD-11 model (GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride, ReportCard) are missing from prisma/schema.prisma. They need a new migration.\",\n    \"GradeExemption (schema.prisma ~L801) already exists. Its comment says a row is the PRD-11 'exclude from gradebook' flag, so sync maps it to Grade.excused = true.\",\n    \"Submission has finalScore and returnedAt. A submission counts as returned when returnedAt is non-null.\",\n    \"Quiz.isPractice exists. Practice quizzes must never sync.\",\n    \"No function named getStudentQuizScore exists. The closest helpers are src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) and quiz-service scoreOf. The architect should create or name getStudentQuizScore from these instead of duplicating them.\",\n    \"Section.homeroomTeacherId exists. Homeroom access already exists in src/server/auth/student-access.ts and attendance-service.\",\n    \"src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts has Decimal helpers, and src/server/csv.ts has CSV export. Reuse both.\",\n    \"src/config/student-tabs.ts has courses, attendance and assignments. Add grades and report-cards here.\",\n    \"No gradebook:backfill npm script exists yet. Seeding runs through 'db:seed' (tsx prisma/seed.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums GradeItemSource (ASSIGNMENT, QUIZ, MANUAL) and ReportCardStatus (DRAFT, PUBLISHED), plus the models GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride and ReportCard, exactly as specified, in a new prisma migrate migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Course.gradingScaleId (nullable, null = school default scale) and nullable categoryId to Assignment and Quiz. Add a category select to the assignment editor and the quiz editor.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 trailing paragraph\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a GradeItem (source + sourceId, title, maxPoints, dueAt, category). Its term is the one containing dueAt (assignment)\n# SH-11 — User Stories (PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards)\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. Each story cites its requirement id(s) in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Data & Sync\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-2)** — As a developer, I want the gradebook models, a Course grading scale, and a category on assignments and quizzes, so that every grade has a stored home.\n- **US-2 (FR-3, FR-4)** — As a teacher, I want published assignments and graded (non-practice) quizzes to appear in the gradebook automatically, so that I never enter them twice.\n- **US-3 (FR-5, FR-6)** — As a teacher, I want a returned submission's final score (or its exemption) to sync to the gradebook, so that the gradebook stays current. Unreturned scores stay hidden from students.\n- **US-4 (FR-7)** — As a teacher, I want a quiz score to sync once the attempt is graded and its results are visible, so that quiz results count without manual entry.\n- **US-5 (FR-8)** — As an admin, I want an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, so that data created before this PRD appears in the gradebook.\n- **US-6 (FR-9)** — As a teacher, I want synced grades to be read-only except for the comment, so that the source page remains the single place to edit them.\n\n## Calculation\n\n- **US-7 (FR-10 – FR-15)** — As a teacher, I want term grades calculated the same way across the school (excused and missing items, drop lowest, weight re-normalisation, half-up rounding, then band lookup, then overrides), so that grades are consistent and correct. For example, Homework 40% (18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60% (70/100) give 78.0% C+.\n\n## Setup\n\n- **US-8 (FR-16)** — As an admin, I want to define grading scales with validated bands and exactly one default, so that letter grades are consistent.\n- **US-9 (FR-17, FR-40)** — As a teacher, I want to set weighted categories that must total 100, with a live sum indicator, and choose a grading scale per course, so that grades reflect my syllabus.\n\n## Gradebook Grid\n\n- **US-10 (FR-18, FR-19)** — As a teacher, I want a spreadsheet-like grid of students × items, grouped by category, with averages and the term grade, so that I can see my whole class at a glance.\n- **US-11 (FR-20)** — As a teacher, I want to edit manual-item grades with the keyboard (numbers, Enter or arrows, E, M, Delete), with optimistic saves, so that I can enter grades quickly.\n- **US-12 (FR-21)** — As a teacher, I want clicking a synced cell to open its submission or quiz attempt, so that I edit the grade at its source.\n- **US-13 (FR-22)** — As a teacher, I want to add manual grade items for offline work, so that all assessment is in one place.\n- **US-14 (FR-23)** — As a teacher, I want to override a student's term grade or letter and add a comment, so that I can apply professional judgement on the report card.\n- **US-15 (FR-24)** — As a teacher, I want column actions (hide/show, mark ungraded as missing, statistics), so that I can manage items in bulk.\n- **US-16 (FR-25)** — As a teacher, I want to export the grid as CSV, so that I can share or archive it.\n\n## Student & Parent Views\n\n- **US-17 (FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-42)** — As a student or parent, I want to see current course grades and individual visible scores (on the student tab, on `/grades` and on the course Grades tab), so that we know where the student stands.\n\n## Report Cards\n\n- **US-18 (FR-29)** — As an admin, I want a term-filtered list of students with report card status and missing-data warnings, so that I can fix gaps before generating.\n- **US-19 (FR-30, FR-31)** — As an admin, I want to generate draft report cards as frozen snapshots, so that published results never change afterwards.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T16:01:17.472Z\",\n  \"succeeded\": true,\n  \"phases\": {\n    \"intake\": {\n      \"succeededCount\": 1,\n      \"failedCount\": 0,\n      \"cost\": {\n        \"totalUsd\": 0.8144498,\n        \"tokens\": {\n          \"input\": 16,\n          \"output\": 14324,\n          \"cacheRead\": 305249,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 58357\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"architect\": {\n      \"succeededCount\": 4,\n      \"failedCount\": 0,\n      \"cost\": {\n        \"totalUsd\": 3.708793,\n        \"tokens\": {\n          \"input\": 86,\n          \"output\": 66417,\n          \"cacheRead\": 2093665,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 245172\n        }\n      }\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 10:23 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1734 Nov  9 17:02 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  20247 Nov  9 17:02 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1139 Nov  9 17:02 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   5771 Nov  9 17:02 user-stories.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5ee16ee-e095-4181-884c-a98d424b627c","uuid":"ea6315e2-402b-4cba-bad5-107dc65d93cb","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:26:35.847Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 55,\n  \"functionalCount\": 42,\n  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 13,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"figmaPresent\": false,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"assumptionsFlagged\": [\n    \"FR-6 (MEDIUM): removing a GradeExemption clears excused and re-syncs the score.\",\n    \"FR-7: getStudentQuizScore does not exist. Build it on src/server/quiz/grading.ts applyScoringPolicy + resultsVisible.\",\n    \"FR-13: in the seed scale 89.95 → 90.0 lands in A− (90), not A (93). The test should assert 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\",\n    \"FR-27/FR-33 (MEDIUM): add nav entries for /grades (STUDENT, PARENT) and /report-cards (TEACHER).\",\n    \"NFR-10 (MEDIUM): 'past due' = now > dueAt. Items with no term to place them in are skipped and a warning is logged.\"\n  ],\n  \"keyRisks\": [\n    \"NFR-5 privacy: student and parent serializers must exclude hidden items, unreturned submissions and not-yet-visible quiz results. Sync only on return or visibility, so Grade rows never hold unreleased scores.\",\n    \"FR-31 snapshot immutability: regeneration must filter status = DRAFT, and grade edits must never touch ReportCard.\",\n    \"NFR-3: 600×8 generation must batch-load items, grades, overrides and attendance per course or term, then run the pure calc in memory.\",\n    \"FR-20: keyboard editing (E/M/Delete) within MIT DataGrid processRowUpdate and custom edit cells must be checked against the mui-mcp docs for v9.5.0.\",\n    \"FR-2: adding categoryId to the Assignment and Quiz editors touches PRD-09/10 code. Only add the field; don't change existing behaviour.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"The PRD declares '--brownfield --tech-stack react', and package.json confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright. The MUI packages are pinned at 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), with @mui/x-internals overridden to 9.1.0. PRD-11 needs no new dependencies. The MIT x-data-grid covers the gradebook grid (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation); papaparse and src/server/csv.ts cover CSV export; Prisma.Decimal and src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts cover the arithmetic; and src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) covers quiz scores. Printing uses @media print and window.print(), so no PDF library is needed. The mui-mcp server is available for component lookup. Styling goes only through the MUI theme, sx and styled().\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-011 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-11.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Assignment.categoryId, Quiz.categoryId, Course.gradingScaleId and every PRD-11 model (GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride, ReportCard) are missing from prisma/schema.prisma. They need a new migration.\",\n    \"GradeExemption (schema.prisma ~L801) already exists. Its comment says a row is the PRD-11 'exclude from gradebook' flag, so sync maps it to Grade.excused = true.\",\n    \"Submission has finalScore and returnedAt. A submission counts as returned when returnedAt is non-null.\",\n    \"Quiz.isPractice exists. Practice quizzes must never sync.\",\n    \"No function named getStudentQuizScore exists. The closest helpers are src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) and quiz-service scoreOf. The architect should create or name getStudentQuizScore from these instead of duplicating them.\",\n    \"Section.homeroomTeacherId exists. Homeroom access already exists in src/server/auth/student-access.ts and attendance-service.\",\n    \"src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts has Decimal helpers, and src/server/csv.ts has CSV export. Reuse both.\",\n    \"src/config/student-tabs.ts has courses, attendance and assignments. Add grades and report-cards here.\",\n    \"No gradebook:backfill npm script exists yet. Seeding runs through 'db:seed' (tsx prisma/seed.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums GradeItemSource (ASSIGNMENT, QUIZ, MANUAL) and ReportCardStatus (DRAFT, PUBLISHED), plus the models GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride and ReportCard, exactly as specified, in a new prisma migrate migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Course.gradingScaleId (nullable, null = school default scale) and nullable categoryId to Assignment and Quiz. Add a category select to the assignment editor and the quiz editor.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 trailing paragraph\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a GradeItem (source + sourceId, title, maxPoints, dueAt, category). Its term is the one containing dueAt (assignment)\n# SH-11 — User Stories (PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards)\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. Each story cites its requirement id(s) in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Data & Sync\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-2)** — As a developer, I want the gradebook models, a Course grading scale, and a category on assignments and quizzes, so that every grade has a stored home.\n- **US-2 (FR-3, FR-4)** — As a teacher, I want published assignments and graded (non-practice) quizzes to appear in the gradebook automatically, so that I never enter them twice.\n- **US-3 (FR-5, FR-6)** — As a teacher, I want a returned submission's final score (or its exemption) to sync to the gradebook, so that the gradebook stays current. Unreturned scores stay hidden from students.\n- **US-4 (FR-7)** — As a teacher, I want a quiz score to sync once the attempt is graded and its results are visible, so that quiz results count without manual entry.\n- **US-5 (FR-8)** — As an admin, I want an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, so that data created before this PRD appears in the gradebook.\n- **US-6 (FR-9)** — As a teacher, I want synced grades to be read-only except for the comment, so that the source page remains the single place to edit them.\n\n## Calculation\n\n- **US-7 (FR-10 – FR-15)** — As a teacher, I want term grades calculated the same way across the school (excused and missing items, drop lowest, weight re-normalisation, half-up rounding, then band lookup, then overrides), so that grades are consistent and correct. For example, Homework 40% (18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60% (70/100) give 78.0% C+.\n\n## Setup\n\n- **US-8 (FR-16)** — As an admin, I want to define grading scales with validated bands and exactly one default, so that letter grades are consistent.\n- **US-9 (FR-17, FR-40)** — As a teacher, I want to set weighted categories that must total 100, with a live sum indicator, and choose a grading scale per course, so that grades reflect my syllabus.\n\n## Gradebook Grid\n\n- **US-10 (FR-18, FR-19)** — As a teacher, I want a spreadsheet-like grid of students × items, grouped by category, with averages and the term grade, so that I can see my whole class at a glance.\n- **US-11 (FR-20)** — As a teacher, I want to edit manual-item grades with the keyboard (numbers, Enter or arrows, E, M, Delete), with optimistic saves, so that I can enter grades quickly.\n- **US-12 (FR-21)** — As a teacher, I want clicking a synced cell to open its submission or quiz attempt, so that I edit the grade at its source.\n- **US-13 (FR-22)** — As a teacher, I want to add manual grade items for offline work, so that all assessment is in one place.\n- **US-14 (FR-23)** — As a teacher, I want to override a student's term grade or letter and add a comment, so that I can apply professional judgement on the report card.\n- **US-15 (FR-24)** — As a teacher, I want column actions (hide/show, mark ungraded as missing, statistics), so that I can manage items in bulk.\n- **US-16 (FR-25)** — As a teacher, I want to export the grid as CSV, so that I can share or archive it.\n\n## Student & Parent Views\n\n- **US-17 (FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-42)** — As a student or parent, I want to see current course grades and individual visible scores (on the student tab, on `/grades` and on the course Grades tab), so that we know where the student stands.\n\n## Report Cards\n\n- **US-18 (FR-29)** — As an admin, I want a term-filtered list of students with report card status and missing-data warnings, so that I can fix gaps before generating.\n- **US-19 (FR-30, FR-31)** — As an admin, I want to generate draft report cards as frozen snapshots, so that published results never change afterwards.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T16:01:17.472Z\",\n  \"succeeded\": true,\n  \"phases\": {\n    \"intake\": {\n      \"succeededCount\": 1,\n      \"failedCount\": 0,\n      \"cost\": {\n        \"totalUsd\": 0.8144498,\n        \"tokens\": {\n          \"input\": 16,\n          \"output\": 14324,\n          \"cacheRead\": 305249,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 58357\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"architect\": {\n      \"succeededCount\": 4,\n      \"failedCount\": 0,\n      \"cost\": {\n        \"totalUsd\": 3.708793,\n        \"tokens\": {\n          \"input\": 86,\n          \"output\": 66417,\n          \"cacheRead\": 2093665,\n          \"cacheWrite\": 245172\n        }\n      }\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 10:23 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1734 Nov  9 17:02 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  20247 Nov  9 17:02 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1139 Nov  9 17:02 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   5771 Nov  9 17:02 user-stories.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Eg6xP1J2JVctvCpwHsPeVe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
