{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsfhC2rV88eUG69QisV9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NFpB3b2HUSr5bXgMYsXSPv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T18:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-12: Announcements & News\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-012 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-12.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment or AnnouncementRead models and no AnnouncementStatus or AudienceType enums. They need a new migration, plus back-relations on User (authored announcements, reads) and FileObject (announcement attachments).\",\n    \"The audience-resolution data already exists: User.status/archivedAt (ACTIVE, non-archived filter), StudentProfile.gradeLevelId, ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId), Section.homeroomTeacherId and gradeLevelId, SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId), Course.teacherId + coTeacherIds String[] + sectionId + academicYearId, and Enrollment.status (ACTIVE).\",\n    \"File access registry: src/server/files/access.ts exports registerFileAccess(context, resolver). Built-in contexts are registered in src/server/files/contexts.ts. Resolvers receive null for anonymous callers, which is what the public-announcement case needs.\",\n    \"Notification types live in src/server/notifications/types.ts with {category, mandatoryInApp, ...}. COMMUNICATION is already a category. notify() is in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\",\n    \"The 'generic-notification' email template is already registered in src/server/email/render.ts.\",\n    \"The maintenance run is POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (CRON_SECRET-gated). It calls dispatchEmails, sendDueReminders and the quiz maintenance passes. publishDueAnnouncements() should be added there, following src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts (batched and idempotent).\",\n    \"src/config/public-routes.ts has PUBLIC_API_PATHS. '/api/public/news' must be added (FR-8 / API table).\",\n    \"src/config/course-tabs.ts is where the course 'Announcements' tab goes (FR-5.4). src/config/navigation.ts NavItem has no badge field, so the unread-count badge needs a small extension. src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx already shows a Badge-and-poll pattern to reuse.\",\n    \"Shared components are in src/components/<Name>/ (MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, FileList, DataTable, ConfirmDialog, UserPicker, EmptyState, PageHeader, StatCard, Toast/useToast), not in src/components/shared/ as the platform context says. Reuse them where they are.\",\n    \"src/server/csv.ts already handles CSV export (FR-6.2). src/server/rate-limit.ts exists, but the 24h reminder throttle is a per-announcement business rule, not a rate limit.\",\n    \"Seed personas: Tom (teacher@), Sam (student@), Pat (parent@). Course lookups by code (MATH-7A) go through findCourse and skip when the course is missing. Neither prisma/seed.ts nor the scripts create 7A/7B/6A sections or ParentStudentLink rows. Seed announcements that target Grade 7, MATH-7A or 6A must follow the same skip-if-missing pattern.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums AnnouncementStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED, ARCHIVED) and AudienceType (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE), plus the models Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment and AnnouncementRead (composite PK announcementId+userId), exactly as specified, in a new prisma migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Validate title ≤ 150 chars and body (Markdown) ≤ 20,000 chars in a shared Zod schema at src/lib/validators/announcements.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (field comments); Platform Context › Validation\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) in src/server/announcements/audience.ts returns the deduplicated ids of ACTIVE, non-archived users. SCHOOL = everyone, STAFF = ADMIN + TEACHER, ROLE = users whose role is refId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"GRADE_LEVEL audience: students whose profile grade level is refId (includeStudents), their linked parents (includeParents), and teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade level (includeTeachers).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"SECTION audience: section members, their parents, the homeroom teacher and the teachers of the section's courses, each gated by the same include flags. 'Section members' is taken to mean current academic-year SectionMember rows.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"COURSE audience: students with ACTIVE enrollment, their parents, and the course teacher plus co-teachers (Course.coTeacherIds), each gated by the include flags.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"isUserInAudience(user, audiences) answers membership for one user through targeted SQL/Prisma joins, without loading every recipient. It must agree with resolveAudienceUserIds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; NFR Performance; Test Requirements › Integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"The audience service is generic (no announcement-specific coupling) so PRD-14 calendar events can reuse it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"ADMIN may target any audience type and set isPublic.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"TEACHER may target only COURSE audiences for courses they manage (teacher or co-teacher) and SECTION audiences for the section they homeroom. Any other audience, or isPublic=true, is rejected server-side with 403 FORBIDDEN.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; NFR Security; AC-3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"STUDENT and PARENT cannot create announcements (403).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Authors may edit their own announcements, and admins may edit or archive any. Archiving sets status ARCHIVED. When an admin changes someone else's announcement, write an AuditLog row through audit().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; API table (archive); Platform Context › audit()\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The composer pages /announcements/new and /announcements/[id]/edit have: title, body (the PRD-08 MarkdownEditor), optional cover image, attachments, an audience builder (rows of type → entity picker → include students/parents/teachers checkboxes), pinned, requires acknowledgement, public (admins only), publish now / schedule (publishAt) / save draft, and an expiry date.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"A live recipient count next to the audience builder ('Will reach 412 people: 180 students, 214 parents, 18 teachers'), computed by POST /api/announcements/preview-audience, which returns counts by role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Publishing (now or scheduled) with zero resolved recipients is refused with a VALIDATION_ERROR. Drafts may have zero recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Scheduling sets status SCHEDULED with publishAt. An announcement becomes visible once publishAt <= now, evaluated at read time, so a cron is not needed for visibility.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Feed /announcements (GET /api/announcements) for all roles: published, non-expired announcements whose audience includes the user. Up to 3 pinned show first, then newest. Unread items show a dot. Filter tabs: All / Unread / Requires acknowledgement. Paginated per platform conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"A feed card shows the cover thumbnail, title, author and role, date, audience chips (e.g. 'Grade 7 · Parents'), a 200-character plain-text excerpt and the attachment count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Detail /announcements/[id] (GET /api/announcements/:id; allowed for audience members, the author and ADMIN) shows the full sanitised body and attachments, and upserts AnnouncementRead.readAt on open.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"When requiresAck is set, an 'I acknowledge' button calls POST /api/announcements/:id/ack (audience members only) and stores acknowledgedAt. The button then reads 'Acknowledged on 14 Sep', shown in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"A course 'Announcements' tab (registered in src/config/course-tabs.ts) lists announcements whose audience includes that course (GET /api/announcements?courseId=).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"In the parent feed, an item with a grade, section or course audience is labelled with the linked child it relates to ('For Sam').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; AC-8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Manage view /announcements/manage (GET /api/announcements/manage): teachers see the announcements they authored, admins see all, including expired and archived ones. Columns: status, audience summary, reach, read %, and acknowledged % when required.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; AC-6; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"A per-announcement stats page (GET /api/announcements/:id/stats; author or ADMIN) shows counts and a recipient table (name, role, read at, acknowledged at) with Unread / Not acknowledged filters and CSV export via ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; API table; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Send reminder' (POST /api/announcements/:id/remind; author or ADMIN) notifies only recipients who have not acknowledged (type announcement.reminder). A second reminder within 24 hours is refused. A refused reminder returns 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT; the architect picks one.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type announcement.published (category COMMUNICATION, default email true, mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck) and the type announcement.reminder in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; FR-6.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Send announcement.published exactly once, when the announcement first becomes visible: immediately on publish-now, or by publishDueAnnouncements() in the maintenance run for scheduled ones. notifiedAt is set atomically to keep this idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; AC-4; Test Requirements › Integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The email uses the generic-notification template with the title, the first 300 characters of the body as plain text, and a 'Read announcement' button linking to /announcements/[id].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Editing the audience after publish does not re-notify.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table (PATCH notes)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Register file access context 'announcement'. Access is allowed for audience members, the author and admins, and for everyone, including anonymous users, when the announcement is isPublic and published. This covers the cover image and attachments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"getPublicNews({ page }) returns public, published, non-expired announcements. GET /api/public/news exposes it without authentication and is added to public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; API table; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Announcements' sidebar entry for all roles, with an unread count badge from GET /api/announcements/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"TEACHER and ADMIN see a 'New announcement' button on the feed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"REST endpoints exactly as listed in the PRD API table: GET/POST /api/announcements, GET unread-count, GET/PATCH /:id, POST /:id/archive, POST /:id/ack, POST preview-audience, GET manage, GET /:id/stats, POST /:id/remind, GET /api/public/news. Each uses thin Zod handlers and the platform response/error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context › Code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed 6 announcements: school-wide welcome (pinned, public), Grade 7 parents field-trip consent (requires ack), MATH-7A homework club (by Tom), staff meeting (STAFF), sports day notice scheduled 2 days ahead (public), and an expired exam timetable notice.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Services go in src/server/announcements/ (announcements-service.ts and audience.ts), following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 heading; Platform Context › Code layout\"}\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: use only Material UI (@mui/material 9.5.0, icons, MUI X). Look up every component through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. No banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, notistack, etc.). Toasts go through useToast(), confirmations use Dialog, pickers use Autocomplete, and Markdown renders to MUI components. If mui-mcp is unreachable, report a blocker. QA must verify there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › UI component rule (item 6)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the feed query for a parent with 3 children returns in under 200 ms with 2,000 announcements. Membership is resolved through SQL joins on audience rows, never by loading all recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 1 Performance\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces access server-side. A teacher who submits a SCHOOL audience gets 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security; AC-3; Platform Context › requireRole\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: sanitise Markdown bodies as in PRD-08 (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize through the existing MarkdownView), including excerpts and the plain-text email body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: unread dots carry screen-reader text 'Unread'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 3 Accessibility\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Privacy: users only see announcements whose audience includes them. Detail, ack, file and stats endpoints return 403/404 to non-members. Scheduled and expired items are hidden from feeds and from non-author detail.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goal 2; FR-5.1; API table roles\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC. publishAt, expiresAt and the 'Acknowledged on' date are interpreted and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions; Assumptions\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse the existing services and components (notify, audit, registerFileAccess, csv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload, DataTable, UserPicker, useToast). Don't re-scaffold or rename existing routes or models. Keep lint, typecheck and existing tests passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Constraints\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Scope: no comments or reactions, no translation, no SMS. Don't implement the PRD-18 public website pages; only expose getPublicNews and /api/public/news.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Constraints\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for audience resolution per type and flag combination and for teacher permission rules. Integration tests that isUserInAudience matches resolveAudienceUserIds for every seed user (property-style) and that scheduled publish notification is idempotent. A Playwright e2e test: admin composes a targeted announcement with ack, parent reads and acknowledges, admin sees stats.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Use logger from src/lib/logger.ts, never console.log, in new code. The existing seed file's console.log convention may stay as it is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions\"}\n  ],\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Admin targets GRADE_LEVEL Grade 7 with parents only. The preview shows only Grade 7 parents, and after publishing only they see it.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-4\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-17\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Tom targets COURSE MATH-7A. MATH-7A students, their parents and Tom see it. A 7B student does not.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-6\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-17\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"Tom targets SCHOOL via the API and gets 403.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-10\", \"NFR-3\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"An announcement scheduled for 07:00 tomorrow is invisible until 07:00. Its notification is sent once, by the first maintenance run after 07:00.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-27\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"With requiresAck, 50 recipients and 30 acknowledged: stats show 60% acknowledged, the reminder notifies exactly 20 users, and a second reminder within 24h is refused.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-25\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"An expired announcement is absent from feeds but present in the author's manage view.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-23\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"GET /api/public/news returns public announcements without auth and omits non-public ones.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-31\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-8\", \"text\": \"Pat has Sam (7A) and a child in 6A. A 6A section announcement is labelled 'For <6A child's name>' in Pat's feed.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-22\", \"FR-5\"]}\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Do 'section members' mean only current academic-year SectionMember rows?\",\n        \"FR-15: Can a draft be saved with zero recipients, with the zero-recipient refusal applied only at publish/schedule time?\",\n        \"FR-25: Should a refused second reminder within 24h return 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT? And how is the last reminder time stored (a new column such as Announcement.lastRemindedAt, or derived from Notification rows)?\",\n        \"FR-1 vs FR-25: The FR-1 schema has no field for the reminder throttle. Is adding a nullable column acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-17: If more than 3 announcements are pinned, do the extra ones fall back into the newest-first list?\",\n        \"AC-8 / seed: The seed creates no 6A section and no ParentStudentLink rows. Should the seed (or the e2e/integration fixture) create the 6A child linked to Pat?\",\n        \"FR-12: Can an author edit an announcement after it is archived, or is archive terminal?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 section membership scope: defaulting to current academic year.\",\n        \"FR-15 draft with zero recipients: defaulting to allowed; refusal only on publish/schedule.\",\n        \"FR-25 reminder throttle status code and storage: architect decides. Suggested: a nullable lastRemindedAt column and 429 RATE_LIMITED.\",\n        \"FR-17 overflow pins: defaulting to the extra pinned items flowing into newest-first order.\",\n        \"AC-8 fixture: the test fixture creates the 6A child and the Pat link if the seed lacks them.\",\n        \"FR-12 archived edits: defaulting to archive being terminal for authors, with admins still able to edit.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":52143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5ee16ee-e095-4181-884c-a98d424b627c","uuid":"2605b767-3095-4c1c-b43d-99a169c5bb71","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:28:03.592Z","request_id":"req_011CgsfhBmE5n9wweNjSBcPf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NFpB3b2HUSr5bXgMYsXSPv":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T18:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-12: Announcements & News\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-012 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-12.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment or AnnouncementRead models and no AnnouncementStatus or AudienceType enums. They need a new migration, plus back-relations on User (authored announcements, reads) and FileObject (announcement attachments).\",\n    \"The audience-resolution data already exists: User.status/archivedAt (ACTIVE, non-archived filter), StudentProfile.gradeLevelId, ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId), Section.homeroomTeacherId and gradeLevelId, SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId), Course.teacherId + coTeacherIds String[] + sectionId + academicYearId, and Enrollment.status (ACTIVE).\",\n    \"File access registry: src/server/files/access.ts exports registerFileAccess(context, resolver). Built-in contexts are registered in src/server/files/contexts.ts. Resolvers receive null for anonymous callers, which is what the public-announcement case needs.\",\n    \"Notification types live in src/server/notifications/types.ts with {category, mandatoryInApp, ...}. COMMUNICATION is already a category. notify() is in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\",\n    \"The 'generic-notification' email template is already registered in src/server/email/render.ts.\",\n    \"The maintenance run is POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (CRON_SECRET-gated). It calls dispatchEmails, sendDueReminders and the quiz maintenance passes. publishDueAnnouncements() should be added there, following src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts (batched and idempotent).\",\n    \"src/config/public-routes.ts has PUBLIC_API_PATHS. '/api/public/news' must be added (FR-8 / API table).\",\n    \"src/config/course-tabs.ts is where the course 'Announcements' tab goes (FR-5.4). src/config/navigation.ts NavItem has no badge field, so the unread-count badge needs a small extension. src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx already shows a Badge-and-poll pattern to reuse.\",\n    \"Shared components are in src/components/<Name>/ (MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, FileList, DataTable, ConfirmDialog, UserPicker, EmptyState, PageHeader, StatCard, Toast/useToast), not in src/components/shared/ as the platform context says. Reuse them where they are.\",\n    \"src/server/csv.ts already handles CSV export (FR-6.2). src/server/rate-limit.ts exists, but the 24h reminder throttle is a per-announcement business rule, not a rate limit.\",\n    \"Seed personas: Tom (teacher@), Sam (student@), Pat (parent@). Course lookups by code (MATH-7A) go through findCourse and skip when the course is missing. Neither prisma/seed.ts nor the scripts create 7A/7B/6A sections or ParentStudentLink rows. Seed announcements that target Grade 7, MATH-7A or 6A must follow the same skip-if-missing pattern.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums AnnouncementStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED, ARCHIVED) and AudienceType (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE), plus the models Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment and AnnouncementRead (composite PK announcementId+userId), exactly as specified, in a new prisma migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Validate title ≤ 150 chars and body (Markdown) ≤ 20,000 chars in a shared Zod schema at src/lib/validators/announcements.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (field comments); Platform Context › Validation\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) in src/server/announcements/audience.ts returns the deduplicated ids of ACTIVE, non-archived users. SCHOOL = everyone, STAFF = ADMIN + TEACHER, ROLE = users whose role is refId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"GRADE_LEVEL audience: students whose profile grade level is refId (includeStudents), their linked parents (includeParents), and teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade level (includeTeachers).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"SECTION audience: section members, their parents, the homeroom teacher and the teachers of the section's courses, each gated by the same include flags. 'Section members' is taken to mean current academic-year SectionMember rows.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"COURSE audience: students with ACTIVE enrollment, their parents, and the course teacher plus co-teachers (Course.coTeacherIds), each gated by the include flags.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"isUserInAudience(user, audiences) answers membership for one user through targeted SQL/Prisma joins, without loading every recipient. It must agree with resolveAudienceUserIds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; NFR Performance; Test Requirements › Integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"The audience service is generic (no announcement-specific coupling) so PRD-14 calendar events can reuse it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"ADMIN may target any audience type and set isPublic.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"TEACHER may target only COURSE audiences for courses they manage (teacher or co-teacher) and SECTION audiences for the section they homeroom. Any other audience, or isPublic=true, is rejected server-side with 403 FORBIDDEN.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; NFR Security; AC-3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"STUDENT and PARENT cannot create announcements (403).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Authors may edit their own announcements, and admins may edit or archive any. Archiving sets status ARCHIVED. When an admin changes someone else's announcement, write an AuditLog row through audit().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; API table (archive); Platform Context › audit()\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The composer pages /announcements/new and /announcements/[id]/edit have: title, body (the PRD-08 MarkdownEditor), optional cover image, attachments, an audience builder (rows of type → entity picker → include students/parents/teachers checkboxes), pinned, requires acknowledgement, public (admins only), publish now / schedule (publishAt) / save draft, and an expiry date.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"A live recipient count next to the audience builder ('Will reach 412 people: 180 students, 214 parents, 18 teachers'), computed by POST /api/announcements/preview-audience, which returns counts by role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Publishing (now or scheduled) with zero resolved recipients is refused with a VALIDATION_ERROR. Drafts may have zero recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Scheduling sets status SCHEDULED with publishAt. An announcement becomes visible once publishAt <= now, evaluated at read time, so a cron is not needed for visibility.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Feed /announcements (GET /api/announcements) for all roles: published, non-expired announcements whose audience includes the user. Up to 3 pinned show first, then newest. Unread items show a dot. Filter tabs: All / Unread / Requires acknowledgement. Paginated per platform conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"A feed card shows the cover thumbnail, title, author and role, date, audience chips (e.g. 'Grade 7 · Parents'), a 200-character plain-text excerpt and the attachment count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Detail /announcements/[id] (GET /api/announcements/:id; allowed for audience members, the author and ADMIN) shows the full sanitised body and attachments, and upserts AnnouncementRead.readAt on open.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"When requiresAck is set, an 'I acknowledge' button calls POST /api/announcements/:id/ack (audience members only) and stores acknowledgedAt. The button then reads 'Acknowledged on 14 Sep', shown in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"A course 'Announcements' tab (registered in src/config/course-tabs.ts) lists announcements whose audience includes that course (GET /api/announcements?courseId=).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"In the parent feed, an item with a grade, section or course audience is labelled with the linked child it relates to ('For Sam').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; AC-8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Manage view /announcements/manage (GET /api/announcements/manage): teachers see the announcements they authored, admins see all, including expired and archived ones. Columns: status, audience summary, reach, read %, and acknowledged % when required.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; AC-6; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"A per-announcement stats page (GET /api/announcements/:id/stats; author or ADMIN) shows counts and a recipient table (name, role, read at, acknowledged at) with Unread / Not acknowledged filters and CSV export via ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; API table; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Send reminder' (POST /api/announcements/:id/remind; author or ADMIN) notifies only recipients who have not acknowledged (type announcement.reminder). A second reminder within 24 hours is refused. A refused reminder returns 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT; the architect picks one.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type announcement.published (category COMMUNICATION, default email true, mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck) and the type announcement.reminder in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; FR-6.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Send announcement.published exactly once, when the announcement first becomes visible: immediately on publish-now, or by publishDueAnnouncements() in the maintenance run for scheduled ones. notifiedAt is set atomically to keep this idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; AC-4; Test Requirements › Integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The email uses the generic-notification template with the title, the first 300 characters of the body as plain text, and a 'Read announcement' button linking to /announcements/[id].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Editing the audience after publish does not re-notify.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table (PATCH notes)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Register file access context 'announcement'. Access is allowed for audience members, the author and admins, and for everyone, including anonymous users, when the announcement is isPublic and published. This covers the cover image and attachments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"getPublicNews({ page }) returns public, published, non-expired announcements. GET /api/public/news exposes it without authentication and is added to public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; API table; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Announcements' sidebar entry for all roles, with an unread count badge from GET /api/announcements/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"TEACHER and ADMIN see a 'New announcement' button on the feed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"REST endpoints exactly as listed in the PRD API table: GET/POST /api/announcements, GET unread-count, GET/PATCH /:id, POST /:id/archive, POST /:id/ack, POST preview-audience, GET manage, GET /:id/stats, POST /:id/remind, GET /api/public/news. Each uses thin Zod handlers and the platform response/error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context › Code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed 6 announcements: school-wide welcome (pinned, public), Grade 7 parents field-trip consent (requires ack), MATH-7A homework club (by Tom), staff meeting (STAFF), sports day notice scheduled 2 days ahead (public), and an expired exam timetable notice.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Services go in src/server/announcements/ (announcements-service.ts and audience.ts), following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 heading; Platform Context › Code layout\"}\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: use only Material UI (@mui/material 9.5.0, icons, MUI X). Look up every component through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. No banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, notistack, etc.). Toasts go through useToast(), confirmations use Dialog, pickers use Autocomplete, and Markdown renders to MUI components. If mui-mcp is unreachable, report a blocker. QA must verify there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › UI component rule (item 6)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the feed query for a parent with 3 children returns in under 200 ms with 2,000 announcements. Membership is resolved through SQL joins on audience rows, never by loading all recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 1 Performance\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces access server-side. A teacher who submits a SCHOOL audience gets 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security; AC-3; Platform Context › requireRole\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: sanitise Markdown bodies as in PRD-08 (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize through the existing MarkdownView), including excerpts and the plain-text email body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: unread dots carry screen-reader text 'Unread'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 3 Accessibility\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Privacy: users only see announcements whose audience includes them. Detail, ack, file and stats endpoints return 403/404 to non-members. Scheduled and expired items are hidden from feeds and from non-author detail.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goal 2; FR-5.1; API table roles\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC. publishAt, expiresAt and the 'Acknowledged on' date are interpreted and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions; Assumptions\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse the existing services and components (notify, audit, registerFileAccess, csv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload, DataTable, UserPicker, useToast). Don't re-scaffold or rename existing routes or models. Keep lint, typecheck and existing tests passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Constraints\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Scope: no comments or reactions, no translation, no SMS. Don't implement the PRD-18 public website pages; only expose getPublicNews and /api/public/news.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Constraints\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for audience resolution per type and flag combination and for teacher permission rules. Integration tests that isUserInAudience matches resolveAudienceUserIds for every seed user (property-style) and that scheduled publish notification is idempotent. A Playwright e2e test: admin composes a targeted announcement with ack, parent reads and acknowledges, admin sees stats.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Use logger from src/lib/logger.ts, never console.log, in new code. The existing seed file's console.log convention may stay as it is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions\"}\n  ],\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Admin targets GRADE_LEVEL Grade 7 with parents only. The preview shows only Grade 7 parents, and after publishing only they see it.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-4\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-17\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Tom targets COURSE MATH-7A. MATH-7A students, their parents and Tom see it. A 7B student does not.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-6\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-17\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"Tom targets SCHOOL via the API and gets 403.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-10\", \"NFR-3\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"An announcement scheduled for 07:00 tomorrow is invisible until 07:00. Its notification is sent once, by the first maintenance run after 07:00.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-27\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"With requiresAck, 50 recipients and 30 acknowledged: stats show 60% acknowledged, the reminder notifies exactly 20 users, and a second reminder within 24h is refused.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-25\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"An expired announcement is absent from feeds but present in the author's manage view.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-23\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"GET /api/public/news returns public announcements without auth and omits non-public ones.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-31\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-8\", \"text\": \"Pat has Sam (7A) and a child in 6A. A 6A section announcement is labelled 'For <6A child's name>' in Pat's feed.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-22\", \"FR-5\"]}\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Do 'section members' mean only current academic-year SectionMember rows?\",\n        \"FR-15: Can a draft be saved with zero recipients, with the zero-recipient refusal applied only at publish/schedule time?\",\n        \"FR-25: Should a refused second reminder within 24h return 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT? And how is the last reminder time stored (a new column such as Announcement.lastRemindedAt, or derived from Notification rows)?\",\n        \"FR-1 vs FR-25: The FR-1 schema has no field for the reminder throttle. Is adding a nullable column acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-17: If more than 3 announcements are pinned, do the extra ones fall back into the newest-first list?\",\n        \"AC-8 / seed: The seed creates no 6A section and no ParentStudentLink rows. Should the seed (or the e2e/integration fixture) create the 6A child linked to Pat?\",\n        \"FR-12: Can an author edit an announcement after it is archived, or is archive terminal?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 section membership scope: defaulting to current academic year.\",\n        \"FR-15 draft with zero recipients: defaulting to allowed; refusal only on publish/schedule.\",\n        \"FR-25 reminder throttle status code and storage: architect decides. Suggested: a nullable lastRemindedAt column and 429 RATE_LIMITED.\",\n        \"FR-17 overflow pins: defaulting to the extra pinned items flowing into newest-first order.\",\n        \"AC-8 fixture: the test fixture creates the 6A child and the Pat link if the seed lacks them.\",\n        \"FR-12 archived edits: defaulting to archive being terminal for authors, with admins still able to edit.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFpB3b2HUSr5bXgMYsXSPv","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5ee16ee-e095-4181-884c-a98d424b627c","uuid":"e53d4629-e3fa-471e-8333-8383690b20c7","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:28:03.778Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/requirements.json","content":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T18:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-12: Announcements & News\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-012 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-12.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment or AnnouncementRead models and no AnnouncementStatus or AudienceType enums. They need a new migration, plus back-relations on User (authored announcements, reads) and FileObject (announcement attachments).\",\n    \"The audience-resolution data already exists: User.status/archivedAt (ACTIVE, non-archived filter), StudentProfile.gradeLevelId, ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId), Section.homeroomTeacherId and gradeLevelId, SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId), Course.teacherId + coTeacherIds String[] + sectionId + academicYearId, and Enrollment.status (ACTIVE).\",\n    \"File access registry: src/server/files/access.ts exports registerFileAccess(context, resolver). Built-in contexts are registered in src/server/files/contexts.ts. Resolvers receive null for anonymous callers, which is what the public-announcement case needs.\",\n    \"Notification types live in src/server/notifications/types.ts with {category, mandatoryInApp, ...}. COMMUNICATION is already a category. notify() is in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\",\n    \"The 'generic-notification' email template is already registered in src/server/email/render.ts.\",\n    \"The maintenance run is POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (CRON_SECRET-gated). It calls dispatchEmails, sendDueReminders and the quiz maintenance passes. publishDueAnnouncements() should be added there, following src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts (batched and idempotent).\",\n    \"src/config/public-routes.ts has PUBLIC_API_PATHS. '/api/public/news' must be added (FR-8 / API table).\",\n    \"src/config/course-tabs.ts is where the course 'Announcements' tab goes (FR-5.4). src/config/navigation.ts NavItem has no badge field, so the unread-count badge needs a small extension. src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx already shows a Badge-and-poll pattern to reuse.\",\n    \"Shared components are in src/components/<Name>/ (MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, FileList, DataTable, ConfirmDialog, UserPicker, EmptyState, PageHeader, StatCard, Toast/useToast), not in src/components/shared/ as the platform context says. Reuse them where they are.\",\n    \"src/server/csv.ts already handles CSV export (FR-6.2). src/server/rate-limit.ts exists, but the 24h reminder throttle is a per-announcement business rule, not a rate limit.\",\n    \"Seed personas: Tom (teacher@), Sam (student@), Pat (parent@). Course lookups by code (MATH-7A) go through findCourse and skip when the course is missing. Neither prisma/seed.ts nor the scripts create 7A/7B/6A sections or ParentStudentLink rows. Seed announcements that target Grade 7, MATH-7A or 6A must follow the same skip-if-missing pattern.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums AnnouncementStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED, ARCHIVED) and AudienceType (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE), plus the models Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment and AnnouncementRead (composite PK announcementId+userId), exactly as specified, in a new prisma migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Validate title ≤ 150 chars and body (Markdown) ≤ 20,000 chars in a shared Zod schema at src/lib/validators/announcements.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (field comments); Platform Context › Validation\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) in src/server/announcements/audience.ts returns the deduplicated ids of ACTIVE, non-archived users. SCHOOL = everyone, STAFF = ADMIN + TEACHER, ROLE = users whose role is refId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"GRADE_LEVEL audience: students whose profile grade level is refId (includeStudents), their linked parents (includeParents), and teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade level (includeTeachers).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"SECTION audience: section members, their parents, the homeroom teacher and the teachers of the section's courses, each gated by the same include flags. 'Section members' is taken to mean current academic-year SectionMember rows.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"COURSE audience: students with ACTIVE enrollment, their parents, and the course teacher plus co-teachers (Course.coTeacherIds), each gated by the include flags.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"isUserInAudience(user, audiences) answers membership for one user through targeted SQL/Prisma joins, without loading every recipient. It must agree with resolveAudienceUserIds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; NFR Performance; Test Requirements › Integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"The audience service is generic (no announcement-specific coupling) so PRD-14 calendar events can reuse it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"ADMIN may target any audience type and set isPublic.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"TEACHER may target only COURSE audiences for courses they manage (teacher or co-teacher) and SECTION audiences for the section they homeroom. Any other audience, or isPublic=true, is rejected server-side with 403 FORBIDDEN.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; NFR Security; AC-3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"STUDENT and PARENT cannot create announcements (403).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Authors may edit their own announcements, and admins may edit or archive any. Archiving sets status ARCHIVED. When an admin changes someone else's announcement, write an AuditLog row through audit().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; API table (archive); Platform Context › audit()\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The composer pages /announcements/new and /announcements/[id]/edit have: title, body (the PRD-08 MarkdownEditor), optional cover image, attachments, an audience builder (rows of type → entity picker → include students/parents/teachers checkboxes), pinned, requires acknowledgement, public (admins only), publish now / schedule (publishAt) / save draft, and an expiry date.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"A live recipient count next to the audience builder ('Will reach 412 people: 180 students, 214 parents, 18 teachers'), computed by POST /api/announcements/preview-audience, which returns counts by role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Publishing (now or scheduled) with zero resolved recipients is refused with a VALIDATION_ERROR. Drafts may have zero recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Scheduling sets status SCHEDULED with publishAt. An announcement becomes visible once publishAt <= now, evaluated at read time, so a cron is not needed for visibility.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Feed /announcements (GET /api/announcements) for all roles: published, non-expired announcements whose audience includes the user. Up to 3 pinned show first, then newest. Unread items show a dot. Filter tabs: All / Unread / Requires acknowledgement. Paginated per platform conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"A feed card shows the cover thumbnail, title, author and role, date, audience chips (e.g. 'Grade 7 · Parents'), a 200-character plain-text excerpt and the attachment count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Detail /announcements/[id] (GET /api/announcements/:id; allowed for audience members, the author and ADMIN) shows the full sanitised body and attachments, and upserts AnnouncementRead.readAt on open.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"When requiresAck is set, an 'I acknowledge' button calls POST /api/announcements/:id/ack (audience members only) and stores acknowledgedAt. The button then reads 'Acknowledged on 14 Sep', shown in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"A course 'Announcements' tab (registered in src/config/course-tabs.ts) lists announcements whose audience includes that course (GET /api/announcements?courseId=).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"In the parent feed, an item with a grade, section or course audience is labelled with the linked child it relates to ('For Sam').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; AC-8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Manage view /announcements/manage (GET /api/announcements/manage): teachers see the announcements they authored, admins see all, including expired and archived ones. Columns: status, audience summary, reach, read %, and acknowledged % when required.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; AC-6; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"A per-announcement stats page (GET /api/announcements/:id/stats; author or ADMIN) shows counts and a recipient table (name, role, read at, acknowledged at) with Unread / Not acknowledged filters and CSV export via ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; API table; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Send reminder' (POST /api/announcements/:id/remind; author or ADMIN) notifies only recipients who have not acknowledged (type announcement.reminder). A second reminder within 24 hours is refused. A refused reminder returns 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT; the architect picks one.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type announcement.published (category COMMUNICATION, default email true, mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck) and the type announcement.reminder in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; FR-6.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Send announcement.published exactly once, when the announcement first becomes visible: immediately on publish-now, or by publishDueAnnouncements() in the maintenance run for scheduled ones. notifiedAt is set atomically to keep this idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; AC-4; Test Requirements › Integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The email uses the generic-notification template with the title, the first 300 characters of the body as plain text, and a 'Read announcement' button linking to /announcements/[id].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Editing the audience after publish does not re-notify.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table (PATCH notes)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Register file access context 'announcement'. Access is allowed for audience members, the author and admins, and for everyone, including anonymous users, when the announcement is isPublic and published. This covers the cover image and attachments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"getPublicNews({ page }) returns public, published, non-expired announcements. GET /api/public/news exposes it without authentication and is added to public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; API table; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Announcements' sidebar entry for all roles, with an unread count badge from GET /api/announcements/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"TEACHER and ADMIN see a 'New announcement' button on the feed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"REST endpoints exactly as listed in the PRD API table: GET/POST /api/announcements, GET unread-count, GET/PATCH /:id, POST /:id/archive, POST /:id/ack, POST preview-audience, GET manage, GET /:id/stats, POST /:id/remind, GET /api/public/news. Each uses thin Zod handlers and the platform response/error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context › Code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed 6 announcements: school-wide welcome (pinned, public), Grade 7 parents field-trip consent (requires ack), MATH-7A homework club (by Tom), staff meeting (STAFF), sports day notice scheduled 2 days ahead (public), and an expired exam timetable notice.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Services go in src/server/announcements/ (announcements-service.ts and audience.ts), following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 heading; Platform Context › Code layout\"}\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: use only Material UI (@mui/material 9.5.0, icons, MUI X). Look up every component through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. No banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, notistack, etc.). Toasts go through useToast(), confirmations use Dialog, pickers use Autocomplete, and Markdown renders to MUI components. If mui-mcp is unreachable, report a blocker. QA must verify there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › UI component rule (item 6)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the feed query for a parent with 3 children returns in under 200 ms with 2,000 announcements. Membership is resolved through SQL joins on audience rows, never by loading all recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 1 Performance\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces access server-side. A teacher who submits a SCHOOL audience gets 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security; AC-3; Platform Context › requireRole\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: sanitise Markdown bodies as in PRD-08 (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize through the existing MarkdownView), including excerpts and the plain-text email body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: unread dots carry screen-reader text 'Unread'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 3 Accessibility\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Privacy: users only see announcements whose audience includes them. Detail, ack, file and stats endpoints return 403/404 to non-members. Scheduled and expired items are hidden from feeds and from non-author detail.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goal 2; FR-5.1; API table roles\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC. publishAt, expiresAt and the 'Acknowledged on' date are interpreted and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions; Assumptions\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse the existing services and components (notify, audit, registerFileAccess, csv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload, DataTable, UserPicker, useToast). Don't re-scaffold or rename existing routes or models. Keep lint, typecheck and existing tests passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Constraints\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Scope: no comments or reactions, no translation, no SMS. Don't implement the PRD-18 public website pages; only expose getPublicNews and /api/public/news.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Constraints\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for audience resolution per type and flag combination and for teacher permission rules. Integration tests that isUserInAudience matches resolveAudienceUserIds for every seed user (property-style) and that scheduled publish notification is idempotent. A Playwright e2e test: admin composes a targeted announcement with ack, parent reads and acknowledges, admin sees stats.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Use logger from src/lib/logger.ts, never console.log, in new code. The existing seed file's console.log convention may stay as it is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions\"}\n  ],\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Admin targets GRADE_LEVEL Grade 7 with parents only. The preview shows only Grade 7 parents, and after publishing only they see it.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-4\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-17\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Tom targets COURSE MATH-7A. MATH-7A students, their parents and Tom see it. A 7B student does not.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-6\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-17\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"Tom targets SCHOOL via the API and gets 403.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-10\", \"NFR-3\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"An announcement scheduled for 07:00 tomorrow is invisible until 07:00. Its notification is sent once, by the first maintenance run after 07:00.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-27\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"With requiresAck, 50 recipients and 30 acknowledged: stats show 60% acknowledged, the reminder notifies exactly 20 users, and a second reminder within 24h is refused.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-25\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"An expired announcement is absent from feeds but present in the author's manage view.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-23\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"GET /api/public/news returns public announcements without auth and omits non-public ones.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-31\"]},\n    {\"id\": \"AC-8\", \"text\": \"Pat has Sam (7A) and a child in 6A. A 6A section announcement is labelled 'For <6A child's name>' in Pat's feed.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-22\", \"FR-5\"]}\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-5: Do 'section members' mean only current academic-year SectionMember rows?\",\n        \"FR-15: Can a draft be saved with zero recipients, with the zero-recipient refusal applied only at publish/schedule time?\",\n        \"FR-25: Should a refused second reminder within 24h return 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT? And how is the last reminder time stored (a new column such as Announcement.lastRemindedAt, or derived from Notification rows)?\",\n        \"FR-1 vs FR-25: The FR-1 schema has no field for the reminder throttle. Is adding a nullable column acceptable?\",\n        \"FR-17: If more than 3 announcements are pinned, do the extra ones fall back into the newest-first list?\",\n        \"AC-8 / seed: The seed creates no 6A section and no ParentStudentLink rows. Should the seed (or the e2e/integration fixture) create the 6A child linked to Pat?\",\n        \"FR-12: Can an author edit an announcement after it is archived, or is archive terminal?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-5 section membership scope: defaulting to current academic year.\",\n        \"FR-15 draft with zero recipients: defaulting to allowed; refusal only on publish/schedule.\",\n        \"FR-25 reminder throttle status code and storage: architect decides. Suggested: a nullable lastRemindedAt column and 429 RATE_LIMITED.\",\n        \"FR-17 overflow pins: defaulting to the extra pinned items flowing into newest-first order.\",\n        \"AC-8 fixture: the test fixture creates the 6A child and the Pat link if the seed lacks them.\",\n        \"FR-12 archived edits: defaulting to archive being terminal for authors, with admins still able to edit.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":100,"newStart":1,"newLines":105,"lines":[" {","-  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",","-  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",","+  \"ticketId\": \"SH-12\",","+  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T18:00:00Z\",","   \"phase\": \"intake\",","   \"version\": \"1.0\",","-  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\",","-  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-011 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-11.\",","+  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-12: Announcements & News\",","+  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-012 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-12.\",","   \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",","   \"brownfieldFindings\": [","-    \"Assignment.categoryId, Quiz.categoryId, Course.gradingScaleId and every PRD-11 model (GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride, ReportCard) are missing from prisma/schema.prisma. They need a new migration.\",","-    \"GradeExemption (schema.prisma ~L801) already exists. Its comment says a row is the PRD-11 'exclude from gradebook' flag, so sync maps it to Grade.excused = true.\",","-    \"Submission has finalScore and returnedAt. A submission counts as returned when returnedAt is non-null.\",","-    \"Quiz.isPractice exists. Practice quizzes must never sync.\",","-    \"No function named getStudentQuizScore exists. The closest helpers are src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) and quiz-service scoreOf. The architect should create or name getStudentQuizScore from these instead of duplicating them.\",","-    \"Section.homeroomTeacherId exists. Homeroom access already exists in src/server/auth/student-access.ts and attendance-service.\",","-    \"src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts has Decimal helpers, and src/server/csv.ts has CSV export. Reuse both.\",","-    \"src/config/student-tabs.ts has courses, attendance and assignments. Add grades and report-cards here.\",","-    \"No gradebook:backfill npm script exists yet. Seeding runs through 'db:seed' (tsx prisma/seed.ts).\"","+    \"prisma/schema.prisma has no Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment or AnnouncementRead models and no AnnouncementStatus or AudienceType enums. They need a new migration, plus back-relations on User (authored announcements, reads) and FileObject (announcement attachments).\",","+    \"The audience-resolution data already exists: User.status/archivedAt (ACTIVE, non-archived filter), StudentProfile.gradeLevelId, ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId), Section.homeroomTeacherId and gradeLevelId, SectionMember(studentId, academicYearId), Course.teacherId + coTeacherIds String[] + sectionId + academicYearId, and Enrollment.status (ACTIVE).\",","+    \"File access registry: src/server/files/access.ts exports registerFileAccess(context, resolver). Built-in contexts are registered in src/server/files/contexts.ts. Resolvers receive null for anonymous callers, which is what the public-announcement case needs.\",","+    \"Notification types live in src/server/notifications/types.ts with {category, mandatoryInApp, ...}. COMMUNICATION is already a category. notify() is in src/server/notifications/notify.ts.\",","+    \"The 'generic-notification' email template is already registered in src/server/email/render.ts.\",","+    \"The maintenance run is POST /api/internal/email/dispatch (CRON_SECRET-gated). It calls dispatchEmails, sendDueReminders and the quiz maintenance passes. publishDueAnnouncements() should be added there, following src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts (batched and idempotent).\",","+    \"src/config/public-routes.ts has PUBLIC_API_PATHS. '/api/public/news' must be added (FR-8 / API table).\",","+    \"src/config/course-tabs.ts is where the course 'Announcements' tab goes (FR-5.4). src/config/navigation.ts NavItem has no badge field, so the unread-count badge needs a small extension. src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx already shows a Badge-and-poll pattern to reuse.\",","+    \"Shared components are in src/components/<Name>/ (MarkdownEditor, MarkdownView, FileUpload, FileList, DataTable, ConfirmDialog, UserPicker, EmptyState, PageHeader, StatCard, Toast/useToast), not in src/components/shared/ as the platform context says. Reuse them where they are.\",","+    \"src/server/csv.ts already handles CSV export (FR-6.2). src/server/rate-limit.ts exists, but the 24h reminder throttle is a per-announcement business rule, not a rate limit.\",","+    \"Seed personas: Tom (teacher@), Sam (student@), Pat (parent@). Course lookups by code (MATH-7A) go through findCourse and skip when the course is missing. Neither prisma/seed.ts nor the scripts create 7A/7B/6A sections or ParentStudentLink rows. Seed announcements that target Grade 7, MATH-7A or 6A must follow the same skip-if-missing pattern.\"","   ],","   \"functionalRequirements\": [","-    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums GradeItemSource (ASSIGNMENT, QUIZ, MANUAL) and ReportCardStatus (DRAFT, PUBLISHED), plus the models GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride and ReportCard, exactly as specified, in a new prisma migrate migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Course.gradingScaleId (nullable, null = school default scale) and nullable categoryId to Assignment and Quiz. Add a category select to the assignment editor and the quiz editor.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 trailing paragraph\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a GradeItem (source + sourceId, title, maxPoints, dueAt, category). Its term is the one containing dueAt (assignment) or availableUntil (quiz), falling back to the current term.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Unpublishing or archiving the source sets GradeItem.isVisible = false. Deleting the source deletes the GradeItem.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"When a submission is returned, upsert its Grade with score = finalScore. Saving a grade without returning it must not sync.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; AC-3\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"A grade exemption (the existing GradeExemption row) sets Grade.excused = true. Removing the exemption clears it.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2 'Exemptions set excused = true'; schema.prisma GradeExemption comment. The PRD does not state the clearing behaviour.\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and its results are visible, upsert Grade.score from the student's policy-applied quiz score (getStudentQuizScore), scaled to the quiz maxScore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Add an idempotent one-time backfill script, `npm run gradebook:backfill`. It creates GradeItems and Grades for assignments, quizzes, submissions and attempts that existed before this PRD, and the seed runs it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4; Test Requirements (backfill idempotency)\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI and API except for comment. Grades on manual items are fully editable.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5; API PATCH /api/grade-items/:id notes\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Add pure grade-calculation functions in src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts. They consider only visible items in the term whose grade is not excused. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and marked missing (counts as 0). Ungraded items not marked missing are ignored.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; AC-5\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Per category, drop the dropLowest lowest item percentages (never dropping every item). categoryPercent = Σscore / Σmax × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; AC-2\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Course percent is the weighted mean of category percentages, using only categories with at least one counted item and re-normalising weights to those categories. Uncategorised items form an implicit 'Uncategorised' category. A course with no categories uses total points earned / total possible × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Round the percent half-up to 1 decimal place, then pick the first band of the effective scale (course scale, else school default) where percent >= minPercent. Example: 89.95 → 90.0 → A− in the seed scale.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; Test Requirements (89.95 → 90.0)\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"TermGradeOverride percent and letter replace the computed values when set. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; AC-6\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The calculation must reproduce the worked example: Homework 40% (18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60% (70/100) gives 78.0% C+. The gradebook and the student Grades tab must both show it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6; AC-1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Add an admin page /admin/grading-scales with CRUD for grading scales and a band editor (letter, minimum %, optional GPA, descriptor). Validate that bands are strictly descending, the lowest minimum is 0, letters are unique, and exactly one scale is the default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add course Gradebook settings where the teacher manages categories (name, weight, drop lowest, order). A live sum indicator shows the weight total, and saving is refused unless weights total 100. Settings also include a course grading scale select that defaults to the school default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Gradebook' tab for TEACHER/ADMIN with a term selector and an MUI X DataGrid (MIT). Columns are: students sorted by last name first, then items grouped by category via columnGroupingModel (header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages, then term percent + letter in bold. Use a sticky header (no pinned columns), horizontal scrolling and virtualisation for up to 60 students × 120 items.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Grid cells show the score, 'EX' (excused), 'M' (missing, red) or '—' (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Manual-item cells are editable through processRowUpdate. A user types a number, Enter or arrow keys move between cells, E marks excused, M marks missing and Delete clears. Changes save on blur with an optimistic update and per-cell error state.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; Test Requirements (Playwright keyboard editing)\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a synced cell opens its source (the submission grading page or the quiz attempt).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Add manual item' dialog with title, category, max points, date and term (POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.5; API table\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a student row action, 'Override term grade / comment', that opens a dialog with percent, letter and teacher comment (max 1,000 chars) and calls PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.6; FR-1 TermGradeOverride; API table\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Item column menu actions: hide/show the item to students (isVisible), set all ungraded grades to missing (only after the due date), and view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.7\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Export CSV' exports the grid as displayed, reusing src/server/csv.ts or papaparse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.8\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Grades' in src/config/student-tabs.ts. For the selected term it shows one card per course with percent, letter and colour (≥80 green, 60–79 amber, <60 red). Expanding a card shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Add a /grades page for STUDENT and PARENT (parents get a child selector) that shows the same content as the Grades tab. Add a sidebar nav entry in src/config/navigation.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Platform Context 'A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry'\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course tab 'Grades' for STUDENT/PARENT that shows that course's items only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.3\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Add /admin/report-cards: select a term, then see a table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated / Draft / Published) and missing-data warnings (for example ungraded items, or no teacher comment for a course).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"'Generate drafts' (POST /api/report-cards/generate) builds a snapshot for each filtered student. It contains the school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year. For each course it records subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor and teacher comment. It also records the term attendance summary (rate, absences, lates) and the grading scale legend.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Regenerating refreshes the snapshot of DRAFT cards only. PUBLISHED cards are never changed by regeneration or by later grade edits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; AC-8; Test Requirements (snapshot immutability)\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a per-card review page with a rendered preview. The homeroom comment is editable by the homeroom teacher or an admin, and the principal comment by an admin only (PATCH /api/report-cards/:id).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; API table\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a /report-cards page where homeroom teachers list their section's drafts to write comments. Add a nav entry for TEACHER.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; Platform Context nav convention\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Publish (per card or in bulk for the filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED, publishedAt and publishedById, and sends report_card.published to the student and parents. Unpublish is admin only, requires a reason and writes an audit entry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.4; API POST /api/report-cards/publish · /unpublish\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Add a print view /report-cards/[id]/print: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for the principal and homeroom teacher, and @media print rules that hide the app sidebar. A 'Print / Save as PDF' button calls window.print(). Bulk 'Print all' renders the filtered published cards with page breaks.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Report cards' that lists published cards (students/parents) or all cards (admin/teacher). Each card opens the print view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.6\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Report card access: ADMIN; the student's teachers; and the student and their parents only when the card is published. Any other student (for example in 7B) gets FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API GET /api/report-cards/:id; AC-7\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register notification types grade.posted (student + parents when a manual item grade is entered, default email false, one notification per student per item) and report_card.published (default email true) in src/server/notifications/types.ts, sent via notify().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9; FR-8.4\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Implement the REST endpoints in the API table with the listed roles. 'manage' and 'view' reuse the existing course-access checks, and GET /api/grading-scales is open to any authenticated user. Handlers are thin: Zod validators in src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts, then services in src/server/gradebook/, then the standard response and error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context code layout\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories replaces the full category list and validates that weights total 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed data: the default scale 'Standard A–F' (A 93, A− 90, B+ 87, B 83, B− 80, C+ 77, C 73, C− 70, D+ 67, D 63, D− 60, F 0, with descriptors); categories Homework 30 / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 (drop lowest 1 homework) for all 7A courses; a manual item 'Oral presentation' in ENG-7A graded for all students; and draft Semester 1 report cards for 7A with teacher comments for MATH and ENG.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},","-    {\"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"GET /api/students/:id/grades returns only visible items and only synced (returned or results-visible) scores, under the existing student-access rules (own student, linked parent, teacher, admin).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; NFR-4 Privacy; Roles\"}","+    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums AnnouncementStatus (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED, ARCHIVED) and AudienceType (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE), plus the models Announcement, AnnouncementAudience, AnnouncementAttachment and AnnouncementRead (composite PK announcementId+userId), exactly as specified, in a new prisma migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Validate title ≤ 150 chars and body (Markdown) ≤ 20,000 chars in a shared Zod schema at src/lib/validators/announcements.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model (field comments); Platform Context › Validation\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) in src/server/announcements/audience.ts returns the deduplicated ids of ACTIVE, non-archived users. SCHOOL = everyone, STAFF = ADMIN + TEACHER, ROLE = users whose role is refId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"GRADE_LEVEL audience: students whose profile grade level is refId (includeStudents), their linked parents (includeParents), and teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade level (includeTeachers).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"SECTION audience: section members, their parents, the homeroom teacher and the teachers of the section's courses, each gated by the same include flags. 'Section members' is taken to mean current academic-year SectionMember rows.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"COURSE audience: students with ACTIVE enrollment, their parents, and the course teacher plus co-teachers (Course.coTeacherIds), each gated by the include flags.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"isUserInAudience(user, audiences) answers membership for one user through targeted SQL/Prisma joins, without loading every recipient. It must agree with resolveAudienceUserIds.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; NFR Performance; Test Requirements › Integration\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"The audience service is generic (no announcement-specific coupling) so PRD-14 calendar events can reuse it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"ADMIN may target any audience type and set isPublic.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"TEACHER may target only COURSE audiences for courses they manage (teacher or co-teacher) and SECTION audiences for the section they homeroom. Any other audience, or isPublic=true, is rejected server-side with 403 FORBIDDEN.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; NFR Security; AC-3\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"STUDENT and PARENT cannot create announcements (403).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Authors may edit their own announcements, and admins may edit or archive any. Archiving sets status ARCHIVED. When an admin changes someone else's announcement, write an AuditLog row through audit().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; API table (archive); Platform Context › audit()\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"The composer pages /announcements/new and /announcements/[id]/edit have: title, body (the PRD-08 MarkdownEditor), optional cover image, attachments, an audience builder (rows of type → entity picker → include students/parents/teachers checkboxes), pinned, requires acknowledgement, public (admins only), publish now / schedule (publishAt) / save draft, and an expiry date.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"A live recipient count next to the audience builder ('Will reach 412 people: 180 students, 214 parents, 18 teachers'), computed by POST /api/announcements/preview-audience, which returns counts by role.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.2; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Publishing (now or scheduled) with zero resolved recipients is refused with a VALIDATION_ERROR. Drafts may have zero recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Scheduling sets status SCHEDULED with publishAt. An announcement becomes visible once publishAt <= now, evaluated at read time, so a cron is not needed for visibility.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Feed /announcements (GET /api/announcements) for all roles: published, non-expired announcements whose audience includes the user. Up to 3 pinned show first, then newest. Unread items show a dot. Filter tabs: All / Unread / Requires acknowledgement. Paginated per platform conventions.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"A feed card shows the cover thumbnail, title, author and role, date, audience chips (e.g. 'Grade 7 · Parents'), a 200-character plain-text excerpt and the attachment count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.2\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Detail /announcements/[id] (GET /api/announcements/:id; allowed for audience members, the author and ADMIN) shows the full sanitised body and attachments, and upserts AnnouncementRead.readAt on open.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"When requiresAck is set, an 'I acknowledge' button calls POST /api/announcements/:id/ack (audience members only) and stores acknowledgedAt. The button then reads 'Acknowledged on 14 Sep', shown in the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.3; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"A course 'Announcements' tab (registered in src/config/course-tabs.ts) lists announcements whose audience includes that course (GET /api/announcements?courseId=).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.4; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"In the parent feed, an item with a grade, section or course audience is labelled with the linked child it relates to ('For Sam').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.5; AC-8\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Manage view /announcements/manage (GET /api/announcements/manage): teachers see the announcements they authored, admins see all, including expired and archived ones. Columns: status, audience summary, reach, read %, and acknowledged % when required.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1; AC-6; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"A per-announcement stats page (GET /api/announcements/:id/stats; author or ADMIN) shows counts and a recipient table (name, role, read at, acknowledged at) with Unread / Not acknowledged filters and CSV export via ?format=csv.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; API table; AC-5\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Send reminder' (POST /api/announcements/:id/remind; author or ADMIN) notifies only recipients who have not acknowledged (type announcement.reminder). A second reminder within 24 hours is refused. A refused reminder returns 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT; the architect picks one.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2; AC-5\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register the notification type announcement.published (category COMMUNICATION, default email true, mandatoryInApp true when requiresAck) and the type announcement.reminder in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; FR-6.2\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Send announcement.published exactly once, when the announcement first becomes visible: immediately on publish-now, or by publishDueAnnouncements() in the maintenance run for scheduled ones. notifiedAt is set atomically to keep this idempotent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1; AC-4; Test Requirements › Integration\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"The email uses the generic-notification template with the title, the first 300 characters of the body as plain text, and a 'Read announcement' button linking to /announcements/[id].\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Editing the audience after publish does not re-notify.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table (PATCH notes)\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"Register file access context 'announcement'. Access is allowed for audience members, the author and admins, and for everyone, including anonymous users, when the announcement is isPublic and published. This covers the cover image and attachments.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"getPublicNews({ page }) returns public, published, non-expired announcements. GET /api/public/news exposes it without authentication and is added to public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; API table; AC-7\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Announcements' sidebar entry for all roles, with an unread count badge from GET /api/announcements/unread-count.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1; API table\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"TEACHER and ADMIN see a 'New announcement' button on the feed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"REST endpoints exactly as listed in the PRD API table: GET/POST /api/announcements, GET unread-count, GET/PATCH /:id, POST /:id/archive, POST /:id/ack, POST preview-audience, GET manage, GET /:id/stats, POST /:id/remind, GET /api/public/news. Each uses thin Zod handlers and the platform response/error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context › Code layout\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Seed 6 announcements: school-wide welcome (pinned, public), Grade 7 parents field-trip consent (requires ack), MATH-7A homework club (by Tom), staff meeting (STAFF), sports day notice scheduled 2 days ahead (public), and an expired exam timetable notice.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},","+    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Services go in src/server/announcements/ (announcements-service.ts and audience.ts), following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 heading; Platform Context › Code layout\"}","   ],","   \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Correctness: grade calculation lives in pure functions, all arithmetic uses Decimal (Prisma.Decimal / the existing grading-math helpers), and an exhaustive unit test matrix covers no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides and rounding at band edges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-1; Test Requirements (Unit)\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses during report card generation finishes in under 30 s, using batched queries rather than per-student N+1 calls.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Auditability: every manual grade change, term override and report card unpublish writes an AuditLog row via audit(), with old and new values.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-3; FR-8.4; Platform Context audit rule\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Privacy: hidden items, unreturned assignment scores, not-yet-visible quiz results and unpublished report cards never appear in student or parent responses. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-4; FR-2.2; AC-3; AC-7\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Access control: every handler and server page enforces roles server-side (requireUser/requireRole plus per-entity checks). Teachers see only courses they teach and their homeroom section; parents see only linked students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Code layout & Roles\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/x-scheduler) at the installed 9.5.0. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs and fetchDocs) before use, and only documented props are used. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Recharts, @tanstack/react-table, notistack, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. Toasts use useToast(), confirmations use Dialog and searchable selects use Autocomplete. QA verifies there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1–6\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"DataGrid features are limited to the MIT tier: column groups and cell editing are allowed; pinned columns and other Pro/Premium-only features are not.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models, services and helpers (course access, student-access, csv.ts, grading-math, quiz grading, notify, audit, logger, DataTable, useToast). Do not re-scaffold, rename routes or models, or add console.log. New code goes in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Code layout\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC and shown in SchoolSettings.timezone. 'Past due' and term-containment checks use the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Assumptions ('school timezone is the reference for every date rule')\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Print view: each student's card fits on A4 portrait pages without the app chrome.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test pass. Add tests: unit (calculation matrix); integration (assignment-return and quiz-grading sync hooks, backfill idempotency, snapshot immutability); Playwright (teacher keyboard-edits manual grades, admin generates and publishes report cards, parent views a report card).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Constraints; Test Requirements\"},","-    {\"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope: standards-based grading, GPA/class rank and multi-year transcripts are out of scope. GPA on a band is stored only and never computed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; FR-1 bands gpa?\"}","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: use only Material UI (@mui/material 9.5.0, icons, MUI X). Look up every component through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. No banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, notistack, etc.). Toasts go through useToast(), confirmations use Dialog, pickers use Autocomplete, and Markdown renders to MUI components. If mui-mcp is unreachable, report a blocker. QA must verify there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › UI component rule (item 6)\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the feed query for a parent with 3 children returns in under 200 ms with 2,000 announcements. Membership is resolved through SQL joins on audience rows, never by loading all recipients.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 1 Performance\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Security: every handler and server page enforces access server-side. A teacher who submits a SCHOOL audience gets 403.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security; AC-3; Platform Context › requireRole\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Security: sanitise Markdown bodies as in PRD-08 (react-markdown + rehype-sanitize through the existing MarkdownView), including excerpts and the plain-text email body.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 2 Security\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Accessibility: unread dots carry screen-reader text 'Unread'.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR 3 Accessibility\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Privacy: users only see announcements whose audience includes them. Detail, ack, file and stats endpoints return 403/404 to non-members. Scheduled and expired items are hidden from feeds and from non-author detail.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Goal 2; FR-5.1; API table roles\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Store timestamps in UTC. publishAt, expiresAt and the 'Acknowledged on' date are interpreted and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions; Assumptions\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse the existing services and components (notify, audit, registerFileAccess, csv, MarkdownEditor/View, FileUpload, DataTable, UserPicker, useToast). Don't re-scaffold or rename existing routes or models. Keep lint, typecheck and existing tests passing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Constraints\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Scope: no comments or reactions, no translation, no SMS. Don't implement the PRD-18 public website pages; only expose getPublicNews and /api/public/news.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; Constraints\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for audience resolution per type and flag combination and for teacher permission rules. Integration tests that isUserInAudience matches resolveAudienceUserIds for every seed user (property-style) and that scheduled publish notification is idempotent. A Playwright e2e test: admin composes a targeted announcement with ack, parent reads and acknowledges, admin sees stats.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"},","+    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Use logger from src/lib/logger.ts, never console.log, in new code. The existing seed file's console.log convention may stay as it is.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context › conventions\"}","   ],","-  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,","+  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [","+    {\"id\": \"AC-1\", \"text\": \"Admin targets GRADE_LEVEL Grade 7 with parents only. The preview shows only Grade 7 parents, and after publishing only they see it.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-4\", \"FR-14\", \"FR-17\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-2\", \"text\": \"Tom targets COURSE MATH-7A. MATH-7A students, their parents and Tom see it. A 7B student does not.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-6\", \"FR-10\", \"FR-17\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-3\", \"text\": \"Tom targets SCHOOL via the API and gets 403.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-10\", \"NFR-3\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-4\", \"text\": \"An announcement scheduled for 07:00 tomorrow is invisible until 07:00. Its notification is sent once, by the first maintenance run after 07:00.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-16\", \"FR-27\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-5\", \"text\": \"With requiresAck, 50 recipients and 30 acknowledged: stats show 60% acknowledged, the reminder notifies exactly 20 users, and a second reminder within 24h is refused.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-24\", \"FR-25\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-6\", \"text\": \"An expired announcement is absent from feeds but present in the author's manage view.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-17\", \"FR-23\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-7\", \"text\": \"GET /api/public/news returns public announcements without auth and omits non-public ones.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-31\"]},","+    {\"id\": \"AC-8\", \"text\": \"Pat has Sam (7A) and a child in 6A. A 6A section announcement is labelled 'For <6A child's name>' in Pat's feed.\", \"traces\": [\"FR-22\", \"FR-5\"]}","+  ],","+  \"overallConfidencePct\": 94,","   \"clarificationLog\": [","     {","       \"round\": 1,","       \"questions\": [","-        \"FR-6: When a GradeExemption is removed, should the Grade revert to excused = false and re-sync the score?\",","-        \"FR-7: The PRD names getStudentQuizScore, but that function doesn't exist. Should the gradebook use the quiz's ScoringPolicy (best/latest/average) via applyScoringPolicy?\",","-        \"FR-13: The seed has a separate A− band at 90, so 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A−. Does the test requirement's label 'A' mean the A-band family?\",","-        \"FR-27/FR-33: Should /grades and /report-cards get sidebar nav entries?\",","-        \"NFR-10: Is 'past due' for missing items evaluated against dueAt in UTC or at end of day in the school timezone?\",","-        \"FR-3 term fallback: if dueAt falls outside every term and there is no current term, should the item be skipped or the sync error out?\"","+        \"FR-5: Do 'section members' mean only current academic-year SectionMember rows?\",","+        \"FR-15: Can a draft be saved with zero recipients, with the zero-recipient refusal applied only at publish/schedule time?\",","+        \"FR-25: Should a refused second reminder within 24h return 429 RATE_LIMITED or 409 CONFLICT? And how is the last reminder time stored (a new column such as Announcement.lastRemindedAt, or derived from Notification rows)?\",","+        \"FR-1 vs FR-25: The FR-1 schema has no field for the reminder throttle. Is adding a nullable column acceptable?\",","+        \"FR-17: If more than 3 announcements are pinned, do the extra ones fall back into the newest-first list?\",","+        \"AC-8 / seed: The seed creates no 6A section and no ParentStudentLink rows. Should the seed (or the e2e/integration fixture) create the 6A child linked to Pat?\",","+        \"FR-12: Can an author edit an announcement after it is archived, or is archive terminal?\"","       ],","       \"unresolved\": [","-        \"FR-6 exemption removal behaviour. Assumption: excused = false and the score re-syncs from source.\",","-        \"FR-7 quiz score source. Assumption: getStudentQuizScore is a new helper built on applyScoringPolicy + resultsVisible.\",","-        \"FR-13 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A− under the seed scale. Assumption: the test asserts 90.0 rounding and the letter of the 90 band (A−).\",","-        \"FR-27/FR-33 nav entries. Assumption: add them per the platform convention.\",","-        \"NFR-10 'past due' = now > dueAt (exact instant).\",","-        \"FR-3 no-term fallback. Assumption: skip creating the item and log a warning.\"","+        \"FR-5 section membership scope: defaulting to current academic year.\",","+        \"FR-15 draft with zero recipients: defaulting to allowed; refusal only on publish/schedule.\",","+        \"FR-25 reminder throttle status code and storage: architect decides. Suggested: a nullable lastRemindedAt column and 429 RATE_LIMITED.\",","+        \"FR-17 overflow pins: defaulting to the extra pinned items flowing into newest-first order.\",","+        \"AC-8 fixture: the test fixture creates the 6A child and the Pat link if the seed lacks them.\",","+        \"FR-12 archived edits: defaulting to archive being terminal for authors, with admins still able to edit.\"","       ]","     }","   ],"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-11\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prdTitle\": \"PRD-11: Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\",\n  \"prdTicketRef\": \"SCH-011 (PRD header). The pipeline ticket is SH-11.\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Assignment.categoryId, Quiz.categoryId, Course.gradingScaleId and every PRD-11 model (GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride, ReportCard) are missing from prisma/schema.prisma. They need a new migration.\",\n    \"GradeExemption (schema.prisma ~L801) already exists. Its comment says a row is the PRD-11 'exclude from gradebook' flag, so sync maps it to Grade.excused = true.\",\n    \"Submission has finalScore and returnedAt. A submission counts as returned when returnedAt is non-null.\",\n    \"Quiz.isPractice exists. Practice quizzes must never sync.\",\n    \"No function named getStudentQuizScore exists. The closest helpers are src/server/quiz/grading.ts (applyScoringPolicy, resultsVisible, percentOf) and quiz-service scoreOf. The architect should create or name getStudentQuizScore from these instead of duplicating them.\",\n    \"Section.homeroomTeacherId exists. Homeroom access already exists in src/server/auth/student-access.ts and attendance-service.\",\n    \"src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts has Decimal helpers, and src/server/csv.ts has CSV export. Reuse both.\",\n    \"src/config/student-tabs.ts has courses, attendance and assignments. Add grades and report-cards here.\",\n    \"No gradebook:backfill npm script exists yet. Seeding runs through 'db:seed' (tsx prisma/seed.ts).\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"FR-1\", \"description\": \"Add enums GradeItemSource (ASSIGNMENT, QUIZ, MANUAL) and ReportCardStatus (DRAFT, PUBLISHED), plus the models GradingScale, GradeCategory, GradeItem, Grade, TermGradeOverride and ReportCard, exactly as specified, in a new prisma migrate migration.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-2\", \"description\": \"Add Course.gradingScaleId (nullable, null = school default scale) and nullable categoryId to Assignment and Quiz. Add a category select to the assignment editor and the quiz editor.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 trailing paragraph\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-3\", \"description\": \"When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a GradeItem (source + sourceId, title, maxPoints, dueAt, category). Its term is the one containing dueAt (assignment) or availableUntil (quiz), falling back to the current term.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-4\", \"description\": \"Unpublishing or archiving the source sets GradeItem.isVisible = false. Deleting the source deletes the GradeItem.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-5\", \"description\": \"When a submission is returned, upsert its Grade with score = finalScore. Saving a grade without returning it must not sync.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2; AC-3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-6\", \"description\": \"A grade exemption (the existing GradeExemption row) sets Grade.excused = true. Removing the exemption clears it.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-2.2 'Exemptions set excused = true'; schema.prisma GradeExemption comment. The PRD does not state the clearing behaviour.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-7\", \"description\": \"When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and its results are visible, upsert Grade.score from the student's policy-applied quiz score (getStudentQuizScore), scaled to the quiz maxScore.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-8\", \"description\": \"Add an idempotent one-time backfill script, `npm run gradebook:backfill`. It creates GradeItems and Grades for assignments, quizzes, submissions and attempts that existed before this PRD, and the seed runs it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.4; Test Requirements (backfill idempotency)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-9\", \"description\": \"Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI and API except for comment. Grades on manual items are fully editable.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2.5; API PATCH /api/grade-items/:id notes\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"Add pure grade-calculation functions in src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts. They consider only visible items in the term whose grade is not excused. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and marked missing (counts as 0). Ungraded items not marked missing are ignored.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.1; AC-5\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"Per category, drop the dropLowest lowest item percentages (never dropping every item). categoryPercent = Σscore / Σmax × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.2; AC-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"Course percent is the weighted mean of category percentages, using only categories with at least one counted item and re-normalising weights to those categories. Uncategorised items form an implicit 'Uncategorised' category. A course with no categories uses total points earned / total possible × 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Round the percent half-up to 1 decimal place, then pick the first band of the effective scale (course scale, else school default) where percent >= minPercent. Example: 89.95 → 90.0 → A− in the seed scale.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.4; Test Requirements (89.95 → 90.0)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"TermGradeOverride percent and letter replace the computed values when set. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.5; AC-6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"The calculation must reproduce the worked example: Homework 40% (18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60% (70/100) gives 78.0% C+. The gradebook and the student Grades tab must both show it.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3.6; AC-1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"Add an admin page /admin/grading-scales with CRUD for grading scales and a band editor (letter, minimum %, optional GPA, descriptor). Validate that bands are strictly descending, the lowest minimum is 0, letters are unique, and exactly one scale is the default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"Add course Gradebook settings where the teacher manages categories (name, weight, drop lowest, order). A live sum indicator shows the weight total, and saving is refused unless weights total 100. Settings also include a course grading scale select that defaults to the school default.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5.1; AC-4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"Add a course 'Gradebook' tab for TEACHER/ADMIN with a term selector and an MUI X DataGrid (MIT). Columns are: students sorted by last name first, then items grouped by category via columnGroupingModel (header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages, then term percent + letter in bold. Use a sticky header (no pinned columns), horizontal scrolling and virtualisation for up to 60 students × 120 items.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"Grid cells show the score, 'EX' (excused), 'M' (missing, red) or '—' (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"Manual-item cells are editable through processRowUpdate. A user types a number, Enter or arrow keys move between cells, E marks excused, M marks missing and Delete clears. Changes save on blur with an optimistic update and per-cell error state.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.3; Test Requirements (Playwright keyboard editing)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Clicking a synced cell opens its source (the submission grading page or the quiz attempt).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Add manual item' dialog with title, category, max points, date and term (POST /api/courses/:id/grade-items).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.5; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Add a student row action, 'Override term grade / comment', that opens a dialog with percent, letter and teacher comment (max 1,000 chars) and calls PUT /api/courses/:id/term-overrides/:studentId.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.6; FR-1 TermGradeOverride; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Item column menu actions: hide/show the item to students (isVisible), set all ungraded grades to missing (only after the due date), and view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"'Export CSV' exports the grid as displayed, reusing src/server/csv.ts or papaparse.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Grades' in src/config/student-tabs.ts. For the selected term it shows one card per course with percent, letter and colour (≥80 green, 60–79 amber, <60 red). Expanding a card shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Add a /grades page for STUDENT and PARENT (parents get a child selector) that shows the same content as the Grades tab. Add a sidebar nav entry in src/config/navigation.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Platform Context 'A PRD that adds a page adds its nav entry'\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Add a course tab 'Grades' for STUDENT/PARENT that shows that course's items only.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7.3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-29\", \"description\": \"Add /admin/report-cards: select a term, then see a table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated / Draft / Published) and missing-data warnings (for example ungraded items, or no teacher comment for a course).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-30\", \"description\": \"'Generate drafts' (POST /api/report-cards/generate) builds a snapshot for each filtered student. It contains the school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year. For each course it records subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor and teacher comment. It also records the term attendance summary (rate, absences, lates) and the grading scale legend.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-31\", \"description\": \"Regenerating refreshes the snapshot of DRAFT cards only. PUBLISHED cards are never changed by regeneration or by later grade edits.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.2; AC-8; Test Requirements (snapshot immutability)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-32\", \"description\": \"Add a per-card review page with a rendered preview. The homeroom comment is editable by the homeroom teacher or an admin, and the principal comment by an admin only (PATCH /api/report-cards/:id).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-33\", \"description\": \"Add a /report-cards page where homeroom teachers list their section's drafts to write comments. Add a nav entry for TEACHER.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-8.3; Platform Context nav convention\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-34\", \"description\": \"Publish (per card or in bulk for the filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED, publishedAt and publishedById, and sends report_card.published to the student and parents. Unpublish is admin only, requires a reason and writes an audit entry.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.4; API POST /api/report-cards/publish · /unpublish\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-35\", \"description\": \"Add a print view /report-cards/[id]/print: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for the principal and homeroom teacher, and @media print rules that hide the app sidebar. A 'Print / Save as PDF' button calls window.print(). Bulk 'Print all' renders the filtered published cards with page breaks.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-36\", \"description\": \"Register a student tab 'Report cards' that lists published cards (students/parents) or all cards (admin/teacher). Each card opens the print view.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-37\", \"description\": \"Report card access: ADMIN; the student's teachers; and the student and their parents only when the card is published. Any other student (for example in 7B) gets FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API GET /api/report-cards/:id; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-38\", \"description\": \"Register notification types grade.posted (student + parents when a manual item grade is entered, default email false, one notification per student per item) and report_card.published (default email true) in src/server/notifications/types.ts, sent via notify().\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9; FR-8.4\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-39\", \"description\": \"Implement the REST endpoints in the API table with the listed roles. 'manage' and 'view' reuse the existing course-access checks, and GET /api/grading-scales is open to any authenticated user. Handlers are thin: Zod validators in src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts, then services in src/server/gradebook/, then the standard response and error shapes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; Platform Context code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-40\", \"description\": \"PUT /api/courses/:id/grade-categories replaces the full category list and validates that weights total 100.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-41\", \"description\": \"Seed data: the default scale 'Standard A–F' (A 93, A− 90, B+ 87, B 83, B− 80, C+ 77, C 73, C− 70, D+ 67, D 63, D− 60, F 0, with descriptors); categories Homework 30 / Quizzes 30 / Exams 40 (drop lowest 1 homework) for all 7A courses; a manual item 'Oral presentation' in ENG-7A graded for all students; and draft Semester 1 report cards for 7A with teacher comments for MATH and ENG.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\"},\n    {\"id\": \"FR-42\", \"description\": \"GET /api/students/:id/grades returns only visible items and only synced (returned or results-visible) scores, under the existing student-access rules (own student, linked parent, teacher, admin).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"API table; NFR-4 Privacy; Roles\"}\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Correctness: grade calculation lives in pure functions, all arithmetic uses Decimal (Prisma.Decimal / the existing grading-math helpers), and an exhaustive unit test matrix covers no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, missing vs ungraded, overrides and rounding at band edges.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-1; Test Requirements (Unit)\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Performance: the gradebook for 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Performance: computing term grades for 600 students × 8 courses during report card generation finishes in under 30 s, using batched queries rather than per-student N+1 calls.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Auditability: every manual grade change, term override and report card unpublish writes an AuditLog row via audit(), with old and new values.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-3; FR-8.4; Platform Context audit rule\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Privacy: hidden items, unreturned assignment scores, not-yet-visible quiz results and unpublished report cards never appear in student or parent responses. This is enforced server-side.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"NFR-4; FR-2.2; AC-3; AC-7\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Access control: every handler and server page enforces roles server-side (requireUser/requireRole plus per-entity checks). Teachers see only courses they teach and their homeroom section; parents see only linked students.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Code layout & Roles\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"UI component rule: only Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material, @mui/x-data-grid, @mui/x-date-pickers, @mui/x-charts, @mui/x-scheduler) at the installed 9.5.0. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs and fetchDocs) before use, and only documented props are used. Banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Recharts, @tanstack/react-table, notistack, etc.) and hand-styled raw HTML are not allowed. Toasts use useToast(), confirmations use Dialog and searchable selects use Autocomplete. QA verifies there are no banned imports.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context 'UI component rule' items 1–6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"DataGrid features are limited to the MIT tier: column groups and cell editing are allowed; pinned columns and other Pro/Premium-only features are not.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6.1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-9\", \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models, services and helpers (course access, student-access, csv.ts, grading-math, quiz grading, notify, audit, logger, DataTable, useToast). Do not re-scaffold, rename routes or models, or add console.log. New code goes in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context; Code layout\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-10\", \"description\": \"Timestamps are stored in UTC and shown in SchoolSettings.timezone. 'Past due' and term-containment checks use the school timezone.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"Platform Context Assumptions ('school timezone is the reference for every date rule')\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-11\", \"description\": \"Print view: each student's card fits on A4 portrait pages without the app chrome.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8.5; AC-9\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-12\", \"description\": \"Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test pass. Add tests: unit (calculation matrix); integration (assignment-return and quiz-grading sync hooks, backfill idempotency, snapshot immutability); Playwright (teacher keyboard-edits manual grades, admin generates and publishes report cards, parent views a report card).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Constraints; Test Requirements\"},\n    {\"id\": \"NFR-13\", \"description\": \"Scope: standards-based grading, GPA/class rank and multi-year transcripts are out of scope. GPA on a band is stored only and never computed.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope; FR-1 bands gpa?\"}\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"FR-6: When a GradeExemption is removed, should the Grade revert to excused = false and re-sync the score?\",\n        \"FR-7: The PRD names getStudentQuizScore, but that function doesn't exist. Should the gradebook use the quiz's ScoringPolicy (best/latest/average) via applyScoringPolicy?\",\n        \"FR-13: The seed has a separate A− band at 90, so 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A−. Does the test requirement's label 'A' mean the A-band family?\",\n        \"FR-27/FR-33: Should /grades and /report-cards get sidebar nav entries?\",\n        \"NFR-10: Is 'past due' for missing items evaluated against dueAt in UTC or at end of day in the school timezone?\",\n        \"FR-3 term fallback: if dueAt falls outside every term and there is no current term, should the item be skipped or the sync error out?\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"FR-6 exemption removal behaviour. Assumption: excused = false and the score re-syncs from source.\",\n        \"FR-7 quiz score source. Assumption: getStudentQuizScore is a new helper built on applyScoringPolicy + resultsVisible.\",\n        \"FR-13 89.95 → 90.0 maps to A− under the seed scale. Assumption: the test asserts 90.0 rounding and the letter of the 90 band (A−).\",\n        \"FR-27/FR-33 nav entries. Assumption: add them per the platform convention.\",\n        \"NFR-10 'past due' = now > dueAt (exact instant).\",\n        \"FR-3 no-term fallback. Assumption: skip creating the item and log a warning.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NFpB3b2HUSr5bXgMYsXSPv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgsfmwb5nhHwuwpsZYHXj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LBcEK5byqmkVe5sA3Ve8p1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-12 — User Stories (PRD-12: Announcements & News)\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. Each story cites its requirement id(s) in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Data & Audience\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-2, FR-36)**: As a developer, I want the announcement models, enums and validators, so that announcements, audiences, attachments and read receipts are stored consistently.\n- **US-2 (FR-3 – FR-8)**: As an author, I want audiences (school, staff, role, grade level, section, course, each with student/parent/teacher flags) resolved to exactly the right active users, so that my announcement reaches the intended people and nobody else.\n\n## Permissions\n\n- **US-3 (FR-9, FR-11)**: As an admin, I want to target any audience and mark announcements public, so that I can reach anyone, including website visitors. Students and parents cannot post.\n- **US-4 (FR-10)**: As a teacher, I want to post to my courses and my homeroom section, so that my students and their parents hear class news. The server rejects any other audience with 403.\n- **US-5 (FR-12)**: As an author, I want to edit my own announcements, and as an admin I want to edit or archive any, so that mistakes can be corrected. Edits by admins are audited.\n\n## Composing\n\n- **US-6 (FR-13)**: As an admin or teacher, I want a composer with a Markdown body, a cover image, attachments, an audience builder, pin/ack/public options and publish now / schedule / draft with an expiry, so that I can write a complete notice in one place.\n- **US-7 (FR-14, FR-15)**: As an author, I want a live \"Will reach N people\" count by role, and I want publishing to zero recipients refused, so that I know who I'm reaching before I send.\n- **US-8 (FR-16)**: As an admin, I want to schedule an announcement and set an expiry, so that it appears and disappears at the right time.\n\n## Reading\n\n- **US-9 (FR-17, FR-18)**: As any user, I want one feed of announcements meant for me, with pinned items first, unread dots and All / Unread / Requires-ack tabs, so that I don't miss anything.\n- **US-10 (FR-19, FR-20)**: As a recipient, I want to open an announcement (which marks it read) and acknowledge it when required, so that the office knows I've seen it.\n- **US-11 (FR-21)**: As a course member, I want an Announcements tab on the course, so that I can see class news in context.\n- **US-12 (FR-22)**: As a parent, I want each grade, section or course item labelled with the child it relates to (\"For Sam\"), so that I know which child it's about.\n\n## Author Tools\n\n- **US-13 (FR-23)**: As an author, I want a manage view with status, reach, read % and acknowledged %, including expired and archived items, so that I can track my announcements.\n- **US-14 (FR-24, FR-25)**: As an admin, I want per-announcement stats with a recipient table, filters and CSV export, and a \"Send reminder\" button for those who haven't acknowledged (at most once per 24h), so that I can follow up.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **US-15 (FR-26 – FR-29)**: As a recipient, I want one notification (in-app plus email) when an announcement first becomes visible to me, so that I hear about it promptly. Later audience edits don't re-notify.\n\n## Files, Public News & Navigation\n\n- **US-16 (FR-30)**: As a recipient, I want to download the attachments and cover image, so that I get the full notice. Anonymous visitors can download them only for public, published announcements.\n- **US-17 (FR-31)**: As the public website (PRD-18), I want `GET /api/public/news`, so that public announcements appear as school news without a login.\n- **US-18 (FR-32, FR-33)**: As any user, I want an \"Announcements\" sidebar link with an unread badge, and as a teacher or admin I want a \"New announcement\" button, so that the feature is easy to reach.\n\n## Seed\n\n- **US-19 (FR-35)**: As a developer or tester, I want the 6 demo announcements seeded, so that every feed state (pinned, ack, course, staff, scheduled, expired) can be seen.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1**: Material UI only, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first. No banned libraries. QA checks the imports.\n- **NFR-2**: The feed for a parent with 3 children returns in under 200 ms with 2,000 announcements, using SQL joins on audience rows.\n- **NFR-3**: Server-side access checks everywhere. A teacher targeting SCHOOL gets 403.\n- **NFR-4**: Markdown is sanitised as in PRD-08 (body, excerpt, email text).\n- **NFR-5**: Unread dots have screen-reader text \"Unread\".\n- **NFR-6**: No visibility outside the audience. Scheduled and expired items are hidden from feeds.\n- **NFR-7**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-8**: Brownfield reuse, no re-scaffolding. Lint, typecheck and tests stay green.\n- **NFR-9**: Out of scope: comments, reactions, translation, SMS, and the PRD-18 pages themselves.\n- **NFR-10**: Unit, integration (property-style audience parity, notification idempotency) and Playwright tests as listed.\n- **NFR-11**: Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8281,"cache_read_input_tokens":52478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8281,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5ee16ee-e095-4181-884c-a98d424b627c","uuid":"4da143d9-1c8f-4fd9-8d45-35279c13ece7","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:28:21.131Z","request_id":"req_011CgsfmwA36FzbrX5ehHKsB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LBcEK5byqmkVe5sA3Ve8p1":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/intake/user-stories.md","content":"# SH-12 — User Stories (PRD-12: Announcements & News)\n\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`. Each story cites its requirement id(s) in `requirements.json`.\n\n## Data & Audience\n\n- **US-1 (FR-1, FR-2, FR-36)**: As a developer, I want the announcement models, enums and validators, so that announcements, audiences, attachments and read receipts are stored consistently.\n- **US-2 (FR-3 – FR-8)**: As an author, I want audiences (school, staff, role, grade level, section, course, each with student/parent/teacher flags) resolved to exactly the right active users, so that my announcement reaches the intended people and nobody else.\n\n## Permissions\n\n- **US-3 (FR-9, FR-11)**: As an admin, I want to target any audience and mark announcements public, so that I can reach anyone, including website visitors. Students and parents cannot post.\n- **US-4 (FR-10)**: As a teacher, I want to post to my courses and my homeroom section, so that my students and their parents hear class news. The server rejects any other audience with 403.\n- **US-5 (FR-12)**: As an author, I want to edit my own announcements, and as an admin I want to edit or archive any, so that mistakes can be corrected. Edits by admins are audited.\n\n## Composing\n\n- **US-6 (FR-13)**: As an admin or teacher, I want a composer with a Markdown body, a cover image, attachments, an audience builder, pin/ack/public options and publish now / schedule / draft with an expiry, so that I can write a complete notice in one place.\n- **US-7 (FR-14, FR-15)**: As an author, I want a live \"Will reach N people\" count by role, and I want publishing to zero recipients refused, so that I know who I'm reaching before I send.\n- **US-8 (FR-16)**: As an admin, I want to schedule an announcement and set an expiry, so that it appears and disappears at the right time.\n\n## Reading\n\n- **US-9 (FR-17, FR-18)**: As any user, I want one feed of announcements meant for me, with pinned items first, unread dots and All / Unread / Requires-ack tabs, so that I don't miss anything.\n- **US-10 (FR-19, FR-20)**: As a recipient, I want to open an announcement (which marks it read) and acknowledge it when required, so that the office knows I've seen it.\n- **US-11 (FR-21)**: As a course member, I want an Announcements tab on the course, so that I can see class news in context.\n- **US-12 (FR-22)**: As a parent, I want each grade, section or course item labelled with the child it relates to (\"For Sam\"), so that I know which child it's about.\n\n## Author Tools\n\n- **US-13 (FR-23)**: As an author, I want a manage view with status, reach, read % and acknowledged %, including expired and archived items, so that I can track my announcements.\n- **US-14 (FR-24, FR-25)**: As an admin, I want per-announcement stats with a recipient table, filters and CSV export, and a \"Send reminder\" button for those who haven't acknowledged (at most once per 24h), so that I can follow up.\n\n## Notifications\n\n- **US-15 (FR-26 – FR-29)**: As a recipient, I want one notification (in-app plus email) when an announcement first becomes visible to me, so that I hear about it promptly. Later audience edits don't re-notify.\n\n## Files, Public News & Navigation\n\n- **US-16 (FR-30)**: As a recipient, I want to download the attachments and cover image, so that I get the full notice. Anonymous visitors can download them only for public, published announcements.\n- **US-17 (FR-31)**: As the public website (PRD-18), I want `GET /api/public/news`, so that public announcements appear as school news without a login.\n- **US-18 (FR-32, FR-33)**: As any user, I want an \"Announcements\" sidebar link with an unread badge, and as a teacher or admin I want a \"New announcement\" button, so that the feature is easy to reach.\n\n## Seed\n\n- **US-19 (FR-35)**: As a developer or tester, I want the 6 demo announcements seeded, so that every feed state (pinned, ack, course, staff, scheduled, expired) can be seen.\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- **NFR-1**: Material UI only, with every component looked up via mui-mcp first. No banned libraries. QA checks the imports.\n- **NFR-2**: The feed for a parent with 3 children returns in under 200 ms with 2,000 announcements, using SQL joins on audience rows.\n- **NFR-3**: Server-side access checks everywhere. A teacher targeting SCHOOL gets 403.\n- **NFR-4**: Markdown is sanitised as in PRD-08 (body, excerpt, email text).\n- **NFR-5**: Unread dots have screen-reader text \"Unread\".\n- **NFR-6**: No visibility outside the audience. Scheduled and expired items are hidden from feeds.\n- **NFR-7**: Timestamps are stored in UTC and displayed in the school timezone.\n- **NFR-8**: Brownfield reuse, no re-scaffolding. Lint, typecheck and tests stay green.\n- **NFR-9**: Out of scope: comments, reactions, translation, SMS, and the PRD-18 pages themselves.\n- **NFR-10**: Unit, integration (property-style audience parity, notification idempotency) and Playwright tests as listed.\n- **NFR-11**: Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n"}}}
