{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsfpNBEqcGDUxE8Ui23d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I finished the SH-12 intake and the files in `artifacts/intake/` now hand off to the Architect phase. All four files are valid JSON or Markdown, and every requirement has a confidence label and a PRD citation. They replace the SH-11 intake files that were in that folder from the previous run.\n\n- **`requirements.json`**: 36 functional and 11 non-functional requirements, the 8 acceptance criteria mapped to them, and notes on what the existing code already provides. Overall confidence is 94%.\n- **`user-stories.md`**: 19 user stories plus the non-functional requirements.\n- **`tech-stack.json`**: React (Next.js 14, MUI 9.5.0). This feature needs no new packages.\n- **`handoff-to-architect.json`**: status `complete`, no blockers. I wrote it last.\n- **`figma-readiness.json`**: not created, because the PRD has no Figma URL.\n\n**Ticket ID:** your prompt says SH-12 and the PRD header says SCH-012. I used SH-12 in every file and noted the PRD's ID in `requirements.json`.\n\n**Gaps the Architect needs to settle.** I recorded each as unresolved with a default, so nothing is blocked:\n- **Reminder limit:** the PRD's data model has nowhere to store when the last reminder was sent, which the once-per-24-hours rule needs. I suggested adding an optional `lastRemindedAt` field and refusing early reminders with a 429 error, but left the choice to the Architect.\n- **Missing test data:** the seed script creates no 7A, 7B or 6A sections and no parent–child links. Acceptance criterion 8 (Pat's child in 6A) therefore needs a test fixture that creates them.\n- **Smaller defaults:**\n  - A section's members means students in the current school year.\n  - Drafts can be saved with no recipients; only publishing is refused.\n  - If more than 3 announcements are pinned, the extras appear in date order.\n  - Archiving is final for authors, but admins can still edit.\n- **Folder path:** the PRD says shared components are in `src/components/shared/`, but they are actually in `src/components/<Name>/`. I told the Architect to use them where they are.\n\n**Main risks I passed on:**\n- The feed must check whether a user is in an audience with database joins to stay under 200 ms. Loading every recipient would be too slow.\n- The two audience functions must give the same answers for every user.\n- The scheduled-announcement notification must claim `notifiedAt` in a single step, so two maintenance runs can't send it twice.\n- Anonymous downloads of public announcement files must be allowed only once the announcement is published and before it expires."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1562,"cache_read_input_tokens":63573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1562,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5ee16ee-e095-4181-884c-a98d424b627c","uuid":"8540a309-9084-45ed-80b7-f22733dd862b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:28:46.614Z","request_id":"req_011CgsfpMvMQcmW3GUepjPoX"}
